dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-20-2019, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T10:54:47-07:00","id":1337117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337113#post1337113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a stretch goal that expands Deviants beyond human stock. Cool! I have several thoughts about how else Deviant might be expanded (e.g., something like <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/50678\" target=\"_blank\">Reliquary</a>, but built around Deviant's concepts and game systems).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are <i>five</i> Clades... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:12:04-07:00","id":1337120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337117#post1337117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are <i>five</i> Clades... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026which makes me wonder what the other three will cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:15:23-07:00","id":1337121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337107#post1337107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here\u2019s a partial list. These are the ones I tested the splats, Variations, and Scars against in redlines - I would have considered he game a failure if it couldn\u2019t recreate them all.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Guyver</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna take a close look at this one, see if we came to the same conclusions.<br /> <br /> Now most of these may not quite fit in Deviant, since Kronos likes stability and mass production in its creations, but at the very least categories can be assigned...<br /> <br /> <b>Zoalords</b>: the Twelve Divine Generals are mostly Elect, of course, with the possible exceptions of Archanfel (a Cro-Magnon test subject of the Advents, it seems unlikely that they even asked for Volunteers, though those early humans may well have worshipped their Creators enough to not be Unwilling) and Imakarum, who certainly started out as Unwilling but whose upgrade may have involved either brainwashing or a genuine conversion to Archanfel's cause). Although they all have physical transformations, their powers are mostly oriented around manipulation of radiant energy, gravity, and space itself, so I'd put them as Coactives except for Waferdanos and Cablarl Khan (both Hybrids?).<br /> <br /> <b>Zoanoids</b>: the rank and file monsters of Kronos are mostly Volunteers, drawn first from their extensive paramilitary force and then (once they openly rule the world) from civilians enticed by promises of genetic optimization and tax breaks. A substantial minority are Unwilling, in fact not even knowing that they had been abducted and converted for use as sleeper agents. A mix of Hybrid and Coactive, the latter accounting for laser/plasma artillery types such as Vamores.<br /> <br /> Hyper-Zoanoids: mostly Elect or Volunteers at worst, troopers rewarded for exceptional service with individualized Super Prototype templates. Again, Hybrids and Coactives.<br /> <br /> Zoanoids all share one engineered flaw: they are absolutely susceptible to the telepathic commands of the Zoalords, incapable of even <i>trying</i> to resist, no matter their strength of will. As such, they are probably not suitable as player characters. However...<br /> <br /> <b>Lost</b> <b>Numbers</b>: now here we start getting into serious Deviance. The result of a design flaw that crops up in multiple Zoanoid experiments, LNs are all Mutants whose powers may or may not have anything to do with the original plan and whose genetic code is apparently irreproducible by any means. Worse, from Kronos's point of view at least, they are all at least somewhat resistant to telepathy, if not outright immune.<br /> <br /> Even though Lost Numbers normally start out as Elect or Volunteers, and most of them stay Loyal, Kronos keeps them under wraps unless it absolutely needs their bizarre talents.<br /> <br /> Aptom is of course the preeminent Lost Number, a terrifying enormity who if he ever met Alex Mercer would find him inferior, probably not even bothering to eat him because he has nothing Aptom would find novel or useful. Good thing he eventually went Renegade. <br /> <br /> <b>Guyvers</b>: and now we get to the hero and his peers. I <i>think</i> the bio-booster armor counts as Cyborg, given that it centers around the hard-tech Control Medal and its brain interface.<br /> <br /> Guyver 0, like Archanfel, might have been anything from Elect to Unwilling.<br /> <br /> Guyver I, Sho Fukamachi, is the classic Accidental, having had the armor thrown at him by a random explosion. <br /> <br /> Guyver II, Oswald Lisker, also Accidentally bonded with the second Unit when it turned out to be on a hair trigger. Shame about its Flaw. His sister Valkyria, Guyver II-F, appears to have Volunteered for the repaired armor.<br /> <br /> Guyver III, Agito Makishima, is of course an Elect, having stolen the final Unit and decided to activate it after seeing the others in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:18:09-07:00","id":1337122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337120#post1337120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026which makes me wonder what the other three will cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean &quot;other four,&quot; but yes, there is cool stuff ahead if we can hit more Stretch Goals, so spread the word, if you can!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:25:23-07:00","id":1337123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337117#post1337117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are <i>five</i> Clades... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not according to Captain Picard...<br /> <br /> Really loving the preview so far. When you mentioned seeing Deviant characters all over media, Sil from Species popped into my head as a Genotypal Hybrid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:25:42-07:00","id":1337124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337063#post1337063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a pretty good summation of my current thinking on the subject. A lot will depend on what your chronicle needs and which game you're playing. In a Hunter game, Cheiron, VASCU, et. al. have processes that grant members supernatural abilities in a very limited way, and cracked souls are not an outcome within the scope of the game. In a chronicle of a Deviant game that uses Hunter Conspiracies as significant players, Divergence occurs in the process rarely, frequently, or even most of the time (as your chronicle requires). Deviant's core isn't going to address these questions head-on, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow that got me excited for Lucifuge Deviants.<br /> <br /> partly becasue a reread of the Conspiracies regarding this game made it clear how plausible that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:37:01-07:00","id":1337126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337123#post1337123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sil from Species popped into my head as a Genotypal Hybrid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine, too.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>: VASCU is another one. How many people who undergo the Wintergreen Process <i>don't</i> come back as super-detectives and instead become something akin to Slashers themselves? That's an easy crossover plot for a Storyteller running Hunter, if they have access to Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:49:25-07:00","id":1337129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337126#post1337126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>: VASCU is another one. How many people who undergo the Wintergreen Process <i>don't</i> come back as super-detectives and instead become something akin to Slashers themselves? That's an easy crossover plot for a Storyteller running Hunter, if they have access to Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note... looking at some Slashers, Freaks and Mutants particularly, you wonder whether, rather than dying or going through Divergence, some folk take a third option, giving themselves over to murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T12:01:17-07:00","id":1337131,"title":"","content":"Some things I'm really hoping for after reading the backer's preview (well, mostly. That thing is long) is A) a way for Deviants to reach a point where they can toss out that whole broken soul thing without being turned into a baseline human and B) a way where they can reach contentment without revenge. Maybe channel it into some other sort of passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T12:31:00-07:00","id":1337135,"title":"","content":"There's nothing saying that a Renegade can't rely on Loyalty. Just, probably not Loyalty to the Conspiracy that created it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T12:55:03-07:00","id":1337139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337131#post1337131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things I'm really hoping for after reading the backer's preview (well, mostly. That thing is long) is A) a way for Deviants to reach a point where they can toss out that whole broken soul thing without being turned into a baseline human and B) a way where they can reach contentment without revenge. Maybe channel it into some other sort of passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) is against the concept of Deviant, and while there's nothing wrong with you doing something like that in your game, I don't expect such a happy ending to be supported by the game itself.<br /> As for B), the closest you are likely to get is Guardian condition, which is temporary and doesn't outright remove the drive for revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T13:06:42-07:00","id":1337140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337107#post1337107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here\u2019s a partial list. These are the ones I tested the splats, Variations, and Scars against in redlines - I would have considered he game a failure if it couldn\u2019t recreate them all.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Alex Mack<br /> \u2022 Alex Mercer (Prototype)<br /> \u2022 Alister Peck (Fringe)<br /> \u2022 Alligator People (film)<br /> \u2022 Brindle (The Fly - 80s version)<br /> \u2022 Buffy Summers<br /> \u2022 Castor Clones (Orphan Black)<br /> \u2022 Cole (InFamous)<br /> \u2022 Darien Fawkes (The Invisible Man - 90 tv)<br /> \u2022 Dr Jackman (Moffat Jekyll)<br /> \u2022 Dr Jekyll (ITV)<br /> \u2022 Dr Jekyll (Original)<br /> \u2022 Dr Moreau's Creations<br /> \u2022 Dren (Splice)<br /> \u2022 Echo (Dollhouse)<br /> \u2022 Eleven (Stranger Things)<br /> \u2022 Enchantress (DC)<br /> \u2022 Gor (First Born)<br /> \u2022 Griffin (the Invisible Man)<br /> \u2022 Guyver<br /> \u2022 Hollow Man<br /> \u2022 Innsmouth Fishpeople<br /> \u2022 Jessica Jones<br /> \u2022 John Doe<br /> \u2022 June (The Innocents)<br /> \u2022 Kamen Rider<br /> \u2022 Kyle XY<br /> \u2022 Leda Clones (Orphan Black)<br /> \u2022 Luke Cage<br /> \u2022 Matt Murdock<br /> \u2022 Max (Dark Angel)<br /> \u2022 Max (Roswell)<br /> \u2022 Max (Videodrome)<br /> \u2022 Mr Tooms (X-Files)<br /> \u2022 Nick (Push)<br /> \u2022 Olivia Dunham (Fringe)<br /> \u2022 River Tam (Firefly)<br /> \u2022 Robocop (Original)<br /> \u2022 Robocop (Remake)<br /> \u2022 Scanners<br /> \u2022 Tandy and Tyrone (Cloak and Dagger)<br /> \u2022 Tetsuo (Akira)<br /> \u2022 Tetsuo (the Iron Man)<br /> \u2022 The Chrysalids<br /> \u2022 The Fly - original<br /> \u2022 The Hulk<br /> \u2022 The Tomorrow People (90s tv)<br /> \u2022 The Toxic Avenger<br /> \u2022 V (V for Vendetta)<br /> \u2022 Vincent (90s Beauty and the Beast)</div> </div> </div> </div>TOOMS<br /> <br /> Loving the preview so far. I was a bit apprehensive of how such a diverse group would fit with each other, but it seems the writers gave it a lot of thought already. Now to find if Beast consider Deviants kin...<br /> <br /> And that clade companion is looking awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T13:08:49-07:00","id":1337141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337139#post1337139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) is against the concept of Deviant, and while there's nothing wrong with you doing something like that in your game, I don't expect such a happy ending to be supported by the game itself.<br /> As for B), the closest you are likely to get is Guardian condition, which is temporary and doesn't outright remove the drive for revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't expect it honestly, but I can still hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T13:15:26-07:00","id":1337142,"title":"","content":"So, odds are I'll name any Deviant I make Max, since that appears to be the most common name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T13:27:11-07:00","id":1337143,"title":"","content":"Minor thing: I wonder if (and I hope that) Different parts of an Amalgam can have different things like Forms or even Origins (ala one... donor was Self-made and Elect, but the other was Unwilling, and such). I doubt it (especially origins) but it sounds like a cool idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T13:29:50-07:00","id":1337144,"title":"","content":"First Stretch Goal achieved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T14:10:24-07:00","id":1337148,"title":"","content":"...I'll admit some of the stuff I've been seeing the past several months on this game (and particularly what I've read in the KS preview yesterday) has me concerned. Normally, I'm all for the Chronicles of Darkness's tone of &quot;danger's around every corner and turning into a worse monster is something characters must avoid.&quot; At the same time, though, the current tone for Deviant's at a level that even my dark-story-loving self is finding hard to digest. The organization tracking you down is everywhere, can take your life away from you at literally any minute, and any positive change you make is fleeting at best, and undone ridiculously easy by your actions at worst. Even the Integrity counterpart of Loyalty/Conviction and the Instability track seems to hammer this in. A Remade has no sense of self or internal character traits (something that sets off red flags for my inner writer), and any actions that go against pursuing completely extrinsic goals, even for ethical/pragmatic reasons, punish you with the seemingly inevitable endgame of going out violently a la Akira's Tetsuo. My friends and I tend to play our CofD games as, while crapsack, not so much that making some manner of positive change (even if just living to fight another day) is impossible. Yet from what I've read so far, Deviant's mechanics and lore go against such a concept. I hope this is just me misinterpreting what's currently available, though, because the premise of playing an experiment on the run from an organization that considers them property is otherwise a game concept I'm obsessed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T14:54:23-07:00","id":1337155,"title":"","content":"The entire reason the Web of Pain is a thing is because it\u2019s very much supposed to be possible to destroy or otherwise be rid of a conspiracy once and for all, at which point the ST might reasonably (but not necessarily) want there to be another one where it came from. And then you take that one down, and as many more as it takes before either the rest finally know when to fold \u2018em or you\u2019ve accidentally the entire Web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-20-2019, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T14:57:17-07:00","id":1337156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337148#post1337148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'll admit some of the stuff I've been seeing the past several months on this game (and particularly what I've read in the KS preview yesterday) has me concerned. Normally, I'm all for the Chronicles of Darkness's tone of &amp;quot;danger's around every corner and turning into a worse monster is something characters must avoid.&amp;quot; At the same time, though, the current tone for Deviant's at a level that even my dark-story-loving self is finding hard to digest. The organization tracking you down is everywhere, can take your life away from you at literally any minute, and any positive change you make is fleeting at best, and undone ridiculously easy by your actions at worst. Even the Integrity counterpart of Loyalty/Conviction and the Instability track seems to hammer this in. A Remade has no sense of self or internal character traits (something that sets off red flags for my inner writer), and any actions that go against pursuing completely extrinsic goals, even for ethical/pragmatic reasons, punish you with the seemingly inevitable endgame of going out violently a la Akira's Tetsuo. My friends and I tend to play our CofD games as, while crapsack, not so much that making some manner of positive change (even if just living to fight another day) is impossible. Yet from what I've read so far, Deviant's mechanics and lore go against such a concept. I hope this is just me misinterpreting what's currently available, though, because the premise of playing an experiment on the run from an organization that considers them property is otherwise a game concept I'm obsessed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I don't see this as being any different than the perception of Vampire as a game featuring an inevitable slide into a state of monstrosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T15:00:39-07:00","id":1337157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337155#post1337155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire reason the Web of Pain is a thing is because it\u2019s very much supposed to be possible to destroy or otherwise be rid of a conspiracy once and for all, at which point the ST might reasonably (but not necessarily) want there to be another one where it came from. And then you take that one down, and as many more as it takes before either the rest finally know when to fold \u2018em or you\u2019ve accidentally the entire Web.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another purpose of the Web of Pain is that it lets you connect Deviants that were created by different conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T15:13:04-07:00","id":1337162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337155#post1337155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire reason the Web of Pain is a thing is because it\u2019s very much supposed to be possible to destroy or otherwise be rid of a conspiracy once and for all, at which point the ST might reasonably (but not necessarily) want there to be another one where it came from. And then you take that one down, and as many more as it takes before either the rest finally know when to fold \u2018em or you\u2019ve accidentally the entire Web.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes sense. As for the character thing, though? The idea of a character having no characteristics beyond who they love or hate is something I'm admittedly having a hard time wrapping my head around currently<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337156#post1337156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I don't see this as being any different than the perception of Vampire as a game featuring an inevitable slide into a state of monstrosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was the reason why I voiced my concerns in the thread rather than bottled it up. I rationally knew that most CofD games tends to be dark without being hopeless, I was just struggling to get into said mindset this time and was hoping it was just me blowing minor details out of proportion again (I sadly do that a <i>lot,</i> so such an assumption isn't unfounded).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T15:19:19-07:00","id":1337163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337162#post1337162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a character having no characteristics beyond who they love or hate is something I'm admittedly having a hard time wrapping my head around currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>To save you some grief: that's not what &quot;define themselves by their relation to other people&quot; means.<br /> <br /> The Remade can't safely exist in isolation, which is not the same thing as being purely about those relationships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T15:40:47-07:00","id":1337165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337163#post1337163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To save you some grief: that's not what &quot;define themselves by their relation to other people&quot; means.<br /> <br /> The Remade can't safely exist in isolation, which is not the same thing as being purely about those relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's more like the touchstones of other games (where you have to interact with the real world -- and potentially other worlds -- to keep grounded), just made more important to the mechanics? I... kinda feel dumb for adding this up sooner in hindsight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T15:44:59-07:00","id":1337166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337165#post1337165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's more like the touchstones of other games (where you have to interact with the real world -- and potentially other worlds -- to keep grounded), just made more important to the mechanics? I... kinda feel dumb for adding this up sooner in hindsight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vibe I'm getting is its like the Obsessions of mages or the primal need to hunt for werewolves, they don't entirely override your identity and other interests but suddenly the context of your life shifts heavily and they're RP drama hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T16:29:32-07:00","id":1337173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1336994#post1336994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw Deviant stories everywhere I looked, and I could probably give you a separate list of 100 media examples of Deviant characters or Deviant stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a developer's started topic on the forum, guys... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> , please, please do it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T16:30:41-07:00","id":1337174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337166#post1337166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vibe I'm getting is its like the Obsessions of mages or the primal need to hunt for werewolves, they don't entirely override your identity and other interests but suddenly the context of your life shifts heavily and they're RP drama hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing a lot of ideas of other games that would enrich Deviant tremendously. Mages and their Obsessions over Mysteries would form a great basis for mad scientists who create Deviants (among other things); those who want to give Deviants a happy endgame state might borrow ideas from Promethean's Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> I also see a lot of conceptual resonance between Changeling and Deviant (not just the thematic \u201csomeone changed you into something not entirely human, and now you're at odds with them&quot;, but also a certain similarity between Clarity and Stability (both are handled as damage tracks). <br /> <br /> Hunter provides a means of portraying the conspiracies as good guys (or at least as close to good guys as anything in the Chronicles of Darkness ever gets) with Bestowments providing a potentially complementary \u201cpowerset\u201d to what Deviant provides. <br /> <br /> Demon also has a techno-thriller \u201crebel against the establishment\u201d theme to it, though the motives are a bit different. <br /> <br /> I'll leave ties with Vampire, Werewolf, Geist, Mummy, and Beast for others to explore; they're not really my thing, for one, and I just don't see as much resonance between them and Deviant, for other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T16:52:00-07:00","id":1337176,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: For when you want your Loyalty Touchstones to be as up for helping you take down your Conviction Touchstones as possible. Also something something pack bonding + Loyalty.<br /> <br /> Beast: Basically the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-20-2019, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T16:52:33-07:00","id":1337177,"title":"","content":"Speaking a fan (rather than a writer) I 100% guarantee that a) there is a Deviant out there whose Progenitor tried (and failed) to duplicate the Rite of Return and b) it\u2019s probably Last Dynasty International\u2019s fault.<br /> <br /> And actually, just spit balling (aka: fan hat is still on, this could be contradicted at any moment), but mummies became mummies because they were able to declare their Decree to the Judges and rebuild the pillars of their soul. There are a lot of reasons for an Arisen and a metaphysically-aware Renegade to be interested in each other\u2019s experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T17:12:23-07:00","id":1337179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337177#post1337177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking a fan (rather than a writer) I 100% guarantee that a) there is a Deviant out there whose Progenitor tried (and failed) to duplicate the Rite of Return and b) it\u2019s probably Last Dynasty International\u2019s fault.<br /> <br /> And actually, just spit balling (aka: fan hat is still on, this could be contradicted at any moment), but mummies became mummies because they were able to declare their Decree to the Judges and rebuild the pillars of their soul. There are a lot of reasons for an Arisen and a metaphysically-aware Renegade to be interested in each other\u2019s experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could certainly see some interesting conversations that boil down to &quot;oh look, your sheut is leaking.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T17:46:33-07:00","id":1337184,"title":"","content":"For Beast, I could see Begotten trying to artificially incite the Devouring through some forgotten/forbidden Obascus Rite, and instead Divergence happens...breaking the Soul so that no Horror wants to touch it but somehow not creating a Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T18:35:42-07:00","id":1337187,"title":"","content":"Think I might've mentioned one of these ages ago in another thread, but some quick ideas to kick off a Vampire/Deviant thing: <br /> Someone (or a coterie of someones) decides that using a fully-intact, living human for the &quot;Birthing the God&quot; ritual would be a lot faster and easier than gathering a bunch of disparate body parts. Cue the point where things go very, <i>very</i> sideways.<br /> <br /> Someone's been tinkering with the creation of a new Scale, but one of the mortal test subjects came out <i>weird</i>. And <i>angry</i>.<br /> <br /> Turns out, a coterie's rival(s) happens to be quite deeply involved in a conspiracy that a cohort just so happens to have it out for... but of course, said rival has one or a few Devoted in their service, possibly even directly in their thrall through Loyalty and Vinculum alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T18:47:43-07:00","id":1337189,"title":"","content":"I think there's also a lot of crossover potential with most of the gamelines in the form of Deviants who were created using elements of other cosmologies: <br /> <br /> Coactives could be created through specially treated vitae, essence, mana, Pyros, Glamour, plasm, Pillars, or Aether. <br /> <br /> Chimerics could be created using body parts from most of the other supernatural types (except perhaps mages and Beasts, whose \u201csupernatures\u201d don't have a physical component, and Unfleshed or constructed Prometheans and Demons, who would arguably result in Invasives). <br /> <br /> Properly controlled exposure to otherworldly realms (especially to the Astral, but I could also see justifications for the Hedge, the Underworld, and the Shadow) could produce Cephalists, assuming that the energies of those realms don't end up producing Coactives. (In the case of an Underworld-based Cephalist, think of Orpheus projectors \u2014 and suddenly I want to do a Geist/Deviant crossover where the Deviants are all Psychics or Coactives from the Orpheus Group with a Variation that lets them project into ghostly Twilight.)<br /> <br /> But my earlier musings about crossover material were mostly intended to be more thematic and/or psychological in nature than metaphysical: a mage's insatiable curiosity, a Promethean's desire to fix his broken status; a changeling's conflict with entities that abused her; a demon's conflict with something that claims authority over hir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-20-2019, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:31:51-07:00","id":1337196,"title":"","content":"Dear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> <br /> I'd like to ask,If there are Human Deviants and Animal Deviants.<br /> Are there Deviant Places? Like,cities or towns or woods who became magical due to rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:45:34-07:00","id":1337197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337196#post1337196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a><br /> I'd like to ask,If there are Human Deviants and Animal Deviants.<br /> Are there Deviant Places? Like,cities or towns or woods who became magical due to rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of places that are prone to triggering the Divergence, if that's what you mean. The Deviant core - as well as both Contagion Chronicle and Dark Eras 2 - feature some. In the old days (before conspiracies understood the Divergence), it was quite common for young warriors or apprentice mystics to climb a sacred mountain or seek out a mystical oasis in the desert to gain some kind of blessing. Many did not return from the journey - partially because it was often a dangerous path, but also because the undergoing the Divergence is so often fatal, and those who returned were...changed, haunted in some ways, but unquestionably greatly enhanced in prowess or forbidden lore. In the present, conspiracies seek out such place and squat on them, sending test subjects into the heart of the power to achieve Divergence.<br /> <br /> If you're asking about <i>playable</i> towns and forests, that's outside of the game's scope. Hard to be on the run from a conspiracy when you're an immobile dot on a map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:45:36-07:00","id":1337198,"title":"","content":"Or things, or events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:51:22-07:00","id":1337199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337197#post1337197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are lots of places that are prone to triggering the Divergence, if that's what you mean. The Deviant core - as well as both Contagion Chronicle and Dark Eras 2 - feature some. In the old days (before conspiracies understood the Divergence), it was quite common for young warriors or apprentice mystics to climb a sacred mountain or seek out a mystical oasis in the desert to gain some kind of blessing. Many did not return from the journey - partially because it was often a dangerous path, but also because the undergoing the Divergence is so often fatal, and those who returned were...changed, haunted in some ways, but unquestionably greatly enhanced in prowess or forbidden lore. In the present, conspiracies seek out such place and squat on them, sending test subjects into the heart of the power to achieve Divergence.<br /> <br /> If you're asking about <i>playable</i> towns and forests, that's outside of the game's scope. Hard to be on the run from a conspiracy when you're an immobile dot on a map.</div> </div> </div> </div>if I may ask, it is mentioned that there are ephemeral beings becoming deviants in the preview. does this mean we can have a spirit really fucking up the claiming of a human, and becoming a twisted deviant for it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:52:37-07:00","id":1337200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337198#post1337198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or things, or events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Events has the same answer as for places. What kinds of things did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> ETA: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a>: It's more that the being attempts to claim the human and becomes a battery for the new Deviant's supernatural abilities. If the Remade has the Symbiote Form, it usually means that the ephemeral being is still in there and has some small sway over how she uses its powers. The Alternate Persona Scar means that sometimes the ephemeral being inside is in the driver's seat of the shared body. The Stretch Goal refers to a situation like you see in <i>The Golem and the Djinn</i>, where a fire spirit is imprisoned by a sorcerer, and even when it gets out, it is still stuck in a material body and can no longer become immaterial. That said, most Coactives aren't hosts for a full ephemeral entity. It's more common to be twisted by forced exposure to Essence in such a way that some of that energy remains within the Broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-21-2019, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T20:57:54-07:00","id":1337202,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of places, events, or items that were engineered or accidentally exposed to something that resulted in them having something to the effect of Variations and Scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-21-2019, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T21:20:33-07:00","id":1337203,"title":"","content":"Because every game needs a Princess link, especially half-shonen ones, here's some stereotypes I made on the Discord, plus the Clade views:<br /> <br /> <b>Clubs</b>: The unnatural procedure of what was done to you is matched only by its pointlessness. I so sincerely wish I could say I understood you, but I can't - I can only help this never happen again.<br /> <br /> <b>Diamonds:</b> Once, I thought that &quot;things man was not meant to know&quot; was a contradiction in terms. Then you show up. Any question that forces someone else to be the answer doesn't deserve to be asked...<br /> <br /> <b>Hearts:</b> When we're done, the people who did this won't leave a legacy. That's my<i> promise.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Spades:</b> ...I'm sorry. There's nothing funny about this. Except schadenfreude; I'm planning to have a <i>lot</i> of that, wanna help me set it up?<br /> <br /> <b>Swords</b>: Normally, I would tell you that passion dedicated to revenge never solved anything. Normally, I'm not dealing with abusers on a cosmic level. I'll help you pick up the pieces when we're done.<br /> <br /> <b>Tears:</b> There is no end to this; the Rebellious Provinces are in your enemies' thrall. Take who you need, and come with me, away from the conspiracies, away from this rotted world, where it's safe - we just need a few favors, time to time.<br /> <br /> <b>Storms: </b>You <i>get</i> me.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirrors:</b> I...wha...<i>People </i>did this? I...no, no, it's okay, we just have to get those bad guys too, it'll be better, I promise...it has to be...<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <b>Cephalic: </b>Your &quot;Darkness&quot; needs more than strength to beat. Thankfully, I can <i>make</i> its enablers stop.<br /> <br /> <b>Chimeric: </b>Protip of nature; the foundation of any hope is a full stomach and a safe den.<br /> <br /> <b>Coactive: </b>Your power talks back to mine. That's honestly creepy, but it's friendlier than your natural enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Invasive: </b>Tools made from yourself are still ones you can't put down.<br /> <br /> <b>Mutant: </b>Everything is a survival adaptation. Altruism's one that's proven its worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T21:31:19-07:00","id":1337204,"title":"","content":"You want a Princess link? Replace the human conspirators in Deviant with a race of cute but callous aliens, and you have Puella Magi Madoka Magica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-21-2019, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T22:05:41-07:00","id":1337210,"title":"","content":"I have a concern about two of the Clades: the Cephalists and the Mutants. The other three Clades are described in terms of what is done to you. These two are described in terms of how you react to it. In particular, both are defined in terms of how you reject what they try to do to you: Cephalists reject it on a mental, emotional, or perhaps spiritual level, whole Mutants reject it on a physical level. Both imply that your Progenitor was going for something else than what he ended up with. <br /> <br /> But I've seen too many stories featuring what amount to Deviants with powers of the mind or soul who were engineered to be what they are to buy that: for the Cephalists in particular, I think there ought to be at alternate explanation for how you become one that doesn't have rejection of the intended change built into it. It might involve brain surgery, psychoactive drugs, a flatliner process, a hypnosis technique, or a device that messes with your mind. The commonality would be that the process that triggers your Deviation is one that's designed to warp your mind (or soul). <br /> <br /> That said, if it's too late to get something like this into <b>Deviant: the Renegades</b>, perhaps it could be addressed in <b>Deviant: the Devoted</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T22:42:30-07:00","id":1337213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337204#post1337204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a Princess link? Replace the human conspirators in Deviant with a race of cute but callous aliens, and you have Puella Magi Madoka Magica.</div> </div> </div> </div>And going beyond that, there's a lot of other magical girl anime and other such media that works well with the format(specifics in spoilers, and then the format overall)-<br /> <br /> Spoilers for Symphogear, Princess Tutu, Yuki Yuna is a Hero, DNAngel, Kill La Kill, Tokyo Mew Mew, and Sailor Nothing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Double checking how to spoiler, section will be back soon.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Symphogear Season 1 an, to a lesser extent, 2 features body horror that revolves around how the use of the magical girl artifact will invariably kill the lead character, and in other instances features how innocent people can get roped into and used by evil organization, and while the Magical Girl element is not ingrained in their bodies, it has a lot of that good Devoted angles to read regardless.<br /> <br /> Princess Tutu is effectively a magical girl story with multiple Deviant types created to fulfill the twisted desire of their repsective elements, with the eponymous character effectively being what would happen if you a Manticores Variations making them a sort of Invasive Deviant and Princess Krahe being a subtly portrayed Chimeric, and to cap it all off the lead character has to confront the fact that her story ends with her power causing her to vanish.<br /> <br /> Yuki Yuna is a Hero has it's magical girls operate normally until they need to boost up for a major crisis, wherein their second stage of magical girlness causes them to develop crippling disabilities each time it's unleashed-and not only do the powers that be know this, they eventually turn girls too crippled to continue in living idols for the state's faith.<br /> <br /> D.N. Angel is basically the story of a Genotypal Deviant with a multiple personality Scar and a lot of tension in how each of those personalities have different Loyalty Touchstones, all while dealing with another Genotypal Deviant going after them. While not getting into the powers betraying you and dehumanizing you as much, the conflict of interests in the lead characters as entities in the same body feel very on brand, particularly in early episodes.<br /> <br /> I want to mention Earth Maiden Arjuna, but I haven't seen that since I was a freshman in High school, so this is all we get.<br /> <br /> Kill La Kill centers around three Invasive Deviants, given power with consequences when taken to far from Life Fibers, two of which spend a lot of time trying to fuck each other up until they finally get over themselves and go after the third one. Mankanshoku is best Loyalty Touchstone. No explanation for Senketsu or Junketsu, I'll admit.<br /> <br /> Tokyo Mew Mew literally starts with the protagonist getting injected with genes from an endangered cat species, and the rest of the group fleshes out from there. Sometimes they inconveniently turn into animals. I'd comment more, but it has similar problems to Arjuna Not a Magical Girl series, but if you think by that token, Fruits Basket has some decent basis, you'd be correct.<br /> <br /> Sailor Nothing may not burn bodies out directly per se, but it features a whole lot of Volunteers who, as far as they know, have to put up with the physical ailments that denote the presence of their enemies until they die at an inevitably young age, and once the favor of the patron is removed, the titular character finds transformation to just kind of be an terrible experience. It can also radically grow wildly out of control, and can do a lot of damage as a result.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And there's more asides<br /> <br /> At it's core, there are a lot of magical girl stories out there where in the protagonist either literally doesn't get a choice or doesn't fully grasp what it means to take on the mantle, and that with the power comes conditions that tend to mess with their lives and often lead to fatality or severe crippling of the ability to live at all, who are often balanced between their growing relationships to the people around them as they become friendships and their conflict with the series bad guys, with a common point, if not long running arc, being that the characters having to make the decision to abandon the former in order to fight the latter, where in fact keeping with them often has real metaphysical results for them. Bonus points include that for every supernatural entity offering it, there's often a story of a human offering it, often to exploit the empowered, there's a good sized number of &quot;science&quot;-based magical girls, and one of the most common ways to subvert the genre even before Madoka was a thing was to introduce some kind of body horror element to it.<br /> <br /> Now granted, a lot of this is because magical girls share the same spaces as superheroes and tokusatsu shows-but yeah, the genre actually has a wide range of material you could draw from for Deviant if you wanted to, from very lightly associated to Might As Well Have Been a Deviant Story.<br /> <br /> [/magicalgirlgenrenerd](<i>for now</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-21-2019, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T23:10:06-07:00","id":1337216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337210#post1337210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I've seen too many stories featuring what amount to Deviants with powers of the mind or soul who were engineered to be what they are to buy that: for the Cephalists in particular, I think there ought to be at alternate explanation for how you become one that doesn't have rejection of the intended change built into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cephalists are textually built around the trope of trauma-induced psychic powers, which are no exception to the trend of starting Variations toward the aims of the Progenitor. Insofar as Clades have to do with method rather than manifestation, <i>that</i> is &quot;how you become one,&quot; not the writeup's discussed phenomenon of where the frequent attitude of Psychics toward their Divergence comes from.<br /> <br /> Reading the splat writeup too literally will net you weird assumptions like &quot;no conspiracy makes Mutants on purpose.&quot; A Clade is, at its base, defined by how your powers manifest and nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T05:06:33-07:00","id":1337232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337216#post1337216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cephalists are textually built around the trope of trauma-induced psychic powers, which are no exception to the trend of starting Variations toward the aims of the Progenitor. Insofar as Clades have to do with method rather than manifestation, <i>that</i> is &quot;how you become one,&quot; not the writeup's discussed phenomenon of where the frequent attitude of Psychics toward their Divergence comes from.<br /> <br /> Reading the splat writeup too literally will net you weird assumptions like &quot;no conspiracy makes Mutants on purpose.&quot; A Clade is, at its base, defined by how your powers manifest and nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will go so far as to spoil that there is a Progenitor in one of the sample settings who specializes in creating Mutants by carefully selecting for physical traits she has found make the subject predisposed toward that form of Divergence. And now she's trying to do the same with Cephalists, screening for psychological qualities that will crack the soul if she provides the right stimulus <i>here</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T05:38:16-07:00","id":1337237,"title":"","content":"I'm missing something, but it looks like Chimerics can cure their Scars forever if they have time and enough Willpower.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if that's intended, because you can get new Scars, but it's still head-tilting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T05:46:28-07:00","id":1337238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337237#post1337237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm missing something, but it looks like Chimerics can cure their Scars forever if they have time and enough Willpower.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if that's intended, because you can get new Scars, but it's still head-tilting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adaptations only last until the end of the scene. I clipped the section in the preview out of Chapter 3 so that folks wouldn't be staring at Adaptation names in the Clade write-ups without seeing what they actually did, but I didn't clip the more general &quot;here is how all Adaptations work&quot; part that preceded it, which is the cause of the confusion. Chimerics <i>are</i> able to hide their natures for short periods through a combination of their Adaptation and the Mimicry Variation (which is one of their Clade Variations).<br /> <br /> ETA: Looks like we just crossed the $45k threshold!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-21-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T09:28:28-07:00","id":1337255,"title":"","content":"The slow development cycles of the Chronicles of Darkness games have cooled much of my enthusiasm recently. Deviant is actually stoking my excitement way back up now! It's even better so far than I ever imagined...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T15:08:38-07:00","id":1337271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337200#post1337200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Events has the same answer as for places. What kinds of things did you have in mind?<br /> <br /> ETA: <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: It's more that the being attempts to claim the human and becomes a battery for the new Deviant's supernatural abilities. If the Remade has the Symbiote Form, it usually means that the ephemeral being is still in there and has some small sway over how she uses its powers. The Alternate Persona Scar means that sometimes the ephemeral being inside is in the driver's seat of the shared body. The Stretch Goal refers to a situation like you see in <i>The Golem and the Djinn</i>, where a fire spirit is imprisoned by a sorcerer, and even when it gets out, it is still stuck in a material body and can no longer become immaterial. That said, most Coactives aren't hosts for a full ephemeral entity. It's more common to be twisted by forced exposure to Essence in such a way that some of that energy remains within the Broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh ok. thanks for elaborating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T17:20:19-07:00","id":1337280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337202#post1337202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of places, events, or items that were engineered or accidentally exposed to something that resulted in them having something to the effect of Variations and Scars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed this one, earlier. Sacred Flesh (a Mutant Clade Variation) includes a version that allows you to create an object that grants the wielder access to a single Variation once per chapter*, which is a &quot;sort of&quot; to your question. Places and events that grant Variations/Scars aren't something that is covered in the core, but it's a potentially nifty idea. I'll make a note of it. (And yes, I am definitely the sort of ST that will tell my players &quot;you guessed my plan exactly&quot; if they come up with an explanation or plot twist that wasn't what I had planned but that I think is cooler.)<br /> <br /> * Certain restrictions apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T05:04:59-07:00","id":1337314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337177#post1337177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And actually, just spit balling (aka: fan hat is still on, this could be contradicted at any moment), but mummies became mummies because they were able to declare their Decree to the Judges and rebuild the pillars of their soul. There are a lot of reasons for an Arisen and a metaphysically-aware Renegade to be interested in each other\u2019s experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for the Shuankhsen Ammut just said, &quot;There, here's a band-aid. Good enough.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T07:13:10-07:00","id":1337322,"title":"","content":"The Web of Pain has to be my favourite part of the first preview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An enforcer turns up, sharp-suited and tooled up with cutting-edge armaments that can stop even a Remade in her tracks, but the mafia foot-soldiers only know that he\u2019s from \u2018back home in Sicily\u2019. </div> </div> </div> This line alone? Gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T13:59:51-07:00","id":1337369,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I have an appreciation for how organically you can slip a Devoted Deviant into the antagonists of other games as a way of diversifying them.*<br /> <br /> Theoretically that can be said of any of the splats(particularly Beast), of course, but as a point of comparison-If I'm running a game of non-crossover game of Geist but want to spice up the world by having elements of the other lines pop up once in a while(as I do <i>all the time</i>), I <i>could</i> add a werewolf or a changeling to an Eaters of the Dead or Tyrant Krewe, but I've got some things to answer there in order to get it a little more lined up. By contrast, if the players come across a cult of Eaters of the Dead, both mostly human and more inhuman entities, and they have a Deviant with them, I don't have to wonder long how <i>that</i> happened. Games like Mage, Promethean, and Demon almost beg for them to slip in with the rest.<br /> <br /> It's a versatile splat, even if you don't wanna run a Deviant game, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> (That said, &quot;Rejected&quot; and &quot;Ain't No Rest for the Wicked&quot; beg to be Deviant games.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I do like how that sort of mentality works well for complicating personal organizations. Your krewe might decide it's worth chasing, or it might not-but either way, it complicates things when you get to a day when you find a Deviant in your own group.<br /> <br /> *With the obvious understanding that it has to be the results of humanity by itself-but if it conceivably has a human cult with it, and they don't always have access to their patron power, a Deviant emerging isn't impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2019, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:28:16-07:00","id":1337373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337369#post1337369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the obvious understanding that it has to be the results of humanity by itself-but if it conceivably has a human cult with it, and they don't always have access to their patron power, a Deviant emerging isn't impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? Is there a solid metaphysical rule that Progenitors have to be human and not, for example, some Ordo Dracul cabal messing about with human biology to try to get ideas about new Coils, or mages seeing what happens if they stick some pre-fall relic in a live body? Or a Promethean who didn't notice that the body they're trying to infuse with the Divine Fire isn't all the way dead?<br /> <br /> edit: and fansplat-wise, making Deviants sure seems like something the Inspired will be all over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25206,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","user":"Evil Midnight Lurker","date":". 09-22-2019, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:42:41-07:00","id":1337375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337373#post1337373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it? Is there a solid metaphysical rule that Progenitors have to be human and not, for example, some Ordo Dracul cabal messing about with human biology to try to get ideas about new Coils, or mages seeing what happens if they stick some pre-fall relic in a live body? Or a Promethean who didn't notice that the body they're trying to infuse with the Divine Fire isn't all the way dead?<br /> <br /> edit: and fansplat-wise, making Deviants sure seems like something the Inspired will be all over.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why a Deviant's soul cracks and doesn't become something else is because there are no higher powers at work in humanity to guide the transformation once that damage is done. Seers crack over open human souls to make Servitors all the time, and not one of them is a Deviant, as a minor example. It needs that lack of an anchor that humanity has to make a Deviant. If there are more solid metaphysical constants involved in the process, than likely they become b-splats or weirdnesses associated with that splat.<br /> <br /> Stepping away from the Watsonian for the Doylist, this has been openly stated as a means of keeping Deviant from devouring all sub-splats and other such things into it's folds, because it becomes obnoxious to have your Ghouls, Stigmatics, and Hollow Ones all be Deviants all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> If you want a non-canon answer with some precedence though, it's not <i>completely</i> inconceivable that a supernatural entity could make a Deviant <i>if </i>they can successfully step away from their supernatural side enough for the process, in the same way supernaturals could make Prometheans if they stepped away from their supernatural selves and relief on good ol' fashioned raw human desperation for the entire process. As an example, a mage could conceivably make a Deviant <i>if they didn't rely on magic throughout the process</i>. Since Divergence isn't rooted <i>as</i> strongly in that raw desperation as Promethean's generation is, though, it's debateable how much that would affect it.<br /> <br /> TL;DR-Yes, it is a metaphysical rule that Deviants need humanity's lack of metaphysical constants that might otheriwse guide a transformation to, well, diverge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting is that, for most splats, a Deviant would be a more significant failure than it would be for humanity. Most splats have a script to follow-for example, the lack of inherent control over- or subtlety exhibited by- Deviants is particularly favorable to angels.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say they wouldn't, and it's easier to imagine how it might work out, but that there <i>are</i> limits to how usable they are for the splats in question.<br /> <br /> Their human cults, on the other hand, might not be so picky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2019, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:44:55-07:00","id":1337376,"title":"","content":"Fansplat-wise, I'm half expecting Deviant (or Clade Companion) to provide mad scientists as a secondary template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:46:55-07:00","id":1337377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337213#post1337213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No explanation for Senketsu or Junketsu, I'll admit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Manticore symbionts engineered from the alien Life Fibers rather than terrestrial lifeforms, or else the result of a Form that externalizes the Divergence as a separate object or entity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T14:47:22-07:00","id":1337378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337377#post1337377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Manticore symbionts engineered from the alien Life Fibers rather than terrestrial lifeforms, or else the result of a Form that externalizes the Divergence as a separate object or entity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There it is! Thanks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: unrelated question, why is this game making me wanting to play all the songs I used to listen to in high school. This is unnerving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2019, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T15:35:56-07:00","id":1337388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337375#post1337375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why a Deviant's soul cracks and doesn't become something else is because there are no higher powers at work in humanity to guide the transformation once that damage is done. Seers crack over open human souls to make Servitors all the time, and not one of them is a Deviant, as a minor example. It needs that lack of an anchor that humanity has to make a Deviant. If there are more solid metaphysical constants involved in the process, than likely they become b-splats or weirdnesses associated with that splat.<br /> <br /> Stepping away from the Watsonian for the Doylist, this has been openly stated as a means of keeping Deviant from devouring all sub-splats and other such things into it's folds, because it becomes obnoxious to have your Ghouls, Stigmatics, and Hollow Ones all be Deviants all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> If you want a non-canon answer with some precedence though, it's not <i>completely</i> inconceivable that a supernatural entity could make a Deviant <i>if </i>they can successfully step away from their supernatural side enough for the process, in the same way supernaturals could make Prometheans if they stepped away from their supernatural selves and relief on good ol' fashioned raw human desperation for the entire process. As an example, a mage could conceivably make a Deviant <i>if they didn't rely on magic throughout the process</i>. Since Divergence isn't rooted <i>as</i> strongly in that raw desperation as Promethean's generation is, though, it's debateable how much that would affect it.<br /> <br /> TL;DR-Yes, it is a metaphysical rule that Deviants need humanity's lack of metaphysical constants that might otheriwse guide a transformation to, well, diverge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting is that, for most splats, a Deviant would be a more significant failure than it would be for humanity. Most splats have a script to follow-for example, the lack of inherent control over- or subtlety exhibited by- Deviants is particularly favorable to angels.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say they wouldn't, and it's easier to imagine how it might work out, but that there <i>are</i> limits to how usable they are for the splats in question.<br /> <br /> Their human cults, on the other hand, might not be so picky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, that makes total sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> (I stand by Genius though, as (a) they can canonically deliberately make Prometheans already, and (b) both Prometheans and Deviants count as significant <i>successes</i> for the Inspired as they won't break when mundanes squint at them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T15:43:43-07:00","id":1337389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337388#post1337388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, yeah, that makes total sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> (I stand by Genius though, as (a) they can canonically deliberately make Prometheans already, and (b) both Prometheans and Deviants count as significant <i>successes</i> for the Inspired as they won't break when mundanes squint at them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pffffffffffffffffff<br /> <br /> Of course Genius would state they can make Prometheans without acknowledging the caveats presented in it's own material.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it depends on the margin of success you describe. I mentioned Angels, but by contrast, Seers don't exactly stress over how to make people do what they want. Mix those fuckers in with the Myrmidons, have a party, so long as it doesn't fuck the bottom line.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyways, I should make a note, since I pffed it-No, a Genius can't, not unless they aren't willing to employ Inspiration in the process. If they do, they end up with Igors, not Deviants. Inspiration is clearly enough of an alien entity at work that people worked on in a way that might otherwise trigger Divergence anchors into [whateverthefuckisgoingonwithgeniusfuckigotmadabout itslackofanythingallover again] that Inspiration makes up.<br /> <br /> Scars and Variations emerge 'naturally' from the wounding as a result of there being <i>nothing to guide the process</i>, on a metaphysical level. Inspiration, whatever the fuck it is at the end of the day, is at least a guiding principle that makes Wonders and all other manner of whatthefuckery work. That will, in turn, guide the damage and transformation of a Deviant around itself, into something that is Not A Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T16:00:09-07:00","id":1337391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337388#post1337388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, yeah, that makes total sense, thanks.<br /> <br /> (I stand by Genius though, as (a) they can canonically deliberately make Prometheans already, and (b) both Prometheans and Deviants count as significant <i>successes</i> for the Inspired as they won't break when mundanes squint at them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cCanonically\u201d? For a fansplat? Does not compute. <br /> <br /> As I hinted at before, I'm more inclined to think of Deviant as the \u201ccanonical\u201d Mad Science gameline of the Chronicles of Darkness, with the inventors who can pull off the sorts of inventions that Deviant features <i>without</i> the backing of a conspiracy being a \u201clesser template\u201d (if that notion has any applicability where Deviant is concerned). Much like how Geist is the Chronicles of Darkness game about post-death characters, but ghosts are a \u201csecondary template\u201d instead of being the central focus of the game the way they are in Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T16:06:57-07:00","id":1337392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337391#post1337391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cCanonically\u201d? For a fansplat? Does not compute.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume they are talking about Genius's canon, which<br /> <br /> *twitch*<br /> <br /> ANYWAYS, such a thing exists within it's own sphere.<br /> <br /> As for Mad Science, it has representation within, but not limited to, Mage, Promethean, Demon, and now Deviant. Mad Science works better as a sub-trend throughout Chronicles than it's own concrete entity, to be honest-but admittedly, Deviant is one of the better manifestations of the spirit of Mad Science, as it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T16:17:54-07:00","id":1337393,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science\">I tend to agree.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T16:54:03-07:00","id":1337398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337392#post1337392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume they are talking about Genius's canon, which<br /> <br /> *twitch*</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth pointing out as both a note and a reminder that it's &quot;canonical&quot; in the sense that it's an &quot;at the Storyteller's option&quot; point in the exceptional success result of a five-dot power in a game where the five-dot powers are designed expressly to border on plot-devices, in this case specifically the one for resurrecting the dead. It's not the strongest argument even in its own context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T16:57:52-07:00","id":1337399,"title":"","content":"well we hit the 50,000 mark.<br /> <br /> just a small part about the Autotourgic introduction. I really like the line &quot;Look at what you are now. Look at what you wanted.&quot; at page 17 of the manuscript. it may just be me, but the mocking tone really fits the horror of intentionally changing yourself into a deviant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T17:28:16-07:00","id":1337400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337369#post1337369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically that can be said of any of the splats(particularly Beast), of course, but as a point of comparison-If I'm running a game of non-crossover game of Geist but want to spice up the world by having elements of the other lines pop up once in a while(as I do <i>all the time</i>), I <i>could</i> add a werewolf or a changeling to an Eaters of the Dead or Tyrant Krewe, but I've got some things to answer there in order to get it a little more lined up. By contrast, if the players come across a cult of Eaters of the Dead, both mostly human and more inhuman entities, and they have a Deviant with them, I don't have to wonder long how <i>that</i> happened. Games like Mage, Promethean, and Demon almost beg for them to slip in with the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also a good way to have a major One Winged Angel moment, when a mortal at the heart of a conspiracy feels cornered, but isn't separated from their equipment, and decides to take drastic measures....<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt that the Elect get a free Overt Variation, meaning the new high-Magnitude Devoted coming at them has an extra helping of something big and loud, and likely regards their enemies as a Conviction Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Also, really, this is perfect for my Eater of the Dead, Professor Lemniscate, who was always about nercomantic pharmaceuticals. A couple extra doses here for those with the proper neural architecture - wonders, and a new product line to sell to his legion of clients/enablers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T17:42:04-07:00","id":1337402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337400#post1337400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also a good way to have a major One Winged Angel moment, when a mortal at the heart of a conspiracy feels cornered, but isn't separated from their equipment, and decides to take drastic measures....<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt that the Elect get a free Overt Variation, meaning the new high-Magnitude Devoted coming at them has an extra helping of something big and loud, and likely regards their enemies as a Conviction Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Also, really, this is perfect for my Eater of the Dead, Professor Lemniscate, who was always about nercomantic pharmaceuticals. A couple extra doses here for those with the proper neural architecture - wonders, and a new product line to sell to his legion of clients/enablers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flexibility is a word of use here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T18:25:18-07:00","id":1337406,"title":"","content":"Loving the conversation going on here! It has not escaped my attention that Remade make great supporting antagonists (or allies) in a chronicle otherwise focused on another line. In fact, it is quite intentional! As you've seen with Bioluminescence, I've included several powers that are cool in their own way but are <i>especially</i> upsetting to certain supernatural creature types a Deviant might cross paths with.<br /> <br /> I don't have much familiarity with Genius, so I can't say much about that piece, but yeah, a game that involves medical body horror is going to have a fair amount of connection to anything focused on weird/mad science.<br /> <br /> Also, woot for $50k!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T18:28:14-07:00","id":1337407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337406#post1337406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loving the conversation going on here! It has not escaped my attention that Remade make great supporting antagonists (or allies) in a chronicle otherwise focused on another line. In fact, it is quite intentional! As you've seen with Bioluminescence, I've included several powers that are cool in their own way but are <i>especially</i> upsetting to certain supernatural creature types a Deviant might cross paths with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It particularly strikes me as neat because I had a conversation yesterday regarding a different line about how a certain antagonist wasn't really all that good as a crossover antagonist, and so diving into Chapter 2 and realizing that versatility is a refreshing contrast.<br /> <br /> Deviants upset status quos, yo.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I have a Beast character I want to play who, on learning about Deviants, basically would dedicate a small part of her cult to making them, and I love all the ways that goes wrong in my imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2019, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T18:44:51-07:00","id":1337410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337406#post1337406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loving the conversation going on here! It has not escaped my attention that Remade make great supporting antagonists (or allies) in a chronicle otherwise focused on another line. In fact, it is quite intentional! As you've seen with Bioluminescence, I've included several powers that are cool in their own way but are <i>especially</i> upsetting to certain supernatural creature types a Deviant might cross paths with.<br /> <br /> I don't have much familiarity with Genius, so I can't say much about that piece, but yeah, a game that involves medical body horror is going to have a fair amount of connection to anything focused on weird/mad science.<br /> <br /> Also, woot for $50k!</div> </div> </div> </div>if it's ok with you, may you share how it felt to see your idea be realized in less than a day (referencing the successful kickstarter for Deviant)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T18:52:44-07:00","id":1337413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337375#post1337375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a non-canon answer with some precedence though, it's not <i>completely</i> inconceivable that a supernatural entity could make a Deviant <i>if </i>they can successfully step away from their supernatural side enough for the process, in the same way supernaturals could make Prometheans if they stepped away from their supernatural selves and relief on good ol' fashioned raw human desperation for the entire process. As an example, a mage could conceivably make a Deviant <i>if they didn't rely on magic throughout the process</i>. Since Divergence isn't rooted <i>as</i> strongly in that raw desperation as Promethean's generation is, though, it's debateable how much that would affect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced that this works. Supernaturals can't make Prometheans because the Divine Fire is the only source of Prometheans, and the Fire doesn't play well with other supernatural powers. But the Coactive Clade of Deviants are <i>expressly</i> what happens when you combine Divergence's damage to a soul with esoteric power sources - and ephemera are on the list of sources. It seems to me that supernatural beings experimenting with their powers could perfectly well make a Deviant. It's not by any means the <i>normal</i> result, but it's still possible.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, if bog-standard humans <i>can</i> do something, that's no reason whatsoever to conclude that supernaturals therefore <i>can't</i> do it, or that they have to do it the same way humans do. And the Deviant syndrome is, in principle, something any type of supernatural power can cause, not something that calls for one specific type.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T19:06:46-07:00","id":1337416,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that's Hunter and Deviant share an agnosticism toward metaphysics. Yes, deviant explains things through a cracked soul; but it doesn't explain for the particulars. And I'm fine with that. It's part of the game's versatility. What I'm thinking of is the diversity in Hunter Endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T19:17:33-07:00","id":1337419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337413#post1337413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not convinced that this works. Supernaturals can't make Prometheans because the Divine Fire is the only source of Prometheans, and the Fire doesn't play well with other supernatural powers. But the Coactive Clade of Deviants are <i>expressly</i> what happens when you combine Divergence's damage to a soul with esoteric power sources - and ephemera are on the list of sources. It seems to me that supernatural beings experimenting with their powers could perfectly well make a Deviant. It's not by any means the <i>normal</i> result, but it's still possible.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, if bog-standard humans <i>can</i> do something, that's no reason whatsoever to conclude that supernaturals therefore <i>can't</i> do it, or that they have to do it the same way humans do. And the Deviant syndrome is, in principle, something any type of supernatural power can cause, not something that calls for one specific type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would buy that if I hadn't read direct comments from the developers that contradicted it. Problem is, I like following production processes as much as I can? So I have things like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/947212-deviant-the-renegades?p=973767#post973767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the Remade's whole deal is that they're the result of transformation without a guiding &quot;thing&quot; behind it - ghouls, proximi, faetouched, and anything else related to a supernatural being that has a template aren't Deviants.<br /> <br /> The game will be as crossover agnostic as anything that isn't Beast. But you won't see Remade fuelled by any fuel stats you know: it's the metaphysical line in the sand I've scratched out to stop Deviant consuming all minor templates, which I am actively disinterested in it doing.<br /> <br /> I get that with a new game everyone's first instinct is to think up crossovers and how it affects their ongoing chronicles or favourite, but I'm the guy who won't mention the God-Machine in Mage. Save it for the Crossover Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>did</i> mention that the last part I presented was a)fandom, and inherently( by now I hope with anyone familiar with my dialogue) b)wibbly and therefore unlikely.<br /> <br /> You want me to draw a hard line based on what I have, I don't fucking care what elements are at play, <i>no</i>, no supernatural can produce a Deviant <i>because</i> I have that line in the sand to work with, alongside the text we have from the book.<br /> <br /> I am <i>willing</i> to draw a comparison between this and Supernaturals Making Prometheans because They Look <i>Just Enough</i> Alike that I might ignore it at my table for the sake of interest, and it plays well enough with the metaphysical constant at play.. This is not the same as twisting the material beyond what it states-ie, it takes humanity's lack of anything to make a Deviant(ergo, if a supernatural were to try, they'd have to divorce themselves from their supernatural state enough to do so, <i>possibly.</i>)<br /> <br /> Progenitors may exploit fairies, ghosts, spirits, gods, and demons alike in terms of their ventures, but the act that makes a Deviant? That's all humanity, in it's ugliest, most ambitious form. If a monster wants to access that? They had better play the part.<br /> <br /> Bog-standard is still the standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:00:03-07:00","id":1337428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337410#post1337410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if it's ok with you, may you share how it felt to see your idea be realized in less than a day (referencing the successful kickstarter for Deviant)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been working on this game in some capacity for more than a year, and my family feels like I've done practically nothing else since December, so saying it was &quot;realized in less than a day&quot; seems a bit weird to me. *laughs*<br /> <br /> I'm thrilled with how things have been going so far, and I'm really hoping to see the Stretch Goals I helped plan come into reality so that I can add more cool toys to the base game. Like, really, <i>really</i> hoping. With outlines. And a list of freelancers I definitely want to have involved. So I'm really delighted by the positive response <b>Deviant</b> has gotten, so far, and I'm looking forward to having a chance to share some of the crunchier parts of the system, which tends to be where &quot;substance&quot; has to live up to the &quot;style&quot; of those early chapters (at once an exciting and terrifying prospect!).<br /> <br /> Regarding major templates creating Deviants, I'm not going to slam the door on that possibility, but I'm not doing it in the core. I'm likely to address crossover in some form of a Deviant Storytellers Guide. But there won't be a &quot;Create Deviant&quot; spell for mages or a &quot;Rite of the Broken Soul&quot; for vampires. Deviants are the exceptions, the failures, the accidents, the unexpected (but largely unrepeatable) successes. Even conspiracies who &quot;mass-produce&quot; or &quot;carefully screen&quot; candidates have lots of failed experiments. If you tap into ineffable power or seek to achieve the impossible, most of the time you just fail, and your test subject meets a messy end (and if that test subject is you, you become a cautionary tale told to future generations), but sometimes <i>something unexpected happens</i>. That's a Deviant. Regardless of how it happens or why, the Divergence is never a completely controlled process with predictable results - not even when Masters of Death and Spirit (or the God-Machine) get involved with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:02:03-07:00","id":1337430,"title":"","content":"Part of being agnostic is that while you can't confirm the involvement of a particular metaphysics, you can't reject it either. Take the Cainite Heresy: their Endowment is fueled by the metaphysical properties of blood. Is it fueled by the <i>same</i> properties that manifest as Vitae in a vampire? Maybe; maybe not. And then there's the Cheiron Group. <br /> <br /> I don't think that Dave meant that nothing that empowers Deviants comes from any other gameline's metaphysics; only that Deviant won't explicitly tie it together, and there will always be the (additional?) factor of a cracked soul that sets Deviants apart from other modified humans (ghouls, wolfbloods, Proximi, and so on). In particular, I wouldn't rule out, say, a ghoul-like Deviant that was created by processing Vitae and injecting it into a subject in a way that triggers a Divergence. It just wouldn't be a ghoul; that's a separate thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:13:13-07:00","id":1337433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337428#post1337428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been working on this game in some capacity for more than a year, and my family feels like I've done practically nothing else since December, so saying it was &amp;quot;realized in less than a day&amp;quot; seems a bit weird to me. *laughs*<br /> <br /> I'm thrilled with how things have been going so far, and I'm really hoping to see the Stretch Goals I helped plan come into reality so that I can add more cool toys to the base game. Like, really, <i>really</i> hoping. With outlines. And a list of freelancers I definitely want to have involved. So I'm really delighted by the positive response <b>Deviant</b> has gotten, so far, and I'm looking forward to having a chance to share some of the crunchier parts of the system, which tends to be where &amp;quot;substance&amp;quot; has to live up to the &amp;quot;style&amp;quot; of those early chapters (at once an exciting and terrifying prospect!).<br /> <br /> Regarding major templates creating Deviants, I'm not going to slam the door on that possibility, but I'm not doing it in the core. I'm likely to address crossover in some form of a Deviant Storytellers Guide. But there won't be a &amp;quot;Create Deviant&amp;quot; spell for mages or a &amp;quot;Rite of the Broken Soul&amp;quot; for vampires. Deviants are the exceptions, the failures, the accidents, the unexpected (but largely unrepeatable) successes. Even conspiracies who &amp;quot;mass-produce&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;carefully screen&amp;quot; candidates have lots of failed experiments. If you tap into ineffable power or seek to achieve the impossible, most of the time you just fail, and your test subject meets a messy end (and if that test subject is you, you become a cautionary tale told to future generations), but sometimes <i>something unexpected happens</i>. That's a Deviant. Regardless of how it happens or why, the Divergence is never a completely controlled process with predictable results - not even when Masters of Death and Spirit (or the God-Machine) get involved with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>weird is understandable lol. but I'm sorry if it seemed like I was downplaying the accomplishment. i should've said &quot;being funded in less than a day&quot; lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:28:32-07:00","id":1337438,"title":"","content":"Something I'm hoping to see when and if we get Deviant's items: something to the effect of Hunter R&amp;D (which I hope in the second edition will be based off of the Investigation rules), designed primarily for making tools but also capable of being used to create Manticores and maybe even Deviants. In addition to its utility in helping enterprising Deviants equip themselves (and driving stories as they seek out the resources needed to make whatever they're trying to make), it could also be used to show, not tell, exactly how unreliable the process is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:44:06-07:00","id":1337439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337430#post1337430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of being agnostic is that while you can't confirm the involvement of a particular metaphysics, you can't reject it either. Take the Cainite Heresy: their Endowment is fueled by the metaphysical properties of blood. Is it fueled by the <i>same</i> properties that manifest as Vitae in a vampire? Maybe; maybe not. And then there's the Cheiron Group.<br /> <br /> I don't think that Dave meant that nothing that empowers Deviants comes from any other gameline's metaphysics; only that Deviant won't explicitly tie it together, and there will always be the (additional?) factor of a cracked soul that sets Deviants apart from other modified humans (ghouls, wolfbloods, Proximi, and so on). In particular, I wouldn't rule out, say, a ghoul-like Deviant that was created by processing Vitae and injecting it into a subject in a way that triggers a Divergence. It just wouldn't be a ghoul; that's a separate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so. Granted, I'm completely aware that individual troupes' chronicles will tie the metaphysics together in order to explain story events. I certainly do that, and with reckless abandon and zero regrets. The last Mage game I ran ended up involving the God-Machine at the chronicle's conclusion, for example, and of course it had some direct connection with the Awakened. My job is to give Storytellers (and players) something that they can use but that they can also make their own - in short, to enable fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337433#post1337433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> weird is understandable lol. but I'm sorry if it seemed like I was downplaying the accomplishment. i should've said &quot;being funded in less than a day&quot; lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely no offense taken. Just pure amusement. Also, I have a lot of faith that James and the rest of the OPP team know what they're doing with their Kickstarters, by now, so I wasn't too concerned that it wouldn't fund with enough wiggle room to spare for at least a few Stretch Goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-22-2019, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T21:57:05-07:00","id":1337446,"title":"","content":"So hey, I\u2019ve seen tossed around the notion that this could be used to run something Animorphs\u2019y. This is extremely relevant to my interests, and since the writers/dev seem to be here I was just hoping for clarification as to how accurate that was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T23:51:22-07:00","id":1337450,"title":"","content":"Heh, there's too much potential for fun in having other splats be able to make Deviants for me. That's one thing I'm going to kick to the curb personally. That along with the broken soul bit and revenge being their primary positive outlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T02:26:52-07:00","id":1337455,"title":"","content":"The thing about crossover Divergences in Deviant (as opposed to crossover games, like, where a Remade just shows up in a Mage game or something - those work fine) is that it\u2019s not just a matter of the Variations\u2019 and Scars\u2019 wordcount. You have to balance \u201cmy Conspiracy is headed by Vampires\u201d and suchlike in the Conspiracy mechanics as well. That\u2019s why we didn\u2019t do it in the corebook, and why I asked no one do it in Contagion Chronicle.<br /> <br /> But it <i>could</i> be done, and nothing stops Eric devoting the space for it in a future book. You could have a Form per major splat, writeups of how much a vampire coterie or Promethean throng are \u201cworth\u201d in Conspiracy-building points, Variations that explicitly link into the ephemeral entity rules (there weren\u2019t any last I saw the game, because the entity rules weren\u2019t in it) that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> After all, Eric\u2019s the one IIRC who invented the arrangement between the God Machine and Exarchs. You are in safe hands crossover-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T04:33:32-07:00","id":1337466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337413#post1337413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced that this works. Supernaturals can't make Prometheans because the Divine Fire is the only source of Prometheans, and the Fire doesn't play well with other supernatural powers. </div> </div> </div> </div>Small aside: Not quite. The Divine Fire really doesn't play well, but it's explicitly possible for a supernatural being who is that desperate to manipulate it; actually managing to force the ritual to work despite Flux having an advantage still breaks the process, but the Azoth still stabilizes and animates; it's just that the new Promethean is an Extempore.<br /> <br /> Otherwise all true; it's honestly a nitpick given how Extempore are explicitly &quot;the Divine Fire takes 'impossible' as a dare, and it often proves its point.&quot;<br /> <br /> Going back to Deviant, I'm wondering if the Divergence can be considered a side effect of Flux existing; it <i>is </i>fundamentally about mutation and staying desperately ahead of a looming inevitable end, but also survival and adaptation at all costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T05:20:43-07:00","id":1337476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337375#post1337375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Stepping away from the Watsonian for the Doylist, this has been openly stated as a means of keeping Deviant from devouring all sub-splats and other such things into it's folds, because it becomes obnoxious to have your Ghouls, Stigmatics, and Hollow Ones all be Deviants all of a sudden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your argument also include magical mishaps? Because to me that would be a great point to generate crossover material. Sure a Vampire wasn't trying to make a ghoul. They were fucking around to see what kind of results they would get by caging a human in this ancient rune circle and force feeding them vitae while electrifying the cage and oops, the one in a million odds turned on them.<br /> <br /> Or the magical detritus and chances of accidental mortal by blows in a game, all could be the right situation and place and materials for an accidental divergence later. Like the example in the clades with that rune circle. Who is to say whoever makes most use of that place and why it is so alive isn't a random werewolf pack of something?<br /> <br /> I feel like there is more wiggle room than I am reading in your statements here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T09:34:12-07:00","id":1337505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337476#post1337476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does your argument also include magical mishaps? Because to me that would be a great point to generate crossover material. Sure a Vampire wasn't trying to make a ghoul. They were fucking around to see what kind of results they would get by caging a human in this ancient rune circle and force feeding them vitae while electrifying the cage and oops, the one in a million odds turned on them.<br /> <br /> Or the magical detritus and chances of accidental mortal by blows in a game, all could be the right situation and place and materials for an accidental divergence later. Like the example in the clades with that rune circle. Who is to say whoever makes most use of that place and why it is so alive isn't a random werewolf pack of something?<br /> <br /> I feel like there is more wiggle room than I am reading in your statements here.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, the powers that be have spoken in favor of that wiggle room, sooooooo I dunno, do what makes you happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T11:50:45-07:00","id":1337519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337505#post1337505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, the powers that be have spoken in favor of that wiggle room, sooooooo I dunno, do what makes you happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being happy is forbidden! And in my defense I didn't realize my phone iteration of the thread at the moment had not been updated so came in late, sorry for being slow on the uptake. I am a useless lump before my brain really gets in gear some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T16:29:31-07:00","id":1337549,"title":"","content":"what do you guys think the True Fae think of human Progenitors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T16:36:56-07:00","id":1337551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337549#post1337549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you guys think the True Fae think of human Progenitors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing they think of Mages. Pretenders, the lot of 'em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T19:09:02-07:00","id":1337573,"title":"","content":"I doubt they would think about them at all other than &quot;another human&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, for anyone familiar with the Wormverse, this seems like a great way to create &quot;capes&quot; in the World of Darkness universe, seeing as how all the capes in the Wormverse are crippled with various weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","user":"Geomancer","date":". 09-23-2019, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T20:26:33-07:00","id":1337579,"title":"","content":"is the number of stretch goals shown the max number? I'm completely ok with it being so, I just dont remember seeing the chimeric companion earlier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T20:27:58-07:00","id":1337580,"title":"","content":"Well, I didn't post this earlier because it seemed off-topic and derail-y for a thread that's not about crossovers or fansplats, but since it seems like that's where we are anyways,<br /> <br /> It'd be so easy to take Luna as a Progenitor, and make the Forsaken Devoted, and the Pure Renegades. Even better? The concept of Luna as a goddess is bullshit: there's a human conspiracy that made it up, and they're quietly and sneakily creating &quot;werewolves&quot; and using a Moon worshipping cult, captained by &quot;Lunes&quot;, to send out marching orders. I mean, could you imagine a game where you realized that these spiritual brands were essentially a system of control for some fucked up bastards who've been at it for God only knows how long, who want to find some way to assert dominance over the Shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T20:32:44-07:00","id":1337581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337573#post1337573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, for anyone familiar with the Wormverse, this seems like a great way to create &quot;capes&quot; in the World of Darkness universe, seeing as how all the capes in the Wormverse are crippled with various weaknesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wormverse and Deviant are very nearly custom-made for each other. You'd have to change the fluff for Origins, but that's really all I've seen you'd need to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T20:55:48-07:00","id":1337583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337579#post1337579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the number of stretch goals shown the max number? I'm completely ok with it being so, I just dont remember seeing the chimeric companion earlier</div> </div> </div> </div>As we hit new Stretch Goals, James will unveil more of them. It appears that he's doing them in pairs but only unlocking the next pair once both the current Stretch Goals are complete. Storyteller's Screen and Cephalist were revealed first, for example, and once we achieved Cephalist, he revealed the Beast Add-on and Chimerics. There was a weird lag on Kickstarter's end that prevented the second pair of Stretch Goals from showing up on the main page until the day after Cephalist was achieved, but James' update posts will let everyone know when more Stretch Goals are revealed.<br /> <br /> We have lots more Stretch Goals in mind, including more rules expansions in the vein of Cephalist &amp; Chimeric that will be provided as PDFs to anyone backing the project at Touchstone level and above (as I've become fond of saying, &quot;there are <i>five</i> Clades&quot;). I am at least as excited about those projects as our backers (and I've been thrilled by the enthusiasm I've seen here and in KS comments). So, spread the word, and let's see how much more cool stuff we can add to this game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T07:06:15-07:00","id":1337629,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, you mentioned in the Kickstarter comments that Chapter 3 will cover two updates. Any word on which rules we're getting tomorrow, and which we'll get next week?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T10:16:12-07:00","id":1337655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337581#post1337581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wormverse and Deviant are very nearly custom-made for each other. You'd have to change the fluff for Origins, but that's really all I've seen you'd need to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you don't even need to change the Stability system since the... uh... you-know-whos encourage conflict and fulfilling it would work well along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T13:26:02-07:00","id":1337686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337107#post1337107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here\u2019s a partial list. These are the ones I tested the splats, Variations, and Scars against in redlines - I would have considered he game a failure if it couldn\u2019t recreate them all.<br /> <br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I saw how excited I am to see Darien Fawkes on this list? My hype for this game hit peak levels when I realized that it'd be hella easy to build him as a Deviant, so seeing him as an example used as a benchmark makes this I-maniac exceedingly happy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T17:35:37-07:00","id":1337737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337629#post1337629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, you mentioned in the Kickstarter comments that Chapter 3 will cover two updates. Any word on which rules we're getting tomorrow, and which we'll get next week?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part 1 is every except the individual Variations and Scars. So, character creation, Conviction/Loyalty/Stability (which have been largely spoiled previously), Forms, character advancement, and the general Variation/Scar systems. Part 2 will be all the Variations/Scars/Deviations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T17:52:00-07:00","id":1337741,"title":"","content":"Oh well. I'm not surprised, mind you; but I had been thinking that maybe we'd get all of chapter 3 at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-24-2019, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T18:34:01-07:00","id":1337745,"title":"","content":"Me: *Sees we have to wait yet another week for the full character creation rules*<br /> <br /> Also me:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/SiVxw2k.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T19:04:34-07:00","id":1337750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337741#post1337741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh well. I'm not surprised, you; but I had been thinking that maybe we'd get all of chapter 3 at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is, hands-down, the longest chapter. This seemed like the most natural breaking point when dividing the whole book into five, roughly equal, sections. I also didn't want to make the KS doldrums of weeks 2 and 3 even sleepier by, say, making an entire preview out of the Storyteller System, which, however much I tried to spice it up by Deviant-ifying Skill Specialties, I wouldn't pretend that a lot of folks won't just skim it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar168_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"168\" data-vbnamecard=\"168\">Aiden</a>: Character creation goes up tomorrow. It's just the individual Variations/Scars that will wait another week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T19:11:53-07:00","id":1337751,"title":"","content":"Oh I understand and approve of the reasoning just fine. I'm just being selfish and desiring all of my delicious mutant cake at once! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T19:18:10-07:00","id":1337752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337750#post1337750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really is, hands-down, the longest chapter. This seemed like the most natural breaking point when dividing the whole book into five, roughly equal, sections. I also didn't want to make the KS doldrums of weeks 2 and 3 even sleepier by, say, making an entire preview out of the Storyteller System, which, however much I tried to spice it up by Deviant-ifying Skill Specialties, I wouldn't pretend that a lot of folks won't just skim it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar168_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"168\" data-vbnamecard=\"168\">Aiden</a>: Character creation goes up tomorrow. It's just the individual Variations/Scars that will wait another week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I'm not surprised; every KS I've been in since they started releasing the manuscript in pieces has basically gone along the lines of:<br /> <br /> Week one: here's the overall concept of the game.<br /> Week two: character creation.<br /> Week three: powers and abilities.<br /> Week four: storyteller stuff. <br /> <br /> I didn't really expect this one to be any different. But based on the chapter outline, I was hoping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-25-2019, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T21:15:04-07:00","id":1337761,"title":"","content":"Oof. Was hoping for all of chapter 3 tomorrow. Planning to get a game going using the KS rules. Looks like we'll postpone session zero a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T21:46:49-07:00","id":1337763,"title":"","content":"So Batman came up in a thread on another site, and I reckon you could do him as a Deviant.<br /> <br /> We know psychics can manifest as body enhancements. We know that Deviant origins are open ended enough that spending years and massive amounts of money traveling around honing your body into a weapon could count, especially if there's spooky extra things added to the training. We know there's Deviants that seek out to become what they are, and while we don't have a comprehensive list of scars, enough of them seem mental enough that &quot;don't kill,&quot; &quot;don't use a gun,&quot; and &quot;dress up like a bat&quot; could all fall under them. I also don't think it would take too much tweaking to have the conspiracy he's up against be Gotham's crime infested nature. It's certainly pervasive enough like a conspiracy, and if he tweak the wrong guy's noses they could come after him like a conspiracy against a Deviant.<br /> <br /> How far off am I?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T00:29:37-07:00","id":1337774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337377#post1337377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] or else the result of a Form that externalizes the Divergence as a separate object or entity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Looking back, this could actually be pretty interesting, expanding Deviants to things like the bearer of a cursed sword, doomed to be dragged along with its murderous urges, or a frail pilot engineered to depend upon and live within their mech suit.<br /> <br /> I'm less sure of how it would work for other Clades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T00:46:05-07:00","id":1337775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337774#post1337774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Looking back, this could actually be pretty interesting, expanding Deviants to things like the bearer of a cursed sword, doomed to be dragged along with its murderous urges, or a frail pilot engineered to depend upon and live within their mech suit.<br /> <br /> I'm less sure of how it would work for other Clades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm, would it need to work for the other ones? Even say, a lich type with an externalized phylactery or someone whose soul is bound to an animal might be best represented using that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T06:24:22-07:00","id":1337803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337774#post1337774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Looking back, this could actually be pretty interesting, expanding Deviants to things like the bearer of a cursed sword, doomed to be dragged along with its murderous urges, or a frail pilot engineered to depend upon and live within their mech suit.<br /> <br /> I'm less sure of how it would work for other Clades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dane Whitman: Deviant knight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T06:29:39-07:00","id":1337804,"title":"","content":"Currently digesting manuscript preview 2. Immediate thought: <b>Armed and Extremely Dangerous</b> is a <i>badass Merit.</i> That's one of those cases where you write one short Merit entry and inspire several character ideas.<br /> <br /> Question: the section on Conviction and Loyalty states that their ratings never sum more than 5, but the Lifeline Merit provides additional Touchstones with associated Conviction or Loyalty dots. Is the Lifeline Merit just an exception to what is otherwise the default rule, allowing Conviction and Loyalty to sum more than 5? This might seem like an obvious question, but I'm still digesting how rising and falling Conviction and Loyalty traits work in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T07:07:28-07:00","id":1337806,"title":"","content":"I have my disagreements with Beast, but Armed and Extremely Dangerous deserves a Kinship Nighrmare, without <br /> <br /> <b>You Can't Stop This Motherfucker</b><br /> <br /> <i>Oh god. It came through the wall. There was a wall here, and now it's a door, and it made it as casually as it could walk. You aren't made for this. They don't pay you enough for this. You aren't the main character, you're a footnote, and if you don't run, you won't even be a memory; you'll just be, at most, a bloodstain that it remembers as a mild inconvenience if at that. Maybe if you claim you don't even like your co-workers, it'll find you amusing enough to spare. Yeah, you hate working here. They are so weird.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 09-25-2019, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T07:24:48-07:00","id":1337808,"title":"","content":"An Amalgam Chimeric: \u201cEd\u2026ward\u2026\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T13:32:10-07:00","id":1337845,"title":"","content":"Minor question because I am confused and this isn\u2019t 100% clear:<br /> Are persistent scars entangled with toggled variations only on when the variation is toggled on, or are they always on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T13:52:27-07:00","id":1337847,"title":"","content":"How would you rationalize a Self-Made Genotypal Remade? The closest I can come is Cu Chulainn, who was born awesome but then he heard about a prophecy and went out to fulfill it (but didn't listen to the full prophecy and it ended up killing him), but that could also be Elect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T13:57:56-07:00","id":1337848,"title":"","content":"So maybe I'm missing something. But do Deviants only get one aspiration for some reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T13:59:16-07:00","id":1337849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>violetdea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337848#post1337848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe I'm missing something. But do Deviants only get one aspiration for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>In explicit contrast with Baselines, yes. Their Touchstones fill a lot of the same role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:19:21-07:00","id":1337852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337804#post1337804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently digesting manuscript preview 2. Immediate thought: <b>Armed and Extremely Dangerous</b> is a <i>badass Merit.</i> That's one of those cases where you write one short Merit entry and inspire several character ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glade you like it. I'm also quite taken with ones like Good Samaritan, Living Progenitor, and Shared Suffering that provide mechanical context for certain behaviors you see represented by characters in Deviant media.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337804#post1337804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: the section on Conviction and Loyalty states that their ratings never sum more than 5, but the Lifeline Merit provides additional Touchstones with associated Conviction or Loyalty dots. Is the Lifeline Merit just an exception to what is otherwise the default rule, allowing Conviction and Loyalty to sum more than 5? This might seem like an obvious question, but I'm still digesting how rising and falling Conviction and Loyalty traits work in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit creates an exception, allowing 6 or 7 Touchstones (depending on the rating of the Merit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337806#post1337806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my disagreements with Beast, but Armed and Extremely Dangerous deserves a Kinship Nighrmare, without<br /> <br /> <b>You Can't Stop This Motherfucker</b><br /> <br /> <i>Oh god. It came through the wall. There was a wall here, and now it's a door, and it made it as casually as it could walk. You aren't made for this. They don't pay you enough for this. You aren't the main character, you're a footnote, and if you don't run, you won't even be a memory; you'll just be, at most, a bloodstain that it remembers as a mild inconvenience if at that. Maybe if you claim you don't even like your co-workers, it'll find you amusing enough to spare. Yeah, you hate working here. They are so weird.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I love it! Would be interested to see how the mechanics work, but no pressure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337845#post1337845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor question because I am confused and this isn\u2019t 100% clear:<br /> Are persistent scars entangled with toggled variations only on when the variation is toggled on, or are they always on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Persistent Scars are always active. Toggled vs. Perpetual determines whether a Variation entangled with a Persistent Scar is &quot;always on&quot; or whether you need to activate it in order to use it during a scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337847#post1337847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you rationalize a Self-Made Genotypal Remade? The closest I can come is Cu Chulainn, who was born awesome but then he heard about a prophecy and went out to fulfill it (but didn't listen to the full prophecy and it ended up killing him), but that could also be Elect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question. I think that's about as close as it gets, but no need to tie yourself in knots if a particular combination just doesn't make sense to you. The game permits tremendous versatility of character concept, but its options aren't infinitely varied.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:30:00-07:00","id":1337853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337847#post1337847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you rationalize a Self-Made Genotypal Remade? The closest I can come is Cu Chulainn, who was born awesome but then he heard about a prophecy and went out to fulfill it (but didn't listen to the full prophecy and it ended up killing him), but that could also be Elect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... reincarnate yourself into a fetus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:30:38-07:00","id":1337854,"title":"","content":"I suppose this is a question for Eric then. If the Remade have fewer aspirations do they have something else to help them generate the beats that would normally had for fulfilling aspirations? Or do they just gain experience at a slower rate than all the other gamelines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:32:55-07:00","id":1337855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>violetdea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337854#post1337854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose this is a question for Eric then. If the Remade have fewer aspirations do they have something else to help them generate the beats that would normally had for fulfilling aspirations? Or do they just gain experience at a slower rate than all the other gamelines?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> (not Eric but not a hard question) This is fairly simple actually. They mostly rely on Touchstones (acting in accordance with a Touchstone gives a Beat i think) and Scars (Your scar fucking you or your allies up gives a beat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:36:55-07:00","id":1337856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>violetdea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337854#post1337854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose this is a question for Eric then. If the Remade have fewer aspirations do they have something else to help them generate the beats that would normally had for fulfilling aspirations? Or do they just gain experience at a slower rate than all the other gamelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>They earn Beats by making progress toward Conviction Touchstones. And they also earn Beats whenever a Scar creates a complication for them (or their cohort) during a scene, which should be quite often, given the importance of Scars to the game's characters. (The &quot;Scars earn Beats&quot; information got left off the bullet pointed list, somehow (I've added it to my working draft), but it's mentioned in the section on Scars.<br /> <br /> ETA: Ninja'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T14:39:41-07:00","id":1337857,"title":"","content":"Missed the bit on Conviction Touchstones! Thanks both of you for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2989-violetdea","name":"violetdea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T15:20:35-07:00","id":1337860,"title":"","content":"Is there a description of Wavering Touchstones anywhere? I can't really tell the difference between Faltered and Wavering without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T16:10:10-07:00","id":1337867,"title":"","content":"So let's take a stab at a few subjects, starting with the obvious...<br /> <br /> Bruce Banner is a Self-Made Pathological Mutant with Alternate Personas.<br /> <br /> Ikuro Hashizawa (Baoh) is an Exomorph Mutant with Symbiote Form.<br /> <br /> Sho Fukamachi (Guyver I) is an Exomorph Cyborg with Symbiote Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T16:31:26-07:00","id":1337873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337860#post1337860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a description of Wavering Touchstones anywhere? I can't really tell the difference between Faltered and Wavering without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The simple version is that &quot;Faltering&quot; is Deviant's equivalent of a breaking point, Act of Hubris, Detachment, crisis point, step backwards, et cetera, whereas &quot;Wavering&quot; is a descriptor attached to a Touchstone to denote that it is not currently contributing to your Conviction or Loyalty ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T17:20:19-07:00","id":1337881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337847#post1337847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you rationalize a Self-Made Genotypal Remade? The closest I can come is Cu Chulainn, who was born awesome but then he heard about a prophecy and went out to fulfill it (but didn't listen to the full prophecy and it ended up killing him), but that could also be Elect.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Deviant who was born with potential power, but whom the relevant conspiracies simply lost track of? He develops Scars and Variations as he ages, with no clear trigger event, and without any training from Progenitors. The conspiracies don't spot him until he starts using his powers.<br /> <br /> A Self-Made Epimorph would be someone who put themselves through Divergence without realizing what the procedure would actually do; maybe they thought it would cure an inoperable cancer, or that it was a new recreational drug, or that it was a genie who would grant three wishes.<br /> <br /> Now, you couldn't rationalize a Self-Made Exomorph. Unwilling victims of a deliberate Divergence <i>must</i> have a Progenitor other than themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T17:36:08-07:00","id":1337884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337881#post1337881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you couldn't rationalize a Self-Made Exomorph. Unwilling victims of a deliberate Divergence <i>must</i> have a Progenitor other than themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-induced amnesia and the &quot;new&quot; guy hates what's been done to him? I'm pretty sure I've seen that one somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T19:09:29-07:00","id":1337905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337881#post1337881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you couldn't rationalize a Self-Made Exomorph. Unwilling victims of a deliberate Divergence <i>must</i> have a Progenitor other than themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have an example for that one: Dr. Daniel Schrebe from Dark City. Your Self-Made Genotypal seems fine, though (not all STs/troupes will agree, but some will).<br /> <br /> ETA: Stretch Goal achieved. New Stretch Goals announced in the Updates (main campaign page should be updated soon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-25-2019, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T19:18:20-07:00","id":1337907,"title":"","content":"From the Kickstarter Update #10, we have our next stretch goal:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At $62,000 in funding \u2013 SUPPLEMENT EXPANSION: The Clades Companion PDF. Coactives have connections to worlds not our own, and so The Clades Companion PDF will be expanded to include full ephemeral entities rules, including guidelines for creating new Numina and parallel worlds using Deviant\u2019s toolbox approach, as well as guidance on how these beings interact with Variations such as Otherworldly Connection. </div> </div> </div>\u2026I wasn't expecting <i>that</i>. Oh, this gonna be <i>good</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> (Cyberspace, ho!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=