b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been following the previews, and I've been trying to figure out how to make a character idea I came up with years ago when I first heard that Deviant was going to be a thing: a psychic girl with bird wings on her back. Problem is, there doesn't seem to be an option to combine Clades, and I was going to make her a Cephalist foremost, even though the wings would make her Chimeric. I want to keep both aspects, so how would you all suggest I go about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cThese Variations are for these Clades\u201d is going to be more of a suggestion than a rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T17:55:43-07:00","id":1338083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338042#post1338042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh cool, for those that want to go the Captain America angle...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or Red Skull <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T18:16:02-07:00","id":1338085,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12738\" data-vbnamecard=\"12738\">Minty</a> and @Inodiv are correct regarding Instability. Good question about whether the boost from medium is &quot;retroactive&quot; if you were maxed out on all your Variations and then get a major Instability. The text isn't explicit. I'm inclined to to say it probably shouldn't be, since we have a system for adding new, unentangled Scars that assumes players have a decent amount of say over the Magnitude of those Scars. It isn't likely to come up tooooo often, but I'm open to others' thoughts on the subject.<br /> <br /> @espiritdecalmar: I like that train of thought. Fun concept. You could even have the Progenitor and a victim in the same cohort.<br /> <br /> @Dataweaver: Also a really cool character concept.<br /> <br /> With all the neat stuff folks are already doing with Forms, I looking forward to seeing what people come up with once the other half of Chapter 3 is posted!<br /> <br /> @SirDragos is on target here. Higher-Magnitude Scars come with mechanics that impose direct penalties/problems, but they're a source of Beats when they create significant story complications just like Magnitude 1 Scars are.<br /> <br /> RE: Super Soldier, I shouldn't be at all surprised that they chose now to spoil that. Absolutely perfect during the week when we're previewing the chapter with all the other Forms, and it seems to be working, since we pulled in over $1,000 in new backers within a few hours of that going up. Less than $1,500 left to go until the next Stretch Goal, now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheHailStormer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338064#post1338064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been following the previews, and I've been trying to figure out how to make a character idea I came up with years ago when I first heard that Deviant was going to be a thing: a psychic girl with bird wings on her back. Problem is, there doesn't seem to be an option to combine Clades, and I was going to make her a Cephalist foremost, even though the wings would make her Chimeric. I want to keep both aspects, so how would you all suggest I go about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might do &quot;Composite Clades&quot; in a future supplement. In the meantime, pick the Clade whose Adaptations and Variations are most useful to you. Deviants are full of weird exceptions and statistical anomalies, no matter how much the conspiracies would like to place them in neat categories, it's okay if a character isn't a perfect fit for a single Clade.<br /> <br /> @Gellydog: If creating Simpson memes based on a game I'm developing is a sin, than I love me the sinners. Nicely done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T18:21:28-07:00","id":1338086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338083#post1338083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Red Skull </div> </div> </div> </div> Would Wonder Woman count as a super soldier on a more mystical level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T18:27:29-07:00","id":1338090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338085#post1338085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might do &quot;Composite Clades&quot; in a future supplement. In the meantime, pick the Clade whose Adaptations and Variations are most useful to you. Deviants are full of weird exceptions and statistical anomalies, no matter how much the conspiracies would like to place them in neat categories, it's okay if a character isn't a perfect fit for a single Clade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to hear it straight from a developer. I'll probably stick with Cephalist for now, have the wings be mostly cosmetic. Unless <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a> is correct about the Variations for each Clade being more of a suggestion than a hard rule. I've been looking forward to this game for awhile now, and my friends and I are already making plans for a Chronicle of it. Hell, I've even got plans of getting artwork done of my character in celebration of the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11208-thehailstormer","name":"TheHailStormer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11208_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T19:06:30-07:00","id":1338093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheHailStormer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338090#post1338090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to hear it straight from a developer. I'll probably stick with Cephalist for now, have the wings be mostly cosmetic. Unless <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a> is correct about the Variations for each Clade being more of a suggestion than a hard rule. I've been looking forward to this game for awhile now, and my friends and I are already making plans for a Chronicle of it. Hell, I've even got plans of getting artwork done of my character in celebration of the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Variation is available to every Clade. A Deviant must have at least half her Magnitude of Variations in some combination of Universal Variations and her Clade's Variations, but beyond that (and the cosmetics), there aren't any restrictions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T19:20:37-07:00","id":1338094,"title":"","content":"Great. I love how much stuff we have to play with for Deviants. A ton of flexibility is one of the things I love about this game so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11208-thehailstormer","name":"TheHailStormer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11208_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T21:49:53-07:00","id":1338107,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we'll get anything like Intuitive Aptitude (/Empathic Mimicry) from Heroes. I saw something about a killing urge scar, which gets us nearly 50% of the way to Sylar's core power set...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 09-27-2019, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T06:11:01-07:00","id":1338131,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">From the Public Preview:<br /> The Cephalist\u2019s lightning-quick telekinetic strike grapples her foe (Bruising Athletics Lash; Channel [Telekinesis], Gunshot).<br /> <br /> I'm not terribly familiar with the previewed Scars but if both Lash and Telekinesis were entangled with scars that required resistance rolls to avoid some sort of depletion would you have to roll both?I<br /> <br /> Say you roll the Str + Athletics (ignoring defense since ... Gunshot) to lash a target and get three succ.<br /> Do I then need to roll a Scar Finesse roll to grapple telekinetically or is that covered by the previous 3 succ?<br /> <br /> I know that this particular lash is intended to grapple but could the cephalisst instead punch followed by the telekinesis power Throw to punch and send someone back a mighty distance potentially damaging them twice, albeit quite flavorfully?<br /> <br /> Can said cephalist decide from turn to turn which to do? The grapple or super knockback punch?<br /> <br /> Finally the toggled descriptor in Lash means I can turn my power on in turn one and not worry about activating it again as I switch targets from turn to turn... correct?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":". 09-27-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T07:15:32-07:00","id":1338134,"title":"","content":"Looking at the latest preview, I see one of the options imposes an initiative penalty...<br /> <br /> That seems kind of needlessly fiddly to me. The rules framework isn't super clear about how one would apply an initiative penalty to someone that has a power that may represent inborn ability, as opposed to gear. Is it always active, because they are always 'equipped' with the ability? Is it only active once they've used it in a conflict scene? Is it only active if they *intend* to use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T09:10:27-07:00","id":1338150,"title":"","content":"Do Explosive Lashes use the normal rules for damage type as a function of distance (aggravated at close range, lethal within blast radius, bashing between 1x and 2x blast radius) or does Gentle/Bruising/Cutting/Horrendous determine the damage type at all distances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T10:08:10-07:00","id":1338156,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, I was just wondering how I'd express the Glassmaker's Scythe in Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T11:01:46-07:00","id":1338161,"title":"","content":"Just had a conversation with a friend about this game that ended with the conclusion that Light Yagami (Death Note; Cutting Firearm Lash 5; Conjured, Devastating, Gunshot, Horrendous, Line-of-Sight) is not OP because being able to take out nearly anyone 1-v-1 does not really help all that much in a game where your opponent is a faceless organization that doesn't mind losing a few agents to get you and can just send snipers or drones after you, or just come after you while you sleep, AND if they have to send a single important person after you they can probably just send The Pain (Metal Gear Solid 3; Boneless 4; Bruising Firearms Lash 1; Envenomed) after him and there would be nothing Light could do about it.<br /> <br /> This game rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T11:41:27-07:00","id":1338166,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Too true, this game is shaping up so nicely. You might take on that guy, but there's always a squad behind him. You might take out that squad but your attack of incredible killingness means nothing to that national corporation sending them. You might take down the head of that corporation but there's the world wide conglomeration looking at you from the distance... And when you get to them if you take them out there's the pipeline into the spirit world they set up to get the spirit power they shoved into you. <br /> <br /> There's hopefully a breathe of reprieve between things, but the shit just gets deeper until, as they said in Firestarter, you crack the world...I<br /> <br /> You almost yearn for that death scene. I find myself trying to see how it will end for my favorite character type the telepath/telekinetic (ala Ms. Grey, and so many more) and I imagine a scene where suddenly as my head explodes everyone within 10 miles of the place knows all my enemies secrets, what his Corp has been up to, everything. Or everyone in that same radius knows that person is evil and hates him. Those of course are the best of the head explodey options there's also everyone in a mile goes into a coma, the building with all my friends in it blows, or I die and as I send my final telepathic goodbyes to all my touchstones the Storyteller let's me know that in my deaththroes I've accidentally broken them all and my next character can be one of them.<br /> <br /> The shit just gets deeper. I love it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T12:07:34-07:00","id":1338167,"title":"","content":"Someone was asking earlier (Hopefully in this forum? I've been reading so much...) how to bring their player cohort together when different Conspiracies created them...<br /> <br /> I intend to start the game I'm going to run at an auction. The players will have been transported there to be sold to those in want. Of course... breakout. Then perhaps later trying to find the auctioneer to find out who created them; then each helping the other to deal with the meting out of justice.<br /> <br /> Or you could begin with each person escaping from / dealing with their Progenitor only to find out the individual was funded by a larger organization that has its fingers in many pies, all funneled through a law firm. So the players all come together at the end of the game staking out the offices of Dewey, Cheatum and Howe. It's good for a drink at the bar as everyone gets to know each other and hopefully decide to work together.<br /> <br /> Or there's alway: the game starts with you all having found each other. X give me a brief description of how you met Y, then Y to Z and then Z to X.<br /> <br /> Ooh more fun... Have the game start with them already bought from the auction by a Vampire unpacking his new toys. Do they serve until they find the right moment to break free? Does that Bioluminescent girl send him into a running panic and they have to fight their way out past his childer and ghouls. Then work on finding the auction house, which leads to the lawyers... Is the Vampire chasing them trying to get blood down their throats... much fun. Can they even be bound? Hmm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T14:58:01-07:00","id":1338189,"title":"","content":"Making sure I've understood part of character creation properly: the important part if your Origin's Scar-free Magnitude is that it's Scar-free - it's not added on top of the Magnitude dots set by the chronicle's threat level, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T15:10:03-07:00","id":1338196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338189#post1338189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making sure I've understood part of character creation properly: the important part if your Origin's Scar-free Magnitude is that it's Scar-free - it's not added on top of the Magnitude dots set by the chronicle's threat level, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading, it is in fact added on-top of those. Not sure if that's explicit in the text, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T15:14:12-07:00","id":1338199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338196#post1338196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my reading, it is in fact added on-top of those. Not sure if that's explicit in the text, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure I saw it explicitly in the text, but I'll double check when I get home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T15:28:47-07:00","id":1338202,"title":"","content":"Looking again, there's mention of a bonus dot in the example of character creation, but the actual Variation Magnitude section currently says that the total Magnitude can't exceed the threat level's total.<br /> <br /> Eric, can you clarify?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T17:42:31-07:00","id":1338211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338131#post1338131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I know that this particular lash is intended to grapple but could the cephalisst instead punch followed by the telekinesis power Throw to punch and send someone back a mighty distance potentially damaging them twice, albeit quite flavorfully?<br /> <br /> Can said cephalist decide from turn to turn which to do? The grapple or super knockback punch?<br /> <br /> Finally the toggled descriptor in Lash means I can turn my power on in turn one and not worry about activating it again as I switch targets from turn to turn... correct?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>With all the examples of Variation/Scar entanglement, I tried to keep it simple, not even telling you the Magnitude of the relevant Variation/Scar. You can channel Telekinesis to throw your enemies, as long as your Telekinesis is of sufficient Magnitude, and yes, you can switch different effects if you're channeling a Tiered Variation. Once activated, all Variations remain active until the end of the scene, allowing you to call upon their effects each turn as long as you have the actions to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338134#post1338134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the latest preview, I see one of the options imposes an initiative penalty...<br /> <br /> That seems kind of needlessly fiddly to me. The rules framework isn't super clear about how one would apply an initiative penalty to someone that has a power that may represent inborn ability, as opposed to gear. Is it always active, because they are always 'equipped' with the ability? Is it only active once they've used it in a conflict scene? Is it only active if they *intend* to use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Initiative penalties with weapons have always felt needlessly fiddly to me, TBH, but the CofD system has them, and so Lash does, too. I'd only impose the Initiative penalty while the Variation is active - just like you'd only suffer a penalty for a sword while that sword was in your hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338150#post1338150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Explosive Lashes use the normal rules for damage type as a function of distance (aggravated at close range, lethal within blast radius, bashing between 1x and 2x blast radius) or does Gentle/Bruising/Cutting/Horrendous determine the damage type at all distances?</div> </div> </div> </div>A good question, since it doesn't say in the text. Given that Stun has its own effect, it might be easiest to say Explosive Lashes must be Cutting and follow the same rules as normal explosives (Agg at ground zero, lethal nearby, bashing farther away).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338161#post1338161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to take out nearly anyone 1-v-1 does not really help all that much in a game where your opponent is a faceless organization that doesn't mind losing a few agents to get you and can just send snipers or drones after you, or just come after you while you sleep, AND if they have to send a single important person after you they can probably just send The Pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338202#post1338202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking again, there's mention of a bonus dot in the example of character creation, but the actual Variation Magnitude section currently says that the total Magnitude can't exceed the threat level's total.<br /> <br /> Eric, can you clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 11 under a &quot;Variations &amp; Scars&quot; heading, somehow <i>following</i> the character creation summary? Some kind of copy/paste hiccup going on there. I'll make sure it's fixed in the working draft. Yes, it's supposed to be Magnitude of Variations as determined by threat level, plus the bonus dot provided by Origin. Good catch, though.<br /> <br /> Not ignoring the rest of you. I'll have to answer those questions once I'm not simultaneously listing to &quot;Baby Shark&quot; and a random Minecraft YouTube video. This one was easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-27-2019, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T18:12:34-07:00","id":1338214,"title":"","content":"Compiling the bits for convenience's sake now that I'm not scrolling back through the doc on mobile during my lunch break:<br /> <br /> Page 3's threat level chart includes the explicit footnote/asterisk'd statement that it doesn't include the free dot.<br /> <br /> Page 7's &quot;Variations&quot; section says that the total Magnitude of Variations cannot exceed that permitted by the chronicle's chosen threat level and makes no reference to how the Origin dot is factored.<br /> <br /> Page 9's Example of Step Six of character creation says that the chosen threat level gives Luke ten dots to spend on Variations, &quot;plus the bonus from Lee's origin.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 12's &quot;Variations &amp; Scars&quot; heading includes &quot;and adjusted by Origin&quot; after its own mention of the threat level-determined Variation Magnitude dots.<br /> <br /> So it's pretty much just the Page 7 one that was giving the impression of ambiguity, though the one on Page 12 is definitely still weird.<br /> <br /> Glad to get that figured out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T19:38:11-07:00","id":1338224,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>: I just realized what happened. There's a cheat sheet of all the Variations and Scars, and I originally put it at the end of character creation, and that paragraph on page 12 was meant to &quot;introduce&quot; those tables. At the behest of people who know layout protocols better than I do, I moved the tables to the end of the chapter, but I didn't move the intro paragraph. Granted, some of the wording on page 12 was more clear than what was on page 7, so I moved it up to page 7, deleted that confusing language, and then removed that into paragraph.<br /> <br /> A whole lot of more information than you needed to know, but this is how artifacts of this sort tend to happen. Thanks for lending a hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T22:04:55-07:00","id":1338234,"title":"","content":"So considering the theme of isolation it's really easy to make Deviant a metaphor for... Honestly a lot of stuff. LGBT stuff, disabilities, abuse... I mean, equating the unwilling to surviving rape is a pretty low hanging fruit after all.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering how much of that is intentional and how much of it is just a result of Deviant's natural versatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T00:03:19-07:00","id":1338239,"title":"","content":"LGBT issues - I put in Deviant\u2019s bible an instruction that while I welcomed individual characters being so (and I\u2019m Bi myself) the writers were *not* to queer code the Remade as a whole. I didn\u2019t want being, say, Trans, to be equated to being a terminal condition.<br /> <br /> Deviant\u2019s metaphorically about the reaction to being chronically ill or disabled, the notion that your body has failed you and it pisses you off.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s a big umbrella of a game, so take what you find in it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T00:33:23-07:00","id":1338240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338239#post1338239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LGBT issues - I put in Deviant\u2019s bible an instruction that while I welcomed individual characters being so (and I\u2019m Bi myself) the writers were *not* to queer code the Remade as a whole. I didn\u2019t want being, say, Trans, to be equated to being a terminal condition.<br /> <br /> Deviant\u2019s metaphorically about the reaction to being chronically ill or disabled, the notion that your body has failed you and it pisses you off.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s a big umbrella of a game, so take what you find in it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. That's good to hear. I will say, the disabled metaphor stuck out first for me. *Cough* Perhaps a bit too much at times. Like you said, equating it to a terminal condition, but hey! It's chronicles of darkness. It is what it is. Besides, if an option for giving the characters a happy ending isn't included in the book then it should at least be easy to house rule in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T06:57:26-07:00","id":1338263,"title":"","content":"The text isn't very clear on the experience cost of Variations.<br /> The Acquiring New Scars section on page 55 of the second preview indicates that that the cost of a Variation is always 4x, no matter its Magnitude, but the experience cost chart lists the cost <i>per dot</i>.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there's nothing specifying the Magnitude of newly-developed Variations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T07:16:29-07:00","id":1338266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338263#post1338263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text isn't very clear on the experience cost of Variations.<br /> The Acquiring New Scars section on page 55 of the second preview indicates that that the cost of a Variation is always 4x, no matter its Magnitude, but the experience cost chart lists the cost <i>per dot</i>.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there's nothing specifying the Magnitude of newly-developed Variations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former is probably just a quirk of the chart formatting. Variations aren't bought per dot. For the latter, you can only buy new variations if you have a scar to entangle with, which would determine the magnitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T07:18:13-07:00","id":1338267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338263#post1338263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text isn't very clear on the experience cost of Variations.<br /> The Acquiring New Scars section on page 55 of the second preview indicates that that the cost of a Variation is always 4x, no matter its Magnitude, but the experience cost chart lists the cost <i>per dot</i>.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there's nothing specifying the Magnitude of newly-developed Variations.</div> </div> </div> </div>New Variations can be of any Magnitude for which the Broken already has a Scar available to entangle with it. I'll fix the column header (which was unintentionally confusing) and clarify throughout.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:24:52-07:00","id":1338278,"title":"","content":"Question on the Lash preview. Could a Remade have multiple instances of Lash? Say they have gruesome spines they extend out of their body, but also can spit acid a long distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:32:44-07:00","id":1338280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338278#post1338278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on the Lash preview. Could a Remade have multiple instances of Lash? Say they have gruesome spines they extend out of their body, but also can spit acid a long distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This Variation may be purchased any number of times to represent different means of attack.&quot; So yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T08:45:51-07:00","id":1338282,"title":"","content":"Damn, too much skimming it seems. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T10:11:16-07:00","id":1338300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338239#post1338239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LGBT issues - I put in Deviant\u2019s bible an instruction that while I welcomed individual characters being so (and I\u2019m Bi myself) the writers were *not* to queer code the Remade as a whole. I didn\u2019t want being, say, Trans, to be equated to being a terminal condition.<br /> <br /> Deviant\u2019s metaphorically about the reaction to being chronically ill or disabled, the notion that your body has failed you and it pisses you off.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s a big umbrella of a game, so take what you find in it!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured. And yeah, good call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T11:08:58-07:00","id":1338322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338282#post1338282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, too much skimming it seems. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T16:43:09-07:00","id":1338349,"title":"","content":"Of possible interest to people in this thread (since we don't have a Deviant forum yet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I've just finished watching a movie called &quot;Upgrade&quot; which hits a lot of Deviant notes. Well worth a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T18:10:12-07:00","id":1338361,"title":"","content":"$62,000 achieved. I was afraid we wouldn't get all the Clades in the supplement, but we are doing really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T19:08:55-07:00","id":1338368,"title":"","content":"Next up, the gadgetry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T19:15:21-07:00","id":1338369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338368#post1338368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next up, the gadgetry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what's a game like this without unstable, experimental prototypes based on occult/alien technology? I'm sure you can tell I had a lot of fun deciding what to put into this series of Stretch Goal supplements. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-28-2019, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:05:59-07:00","id":1338379,"title":"","content":"Will the tech include both science and magic toys?<br /> <br /> Is the electric fish from the Deviant art a piece of tech, a deviant, a manticore, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:24:47-07:00","id":1338381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338379#post1338379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the tech include both science and magic toys?<br /> <br /> Is the electric fish from the Deviant art a piece of tech, a deviant, a manticore, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>As conceived, it will be less a &quot;here are X experimental/occult/alien devices you can include in your game&quot; and more a set of systems for representing goods and services that are not as reliable as the mundane standbys (whether because they are experimental, operate according to alien/occult laws, or are inherently inferior). It will also have a bunch of otherwise mundane equipment for the same sort of reason that the Chimeric expansion has a bunch of animal stats. Just like Chimerics have a Clade Variation that lets them transform into an animal (so it's super-useful to have some stats for the animal forms they might take), Invasives have a Clade Variation that lets them produce conveniently useful (but generally small, mundane, and inexpensive) equipment when they need it (making an expansion to the equipment lists especially useful to them).<br /> <br /> You're not cleared for information about the electric fish. And if you were, you'd wish you weren't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:35:01-07:00","id":1338383,"title":"","content":"I guess we'll just have to wait for the Electric Fish Dossier Stretch Goal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-28-2019, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:43:18-07:00","id":1338384,"title":"","content":"Holy shit, Dark Eras as an add-on is new and $11 bucks for it is a steal of a deal! One can hope this augers well for the future...<br /> <br /> *Crosses fingers for a book of Deviant Dark Eras*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:48:47-07:00","id":1338386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338383#post1338383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess will just have to wait for the Electric Fish Dossier Stretch Goal...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Electric Fish Dossier&quot; - I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T22:09:53-07:00","id":1338398,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, the Caustic ability for Lash says: &quot;The Lash splashes the target with a caustic chemical with an intensity of +0 and coverage of 1 (2 on an exceptional success).&quot;<br /> <br /> What does that mean? I don't see anywhere in the rules where the words intensity or coverage are used in this kind of context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T23:30:33-07:00","id":1338405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338398#post1338398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so, the Caustic ability for Lash says: &quot;The Lash splashes the target with a caustic chemical with an intensity of +0 and coverage of 1 (2 on an exceptional success).&quot;<br /> <br /> What does that mean? I don't see anywhere in the rules where the words intensity or coverage are used in this kind of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it will be explained in an upcoming preview. Similarly, the Bioluminescence preview talks about ionic radiation... I looked for that one too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T00:01:51-07:00","id":1338406,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that the fifth part of the Clades Companion (corresponding with the Mutants) will be strange phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T04:50:26-07:00","id":1338434,"title":"","content":"How exactly does one become a Genotypal Invasive? Was Jean-Baptiste Lamarck right all along? Have these nanomachines been passed down the Armstrong line for generations, son?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T05:46:46-07:00","id":1338444,"title":"","content":"I imagine that being experimented on as a baby would probably count as well. It seems to be as much about your reaction to the change as anything else, so if you get this macguffin installed while you're a baby and you wind up growing up with it then that would probably count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T05:50:43-07:00","id":1338445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338434#post1338434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does one become a Genotypal Invasive? Was Jean-Baptiste Lamarck right all along? Have these nanomachines been passed down the Armstrong line for generations, son?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nanomachines.<br /> You are the Xth son of an Xth son of a family of machine god cultists and have been duly blessed.<br /> You were born from an artificial womb, but inherited something from your surrogate mother that no one saw coming.<br /> A pharmaceutical company has been buying up mystical artifacts and rendering them down into prenatal supplements in the hopes of creating gifted children. That's where you come in.<br /> Your mother was possessed by a technology spirit while pregnant with you, and even though it was cast out some of it was left behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T06:09:53-07:00","id":1338449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338405#post1338405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it will be explained in an upcoming preview. Similarly, the Bioluminescence preview talks about ionic radiation... I looked for that one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. We added radiation, explosives, and corrosive substances to the Storyteller System rules. Radiation comes from Night Horrors: The Tormented. Explosives are originally from Hurt Locker. Corrosive substances are new but work similar to fire. Intensity is how strong a reaction it causes (analogous to heat), while coverage is how much of your body has been exposed to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338434#post1338434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does one become a Genotypal Invasive? Was Jean-Baptiste Lamarck right all along? Have these nanomachines been passed down the Armstrong line for generations, son?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inherited nanotech would certainly qualify. Someone engineered or destined to wield a particular artifact (or exotic technology) would also fall into that category. While skilled Progenitors generally screen potential candidates for physical and psychological traits that make them potentially good candidates for their favored Divergence methodology, Genotypals were <i>made</i> for Divergence.<br /> <br /> ETA:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338444#post1338444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that being experimented on as a baby would probably count as well. It seems to be as much about your reaction to the change as anything else, so if you get this macguffin installed while you're a baby and you wind up growing up with it then that would probably count.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also works. In sum, you can't remember a time when the artifact/tech wasn't a part of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 09-29-2019, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T06:51:03-07:00","id":1338455,"title":"","content":"Ladies and gentlemen: I give you, the Electric Fish backstory, part 1.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/346401857603764246/627804623847292929/f94497b848f25fcba4b85fd976e9980e.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T10:02:31-07:00","id":1338474,"title":"","content":"(disregard)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 09-29-2019, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T10:34:40-07:00","id":1338478,"title":"","content":"I thought that only applied to the starting ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T11:08:49-07:00","id":1338482,"title":"","content":"(disregard)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 09-29-2019, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T11:18:59-07:00","id":1338485,"title":"","content":"I was only mildly interested in the concept of Deviant when it first was announced, but the more I read the more I am in love. This is the first time I have actually put down money for an Onyx Path kickstarter, and it got me to sign up for the forums. I kind of want to run a CoD game with only Deviant. Vampires and Werewolves and such may exist, but they are not Requiem Vampires or Forsaken Werewolves and all their associated faction and metaphysics baggage. All major enemies arise from the Web of Pain (which is a fantastic concept, btw).<br /> <br /> I do have a few questions, however.<br /> <br /> Why does the Telekinesis power replace a Strength + Brawl roll with Scar Finesse? Shouldn't it be Scar Power?<br /> <br /> Perhaps I missed this, but how does the Variation magnitude cap work? My assumption is that can't buy up permanent dots past 5 as per tradition, but temporary ones like from the Adaptations can exceed this. Does that sound right?<br /> <br /> Armed and Extremely Dangerous is an awesome merit, but I am bewildered at the prerequisites. I feel like it should have an alternative prereq like &quot;or a Variation capable of causing damage at 4+ dots&quot;. If you doubt me, go watch episode 1 of Elfen Lied and tell me Lucy does not have this merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25689-luckyblackcat","name":"LuckyBlackCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T11:20:05-07:00","id":1338486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337446#post1337446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hey, I\u2019ve seen tossed around the notion that this could be used to run something Animorphs\u2019y. This is extremely relevant to my interests, and since the writers/dev seem to be here I was just hoping for clarification as to how accurate that was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just tossing this back up. Not busting out the puppydog eyes intensifies gif... Yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T11:49:40-07:00","id":1338490,"title":"","content":"They can turn into any animal they touch, but only for 2 hours, says Wikipedia. (I seriously had to look up what Animorphs are - but then again, I think Eric had to look up what Chrysalids and the Tomorrow People were from my list). <br /> <br /> That should be perfectly doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T13:01:25-07:00","id":1338499,"title":"","content":"Not sure if now is too early in the process to observe errata details, but while glancing through the Fighting Merits again, I noticed that Iron Skin is currently given with either Martial Arts or Street Fighting as prerequisites, but the Martial Arts Merit is not included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T14:17:29-07:00","id":1338506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338478#post1338478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that only applied to the starting ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. Someone pointed out an artifact from an earlier draft in the character creation section a day or two ago, and I updated the Magnitude language to be more clear when I fixed that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LuckyBlackCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338485#post1338485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was only mildly interested in the concept of Deviant when it first was announced, but the more I read the more I am in love. This is the first time I have actually put down money for an Onyx Path kickstarter, and it got me to sign up for the forums. I kind of want to run a CoD game with only Deviant. Vampires and Werewolves and such may exist, but they are not Requiem Vampires or Forsaken Werewolves and all their associated faction and metaphysics baggage. All major enemies arise from the Web of Pain (which is a fantastic concept, btw).<br /> <br /> I do have a few questions, however.<br /> <br /> Why does the Telekinesis power replace a Strength + Brawl roll with Scar Finesse? Shouldn't it be Scar Power?<br /> <br /> Perhaps I missed this, but how does the Variation magnitude cap work? My assumption is that can't buy up permanent dots past 5 as per tradition, but temporary ones like from the Adaptations can exceed this. Does that sound right?<br /> <br /> Armed and Extremely Dangerous is an awesome merit, but I am bewildered at the prerequisites. I feel like it should have an alternative prereq like &quot;or a Variation capable of causing damage at 4+ dots&quot;. If you doubt me, go watch episode 1 of Elfen Lied and tell me Lucy does not have this merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Telekinesis: </b>It's because Scar Finesse rolls are used to &quot;aim&quot; effects or otherwise guide their results.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnitude 5:</b> Magnitude 5 is the limit. If a Variation is already at Magnitude 5, you can't use an Adaptation to increase its Magnitude further.<br /> <br /> <b>Armed and Extremely Dangerous:</b> A really flavorful Merit that could probably use a bit of revision, since it doesn't give any mechanical guidance. I've cut that prerequisite in my working draft and added some mechanics:<br /> <br /> &quot;Agents of a conspiracy who encounter you without having prepared themselves for the confrontation suffer the Beaten Down Tilt (p. XX) when they realize their predicament, unless they outnumber you and your allies by at least the rating of your Highest Magnitude Variation.&quot; And in its Drawback: &quot;Agents sent to engage you (or your cohort) as part of a conspiracy action are immune to the Beaten Down Tilt in the current scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338486#post1338486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just tossing this back up. Not busting out the puppydog eyes intensifies gif... Yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Dave says, well within reach. Animal Transformation with the Shapeshifter Deviation gets you there. More details on Tuesday!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338499#post1338499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if now is too early in the process to observe errata details, but while glancing through the Fighting Merits again, I noticed that Iron Skin is currently given with either Martial Arts or Street Fighting as prerequisites, but the Martial Arts Merit is not included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts is lengthy. Hm. I'll see if I can find a way to address that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T14:56:20-07:00","id":1338512,"title":"","content":"Was explaining Deviant's Variation/Scar architecture to a friend earlier and wanted to make sure I had a couple things straight:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You may only have up to five unentangled Scars (each successive one of which must be of an increasing minimum Magnitude), but there are no hard limits on how much Magnitude of Scars you have in excess of their entangled Variation ratings (besides the cap of 5 Magnitude per Scar).<br /> <br /> \u2022 Gaining a new permanent Scar to heal or downgrade Instability does not necessarily mean gaining a new unentangled Scar, but since Controlled and Involuntary Scars only work with entangled Variations, any unentangled Scars you develop must be Persistent.<br /> <br /> Are both of these accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:12:51-07:00","id":1338513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338512#post1338512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was explaining Deviant's Variation/Scar architecture to a friend earlier and wanted to make sure I had a couple things straight:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You may only have up to five unentangled Scars (each successive one of which must be of an increasing minimum Magnitude), but there are no hard limits on how much Magnitude of Scars you have in excess of their entangled Variation ratings (besides the cap of 5 Magnitude per Scar).<br /> <br /> \u2022 Gaining a new permanent Scar to heal or downgrade Instability does not necessarily mean gaining a new unentangled Scar, but since Controlled and Involuntary Scars only work with entangled Variations, any unentangled Scars you develop must be Persistent.<br /> <br /> Are both of these accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have an unlimited number of Magnitude 5 Scars, but each one after the 4th <i>must</i> be Magnitude 5. Clearing/downgrading Instability by developing unentangled Scars is something of an act of desperation. Having multiple Magnitude 5 Scars is a heavy, heavy burden.<br /> <br /> Correct on the second point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:27:46-07:00","id":1338515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338513#post1338513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have an unlimited number of Magnitude 5 Scars, but each one after the 4th <i>must</i> be Magnitude 5. Clearing/downgrading Instability by developing unentangled Scars is something of an act of desperation. Having multiple Magnitude 5 Scars is a heavy, heavy burden.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify another part of my meaning, I'm basically asking if there's a hard limit on how much Scar Magnitude a character can have relative to those Scars' entangled Variation Magnitude, or if the only things stopping you from having (to use an extreme example) fifteen one-dot Variations attached to fifteen five-dot Scars are bookkeeping and good sense. (i.e. Can entangled Scars vastly exceed their entangled Variations - really bad idea though it would be - or is there a similar explicit rule like the one for unentangled Scars in place?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:35:58-07:00","id":1338517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338515#post1338515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify another part of my meaning, I'm basically asking if there's a hard limit on how much Scar Magnitude a character can have relative to those Scars' entangled Variation Magnitude, or if the only things stopping you from having (to use an extreme example) fifteen one-dot Variations attached to fifteen five-dot Scars are bookkeeping and good sense. (i.e. Can entangled Scars vastly exceed their entangled Variations - really bad idea though it would be - or is there a similar explicit rule like the one for unentangled Scars in place?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do that, but I can't imagine why anyone would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:41:08-07:00","id":1338518,"title":"","content":"Incredibly, intensely minor thing: I really like the &quot;Prized Experiment&quot; merit, but i find it kinda weird that it requires Living Progenitor. I'd think it'd be possible to be a prized item by a conspiracy without a specific living progenitor to match. You could be a Lucky break for the conspiracy or a &quot;living god&quot; for the whole cult.<br /> <br /> This isn't really an issue, and if you don't think it needs to be changed that's fine, i just think it's a thing that's worth noting on my end","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:54:36-07:00","id":1338521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338517#post1338517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can do that, but I can't imagine why anyone would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, but at the more reasonable end of the spectrum, I wanted to be sure there wasn't anything stopping a player from, say, distributing an extra five Magnitude of room for growth between their starting Variations' Scars to avoid needing to rack up Instability along the way to purchasing new Variations to fold into those entanglements. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarity and confirmation! Really excited to see Tuesday's preview, and here's hoping we can hit 64K tonight for a few Scars to bridge the gap!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:53:22-07:00","id":1338533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338506#post1338506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Telekinesis: </b>It's because Scar Finesse rolls are used to &quot;aim&quot; effects or otherwise guide their results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still seems odd to me. You don't &quot;aim&quot; Telekinesis grapples. I might houserule this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338506#post1338506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magnitude 5:</b> Magnitude 5 is the limit. If a Variation is already at Magnitude 5, you can't use an Adaptation to increase its Magnitude further.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense from a game balance perspective, though it does mean that characters with fewer, stronger Variations get less use out of their Adaptations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338506#post1338506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Armed and Extremely Dangerous:</b> A really flavorful Merit that could probably use a bit of revision, since it doesn't give any mechanical guidance. I've cut that prerequisite in my working draft and added some mechanics:<br /> <br /> &quot;Agents of a conspiracy who encounter you without having prepared themselves for the confrontation suffer the Beaten Down Tilt (p. XX) when they realize their predicament, unless they outnumber you and your allies by at least the rating of your Highest Magnitude Variation.&quot; And in its Drawback: &quot;Agents sent to engage you (or your cohort) as part of a conspiracy action are immune to the Beaten Down Tilt in the current scene.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thank you for the preview.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25689-luckyblackcat","name":"LuckyBlackCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T17:02:17-07:00","id":1338535,"title":"","content":"One of the things that gets me most excited about a new game is how easily I can generate character ideas I really want to play. I have been brimming with them for Deviant. I actually wrote up a few mini stories in the style of the Origins. They may be useful in showing my potential players the variety of characters they can create. They are included below in case anyone is interested.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Do not call up that which you cannot put down.<br /> <br /> That is the first rule of summoning. He was a brilliant student of sorcery. Brilliant enough to know which rules he could bend to the breaking point, or so he thought. But he called up a demon too powerful for him to control. It slew his master and tried to possess him, but he had one more brilliant trick up his sleeve. He did not use his magic to try and repel it. Instead he let it in, and used his magic to bind it.<br /> <br /> He is not much of a sorcerer any more, as most of his magic is used keeping the binding intact. However, the seal is imperfect and things leak through. Sometimes it is power he can draw upon for strength. Sometimes it is voices, whispering into his thoughts.<br /> <br /> Epimorph / Volunteer<br /> Coactive / Infused<br /> Symbiote<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> She had always been normal. Exceedingly so. Average height, average build. Several friends but none close. A few romances but none serious. No great struggles but no great ambitions. She did have an interest in medicine and had a good career as a nurse.<br /> <br /> Everything changed the day she was diagnosed with a brain tumor. It was aggressive, malignant, and too far along for standard medicine to help. Her doctor told her about an experimental treatment that may be her only hope. Having no other options, she agreed.<br /> <br /> The experimental brain surgery was a success, the surgeon told her, but he had other news. While operating they had been surprised at how otherwise *normal* her brain was. No *potential* whatsoever. They really wanted her to be the control subject in their more advanced experiments. No, they were not asking. Consider it the price of saving her life.<br /> <br /> What followed was months of torturous experiments and repeated brain surgeries. She wasn't sure who was more surprised when the *control* subject was the first to awaken to telekinetic powers, but she took advantage of the surprise first. One destructive and bloody breakout later, the formerly normal nurse is now a ticking time bomb desperate to control her powers, or at least channel them against the ones trying to reclaim her.<br /> <br /> Exomorph / Unwilling<br /> Cephalist / Psychic<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Do you know what happens when a pregnant woman is turned by a vampire? Too early, and she has a miscarriage. Too late, and labor is induced immediately. Somewhere in the middle? The new vampire can carry the pregnancy to term, and that is when things get interesting.<br /> <br /> They are called dhampirs, half-vampires, daywalkers. They have many of the vampire's powers but few of their weaknesses. Many creatures of the night consider them a threat, or an abomination that must be put down.<br /> <br /> He doesn't consider himself a vampire hunter. He really just wants to be left alone. But as long as they keep coming after him he will defend himself, and sometimes take the fight back to them.<br /> <br /> He wonders if he will ever find the one who turned his mother. His second father, in a way. That is one he would enjoy hunting.<br /> <br /> Genotypal / Born<br /> Mutant / Grotesque<br /> <br /> (Blade homage, obviously. I wasn't sure if Mutant or Chimeric (Bat) was more appropriate, but the Unpredictable Adaptation seemed useful for the grab bag of powers vampires sometimes display.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The woman was her mother twice over. Once as the loving mom who raised her daughter with kindness and care, even after her father died. Once as the doctor who used forbidden techniques to bring her back after her unfortunate accident.<br /> <br /> Much of her body used to belong to someone else. At least a dozen different people, she thinks, if she is keeping track of the strange memories correctly. At least she can still identify which memories are hers and which are not. She assumes so anyway. Could she even tell if she was wrong?<br /> <br /> Why is everyone after her and her mother? Sure, she is technically back from the dead, and she heals injuries quickly, but the seams between the parts never heal. The stitching will never be able to come out. It chafes. Horribly.<br /> <br /> Pathological / Accident<br /> Invasive / Cyborg<br /> Amalgam<br /> <br /> (If things had gone differently, this could have been a Promethean. At least this way she has her memory and her soul, however messed up they are.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25689-luckyblackcat","name":"LuckyBlackCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T17:21:18-07:00","id":1338538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338490#post1338490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can turn into any animal they touch, but only for 2 hours, says Wikipedia. (I seriously had to look up what Animorphs are - but then again, I think Eric had to look up what Chrysalids and the Tomorrow People were from my list). <br /> <br /> That should be perfectly doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also their enemies are body snatching aliens!<br /> <br /> Anyway, good, good. I\u2019ve never seen a system that could do the premise without being really boring.<br /> <br /> Also Animorphs is totally the best not-for-kids kids book series ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T18:11:39-07:00","id":1338545,"title":"","content":"I would love to see Guyver in Deviant, with Cronos Corp as an evil Conspiracy loaded of Chimeric Devoted fighting Guyver Deviants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T21:02:28-07:00","id":1338560,"title":"","content":"Animorph's ending traumatized me. The middle and beginning did as well. Also, they could transform over the time limit... they just got stuck in that form for the rest of their life.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> : Why the choice of the word &quot;Lash&quot; for the attack? I remember that for the Bound, Rage was their power for a generic attack and it was based on ghosts being angry they were dead (I think) so does Lash have any background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T21:20:28-07:00","id":1338562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LuckyBlackCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338533#post1338533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still seems odd to me. You don't &quot;aim&quot; Telekinesis grapples. I might houserule this one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Telekinesis can have shape. Elfen Lied's vectors are invisible abstracted arms and hands. Stands are telekinetic force in humanoid form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T21:46:22-07:00","id":1338566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338560#post1338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animorph's ending traumatized me. The middle and beginning did as well. Also, they could transform over the time limit... they just got stuck in that form for the rest of their life.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> : Why the choice of the word &quot;Lash&quot; for the attack? I remember that for the Bound, Rage was their power for a generic attack and it was based on ghosts being angry they were dead (I think) so does Lash have any background?</div> </div> </div> </div>The word choice was possibly a subconscious echo of spirit rules from OWoD, TBH. The idea that Deviants are &quot;lashing out&quot; with their power was the intended meaning. Originally, Lash was two different Variations - Lash for ranged attacks and Natural Weapon for melee attacks. But there was so much overlap between the two that it saved a lot of words to merge them into a single Variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T22:32:25-07:00","id":1338570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338566#post1338566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The word choice was possibly a subconscious echo of spirit rules from OWoD, TBH. The idea that Deviants are &quot;lashing out&quot; with their power was the intended meaning. Originally, Lash was two different Variations - Lash for ranged attacks and Natural Weapon for melee attacks. But there was so much overlap between the two that it saved a lot of words to merge them into a single Variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supersoldier Form preview from Dark Eras 2 made reference to Natural Weapon, so you might want to run the change by whoever is in charge of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T22:53:02-07:00","id":1338574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338560#post1338560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animorph's ending traumatized me. The middle and beginning did as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;All emergency power to engines. Ram the Blade ship.&quot;<br /> <br /> It remains one of my favorite endings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T00:25:59-07:00","id":1338580,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Bioluminescence to toss around sunlight... Deadly Ichor for blood that catches on fire.... Yes, soon my vampire killer will be complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T02:26:48-07:00","id":1338592,"title":"","content":"So the Clade Variations update presages good thingsfor tomorrow's manuscript preview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cephalist: Body Snatcher (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> </div> </div> </div> A surprisingly businesslike effect, which would probably be pretty complicated in a different gameline. The permanent body theft of five-dot Body Swap feels like it needs an opposed roll or something, but I suppose that already happened when you activated it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Chimeric: Mimicry (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> </div> </div> </div> Is this the Bruce Banner power, or is there some other way to generally look human? I know that one of the Midwinter characters had a Variation called Hybrid Body, but those were from an earlier build, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Coactive: Otherworldly Connection (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> </div> </div> </div> Possibly my favourite out of these five, in part because it doesn't interact with the ephemeral entity rules (I find them clunky and overwrought). Here, you just get the genre tools to be a medium or exorcist, willing or not.<br /> <br /> You're still supposed to be able to take this as a Controlled or Involuntary Variation, right? All three samples are Persistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Invasive: Hidden Compartments (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> </div> </div> </div> I have no specific comment. It does what it does, and it does it well. The example Coactive usage adds some nice variety and broadens the scope of the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mutant: Deadly Ichor (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> </div> </div> </div> The first time I read this, it seemed pretty awkward, but that's just because I'd missed the Reflexive keyword. Basing it on Lash is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Is <i>Relentless Variation</i> the means by which you can be perpetually invisible, or a huge freak, or otherwise permanently deformed by what would normally be Toggled Variations? I expected that to be a Deviation rather than a Scar of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T05:07:31-07:00","id":1338603,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> I know this may be jumping the gun for what will be released in the Clades Companion, but I was wondering if you could give any insight into how Otherworldly Connection works with other Variations. <br /> <br /> For example, is the third tier of Otherworldly Connection required to hit things in Twilight with a Lash? Can you use Body Snatcher on an already possessed body? Moreover can you use Body Snatcher on the entities of these realms or is it only for use with Baselines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T09:37:28-07:00","id":1338640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338570#post1338570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Supersoldier Form preview from Dark Eras 2 made reference to Natural Weapon, so you might want to run the change by whoever is in charge of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And a character in Light of the Sun has it listed that way, as well. I'll make sure any late changes to formatting and the names of things get applied before the final book comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338592#post1338592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this the Bruce Banner power, or is there some other way to generally look human? I know that one of the Midwinter characters had a Variation called Hybrid Body, but those were from an earlier build, I think.<br /> <br /> Possibly my favourite out of these five, in part because it doesn't interact with the ephemeral entity rules (I find them clunky and overwrought). Here, you just get the genre tools to be a medium or exorcist, willing or not.<br /> <br /> You're still supposed to be able to take this as a Controlled or Involuntary Variation, right? All three samples are Persistent.<br /> <br /> Is <i>Relentless Variation</i> the means by which you can be perpetually invisible, or a huge freak, or otherwise permanently deformed by what would normally be Toggled Variations? I expected that to be a Deviation rather than a Scar of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Yes. Hybrid Form (which I'll probably end up renaming again, because it foolishly uses two existing game terms that are unrelated to it) is the opposite, reflecting a rapid transformation into something obviously inhuman.<br /> <br /> - It should allow Controlled and Involuntary. Not sure why those aren't provided as examples, but possibly it was Persistent-Only in a previous draft.<br /> <br /> - Relentless Variation is a Scar, but it's a weird one in that it has a mandatory secondary Scar (either Controlled of Persistent). It started its life as a Deviation, but I found that it was easier to explain its effects, this way. It is indeed the way you get persistently invisible characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338603#post1338603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> I know this may be jumping the gun for what will be released in the Clades Companion, but I was wondering if you could give any insight into how Otherworldly Connection works with other Variations.<br /> <br /> For example, is the third tier of Otherworldly Connection required to hit things in Twilight with a Lash? Can you use Body Snatcher on an already possessed body? Moreover can you use Body Snatcher on the entities of these realms or is it only for use with Baselines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magnitude 3 is required to interact with immaterial beings, including Lash. Possessing a possessed body with Body Snatcher would be a Clash of Wills, although if memory serves, some supernatural creatures in the CofD are immune to possession (ephemeral entities among them), and this wouldn't overrule that. Within those limits, non-Baselines can fall prey to this Variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T10:35:22-07:00","id":1338649,"title":"","content":"Just to make this explicitly clear: The Toggled and Perpetual keywords on a Variation denote how it works <i>if</i> that Variation is entangled with a Persistent Scar, not that it <i>must</i> be a Persistent Variation with that activation method, which is instead covered by notes like the one in Rapid Healing, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T11:26:08-07:00","id":1338656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338649#post1338649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make this explicitly clear: The Toggled and Perpetual keywords on a Variation denote how it works <i>if</i> that Variation is entangled with a Persistent Scar, not that it <i>must</i> be a Persistent Variation with that activation method, which is instead covered by notes like the one in Rapid Healing, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T14:10:13-07:00","id":1338689,"title":"","content":"so is it too late for the special preview? literally 15 more dollars (no idea when monday is for the timezone)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T15:51:48-07:00","id":1338704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338640#post1338640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relentless Variation is a Scar, but it's a weird one in that it has a mandatory secondary Scar (either Controlled of Persistent). It started its life as a Deviation, but I found that it was easier to explain its effects, this way. It is indeed the way you get persistently invisible characters.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am so very curious about how Relentless Variation interacts with a Controlled Scar, but I think I'll just have to wait until the manuscript drops tomorrow.<br /> <br /> It's going to be dope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T16:42:19-07:00","id":1338708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338506#post1338506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts is lengthy. Hm. I'll see if I can find a way to address that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast corebook changed the prerequisites to Stamina 3 Brawl 2 since it didn't include either of those styles. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T20:24:00-07:00","id":1338738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338704#post1338704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am so very curious about how Relentless Variation interacts with a Controlled Scar, but I think I'll just have to wait until the manuscript drops tomorrow.<br /> <br /> It's going to be dope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably 12-ish hours before all will be revealed (barring James having a bout of insomnia), but the short version is the entangled Variation is &quot;on&quot; unless you pay its &quot;activation cost&quot; to temporarily suppress it. If the secondary Scar is Tribulation, for example, you spend Willpower to <i>stop</i> being gigantic instead of spending a point of Willpower to <i>become</i> gigantic. Instead of Power Failure being the secret weakness your enemies roll out to strip you of your powers, it's the thing you use to keep your always-on power from getting out of hand (Relentless Variation was originally pitched to me as &quot;the Cyclops Scar&quot;, though it has expanded significantly since then).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338708#post1338708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Beast corebook changed the prerequisites to Stamina 3 Brawl 2 since it didn't include either of those styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably the easiest solution, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T03:21:04-07:00","id":1338760,"title":"","content":"Variations and Scars are here! And wow, this will take some time to digest. I was thinking the other day that Merits were one of the only weak points in the CoD character creation process as they're so toolboxy and it's hard to know when to start with... Variations aren't easier xD but it does open a lot of possible characters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T06:37:19-07:00","id":1338775,"title":"","content":"Clearly it is time: We must make The Hulk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:20:37-07:00","id":1338786,"title":"","content":"Welp, I just found a flaw:<br /> <br /> For Magnitude 3 and up Deviants, there is no question of &quot;what genre of boss music do your enemies hear when you are nearby?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:35:37-07:00","id":1338791,"title":"","content":"Mimicry with Relentless Variation vs. Hybrid Form: compare and contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:20:27-07:00","id":1338810,"title":"","content":"This preview is everything I'd hoped it would be. Some thoughts, which I'll probably edit in more of as I go:<br /> <br /> 1) Miniaturization should probably function in a way that makes it compatible with Small-Framed(decreasing size by x, much like Giant does in reverse, instead of the first dot 'setting' the character to Size 4, for example).<br /> <br /> 2) Looking at Hybrid form made me reflect further on scar entanglement scaling. As long as I want exactly two Magnitude 4 abilities for a Magnitude 5 Scar, this works fine. But what if I want 1 Mag 4 ability and a selection of lower magnitude ones? As written, the rules don't support that.<br /> <br /> 3) Seeing a few instances of auras that roll to affect each target individually. This seems like it has the potential to bog down play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-01-2019, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:31:33-07:00","id":1338815,"title":"","content":"Anyone know if Body Snatcher's body swapping lets you keep your variations? It seems to describe what happens to scars but not variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:47:22-07:00","id":1338817,"title":"","content":"I really think it should. It'd be fun to do an antagonist Deviant that's achieved immortality via body snatching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:54:27-07:00","id":1338821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338815#post1338815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know if Body Snatcher's body swapping lets you keep your variations? It seems to describe what happens to scars but not variations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the idea is that the entangled variations go with the scars. You'd still have access to variations attached to mental/social scars on a temporary swap, but lose access to variations attached to physical scars. On a longer swap, maybe you'd gradually get your other variations back as your scar grows on your new body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:54:54-07:00","id":1338822,"title":"","content":"Do Shadow Selves have substance/can deal damage/perform actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T10:05:57-07:00","id":1338824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338822#post1338822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Shadow Selves have substance/can deal damage/perform actions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It looks like they do have substance in that they can opens doors and you can inhabit them to do things. It looks like they can only really act (other than the movement-like actions of opening doors and rope-sliding) when it's actually you or they are functioning as a Retainer. It's a pretty small die pool, but they could probably technically deal damage if they got very lucky or were doing something very easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T10:28:51-07:00","id":1338830,"title":"","content":"Hm. I have some issues with Relentless Variation, which is sad because that was the one i was most excited for.<br /> <br /> 1. Inescapable seems worse in just literally every way vs Suppressible. Suppressible has all the advantages, and you always have the OPTION to just not suppress, while Inescapable you don't have an option AND have a permanent disadvantage.<br /> <br /> 2. The bonus for having a Relentless Variation seems really lackluster, even for the Suppressible version, but ESPECIALLY CRAZY MORE for inescapable. It has basically no advantages vs just having a toggled variation of any case (as a toggled variation has no disadvantage for being toggled on, the disadvantage is the permanent scar), it does something that for certain variations is basically a HORRIBLE scar on its own (Giant and Miniaturization coming to mind, but Camouflage and basically every other Toggled variation with specific exceptions are still really bad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T11:00:45-07:00","id":1338840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338786#post1338786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, I just found a flaw:<br /> <br /> For Magnitude 3 and up Deviants, there is no question of &amp;quot;what genre of boss music do your enemies hear when you are nearby?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly did not expect deviants getting to be so dangerous.<br /> <br /> but damn, that missing limb scar is not worth magnitude 4 and up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T11:24:12-07:00","id":1338844,"title":"","content":"Playtester here. I may be able to help some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338830#post1338830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Inescapable seems worse in just literally every way vs Suppressible. Suppressible has all the advantages, and you always have the OPTION to just not suppress, while Inescapable you don't have an option AND have a permanent disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found this very unclear as well and I talked with Eric about cleaning up the language here. (Edit: I could be wrong on this) There is an advantage to using the Inescapable deviation: it adds a magnitude to Relentless, but not to the secondary scar (which is the unclear part).<br /> Example: You have a Relentless mag 2 scar and you increase the mag to 3 with the Inescapable deviation. You choose a mag 2 secondary scar to attach to it. Then you choose a magnitude 3 variation (or two 2's, etc.) to entangle with Relentless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338830#post1338830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The bonus for having a Relentless Variation seems really lackluster, even for the Suppressible version, but ESPECIALLY CRAZY MORE for inescapable. It has basically no advantages vs just having a toggled variation of any case (as a toggled variation has no disadvantage for being toggled on, the disadvantage is the permanent scar), it does something that for certain variations is basically a HORRIBLE scar on its own (Giant and Miniaturization coming to mind, but Camouflage and basically every other Toggled variation with specific exceptions are still really bad).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my answer to whether the scar itself is good vs. horrible is a more subjective thing. I for one LOVE this scar and have used it in playtesting. This scar is great at modeling characters that work oddly. The Cyclops example with Relentless Power Failure is a good one. A character concept that I considered for testing was one that used two versions of the scar, an Inescapable Relentless Gigantic with a controlled Relentless Camouflage. He's huge, and he has to concentrate to stay visible. It's a scar; it's job is to make your life complicated and make an interesting story while generating beats.<br /> Or consider Animal Transformation: if you want to BE a bear that can shapeshift into a woman on command, that's how to do it. The character I played in playtest sessions had (Inescapable) Relentless Animal Transformation (squirrel) attached to Conspicuous Appearance. I was for most purposes, a squirrel. I had Pheromones to communicate (mostly) normally, but ran into trouble doing things like talking on the phone. That's what I wanted. (Granted there will be a better way to model this later with the new form in the upcoming Clade Companion, but I didn't have that at the time.)<br /> I didn't play the invisible giant because I fell in love with the electrokinetic squirrel. Also I didn't like how you couldn't take advantage of the healing aspect when you can't change your size. This scar might be laden with more drawback than you want to deal with in many cases. But I think it has tons of uses to build interesting characters.<br /> <br /> Edit: added that the squirrel relentless scar was Inescapable.<br /> Fixed terminology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12709,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","user":"Sir Dragos","date":". 10-01-2019, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T11:35:58-07:00","id":1338846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338844#post1338844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playtester here. I may be able to help some.<br /> <br /> <br /> I found this very unclear as well and I talked with Eric about cleaning up the language here. There is an advantage to using the Continual deviation: it adds a magnitude to Relentless, but not to the secondary scar (which is the unclear part).<br /> Example: You have a Relentless mag 2 scar and you increase the mag to 3 with the Continual deviation. You choose a mag 2 secondary scar to attach to it. Then you choose a magnitude 3 variation (or two 2's, etc.) to entangle with Relentless.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>(It's called Inescapable now, and it's not a deviation), and really? i read the power and it said nothing of the sort, only giving +1 Magnitude if the scar is Overt, and that's for both Supressable and Inescapable. If that is true, that feels VERY MUCH like it needs Errata. As written, a Subtle Variation entangled with Relentless (Inescapable), is the same but you can't get rid of it, which in 99% of circumstances<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338844#post1338844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my answer to whether the scar itself is good vs. horrible is a more subjective thing. I for one LOVE this scar and have used it in playtesting. This scar is great at modeling characters that work oddly. The Cyclops example with Relentless Power Failure is a good one. A character concept that I considered for testing was one that used two versions of the scar, a Continuous Relentless Gigantic with a controlled Relentless Camouflage. He's huge, and he has to concentrate to stay visible. It's a scar; it's job is to make your life complicated and make an interesting story while generating beats.<br /> Or consider Animal Transformation: if you want to BE a bear that can shapeshift into a woman on command, that's how to do it. The character I played in playtest sessions had Relentless Animal Transformation (squirrel) attached to Conspicuous Appearance. I was for most purposes, a squirrel. I had Pheromones to communicate (mostly) normally, but ran into trouble doing things like talking on the phone. That's what I wanted. (Granted there will be a better way to model this later with the new form in the upcoming Clade Companion, but I didn't have that at the time.)<br /> I didn't play the invisible giant because I fell in love with the electrokinetic squirrel. Also I didn't like how you couldn't take advantage of the healing aspect when you can't change your size. This scar might be laden with more drawback than you want to deal with in many cases. But I think it has tons of uses to build interesting characters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with you (I LOVE the idea of a variation being permanently on and that being an issue), but it genuinely feels like there are serious problems that are generally represented by significant increases in magnitude that there just aren't with this Scar, and that sorta just feels like something that is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T11:59:10-07:00","id":1338848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338846#post1338846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's called Inescapable now, and it's not a deviation), and really? i read the power and it said nothing of the sort, only giving +1 Magnitude if the scar is Overt, and that's for both Supressable and Inescapable. If that is true, that feels VERY MUCH like it needs Errata. As written, a Subtle Variation entangled with Relentless (Inescapable), is the same but you can't get rid of it, which in 99% of circumstances</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, yes, Inescapable (Sorry, I'm stuck on an old name). I may be wrong on this one. It's possible that we'd been talking past each other when I asked for clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338846#post1338846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree with you (I LOVE the idea of a variation being permanently on and that being an issue), but it genuinely feels like there are serious problems that are generally represented by significant increases in magnitude that there just aren't with this Scar, and that sorta just feels like something that is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly inconvenient, but in an interesting way that you really kinda get to choose for yourself. It will generate beats like a MFer, that's for sure; typically variations don't get to do that. I think I agree with what you are saying though. Inescapable is a beast. <br /> I should note that there are very few toggled, subtle variations and few of them are really a burden to have on all the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:48:36-07:00","id":1338865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338810#post1338810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Looking at Hybrid form made me reflect further on scar entanglement scaling. As long as I want exactly two Magnitude 4 abilities for a Magnitude 5 Scar, this works fine. But what if I want 1 Mag 4 ability and a selection of lower magnitude ones? As written, the rules don't support that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, Hybrid Form's Scar-free Variations work identically to entangling a Scar with multiple Variations. You can't exceed a total of 5 in [Highest Magnitude Variation] + [number of additional Variations], but you're explicitly able to take Variations whose Magnitude is lower than the maximums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T14:04:12-07:00","id":1338869,"title":"","content":"The Variation Healing touch, need a Tag as Directed? It can heal only other subject or the deviant too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T14:10:13-07:00","id":1338870,"title":"","content":"So I'm talking with a potential player, and her concept is the test pilot for a highly experimental time machine who is now unmoored from linear time/stuck in a time loop/both at once.<br /> <br /> There are just so many ways to represent this concept through Scars and Variations, and I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T14:48:18-07:00","id":1338872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338830#post1338830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Inescapable seems worse in just literally every way vs Suppressible. Suppressible has all the advantages, and you always have the OPTION to just not suppress, while Inescapable you don't have an option AND have a permanent disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advantages of Inescapable are that you always have access to the Variation and the only way you can be deprived of it is if another supernatural effect manages to negate it despite the Clash bonus being a Perpetual effect provides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The bonus for having a Relentless Variation seems really lackluster, even for the Suppressible version, but ESPECIALLY CRAZY MORE for inescapable. It has basically no advantages vs just having a toggled variation of any case (as a toggled variation has no disadvantage for being toggled on </div> </div> </div>The advantage is pretty much the same as what Hybrid Form gets you (and the reason Hybrid Form has a minimum Magnitude of 2): Unless a Toggled Variation is also Reflexive, it takes an instant action to activate, which is not always a unit of time you have to spare as a character who is being hunted by conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:01:38-07:00","id":1338874,"title":"","content":"Okay, I kinda wanna make a Chimeric who has a split personality who's a City of Heroes Devoured.<br /> <br /> You know, an eco-terrorist kaiju who knows his way around a laboratory. And also some dark magic.<br /> <br /> &quot;JIM, GET YOUR SPLIT PERSONALITY IN LINE BEFORE WE ALL DIE BECAUSE HE WAS TOO BUSY EATING AN OIL EXEC!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:19:00-07:00","id":1338878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338872#post1338872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advantages of Inescapable are that you always have access to the Variation and the only way you can be deprived of it is if another supernatural effect manages to negate it despite the Clash bonus being a Perpetual effect provides.<br /> <br /> The advantage is pretty much the same as what Hybrid Form gets you (and the reason Hybrid Form has a minimum Magnitude of 2): Unless a Toggled Variation is also Reflexive, it takes an instant action to activate, which is not always a unit of time you have to spare as a character who is being hunted by conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok so like thinking on it, i agree that Suppressible is actually fine as is, but i still believe Inescapable is a crazy absurdly big disadvantage. Suppressible is better in literally every way (same +5 bonus, you can choose to never turn off your disadvantage, ect), Inescapable just removes options AND gives you a persistent Scar. Personally if it were up to me to balance (and i don't know exactly how to balance, so take what i say with a grain of salt), I almost feel like the obvious choice is to make Inescapable fully pay off the entangled variation, as it's basically the same as if someone bought Suppressible and never used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T15:56:07-07:00","id":1338882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338878#post1338878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppressible is better in literally every way (same +5 bonus, you can choose to never turn off your disadvantage, ect), Inescapable just removes options AND gives you a persistent Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning off the Variation requires a roll, costs you every time, and is still just as subject to intensifying from Instability as any other Scar. The roll suppression requires is also (barring Acclimation) a single Attribute that is penalized by any degree of Instability at all, and dramatic failure on that roll gives you more Instability.<br /> <br /> For contrast, Inescapable can pay its price by such things as <i>not being able to speak</i> or <i>needing to perform maintenance to keep the Variation working</i> or <i>having lower effective Presence</i>.<br /> <br /> Persistent Scars are not <i>inherently worse</i> than Controlled Scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:20:58-07:00","id":1338886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338882#post1338882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning off the Variation requires a roll, costs you every time, and is still just as subject to intensifying from Instability as any other Scar. The roll suppression requires is also (barring Acclimation) a single Attribute that is penalized by any degree of Instability at all, and dramatic failure on that roll gives you more Instability.<br /> <br /> For contrast, Inescapable can pay its price by such things as <i>not being able to speak</i> or <i>needing to perform maintenance to keep the Variation working</i> or <i>having lower effective Presence</i>.<br /> <br /> Persistent Scars are not <i>inherently worse</i> than Controlled Scars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that Persistent scars are &quot;<i>inherently worse</i>&quot;. I'm saying that it's &quot;<i>inherently worse</i>&quot; to NOT have an option vs HAVING an option.<br /> <br /> Let's consider something for a moment.<br /> <br /> You have a 5 dot Magnitude Variation and want to entangle it with Relentless Variation. You can<br /> <br /> a. Use Suppressible. You now have an (Very Dangerous and/or Costly and/or Unreliable) OPTION to turn off your power. You may always choose to not turn off your power ever (Controlled Variations will never force you to use them), and the power will have no downsides. <br /> <br /> b. Use Inescapable. You do not have any option to turn off your power. You cannot turn off your power AND you get a Major disadvantage with it.<br /> <br /> Effectively, it's not the difference between a Persistent Scar vs a Controlled Scar, it's the ability to do something vs no ability to do so, and the no ability also comes with a disadvantage. A good comparison is to think of it in reverse. <br /> <br /> Suppressible's best comparison is just having a Variation with a Controlled Scar (in this Analogy, the Variation is the ability to temporarily turn off your Relentless Variation)<br /> <br /> In this analogy then, Inescapable's best comparison is LACKING that Variation, and then getting a Scar that is equally as bad as if you HAD taken the Variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:27:48-07:00","id":1338887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338870#post1338870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm talking with a potential player, and her concept is the test pilot for a highly experimental time machine who is now unmoored from linear time/stuck in a time loop/both at once.<br /> <br /> There are just so many ways to represent this concept through Scars and Variations, and I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div> 100% watch the Fringe Episode &quot;White Tulip&quot; (S02E18). It's not the exact same concept but by god if you're not inspired with where that can go, well I don't know what to tell ya. <br /> <br /> Actually, and I'm sure this has been said before... nearly any/every episode of Fringe can be mined for Deviant ideas. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:40:17-07:00","id":1338888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338886#post1338886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b. Use Inescapable. You do not have any option to turn off your power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can literally tell you of at least two off the top of my head, one of which is &quot;develop Mimicry.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this analogy then, Inescapable's best comparison is LACKING that Variation, and then getting a Scar that is equally as bad as if you HAD taken the Variation. </div> </div> </div>How convenient, then, that the difference between Controlled and Persistent Scars at the most basic level is often &quot;you get Beats for using the Variation&quot; versus &quot;you get Beats for having the Scar.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's not a huge degree of difference between &quot;I can't stop being a cat&quot; and &quot;I have to take damage/Instability/time out for every scene that I am not a cat.&quot; If you're going to use Magnitude 5 examples, being capped at Strength 1 or having a lower threshold for wound penalties is objectively less troublesome than taking a medium Instability or losing all memory of your time without the Variation active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-01-2019, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:51:06-07:00","id":1338890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338865#post1338865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, Hybrid Form's Scar-free Variations work identically to entangling a Scar with multiple Variations. You can't exceed a total of 5 in [Highest Magnitude Variation] + [number of additional Variations], but you're explicitly able to take Variations whose Magnitude is lower than the maximums.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I wasn't being particularly clear when I wrote this, but your response helped clarify what I was misunderstanding anyway, so thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:52:57-07:00","id":1338891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338888#post1338888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can literally tell you of at least two off the top of my head, one of which is &quot;develop Mimicry.&quot;<br /> <br /> How convenient, then, that the difference between Controlled and Persistent Scars at the most basic level is often &quot;you get Beats for using the Variation&quot; versus &quot;you get Beats for having the Scar.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's not a huge degree of difference between &quot;I can't stop being a cat&quot; and &quot;I have to take damage/Instability/time out for every scene that I am not a cat.&quot; If you're going to use Magnitude 5 examples, being capped at Strength 2 or having a lower threshold for wound penalties is objectively less troublesome than taking a medium Instability or losing all memory of your time without the Variation active.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Most people won't have those options (and i'd say developing mimicry to get rid of Relentless Variation falls under &quot;taking away the point of the scar&quot;)<br /> <br /> 2. Yeah there is a huge difference. the difference is that &quot;I have to take damage/Instability/time out for every scene that I am not a cat.&quot; makes it so you can always choose to just be a cat to avoid that issue. it's the difference between &quot;i can fly but i take damage / instability when i do so&quot; and &quot;i cannot fly&quot;. it's objectively worse to not be able to fly, because you can always choose NOT to fly. <br /> <br /> 3. &quot;but you'll get more beats for it!&quot; is not an excuse. I'll get beats for taking 10 unentangled variations, that doesn't make it an option people will say is good<br /> <br /> 4. I literally do not know how to further explain to you the idea that being able to do something at a price (that you always actively choose to pay) is objectively better than not being able to do something, especially when not being able to do something comes at an equally bad price as being able to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:03:56-07:00","id":1338893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338891#post1338891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. &quot;but you'll get more beats for it!&quot; is not an excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it's going to give you more Beats. I'm saying that the option to get Beats is going to be more readily available for characters who get the option without having to turn off their powers at cost, and some people are going to prefer that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. I literally do not know how to further explain to you the idea that being able to do something at a price (that you always actively choose to pay) is objectively better than not being able to do something, especially when not being able to do something comes at an equally bad price as being able to do it. </div> </div> </div>By the same token, I don't know how else to impress upon you the fact that not every player of a game where your powers come with drawbacks such as &quot;you are obviously inhuman&quot; is interested in playing a character who has the convenient ability to decide that they want to take an hour off from having attention-grabbing supernatural powers over playing a character who has to navigate the problems presented by having attention-grabbing supernatural powers constantly manifested.<br /> <br /> One is not actually better than the other in a game where rejection and lack of drive will kill you either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:18:14-07:00","id":1338897,"title":"","content":"Let me try this again: what are the differences, both conceptually and in terms of game systems, between Mimicry with Relentless Variation on the one hand, and Hybrid Form on the other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-01-2019, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:21:16-07:00","id":1338898,"title":"","content":"This is a question mostly for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> - are there systems behind symbiont Manticores inflicting scars on their users that we haven't seen yet, or is this simply left to ST discretion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:34:49-07:00","id":1338900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338893#post1338893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying it's going to give you more Beats. I'm saying that the option to get Beats is going to be more readily available for characters who get the option without having to turn off their powers at cost, and some people are going to prefer that.<br /> <br /> By the same token, I don't know how else to impress upon you the fact that not every player of a game where your powers come with drawbacks such as &quot;you are obviously inhuman&quot; is interested in playing a character who has the convenient ability to decide that they want to take an hour off from having attention-grabbing supernatural powers over playing a character who has to navigate the problems presented by having attention-grabbing supernatural powers constantly manifested.<br /> <br /> One is not actually better than the other in a game where rejection and lack of drive will kill you either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am ACUTELY aware of the fact that some people would prefer a permanent variation to one they can turn off for an hour (in fact, i'm very very much one of them, which is why i'm arguing that the Scar is not balanced against itself right), but i'm saying that option should not be actively punished by the game mechanics. As is, it is JUST a better option to have a Suppressible and never use it vs having Inescapable, and in my opinion that is a problem, as i WANT Inescapable to be a valid option. No option should just be WORSE than another option.<br /> <br /> As is, the game actively discourages Inescapable as an option, which is something i think should be fixed. If it's not changed will i still use it? almost definitely, I love the flavor of it, but i will certainty still bitch about it because a game should not have objectively worse options. <br /> <br /> Quite simply, it's always better to have an option than to not. You may not USE the power to change the outcome of a single dice at the cost of breaking both your legs (as a laughably extreme example), but it's better to have the option than to not.<br /> <br /> As well, despite the fact that the option to NOT have this power is worse than having it just at base, if you choose not to have the ability to change back at at price, you then gain a BONUS disadvantage on top of the fact you are stuck. <br /> <br /> Here's basically what i mean:<br /> <br /> At base, you have a variation that is always on<br /> <br /> if you choose Suppressible, you get a &quot;Variation&quot; (that you can ALWAYS choose not to use) with a Controlled Scar. This makes sense! i'm fine with this.<br /> <br /> if you choose Inescapable, you simply do not get this &quot;Variation&quot; and you get what is effectively an extra &quot;Unentangled&quot; Scar equal to what the Controlled Scar's Magnitude would have been.<br /> <br /> I think this is an issue, and should be fixed. I'm not saying &quot;why would anyone choose Inescapable! it's horrible!&quot;, i'm saying that right now it is objectively worse than Suppressible, and i would like that part of it fixed so i can justify it better from a purely mechanically position. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:37:47-07:00","id":1338901,"title":"","content":"Under Lash, is there any way to represent a wide-area beam attack such as the Guyver's Megasmasher? A particle beam weapon that's something like fifteen feet across and over a hundred yards long, obliterating not just one or more targets but <i>everything</i> in its path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:43:51-07:00","id":1338902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338897#post1338897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try this again: what are the differences, both conceptually and in terms of game systems, between Mimicry with Relentless Variation on the one hand, and Hybrid Form on the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest one is that Hybrid Form is necessarily an Overt Variation made up of multiple smaller Variations attached to a single Scar, whereas Relentless Mimicry suppresses all your Variations below the Scar threshold, but none of those Variations are necessarily Overt, but you have to have bought all of them that you didn't start with. One is &quot;I have managed to develop a way to shut down a bunch of my other Scars at cost so that I can more easily act&quot; and the other is &quot;I have a package deal of Variations that I can unleash in one big burst&quot; \u2014 the sidebar underneath Mimicry just about covers it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T17:53:19-07:00","id":1338903,"title":"","content":"Mimicry <i>with Relentless Variation</i>, which inverts the normal relationship between turning it on and turning it off. <br /> <br /> Good point about Hybrid Form necessarily being Overt while Mimicry isn't; but when Mimicry has Relentless Variation, it also operates on the basis of \u201cthese associated Variations (the ones entangled with certain Scars) aren't available unless you make a deliberate effort to [turn off the Mimicry and] make them available.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T18:16:03-07:00","id":1338906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338903#post1338903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mimicry <i>with Relentless Variation</i>, which inverts the normal relationship between turning it on and turning it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be why I said &quot;Relentless Mimicry.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good point about Hybrid Form necessarily being Overt while Mimicry isn't; but when Mimicry has Relentless Variation, it also operates on the basis of \u201cthese associated Variations (the ones entangled with certain Scars) aren't available unless you make a deliberate effort to [turn off the Mimicry and] make them available.\u201d </div> </div> </div>One more distinction is that Relentless Variation (Suppressible) as applied to Mimicry effectively adds a cost to accessing your other Variations but does not remove those Variations' attendant Scars while you have access to them \u2014 Hybrid Form is primed to be more effective at bundling its attached Variations with fewer or less onerous Scars, whereas making Mimicry Relentless puts more weight on managing the strain all of your other powers impose on your soul with their full weight; without paying the price of Suppressible, you pretty much have to be suffering medium or major Instability to access one of your weaker Variations, and at that point you do so under the effects of more powerful Scars.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Relentless Mimicry punts putting out a bunch of your Variations into the sphere of a long-term balancing act that puts your Stability track dramatically closer to the fore re: managing its drawbacks. (Also, I sure hope you're confident in your ability to deal with the Web of Pain on hard mode, because this is not an escalatory methodology that favors the little guy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T18:29:20-07:00","id":1338907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338901#post1338901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under Lash, is there any way to represent a wide-area beam attack such as the Guyver's Megasmasher? A particle beam weapon that's something like fifteen feet across and over a hundred yards long, obliterating not just one or more targets but <i>everything</i> in its path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, so, here it goes: Magnitude oooo Lash with the following properties:Ranged, Cutting, Reach, Piercing, Deadly, Full Auto (to represent hitting all the targets at once). Not familiar enough with the Guyver mythos to create a Scar. Piercing will make it work equally well against blowing through building and mooks. Reach gives it the range you want. Not exactly right but you might be able to talk your GM into merging Reach and Explosive (instead of Full Auto) to get the beam you want but it won't be as damaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","user":"Geomancer","date":". 10-01-2019, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T19:31:50-07:00","id":1338913,"title":"","content":"A lot to go through, tonight, but given which section of the manuscript dropped today, that doesn't surprise me at all!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338786#post1338786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, I just found a flaw:<br /> <br /> For Magnitude 3 and up Deviants, there is no question of &quot;what genre of boss music do your enemies hear when you are nearby?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I&quot;m afraid I'm not 100% sure I'm interpreting you correctly on this one. Are you concerned about the power level of higher-Magnitude Variations? Which genre are you referencing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338810#post1338810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This preview is everything I'd hoped it would be. Some thoughts, which I'll probably edit in more of as I go:<br /> <br /> 1) Miniaturization should probably function in a way that makes it compatible with Small-Framed(decreasing size by x, much like Giant does in reverse, instead of the first dot 'setting' the character to Size 4, for example).<br /> <br /> 2) Looking at Hybrid form made me reflect further on scar entanglement scaling. As long as I want exactly two Magnitude 4 abilities for a Magnitude 5 Scar, this works fine. But what if I want 1 Mag 4 ability and a selection of lower magnitude ones? As written, the rules don't support that.<br /> <br /> 3) Seeing a few instances of auras that roll to affect each target individually. This seems like it has the potential to bog down play.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Agreed. I'll update it.<br /> <br /> 2) I see others have answered this question.<br /> <br /> 3) Heh. Good catch. This appears to be a throwback to a time when Directed effects were resisted, not contested. Since those <i>are</i> contested, now, I can dispense with the individual targeting, in most cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338817#post1338817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think it should. It'd be fun to do an antagonist Deviant that's achieved immortality via body snatching.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338840#post1338840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> honestly did not expect deviants getting to be so dangerous.<br /> <br /> but damn, that missing limb scar is not worth magnitude 4 and up</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. In a game about running away from shadowy conspiracies, not being able to run seems like a pretty substantial disadvantage. Or were you meaning it another way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338865#post1338865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, Hybrid Form's Scar-free Variations work identically to entangling a Scar with multiple Variations. You can't exceed a total of 5 in [Highest Magnitude Variation] + [number of additional Variations], but you're explicitly able to take Variations whose Magnitude is lower than the maximums.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338869#post1338869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Variation Healing touch, need a Tag as Directed? It can heal only other subject or the deviant too?</div> </div> </div> </div>This crossed my mind, but I believe I opted not to do it because of the way it interacted with some Scars that can be of higher Magnitude if the entangled Variation is Directed, but Healing Touch didn't really make matters worse when tied to those Directed-only effects. I might relent on this one.<br /> <br /> RE Relentless Variation: I'm letting this discussion play out, for now. I agree that Persistent Variations aren't inherently worse than Controlled ones (and an Inescapable Variation isn't so bad that it should make the underlying Variation otherwise Scar-free), but I also see the point regarding not having the option to suppress being a little on the harsh side. I was originally going back and forth between making both a +1 Magnitude effect or having Controlled at +1 and Persistent at +2 (to be clear, this would only apply to Overt Variations). What pros &amp; cons do folks see to the current method vs. this alternative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338897#post1338897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try this again: what are the differences, both conceptually and in terms of game systems, between Mimicry with Relentless Variation on the one hand, and Hybrid Form on the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mimicry's purpose is to hide Scars, which it can do to an almost limitless degree (albeit at a cost of also shutting down access to the entangled Variations). If you have 7 different Scars at or below the Magnitude of Mimicry, you can hide one, some, or all of them, as you wish.<br /> <br /> Applying Relentless Variation to Mimicry<br /> <br /> RE: Relentless Mimicry vs. Hybrid Form: Satchel seems to doing a pretty good job of discussing this one, but let me know if you want me to weigh in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338898#post1338898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question mostly for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> - are there systems behind symbiont Manticores inflicting scars on their users that we haven't seen yet, or is this simply left to ST discretion?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the moment, its a storytelling device.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T19:37:09-07:00","id":1338915,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is really looking like the sort of game I've been wanting for CofD all along, although given the discussion with Relentless Variation I want to see if one of the concepts I'm spitballing is correct in terms of Variations/linked Scars. (yeah, I know the book term is entangled but I keep THINKING &quot;linked&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Concept: Self-made deviant who was working on good old fashioned super-soldier serum or somesuch to become the Ideal Superhuman. without going into specific ranks (although I had the high end in mind for the concept), She has Gigantic, Hybrid Body (with Superhuman Attribute in all the physical stats), and just scratchpadding, I threw in Pheromones with Aura to be a sort of 'super charisma' to boot. The entangled scars are Relentless with Gigantic with the suppressible Power Failure option, Hybrid Body with Conspicuous Appearance to represent a &quot;hulking out&quot;, and after seeing the example in the section I figured the Addictive scar with Pheromones makes sense - bend people to your will and the attention becomes something you crave.<br /> <br /> So: if I understand this right: she could 'dorm down', to use the Aberrant term, to passing for normal human via suppressing Gigantic and simply keeping Hybrid Body off, but there's no particular disadvantage to being huge and superhuman aside from &quot;is huge&quot; and &quot;people tend to get very nervous around the Hulk&quot;. Which are disadvantages when a big organization is trying to hunt you down for their own ends, fair enough. And, by the same token, if she isn't getting people to bow and scrape to her on a regular basis, she starts to have problems.<br /> <br /> And each of these scars need to be ranked in Magnitude as high as their associated Variation, yes, aside from the free dot her origin would give her?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:03:11-07:00","id":1338918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338913#post1338913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I&quot;m afraid I'm not 100% sure I'm interpreting you correctly on this one. Are you concerned about the power level of higher-Magnitude Variations? Which genre are you referencing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a wisecrack on a recent meme. Hostile badass present = video game boss music out of nowhere. I'm not complaining, I'm saying a Deviant feels like a badass to the point where even a would-be Elect who knows about Scars would still become one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:06:54-07:00","id":1338919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338913#post1338913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Relentless Variation: I'm letting this discussion play out, for now. I agree that Persistent Variations aren't inherently worse than Controlled ones (and an Inescapable Variation isn't so bad that it should make the underlying Variation otherwise Scar-free), but I also see the point regarding not having the option to suppress being a little on the harsh side. I was originally going back and forth between making both a +1 Magnitude effect or having Controlled at +1 and Persistent at +2 (to be clear, this would only apply to Overt Variations). What pros &amp; cons do folks see to the current method vs. this alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Normally i'd agree with you, but the specific way that Suppressible *works* makes it so that it's inherently pretty much unarguably better than Inescapable in every context at this point. Because you can always choose to just NOT use your ability to suppress your Variation. <br /> <br /> Even if your Secondary Scar is &quot;Take a Major Instability&quot;, which is a HUGE price to pay, that's still pretty much always BETTER than not having that option, because you can just NOT choose to suppress, and you have no other downsides to your Variation being always-on (besides the fact that it is always on).<br /> <br /> In contrast, if you have Inescapable, you CAN'T use that option (even if you would only use it once every few chapters anyway), and you get new downsides from not having the option, which is a problem <br /> <br /> And i think there's a problem when having an option and not using it is objectively better than not having an option.<br /> <br /> Personally i think you're kinda looking this in the wrong direction. I think you either need to add a SECOND (Persistent) Secondary Scar to Suppressible, or you need to straight up get rid of the Scar for Inescapable.<br /> <br /> Because quite honestly, a Relentless Variation (Inescapable) that has NO Scar is still objectively worse than Relentless Variation (Suppressible) that has a 5 Magnitude Scar. This is because the way Suppressible works is that it adds an option (Suppressing your Scar) and then gives a disadvantage to it (the Controlled Scar). In contrast, the way Inescapable works is that it fundamentally does not have that option, and then gives a disadvantage anyway (the Persistent Scar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:15:49-07:00","id":1338920,"title":"","content":"A couple questions of my own now that I've exorcised the impulse to run through various mechanical turduckens with the various &quot;attach a secondary Scar from another category to this Scar&quot; options:<br /> <br /> 1. Now that the full surrounded context is available I can confirm that the Channel effect of Lash doesn't seem to have any further explanation for &quot;The Lash gains the Exclusive keyword.&quot; Is that an artifact of a name change for another keyword or some other oddity?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Variations that involve secondary Variations like Hybrid Form or Sacred Flesh subject to the rules for proportional Variation dots by Clade, or do only the dots in the primary Variation count toward the total? (e.g. Can my non-Invasive character have a Hybrid Form whose effects are just Computer-Aided Processing and Sensor Array?)<br /> <br /> 3. Can the Disfiguring Scar Standard Deviation alter whether the Overt cost break for Relentless Variation kicks in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-01-2019, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:49:14-07:00","id":1338923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338913#post1338913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot to go through, tonight, but given which section of the manuscript dropped today, that doesn't surprise me at all!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I&amp;quot;m afraid I'm not 100% sure I'm interpreting you correctly on this one. Are you concerned about the power level of higher-Magnitude Variations? Which genre are you referencing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Agreed. I'll update it.<br /> <br /> 2) I see others have answered this question.<br /> <br /> 3) Heh. Good catch. This appears to be a throwback to a time when Directed effects were resisted, not contested. Since those <i>are</i> contested, now, I can dispense with the individual targeting, in most cases.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dunno. In a game about running away from shadowy conspiracies, not being able to run seems like a pretty substantial disadvantage. Or were you meaning it another way?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This crossed my mind, but I believe I opted not to do it because of the way it interacted with some Scars that can be of higher Magnitude if the entangled Variation is Directed, but Healing Touch didn't really make matters worse when tied to those Directed-only effects. I might relent on this one.<br /> <br /> RE Relentless Variation: I'm letting this discussion play out, for now. I agree that Persistent Variations aren't inherently worse than Controlled ones (and an Inescapable Variation isn't so bad that it should make the underlying Variation otherwise Scar-free), but I also see the point regarding not having the option to suppress being a little on the harsh side. I was originally going back and forth between making both a +1 Magnitude effect or having Controlled at +1 and Persistent at +2 (to be clear, this would only apply to Overt Variations). What pros &amp; cons do folks see to the current method vs. this alternative?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mimicry's purpose is to hide Scars, which it can do to an almost limitless degree (albeit at a cost of also shutting down access to the entangled Variations). If you have 7 different Scars at or below the Magnitude of Mimicry, you can hide one, some, or all of them, as you wish.<br /> <br /> Applying Relentless Variation to Mimicry<br /> <br /> RE: Relentless Mimicry vs. Hybrid Form: Satchel seems to doing a pretty good job of discussing this one, but let me know if you want me to weigh in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the moment, its a storytelling device.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that, for me, having the missing limb scar and having a magnitude at 4 and above is just not worth it.<br /> <br /> also anybody, please tell me how to quote a specific part of a post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:58:15-07:00","id":1338925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338923#post1338923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also anybody, please tell me how to quote a specific part of a post</div> </div> </div> </div>Delete the parts inside of the [*quote][*/quote] tags that you don't want quoted, or ensure that those same tags are around each chunk that you want in a separate quote box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:16:57-07:00","id":1338927,"title":"","content":"For Addictive Variations - is using any of the entangled Variations sufficient to 'get a fix', or does the Deviant have to use *all* of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:34:18-07:00","id":1338931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338918#post1338918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a wisecrack on a recent meme. Hostile badass present = video game boss music out of nowhere. I'm not complaining, I'm saying a Deviant feels like a badass to the point where even a would-be Elect who knows about Scars would still become one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense with the context. The Broken are wretches, but that doesn't mean they can't be badass wretches. *smirk* At bottom, I'm aware that people are supposed to <i>play</i> this game, so while we have a lot of grim elements, these characters still have to be fun for people to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338919#post1338919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Relentless Variation (Inescapable) that has NO Scar is still objectively worse than Relentless Variation (Suppressible) that has a 5 Magnitude Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with you quite strongly on this point, and I think it may be because you are comparing it to Suppressible, while I'm comparing it to other Persistent Scars. For example, Enhanced Speed 4 with Relentless Variation (Inescapable) is showy (more likely to attract conspiracy attention), but Glitch 4 is far more of a hassle than a little conspiracy attention. Perpetual Gigantic 5 comes with a host of problems (ranging from &quot;finding clothes in your size&quot; to &quot;fitting into buildings smaller than airline hangers&quot;), but Conspicuous Appearance 5 reduces you to a chance die on Social actions, gives the conspiracy a +5 bonus to surveillance rolls to find you, <i>and</i> attracts monster hunters unconnected to the Web of Pain. I can envision Inescapable as a standalone Magnitude 2 effect (if the entangled Variation is Overt) that allows you to add a secondary Persistent Scar to increase its Magnitude by the Magnitude of the secondary Scar. But I'm not convinced that not being able to turn off your high-Magnitude superpower is enough of a downside to justify not having any other downside to said superpower. Perpetual Camouflage 5 may complicate your life in some ways, but you're still the Invisible Man, and that means your stealth capabilities beyond what any Baseline could achieve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338920#post1338920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple questions of my own now that I've exorcised the impulse to run through various mechanical turduckens with the various &quot;attach a secondary Scar from another category to this Scar&quot; options:<br /> <br /> 1. Now that the full surrounded context is available I can confirm that the Channel effect of Lash doesn't seem to have any further explanation for &quot;The Lash gains the Exclusive keyword.&quot; Is that an artifact of a name change for another keyword or some other oddity?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Variations that involve secondary Variations like Hybrid Form or Sacred Flesh subject to the rules for proportional Variation dots by Clade, or do only the dots in the primary Variation count toward the total? (e.g. Can my non-Invasive character have a Hybrid Form whose effects are just Computer-Aided Processing and Sensor Array?)<br /> <br /> 3. Can the Disfiguring Scar Standard Deviation alter whether the Overt cost break for Relentless Variation kicks in?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The Exclusive keyword was originally meant to prevent Sacred Flesh from granting a Baseline Sacred Flesh and to prevent Sacred Flesh from giving a Baseline a Lash with the Channel effect (essentially nesting Variations). It's probably unnecessary, at this stage.<br /> <br /> 2) Great question. The secondary Variations don't count toward proportions of Clade/Universal Variations. I'll clarify that in my working draft.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes. I'll clarify in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338923#post1338923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant that, for me, having the missing limb scar and having a magnitude at 4 and above is just not worth it.<br /> <br /> also anybody, please tell me how to quote a specific part of a post</div> </div> </div> </div>The sort of general rule I have with Scars is:<br /> <br /> Mag 1: These only come into play when the player roleplays them for a Beat.<br /> Mag 2: These have a couple mechanical teeth but either don\u2019t come into play very often or carry costs that seldom carry beyond the scope of the current scene.<br /> Mag 3: The standard price of power we expect to see in game lines. They clearly carry some cost or risk, but they aren\u2019t so problematic that you would hesitate to use them in a scene where they\u2019re useful.<br /> Mag 4: This is where the price of power begins to get a bit steep. You think carefully before bringing these out (or taking them as Persistent Scars), because the cost is high enough to \u201cfollow\u201d you into other scenes or to severely impede you in the current scene.<br /> Mag 5: These are doozies with the potential to come into play constantly, reshaping the way the Broken\u2019s player interacts with the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338927#post1338927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Addictive Variations - is using any of the entangled Variations sufficient to 'get a fix', or does the Deviant have to use *all* of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was clarified in the working draft after I turned in the KS Previews: &quot;If entangled with multiple Variations, activating any one of them satisfies the addiction.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:45:30-07:00","id":1338934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338927#post1338927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Addictive Variations - is using any of the entangled Variations sufficient to 'get a fix', or does the Deviant have to use *all* of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Relatedly, I'm not sure I understand the timeline of the Lingering effect as it relates to the normal Magnitude 2 effect; you get the Persistent Deprived Condition if you don't use the Variation for at least a scene once per chapter, but it resolves if you go a full story without using the Variation. Or you can just heal a medium or major Instability, which begets the question of why the first resolution option is even mentioned. Is the arc suggested there &quot;use the Variation often or your withdrawal symptoms will need extensive detox to clear&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338919#post1338919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because quite honestly, a Relentless Variation (Inescapable) that has NO Scar is still objectively worse than Relentless Variation (Suppressible) that has a 5 Magnitude Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without leaping to the extremes of comparing it to a Magnitude 5 Scar this is objectively and absurdly wrong. \u200bNine of the twenty-eight core Variations that qualify for Relentless Variation are normally Subtle, and many of them come with no real downsides to their constant activation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T21:45:42-07:00","id":1338935,"title":"","content":"I've never seen this level of responsiveness before. Eric is all over the forums and Kickstarter both. Super impressed.<br /> <br /> More potential questions...how does Force Field work with respect to Telekinesis being a Directed variation? Is the 'target' I choose with my instant action essentially the Force Field itself? If so, do I have to spend another Instant Action every turn to keep it up, or does it last until, for example, the end of the scene? If the latter, can I choose to end it early?<br /> <br /> For that matter, I'm a little fuzzy on how targeting works with Directed Variations and targeting in general. Continuing to use Telekinesis as an example, is a target essentially 'affected' as soon as I spend an action to target them, for the rest of the scene? Or do I have to 'refresh' that control every minute/turn?<br /> <br /> How I'm hoping this works, using a Scar Power of 4 for example:<br /> <br /> Cephalist Joe gets in a firefight.<br /> <br /> Turn 1: Joe spends an instant action to activate Telekinesis and uses the free target selection that comes with activation to activate a Force Field<br /> Turn 2: Joe's forcefield is still up, and he decides to telekinetically grapple an opponent using his instant action to direct the Variation.<br /> Turn 3: The forcefield is still up, and one target is still grappled. Joe uses his instant action to direct the variation to grapple another person.<br /> Turn 4: Forcefield up, two people grappled. A third person grappled means we are at our cap of 4 affected targets.<br /> Turn 5: Joe needs to reflexively direct the Variation to deflect some bullets from anti-armor weaponry directed at him that could pierce his forcefield. This activation 'counts' as an affected target, and so he needs to either release one of the enemies from a grapple or lower his forcefield.<br /> <br /> This interpretation is incredibly powerful (balanced by an appropriately powerful Scar, granted), so I'm not sure if I actually have this right. On the flip side, having to direct the Variation to maintain its effects on a given target turn-to-turn would be underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  Removed additional question 10-02-2019, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:03:49-07:00","id":1338938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338931#post1338931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree with you quite strongly on this point, and I think it may be because you are comparing it to Suppressible, while I'm comparing it to other Persistent Scars. For example, Enhanced Speed 4 with Relentless Variation (Inescapable) is showy (more likely to attract conspiracy attention), but Glitch 4 is far more of a hassle than a little conspiracy attention. Perpetual Gigantic 5 comes with a host of problems (ranging from &quot;finding clothes in your size&quot; to &quot;fitting into buildings smaller than airline hangers&quot;), but Conspicuous Appearance 5 reduces you to a chance die on Social actions, gives the conspiracy a +5 bonus to surveillance rolls to find you, <i>and</i> attracts monster hunters unconnected to the Web of Pain. I can envision Inescapable as a standalone Magnitude 2 effect (if the entangled Variation is Overt) that allows you to add a secondary Persistent Scar to increase its Magnitude by the Magnitude of the secondary Scar. But I'm not convinced that not being able to turn off your high-Magnitude superpower is enough of a downside to justify not having any other downside to said superpower. Perpetual Camouflage 5 may complicate your life in some ways, but you're still the Invisible Man, and that means your stealth capabilities beyond what any Baseline could achieve.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK i can see your point there. In that case, i believe it is important that there is a secondary disadvantage to Suppressible. Compared to other Scars in that case, i feel Suppressible is FAR less crippling, as you have the full power of a perpetual variation with limited downsides. I'd personally have Suppressible have BOTH a Controlled (for when you actually Suppress) and a Persistent (Just Generally) in order to properly compare to Inescapable. This seems like a lot, but it feels like the best choice<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, i was probably over-considering how crippling Inescapable is in *most* cases, and under-counting how useful Perpetual vs Toggled can be. However in that case, i feel like Suppressible really needs a second Secondary (Tertiary?) Scar, both a Controlled and a Persistent (maybe their magnitude is averaged or something to make the final magnitude idk). It feels excessive at first Glance, but it feels genuinely like the best option, as right now it feels like Suppressible can really be used to completely skirt around consequences in a way that is just better than Inescapable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:08:05-07:00","id":1338939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338935#post1338935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related, but entirely different question: can Toggled Variations be paired with Controlled Scars? There are a couple of examples of this (Telekinesis + Perilous Variation) but I'm not sure if those are accurate or oversights.<br /> <br /> I thought that Controlled Variations had to be paired with Controlled Scars, but Telekinesis is listed as Toggled, which is a subtype of Persistent (I think?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Asked about this a couple days ago:\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338649#post1338649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make this explicitly clear: The Toggled and Perpetual keywords on a Variation denote how it works <i>if</i> that Variation is entangled with a Persistent Scar, not that it <i>must</i> be a Persistent Variation with that activation method, which is instead covered by notes like the one in Rapid Healing, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338656#post1338656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:11:54-07:00","id":1338940,"title":"","content":"Re Relentless conversation<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13001_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13001\" data-vbnamecard=\"13001\">SdeSpencer</a> , I certainly understand your point, but I'm not sure that the other point is coming through to you.<br /> I accept that Suppressible is inherently more advantageous; you have been successful in making that point. Having that option to bail out of your power is better from an &quot;I don't want to get screwed&quot; standpoint. But (more advantageous) better does not equal (more interesting story) better. Playing a character who can't just stop being a squirrel when my best friend is dying in the next room because I can't turn this damn doorknob might be the story I want to tell. Having the choice to turn it off changes the dynamic significantly.<br /> <br /> I get that a drawback &quot;should&quot; have a corresponding benefit, because that is how we players think of these things. However, I'd encourage you to think of your scar/variation entanglements as holistic storytelling devices rather than a separate list of powers and flaws. Those two things might not seem like they have anything to do with each other, but consider what those bastards DID to you. It makes your life really hard. They're STILL after you. They need to pay for it. That's the core of the story these mechanics want to tell. Figuring out how to avoid getting screwed is kinda headed in the wrong direction. Setting yourself up to get screwed on terms you think is interesting is more on point. It's not about the beats you get when it happens; it's about what kind of squirrel do you want to be. Are you the one who changes into human form and opens that door or the one who swears revenge as your friend takes their last breath?<br /> That's my take.<br /> <br /> Re Hybrid Form<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Did you realize that you don't &quot;pay&quot; separately for the variations nested under Hybrid too? For example, a starting character with Hybrid 5 could put two 4s or three 3s under it for 5 points of variation.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: I'm not sure on this, but you could probably entangle hybrid form with a mag 4 scar if you used your scar-free point. That's a lot of bang for your buck if that's what you're after. (And yes, I'm crapping all over my above &quot;but the story!&quot; comments with this note. I just want to make sure you all don't make the same assumptions about this variation that I did. I'm a dirty hypocrite. You're welcome.)<br /> <br /> Relentless Mimicry allows you to hide other scars and the entangled variations, which is awesome, but purchasing the variation doesn't buy you those powers. It also has its own scar in addition to the hidden variations' scars, as opposed to Hybrid's variations' being scar free. Mimicry's scar also is &quot;on&quot; when the powers are off rather than hybrid's which is &quot;on&quot; when the powers are on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:22:55-07:00","id":1338941,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Hybrid form - can Deviants with Adaptations that let them boost their Variation Magnitudes boost the ones that come packaged with it, or can they only boost the ones their 'native' Variations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:23:41-07:00","id":1338942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338940#post1338940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re Hybrid Form<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Did you realize that you don't &quot;pay&quot; separately for the variations nested under Hybrid too? For example, a starting character with Hybrid 5 could put two 4s or three 3s under it for 5 points of variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one of the things I was saying about it, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sidenote: I'm not sure on this, but you could probably entangle hybrid form with a mag 4 scar if you used your scar-free point. That's a lot of bang for your buck if that's what you're after. (And yes, I'm crapping all over my above &quot;but the story!&quot; comments with this note. I just want to make sure you all don't make the same assumptions about this variation that I did. I'm a dirty hypocrite. You're welcome.) </div> </div> </div>I can do you one better: Making Hybrid Form Relentless with the appropriate Origin cuts this down to a two-dot discount, which (among other options) neatly fits the special consideration for Power Failure in so you can have a five-dot Hybrid Form whose principal drawback for all its attached powers is that you need a limiter to not be constantly drawing attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:32:18-07:00","id":1338944,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that the original approach of treating Relentless as a Deviation might be simpler: apply it to a Persistent Scar to make it something that you can't turn off, with the Suppressible version requiring you to define a Controlled (or Involuntary?) Scar that you use to suppress it and the Inescapable version just counting as a more severe Deviation. Call it a +2 Deviation if it's Inescapable, and a +1 Deviation if it's Suppressible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:49:06-07:00","id":1338945,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(I\u2019m tired and this is just at the general collective world at this point)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You know what really simple, direct example. You have 3 magnitude Camouflage (A Subtle, Easy Example Variation).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 1: You pick Relentless Variation (Suppressible [Unstable Variation]), and then never Suppress it. You get all the advantages and disadvantages of Perpetual Camouflage, and No Downsides besides those already innate to Perpetual Camouflage. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(You also, if you really need to, have the option to take a medium instability for getting rid of it for a scene, which is a steep price to pay, but the option being there is nice)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 2: You pick Relentless Variation (Inescapable [Sensory Deprivation]). You get all the advantages and disadvantages of Perpetual Camouflage, but also are permanently Deaf.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(You also don't have the Nice, if costly option to bail out, though you were never going to use it)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Other options, for Posterity\u2019s Sake)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 3: You pick Unstable Variation. You get none of the advantages or disadvantages of even a persistent variation, but you can choose to activate Camouflage for the scene for a medium instability. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Option 4: You pick Sensory Deprivation. You can turn Camouflage on for the scene at no penalty, but you are Deaf. However, you do not get the advantages and disadvantages of Perpetual Camouflage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All of these are different in character concept of course, and I can\u2019t really say if 3 or 4 are better, and I honestly can\u2019t say if 2 is better or worse than them either. However, I can say with fairly large personal certainty that 1 is better than 2 or 3 (and presumably 4, though it\u2019s hard to compare them). </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338940#post1338940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re Relentless conversation</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338940#post1338940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I certainly understand your point, but I'm not sure that the other point is coming through to you.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I accept that Suppressible is inherently more advantageous; you have been successful in making that point. Having that option to bail out of your power is better from an &quot;I don't want to get screwed&quot; standpoint. But (more advantageous) better does not equal (more interesting story) better. Playing a character who can't just stop being a squirrel when my best friend is dying in the next room because I can't turn this damn doorknob might be the story I want to tell. Having the choice to turn it off changes the dynamic significantly.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I get that a drawback &quot;should&quot; have a corresponding benefit, because that is how we players think of these things. However, I'd encourage you to think of your scar/variation entanglements as holistic storytelling devices rather than a separate list of powers and flaws. Those two things might not seem like they have anything to do with each other, but consider what those bastards DID to you. It makes your life really hard. They're STILL after you. They need to pay for it. That's the core of the story these mechanics want to tell. Figuring out how to avoid getting screwed is kinda headed in the wrong direction. Setting yourself up to get screwed on terms you think is interesting is more on point. It's not about the beats you get when it happens; it's about what kind of squirrel do you want to be. Are you the one who changes into human form and opens that door or the one who swears revenge as your friend takes their last breath?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That's my take.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I want to state that I understand this idea. I really, truly do. And believe me that if if the issues I mention are never addressed (and Eric is perfectly within his rights to ignore my complaints), i will STILL make MANY characters with Inescapable variations (in fact, I find myself agreeing that Inescapable isn\u2019t incorrectly balanced as is), I just worry about being able to properly design characters when theoretically \u201cstraight up better options\u201d are given. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">My goal isn\u2019t to demean these options or to imply one is dumb for picking them, even as is, and i agree that they are great narritive tools for characters, I just worry how they will function in the long term with these sort of things still really easy to see. They are issues that often get in the way of my enjoyment of character creation occasionally, and I wanted to talk about them because they still feel quite open.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338944#post1338944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking that the original approach of treating Relentless as a Deviation might be simpler: apply it to a Persistent Scar to make it something that you can't turn off, with the Suppressible version requiring you to define a Controlled (or Involuntary?) Scar that you use to suppress it and the Inescapable version just counting as a more severe Deviation. Call it a +2 Deviation if it's Inescapable, and a +1 Deviation if it's Suppressible.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I like this idea, though i don\u2019t know how possible it is at this point (and there could certainly be other issues we aren\u2019t thinking about)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","user":"SdeSpencer","date":". 10-02-2019, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:53:32-07:00","id":1338946,"title":"","content":"An observation - Deviants may be the very first splat that's really heavily incentivized to invest in Attributes over nearly anything else, with how big of a role they play in the functionality of Variations. It's good to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:11:40-07:00","id":1338948,"title":"","content":"Your example helps. Option 1 is effectively just option 2 without the scar if you never activate it to turn the power off for the cost. <br /> I suffer from the same trouble you have with optimization feeling \u201ccorrect\u201d and a non-optimal choice feeling wrong somehow. Other kinds of games reward optimization through success that arrives through a competitive ladder or whatever. I do find that it helps to recontextualize success as serving the narrative instead here. If I\u2019m looking forward to getting screwed interestingly, if that\u2019s the goal, then building for it doesn\u2019t seem as non-optimal. Considering my character\u2019s future failures as a net positive is hard, but seems worthwhile to try to work into my mindset for a game with themes like this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:20:43-07:00","id":1338951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338946#post1338946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An observation - Deviants may be the very first splat that's really heavily incentivized to invest in Attributes over nearly anything else, with how big of a role they play in the functionality of Variations. It's good to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good observation. Wait until you try to work out how to balance an involuntary scar with a directed variation that cares about scar power. All three stats can be come into play in the same turn. It\u2019s maddening, especially when your scars can be split up between different stat groups.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure the last CoD game I played it mattered very little what my attributes were. In this game, they are at the top of the list with Acclimation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12709,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","user":"Sir Dragos","date":". 10-02-2019, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:22:14-07:00","id":1338953,"title":"","content":"Taking a closer look at Force Field - it's going to be providing cover with a Durability of 2 most of the time, rarely 3 (which is the maximum it can provide, at Scar Power 5). On the surface, that's great! Bullets that do 1 (2) damage or less can't penetrate it, everything else subtracts 2 (3) from damage. But then, I found this tidbit in the Chronicles core:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the cover is transparent (bulletproof glass, for example), subtract half the cover\u2019s Durability, rounding down. Both the object and the target take any remaining damage. </div> </div> </div>Most forcefields are (presumably) going to be transparent, that means you're going to be subtracting 1 damage at most from attacks that get through, even if you have Scar Power 5. That seems a bit underwhelming, and I'm wondering if it's intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-02-2019, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T23:37:25-07:00","id":1338955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338945#post1338945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Option 2: You pick Relentless Variation (Inescapable [Sensory Deprivation]). You get all the advantages and disadvantages of Perpetual Camouflage, but also are permanently Deaf.<br /> (You also don't have the Nice, if costly option to bail out, though you were never going to use it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Option 2b: You pick Relentless Variation (Inescapable [Bane; Common, Draining). You get all the benefits of Perpetual Camouflage and exposure to a common stimulus reduces its rating by one dot per minute of exposure for the rest of the scene along with suffering mild pseudo-allergic reactions that don't even count as bashing damage, effectively giving yourself a slightly unpleasant form of Power Failure that doesn't require a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T05:44:30-07:00","id":1338978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338934#post1338934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relatedly, I'm not sure I understand the timeline of the Lingering effect as it relates to the normal Magnitude 2 effect; you get the Persistent Deprived Condition if you don't use the Variation for at least a scene once per chapter, but it resolves if you go a full story without using the Variation. Or you can just heal a medium or major Instability, which begets the question of why the first resolution option is even mentioned. Is the arc suggested there &quot;use the Variation often or your withdrawal symptoms will need extensive detox to clear&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338935#post1338935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen this level of responsiveness before. Eric is all over the forums and Kickstarter both. Super impressed.<br /> <br /> More potential questions...how does Force Field work with respect to Telekinesis being a Directed variation? Is the 'target' I choose with my instant action essentially the Force Field itself? If so, do I have to spend another Instant Action every turn to keep it up, or does it last until, for example, the end of the scene? If the latter, can I choose to end it early?<br /> <br /> For that matter, I'm a little fuzzy on how targeting works with Directed Variations and targeting in general. Continuing to use Telekinesis as an example, is a target essentially 'affected' as soon as I spend an action to target them, for the rest of the scene? Or do I have to 'refresh' that control every minute/turn?<br /> <br /> How I'm hoping this works, using a Scar Power of 4 for example:<br /> <br /> Cephalist Joe gets in a firefight.<br /> <br /> Turn 1: Joe spends an instant action to activate Telekinesis and uses the free target selection that comes with activation to activate a Force Field<br /> Turn 2: Joe's forcefield is still up, and he decides to telekinetically grapple an opponent using his instant action to direct the Variation.<br /> Turn 3: The forcefield is still up, and one target is still grappled. Joe uses his instant action to direct the variation to grapple another person.<br /> Turn 4: Forcefield up, two people grappled. A third person grappled means we are at our cap of 4 affected targets.<br /> Turn 5: Joe needs to reflexively direct the Variation to deflect some bullets from anti-armor weaponry directed at him that could pierce his forcefield. This activation 'counts' as an affected target, and so he needs to either release one of the enemies from a grapple or lower his forcefield.<br /> <br /> This interpretation is incredibly powerful (balanced by an appropriately powerful Scar, granted), so I'm not sure if I actually have this right. On the flip side, having to direct the Variation to maintain its effects on a given target turn-to-turn would be underwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The target would be the area you're targeting (unless you're using it to catch a person, in which case they get to contest). Your Cephalist Joe example is correct. To your question on the next page about transparent cover, that's something I caught late, so now it reads: &quot;The force field provides cover as though it were a non-transparent object with Durability equal to half Scar Power (rounded up).&quot;<br /> <br /> Regarding your observation about Attributes, that's intentional. Raising Attributes is a good use of Experiences for a Deviant in a way that it often isn't in other CofD games. In many ways, it's often a better option than buying new Variations, which can be a bit of a trap, since more (or more powerful) Variations mean more (and worse) Scars, and more Scars mean more (or worse) complications. Getting a ton of nasty Scars can be just as bad for your life expectancy as accumulating too much Instability. Raising Scar Attributes lets you &quot;level up&quot; a Variation in an often quite significant way, without any drawback - on the contrary, in fact, since you also have the benefits of an increased Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T07:13:02-07:00","id":1338986,"title":"","content":"Can i ask another two? Thanks for the previous!<br /> <br /> 1) When my accidental imbued get a new scar from instability... and want to entangle it with a new variation... at what magnitue the variation start? At par with the magnitude of the Scar? At 1?<br /> <br /> 2) If my pc had a Scar of Magnitude 3 and an entangled Variation of Magnitude 2... how much px must pay for get a new Variation of Magnitude 2? 8 Px? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T07:18:59-07:00","id":1338987,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be anything preventing nesting Hybrid Forms within Hybrid Form. I wonder if that's intentional or not. The benefits aren't huge but can definitely be used to gain more Variation Magnitude dots than otherwise. I do like it because then I can have a Hybrid Form with one high Magnitude Variation and multiple low Magnitude Variations without feeling like I'm wasting potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T07:23:42-07:00","id":1338989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338955#post1338955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Option 2b: You pick Relentless Variation (Inescapable [Bane; Common, Draining). You get all the benefits of Perpetual Camouflage and exposure to a common stimulus reduces its rating by one dot per minute of exposure for the rest of the scene along with suffering mild pseudo-allergic reactions that don't even count as bashing damage, effectively giving yourself a slightly unpleasant form of Power Failure that doesn't require a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats... Besides the point and honestly I\u2019d say also falls under the catchall of \u201cCertain combinations of Variations, Scars, and Deviations might render the Scars\u2019 intended drawbacks ineffective\u201d and call that ignoring the main purpose of Inescapable.<br /> <br /> Beyond that of course, that\u2019s making a specific build designed to ignore the effects of Relentless variation, which is specifically something that I was trying to avoid, as it confuses the point in general. I assume that if someone picked Relentless Variation (Inescapable), they don\u2019t want it to be able to turn off their power.<br /> <br /> Beyond all that of course, I specifically stated that Inescapable is pretty ok as is, the thing that I actually have issue with is Suppressible, which is very powerful with very few downsides as is (again, none if you never turn it on). Arguing that I\u2019m not properly presenting Inescapable kinda isn\u2019t arguing my point, and i feel like your goal is just kinda shoving a specific build someone you can make in my face and saying it proves your point (which I\u2019m not even sure of right now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","user":"SdeSpencer","date":". 10-02-2019, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T07:29:52-07:00","id":1338991,"title":"","content":"There's probably something I've missed, as I have a bad habit of just skimming these in chunks and mentally stitching it together rather than in-depth sitting down to read it all the way through, but I'm wondering about Scars that impose a Tilt or Condition as a cost for activating a Variation (Deterioration, for instance). If they give you a Tilt/Condition that lasts beyond the scene (Deterioration 3+ with Lingering, to continue the example), and the Remade is still suffering from it in a later scene, can they still activate the Variation? Is the cost considered already paid, or is it more like 'your arm can't exactly fall off again so you can't pay any further cost' and are therefore out of luck?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T07:54:38-07:00","id":1338993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338955#post1338955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Option 2b: You pick Relentless Variation (Inescapable [Bane; Common, Draining). You get all the benefits of Perpetual Camouflage and exposure to a common stimulus reduces its rating by one dot per minute of exposure for the rest of the scene along with suffering mild pseudo-allergic reactions that don't even count as bashing damage, effectively giving yourself a slightly unpleasant form of Power Failure that doesn't require a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you have to add to or augment a power to bring it to the level of what is supposed to be an equal alternative, all you're doing is proving the imbalance. When someone says 2!=3, going &quot;just add 1 to it!&quot; doesn't change the inequality presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":".  Grammar 10-02-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T08:20:48-07:00","id":1338996,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to end Mimicry early, or is the inability to do so part of the opportunity cost of using the Variation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T08:44:06-07:00","id":1338998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338996#post1338996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to end Mimicry early, or is the inability to do so part of the opportunity cost of using the Variation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should work just like other toggled variations: you can end it as an instant action or it ends normally at the end of the scene. I can't think why it would work differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T09:57:19-07:00","id":1339010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338987#post1338987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn't seem to be anything preventing nesting Hybrid Forms within Hybrid Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second paragraph of the description combined with &quot;When Hybrid Form activates, so do all its nested Variations&quot; indicates that you aren't going to be able to combine multiple times the usual Scar load of Variations into a single form by nesting other mutually exclusive forms into a package that is by design built for mutually inclusive powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T10:02:02-07:00","id":1339012,"title":"","content":"Is there going to be a fiction anthology for Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T10:06:01-07:00","id":1339014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339010#post1339010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second paragraph of the description combined with &quot;When Hybrid Form activates, so do all its nested Variations&quot; indicates that you aren't going to be able to combine multiple times the usual Scar load of Variations into a single form by nesting other mutually exclusive forms into a package that is by design built for mutually inclusive powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I had missed &quot;only one can be active at a time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T10:09:53-07:00","id":1339015,"title":"","content":"I noticed an issue in Sensor Array 3, it refers to supersonic and subsonic sound, these terms mean faster than sound and slower than sound respectively. The correct terms are ultrasound and infrasound, which refer to sound with frequencies higher and lower, respectively, than a human can hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T10:59:01-07:00","id":1339021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339015#post1339015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed an issue in Sensor Array 3, it refers to supersonic and subsonic sound, these terms mean faster than sound and slower than sound respectively. The correct terms are ultrasound and infrasound, which refer to sound with frequencies higher and lower, respectively, than a human can hear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science! Good catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:11:20-07:00","id":1339058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338986#post1338986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i ask another two? Thanks for the previous!<br /> <br /> 1) When my accidental imbued get a new scar from instability... and want to entangle it with a new variation... at what magnitue the variation start? At par with the magnitude of the Scar? At 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Variation starts at whatever Magnitude you want it at, up to the Magnitude of the entangled Scar.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) If my pc had a Scar of Magnitude 3 and an entangled Variation of Magnitude 2... how much px must pay for get a new Variation of Magnitude 2? 8 Px? </div> </div> </div>You don't pay Experiences to add permanent Magnitude to an existing Variation. The cost is simply that you have to have a high enough Magnitude on the entangled Scar to support the new Magnitude of Variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:28:47-07:00","id":1339063,"title":"","content":"Haven\u2019t caught up in the thread yet, but has anyone mentioned the Pretender yet?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Pretender_(TV_series\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_...der_(TV_series</a>)<br /> <br /> It\u2019s... less horrible than Deviant is by default, but one thing it does that could be useful for a Deviant game is looking at how relatively \u201cnot-horrible\u201d people can end up working for a evil conspiracy that abducts and tortures people and the little things they do to fight back. It\u2019s also an amazing example of the Living Progenitor merit and just how weird the relationship between the Deviant and the Progenitor can be.<br /> <br /> First two seasons are up on Amazon for 10$ apiece if anyone is interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:33:49-07:00","id":1339064,"title":"","content":"Oh, just so I\u2019m clear. If I have the Conspicuous Appearance Scar at 2 with the Identifier Deviation at 2 attached to it, then it\u2019s effectively a level 4 Scar for all purposes, right? It can entangle three level 2 Variations and it would need Mimicry 4 to suppress it, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:35:56-07:00","id":1339065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339058#post1339058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Variation starts at whatever Magnitude you want it at, up to the Magnitude of the entangled Scar.<br /> You don't pay Experiences to add permanent Magnitude to an existing Variation. The cost is simply that you have to have a high enough Magnitude on the entangled Scar to support the new Magnitude of Variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, nice! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:45:13-07:00","id":1339066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339064#post1339064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, just so I\u2019m clear. If I have the Conspicuous Appearance Scar at 2 with the Identifier Deviation at 2 attached to it, then it\u2019s effectively a level 4 Scar for all purposes, right? It can entangle three level 2 Variations and it would need Mimicry 4 to suppress it, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's correct.<br /> And then you sleep with one eye open after activating any of your variations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:48:29-07:00","id":1339067,"title":"","content":"As regards Batman, I had a thought for a Deviant chronicle.<br /> <br /> Arkham Asylum is a place where people go to get better. And many of them do. They employ accredited, ethical doctors and psychologists who actually care about their patients and help them get better.<br /> <br /> It makes great cover.<br /> <br /> The Conspiracy is mostly concentrated in the High Security Ward for the Criminally Insane, as few care about the people who end up there and all the security means its very easy to hide things from outsiders, but they have their hooks into other staff members. That way they can provoke an incident to get a promising candidate transferred to the Criminal Ward with relative ease. Add in a few corrupt judges and the Conspiracy is hardly ever short of raw material.<br /> <br /> Their \u201csuccesses\u201d stay locked away for further study ...unless they\u2019ve \u201cescaped\u201d in order for the Conspiracy to watch the results of their most recent experiments. Once they\u2019re done gathering data, they let loose their Devoted hunter to gather up the escapees and bring them \u201chome.\u201d<br /> <br /> After all, he does a hell of a good job, for all that he dresses like a giant Bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T15:04:36-07:00","id":1339070,"title":"","content":"I found another issue, in Paranoia 2, it says &quot;payer&quot; instead of &quot;player&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T15:37:55-07:00","id":1339073,"title":"","content":"How to play a Character That has a Extra-dimisional Being In Their Spine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T15:43:17-07:00","id":1339074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339073#post1339073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to play a Character That has a Extra-dimisional Being In Their Spine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without details on the being, Symbiote and/or Alternate Persona.<br /> <br /> Back the kickstarter and have a look over the document.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T15:53:01-07:00","id":1339075,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s the Alternate Persona.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T16:25:43-07:00","id":1339077,"title":"","content":"Back the KS and you'll have an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T16:35:45-07:00","id":1339078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339075#post1339075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the Alternate Persona.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's bad to answer questions. Alternate Persona is one of many Scars, basically drawbacks to your powers. It is basically what it sounds like but there is some additional teeth to it.<br /> <br /> The manuscript is better at describing that in detail but that's what that is in brief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T16:43:33-07:00","id":1339080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339075#post1339075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s the Alternate Persona.?</div> </div> </div> </div>alternate persona is a scar. it's a possible drawback to entangle with a variation. an example would be a chimeric that sometimes is overpowered by his animal instincts.<br /> <br /> symbiote has more depth, it's a Form that enhances your powers AND takes them away if it wants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T16:49:30-07:00","id":1339082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338991#post1338991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's probably something I've missed, as I have a bad habit of just skimming these in chunks and mentally stitching it together rather than in-depth sitting down to read it all the way through, but I'm wondering about Scars that impose a Tilt or Condition as a cost for activating a Variation (Deterioration, for instance). If they give you a Tilt/Condition that lasts beyond the scene (Deterioration 3+ with Lingering, to continue the example), and the Remade is still suffering from it in a later scene, can they still activate the Variation? Is the cost considered already paid, or is it more like 'your arm can't exactly fall off again so you can't pay any further cost' and are therefore out of luck?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can burn through all your limbs and sense organs before getting to that point, but where you go from there is unclear in the text. I don't have an immediate answer, but I'll make sure to address it in the working draft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339012#post1339012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there going to be a fiction anthology for Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like for there to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339015#post1339015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed an issue in Sensor Array 3, it refers to supersonic and subsonic sound, these terms mean faster than sound and slower than sound respectively. The correct terms are ultrasound and infrasound, which refer to sound with frequencies higher and lower, respectively, than a human can hear.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339070#post1339070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found another issue, in Paranoia 2, it says &quot;payer&quot; instead of &quot;player&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typos aren't nearly so embarrassing, but I've fixed this one, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:31:03-07:00","id":1339086,"title":"","content":"Persistent Drawback is (I believe) listed such that it can be any of Mental, Physical, or Social. However, all of the examples (edit: Except one) have it inherit the category of the linked Scar. Is this a requirement?<br /> <br /> More simply: Can a Persistent Drawback of Conspicuous Appearance be tied to Mental Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-02-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:47:13-07:00","id":1339090,"title":"","content":"If there isn\u2019t a note about \u201cSTs, if a player comes to you with a character that you think is broken or overpowered, please discuss it with them and try to work out the issue. That said, you are free to disallow any \u201ctechnically legal\u201d combination of Variations, Scars, and Deviations that you think is problematic,\u201d in the book somewhere, there probably should be.<br /> <br /> As regards the Relentless Scar discussion, I think I found the best \u201cMunchkin\u201d way to show off the problem with Suppressible. For the record, I\u2019m not sure this is technically legal and, even if it is, please don\u2019t do it.<br /> <br /> So you take Computer Aided Processing at 3 and entangle it with Relentless with a secondary Scar of Missing Limb. For the purposes of this example the Scar Power is 3.<br /> <br /> If I take it as Inescapable, then I get 16 free merit dots ...but I have no arms.<br /> <br /> If I take it as Suppressible, then I get 16 free merit dots.<br /> <br /> ...That\u2019s it, that\u2019s what happens. Sure, I theoretically could decide I wanted to stop getting the merit dots and make my arms fall off at the same time, but...why would you do that?<br /> <br /> (This assumes that the Relentless means the gained merits keep going after the end of the scene when they\u2019d normally turn off.)<br /> <br /> Basically the problem isn\u2019t Inescapable, it\u2019s that Suppressible is giving you a Scar free Variation as long as you don\u2019t mind it being always on and there are enough Variations that aren\u2019t so bad as always on that you can run into problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T18:11:49-07:00","id":1339092,"title":"","content":"This. That's why I suggested putting it back as a Deviation for Persistent Scars: if there isn't a Persistent Scar in effect as you use the Variation, it's easily abused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T18:14:29-07:00","id":1339093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339086#post1339086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persistent Drawback is (I believe) listed such that it can be any of Mental, Physical, or Social. However, all of the examples (edit: Except one) have it inherit the category of the linked Scar. Is this a requirement?<br /> <br /> More simply: Can a Persistent Drawback of Conspicuous Appearance be tied to Mental Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a common trope, too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://www.startrek.com/sites/default/files/styles/content_full/public/images/2019-07/c8ffe9a587b126f152ed3d89a146b445.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px