 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/mega-mind/images/4/45/HurtMegamind.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T19:22:21-07:00","id":1339101,"title":"","content":"Armed and Extremely Dangerous is a super fucking awesome Merit.<br /> <br /> I'm not clear on why it requires mundane physical fighting capacity, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T19:42:23-07:00","id":1339104,"title":"","content":"Still watching the Relentless Variation discussion with interest. Will renew my participation a little later, as I'm currently multi-tasking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339101#post1339101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armed and Extremely Dangerous is a super fucking awesome Merit.<br /> <br /> I'm not clear on why it requires mundane physical fighting capacity, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Others said the same, and I agree. I also noticed it lacked a mechanical effect, so I've added one:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Armed and Extremely Dangerous (\u2022\u2022\u2022) (Overt)</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Deviant<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character had an unusually bloody escape from her conspiracy. Whether she gunned her way through legions of guards and scientists with a stolen automatic weapon, or shredded the facility with nothing but a scalpel and a pair of forceps, she is a fugitive in every sense of the word. Her conspiracy treats her at best with extreme caution, and at worst as a bogeyman, a tale that they tell to new recruits and at bars. Any members of the conspiracy your character meets will either call for backup or flee outright.<br /> Agents of a conspiracy who encounter you without having prepared themselves for the confrontation suffer the Beaten Down Tilt (p. XX) when they realize their predicament, unless they outnumber you and your allies by at least the rating of your highest Magnitude Variation.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> While your conspiracy will only rarely send agents to collect you, when it does, it will send well-equipped, heavily armed hit squads, ready to bring her in dead or alive, regardless of the casualties they might suffer. Agents sent to engage you (or your cohort) as part of a conspiracy action are immune to the Beaten Down Tilt in the current scene. No character may benefit from both this Merit and Prized Experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:23:02-07:00","id":1339109,"title":"","content":"Let me review what I perceive as the current state of the conversation regarding Relentless Variation:<br /> <br /> It appears that Inescapable is largely doing what it is supposed to do. It works out to a +1 Deviation on a Persistent Variation when applied to an Overt Scar, or a +0 Deviation on a Subtle Scar. The increased conspiracy scrutiny, together with the disruptiveness of certain especially \u201cnoisy\u201d Variations (such as Gigantic) is usually on par with other +1 Magnitude Deviations. In some cases, like Gigantic, it is arguably worth +2 (although probably not so much so that an exception is strictly necessary).<br /> <br /> Suppressible seems to be the main cause of concern. Yes, there are cases where an Overt Variation will cause enough of a headache that you\u2019ll want to periodically suppress it to avoid attracting undue attention to yourself (Gigantic being Exhibit A in this category), but there are cases (both Subtle and Overt) where there is no real reason to suppress the Variation If Overt, the +1 Magnitude effect more than makes up for the increased conspiracy attention and the Scar Resistance roll to suppress (which is still not something that is needed all that frequently), and if Subtle, it basically creates an entirely Scar-free Variation (which isn\u2019t my intention). I tried to cover many such cases with Perpetual, but it doesn\u2019t capture all of these.<br /> <br /> I maintain that both versions, conceptually, have a place and lead to compelling character concepts, but I want to head off the most obvious excesses. Before I get too deep into that process, I want to make sure I\u2019m accurately capturing the main concerns about this Scar. Am I accurately representing what folks are saying are the problems with this Scar? Are there any concerns that I\u2019m missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:38:38-07:00","id":1339112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339109#post1339109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any concerns that I\u2019m missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I noticed both in the course of the discussion and in the course of checking over the preview is that it's not entirely clear how some Persistent Tiered Variations interact with the Scar (most obviously Gigantic, once again); there seems to be an assumption in these cases that Relentless Variation doubles as Wild Variation or an approximation thereof, but &quot;you're never not huge&quot; is as true at Magnitude 1 as at Magnitude 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:55:13-07:00","id":1339113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339104#post1339104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Others said the same, and I agree. I also noticed it lacked a mechanical effect, so I've added one:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Armed and Extremely Dangerous (\u2022\u2022\u2022) (Overt)</span><br /> <br /> No character may benefit from both this Merit and Prized Experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>First the secrecy concerning Electric Fish and now this cruel limitation. Deviant is Suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:56:36-07:00","id":1339114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339112#post1339112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I noticed both in the course of the discussion and in the course of checking over the preview is that it's not entirely clear how some Persistent Tiered Variations interact with the Scar (most obviously Gigantic, once again); there seems to be an assumption in these cases that Relentless Variation doubles as Wild Variation or an approximation thereof, but &quot;you're never not huge&quot; is as true at Magnitude 1 as at Magnitude 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCould you explain what it is about Gigantic that wouldn't work with Relentless Variation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:08:21-07:00","id":1339116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339113#post1339113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First the secrecy concerning Electric Fish and now this cruel limitation. Deviant is Suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div>The limitation existed previously, albeit in a different way. Armed and Extremely Dangerous wasn't allowed if you had the Living Progenitor Merit, and Prized Experiment had Living Progenitor as a Prerequisite. The two Merits no longer interact with Living Progenitor in this way (because I can see situations where you escaped violently without your Progenitor dying in the process, or where your Progenitor isn't what makes you a Prized Experiment), but the two effects are still somewhat contradictory. Did you have an argument for why they should be allowed together?<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Electric Fish, I think someone owes us a Part 2 of its backstory/dossier. *smirk*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339114#post1339114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bCould you explain what it is about Gigantic that wouldn't work with Relentless Variation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works just fine, although it makes a great example of a Variation that feels like a legitimate Scar when made Perpetual. Unless I badly misunderstand, Satchel is saying that, because Gigantic is Tiered, it is possible to become anywhere from Size 6 to the maximum Size allowed by the Variation's Magnitude. Just because you have Gigantic 5 as a Relentless Variation doesn't mean you're confined to the largest possible Size - or at least there is nothing written in the Scar that supports that assumption (which a lot of people are making regarding Tiered Variations entangled with Relentless Variation). It's a useful observation, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:17:45-07:00","id":1339117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339114#post1339114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain what it is about Gigantic that wouldn't work with Relentless Variation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it doesn't work with Relentless Variation, it's just that pretty much all the discussion of it seems to assume that the effect operates purely at the highest level \u2014 and &quot;the Variation only operates at its highest level&quot; is a specific separate Deviation distinct from its being made a Perpetual effect. You lose more than just the ability to stop using the Variation at that point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> Separate question about Gigantic, unrelated to Relentless: is it intentional that the Strength and Stamina boosts scale independently of the character's current Size while the Variation is active, such that a character with Gigantic 5 can be Size 6 and receive a +3 bonus to their effective Strength and Stamina, or is that bonus supposed to correspond to the Magnitude of their active Size boost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:21:54-07:00","id":1339119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339109#post1339109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me review what I perceive as the current state of the conversation regarding Relentless Variation:<br /> <br /> It appears that Inescapable is largely doing what it is supposed to do. It works out to a +1 Deviation on a Persistent Variation when applied to an Overt Scar, or a +0 Deviation on a Subtle Scar. The increased conspiracy scrutiny, together with the disruptiveness of certain especially \u201cnoisy\u201d Variations (such as Gigantic) is usually on par with other +1 Magnitude Deviations. In some cases, like Gigantic, it is arguably worth +2 (although probably not so much so that an exception is strictly necessary).<br /> <br /> Suppressible seems to be the main cause of concern. Yes, there are cases where an Overt Variation will cause enough of a headache that you\u2019ll want to periodically suppress it to avoid attracting undue attention to yourself (Gigantic being Exhibit A in this category), but there are cases (both Subtle and Overt) where there is no real reason to suppress the Variation If Overt, the +1 Magnitude effect more than makes up for the increased conspiracy attention and the Scar Resistance roll to suppress (which is still not something that is needed all that frequently), and if Subtle, it basically creates an entirely Scar-free Variation (which isn\u2019t my intention). I tried to cover many such cases with Perpetual, but it doesn\u2019t capture all of these.<br /> <br /> I maintain that both versions, conceptually, have a place and lead to compelling character concepts, but I want to head off the most obvious excesses. Before I get too deep into that process, I want to make sure I\u2019m accurately capturing the main concerns about this Scar. Am I accurately representing what folks are saying are the problems with this Scar? Are there any concerns that I\u2019m missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the main person who's been arguing this, i agree and think you mostly got it straight on the head. Suppressible is definitely the main point of concern. The main issue is that yeah, it can basically create a straight up Scar-Free Variation, and is just an actively better option than inescapable in both cases of Overt and Subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:23:14-07:00","id":1339120,"title":"","content":"I was kidding, but I can imagine a scenario where a deviant is both a prized and valued experiment as well as extremely dangerous.<br /> <br /> However, I certainly wouldn't want to be part of that Conspiracy's retrieval team. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Captain, the target can withstand tank rounds without a scratch, shoots lasers from his eyes, and is en expert in melee fish combat, why are we only being issued tasers?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T21:24:18-07:00","id":1339121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339117#post1339117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separate question about Gigantic, unrelated to Relentless: is it intentional that the Strength and Stamina boosts scale independently of the character's current Size while the Variation is active, such that a character with Gigantic 5 can be Size 6 and receive a +3 bonus to their effective Strength and Stamina, or is that bonus supposed to correspond to the Magnitude of their active Size boost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. It should be based on actual Size. It'll be fun finding a way to word that, but I'll figure it out and update.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339120#post1339120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was kidding, but I can imagine a scenario where a deviant is both a prized and valued experiment as well as extremely dangerous.<br /> <br /> However, I certainly wouldn't want to be part of that Conspiracy's retrieval team.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Captain, the target can withstand tank rounds without a scratch, shoots lasers from his eyes, and is en expert in melee fish combat, why are we only being issued tasers?&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>*laughs* That would indeed be the worst job in the Web of Pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-03-2019, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T22:34:58-07:00","id":1339127,"title":"","content":"It'd be in genre for a conspiracy to seek to test a Deviant in that way, or to push them to get stronger for some nebulous reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T22:39:36-07:00","id":1339128,"title":"","content":"Or they were a rare fluke and the Deviant killed the lab assistants who performed the experiment on them and destroyed the critical bits of research notes that differentiates them from countless failures when they escaped, so the Conspiracy can't create another without studying them to find out why they were a success when the other test subjects died horribly.<br /> <br /> So despite how dangerous they are they can't afford to let them die before they can study them.<br /> <br /> They could still send crazy high skill soldiers with high tech nonlethal weapons. Like rapid hardening glue fired from some sort of military grade squirt guns to restrain them or powerful anesthetics (and an anesthesiologist waiting in the van to stabilize them). Plus they can have regular guns to use on any allies, but are informed that if they kill the subject they will suffer a fate far worse than death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-03-2019, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T22:48:58-07:00","id":1339129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339128#post1339128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could still send crazy high skill soldiers with high tech nonlethal weapons. Like rapid hardening glue fired from some sort of military grade squirt guns to restrain them or powerful anesthetics (and an anesthesiologist waiting in the van to stabilize them). Plus they can have regular guns to use on any allies, but are informed that if they kill the subject they will suffer a fate far worse than death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Task Force Valkyrie has entered the Deviant game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T00:28:46-07:00","id":1339135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339082#post1339082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typos aren't nearly so embarrassing, but I've fixed this one, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another one I stumbled upon in a review, maybe a little more embarrassing:<br /> <br /> The Introduction, under the Conspiracies heading, describes Remade held imprisoned but provided luxuries as living in a &quot;guilted cage.&quot; You might want to gild that cage instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T00:46:05-07:00","id":1339138,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this question has already been answered, but does anyone know if a Variation attached to the Disfiguring Scar deviation alters it in relation to their Origins? If I had Carapace attached to Amnesia with Disfiguring Scar (which is a build of mine I am pondering over), would Carapace no longer be available for an Epimorph to bolster with their starting bonus to a Subtle Variation since, well, it\u2019s not subtle anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T04:14:46-07:00","id":1339154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339135#post1339135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another one I stumbled upon in a review, maybe a little more embarrassing:<br /> <br /> The Introduction, under the Conspiracies heading, describes Remade held imprisoned but provided luxuries as living in a &quot;guilted cage.&quot; You might want to gild that cage instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. That's the sort of typo that the Manuscript Gnomes hide in <i>every</i> large manuscript whenever we're not looking.I've fixed this one, though. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339138#post1339138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this question has already been answered, but does anyone know if a Variation attached to the Disfiguring Scar deviation alters it in relation to their Origins? If I had Carapace attached to Amnesia with Disfiguring Scar (which is a build of mine I am pondering over), would Carapace no longer be available for an Epimorph to bolster with their starting bonus to a Subtle Variation since, well, it\u2019s not subtle anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably wouldn't allow that combination during character creation, but I see no reason that Disfiguring Scar couldn't be applied later if the Scar's Magnitude increased (potentially allowing a permanent increase to Carapace).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T04:43:05-07:00","id":1339157,"title":"","content":"Just want to post again to throw a salute to Eric Z., who as other folks have mentioned earlier, is doing an <i>amazing</i> job keeping up with so much feedback here and in the Kickstarter comments, not just to answer questions or catch small errors but give serious design thought to situations like the Suppressible Relentless Variation Scar. (Look at all that capitalization!) Gotta be riding high on the feeling of the work you were excited to show people finally seeing daylight, but even on top of that high, things have got to be hectic for you doing this, man. I'm impressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T06:54:06-07:00","id":1339167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339154#post1339154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably wouldn't allow that combination during character creation, but I see no reason that Disfiguring Scar couldn't be applied later if the Scar's Magnitude increased (potentially allowing a permanent increase to Carapace).</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, a few questions about the Scar-free dot, some of which are just confirmatory:<br /> 1. Can the Scar-free dot raise a Variation's Magnitude above its attached Scar's Magnitude? (Example of character creation suggests yes.)<br /> 2. Can the Scar-free dot create an exception to the rule for entangling multiple Variations with a single Scar such that a Scar of Magnitude N is supporting a Variation of Magnitude N (with the dot) and a Variation of Magnitude N-1, or an N-1 and two N-2s, and so on down the line? (e.g. can I have Tabula Rasa 4 attached to Boneless 4 and Camouflage 3 as long as Boneless used the bonus dot from Origin?)<br /> 3. Can the Scar-free dot be reassigned to an appropriate other Variation or used to further increase its initial Variation's Magnitude if its entangled Scar increases in Magnitude permanently, or can the free dot from Origin be &quot;lost&quot; in this manner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:03:42-07:00","id":1339181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339167#post1339167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, a few questions about the Scar-free dot, some of which are just confirmatory:<br /> 1. Can the Scar-free dot raise a Variation's Magnitude above its attached Scar's Magnitude? (Example of character creation suggests yes.)<br /> 2. Can the Scar-free dot create an exception to the rule for entangling multiple Variations with a single Scar such that a Scar of Magnitude N is supporting a Variation of Magnitude N (with the dot) and a Variation of Magnitude N-1, or an N-1 and two N-2s, and so on down the line? (e.g. can I have Tabula Rasa 4 attached to Boneless 4 and Camouflage 3 as long as Boneless used the bonus dot from Origin?)<br /> 3. Can the Scar-free dot be reassigned to an appropriate other Variation or used to further increase its initial Variation's Magnitude if its entangled Scar increases in Magnitude permanently, or can the free dot from Origin be &quot;lost&quot; in this manner?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes. Essentially, the Variation counts as Magnitude 3 for the purposes of entanglement but has the mechanical effects of Magnitude 4.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm having trouble seeing a situation where this might happen. If you have, say, Superhuman Strength 5 entangled with Lying Eyes 4, and Instability causes you to raise Lying Eyes to 5, you now have the capacity to entangle a second Scar of up to Magnitude 4 with Lying Eyes. If you have Superhuman Strength 4 and Lying Eyes 3, and Instability causes you to raise Lying Eyes to 4, you can entangle another Scar with Lying Eyes or increase the Magnitude of Superhuman Strength to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:15:58-07:00","id":1339184,"title":"","content":"There's a lot to process in this preview, but I really like basically everything. So much. . . variation.<br /> <br /> I have some questions, though I think most of them can be answered with a few more rereads and reflection, but I was wondering about something: There are a number of Variations that are pretty open-ended with their effects, and I'm curious if there might be design space for, say, a Deviation that limits what a Remade can do with a power--for instance, Otherworldy Connection to spirits, but only stone spirits, or a Hidden Compartment that can only produce repair tools. Or would that wind up too fiddly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:16:53-07:00","id":1339185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339104#post1339104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Armed and Extremely Dangerous (\u2022\u2022\u2022) (Overt)</span><br /> Whether she gunned her way through legions of guards and scientists with a stolen automatic weapon, or <b>shredded the facility with nothing but a scalpel and a pair of forceps</b>, she is a fugitive in every sense of the word. Her conspiracy treats her at best with extreme caution, and <b>at worst [treated] as a bogeyman</b>, a tale that they tell to new recruits and at bars. Any members of the conspiracy your character meets will either call for backup or flee outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome, straight up V for Vendetta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:32:06-07:00","id":1339187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339184#post1339184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot to process in this preview, but I really like basically everything. So much. . . variation.<br /> <br /> I have some questions, though I think most of them can be answered with a few more rereads and reflection, but I was wondering about something: There are a number of Variations that are pretty open-ended with their effects, and I'm curious if there might be design space for, say, a Deviation that limits what a Remade can do with a power--for instance, Otherworldy Connection to spirits, but only stone spirits, or a Hidden Compartment that can only produce repair tools. Or would that wind up too fiddly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on my list of &quot;missing&quot; Deviations to include in a future supplement, with +1 being a significant restriction (your stone spirits, for example) and +2 being a severe restriction (the characters in Sense8 have Telepathy 5, but it only works on members of their 8-person pod, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:10:05-07:00","id":1339196,"title":"","content":"Revisiting Telekinesis since that's what my upcoming character in a post-Kickstarter pre-release game is going to primarily use:<br /> <br /> If 'grappling' multiple people at once with Telekinesis, is the Deviant allowed to use a maneuver (damage, disarm, etc) on both of them on successful rolls? The answer seems to be clearly yes based on extrapolation from the earlier Cephalist Joe example, but I want to make sure I truly understand.<br /> <br /> Also, to resurface an earlier question - does Persistent Drawback have to inherit the Attribute Category of the linked Scar? It doesn't say that it does, but 90% of the examples do. Maybe that's just because, in 90% of those cases, it made sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T11:45:09-07:00","id":1339221,"title":"","content":"Is there a Variation for having extra limbs or anything? I haven\u2019t seen one other than, say, Lash, but that\u2019s really only for combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T11:54:10-07:00","id":1339224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339221#post1339221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Variation for having extra limbs or anything? I haven\u2019t seen one other than, say, Lash, but that\u2019s really only for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the mechanical effect. Certain interpretations of Brachiation and/or Immunity 1 can manage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T12:36:57-07:00","id":1339228,"title":"","content":"If it isn't particularly helpful for anything, it could also just be a Scar, one that let's you eat while playing video games but a Scar nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Also, so do Clades that aren't Universal or part of your Clade cost more or need bigger Scars? Or is that something that will be covered later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","user":"Geomancer","date":". 10-03-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T13:58:37-07:00","id":1339233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339221#post1339221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Variation for having extra limbs or anything? I haven\u2019t seen one other than, say, Lash, but that\u2019s really only for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25668\" data-vbnamecard=\"25668\">Geomancer</a> that it depends on the effect you want it to have. It could even be both a scar and a variation if you are particularly conspicuous when you have extra legs for an Enhanced Speed variation as a part of your Hybrid Form. <br /> <br /> Personally, I love the idea of defeating arm wrack with Immunity because you have extras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T14:03:48-07:00","id":1339235,"title":"","content":"Additional thing that may merit consideration for Relentless Variation: how the effect interacts with Redundancy or Unpredictable. Does a Cyborg who shuts down some or all of her dots in Flight to recover still attract attention as though Relentless Variation was an Overt Scar? Does a Mutant trading out his Miniaturization for a Lash look different but still odd? Are both of these options just flatly unworkable due to the stipulation that the Variation be always active?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Autocorrect shenanigans 10-03-2019, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T14:18:04-07:00","id":1339236,"title":"","content":"How would you make Taylor Herbert from Worm as a Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T14:29:47-07:00","id":1339241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339228#post1339228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, so do Clades that aren't Universal or part of your Clade cost more or need bigger Scars? Or is that something that will be covered later?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was covered in the Character Creation and Variation Basics chunks of Preview 2: At least half the Magnitude of all your Variation dots has to come from your Clade Variations or Universal Variations at any given time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T15:01:19-07:00","id":1339244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339236#post1339236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you make Taylor Herbert from Worm as a Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see... I'd give her, Immunity (Various Pain Tilts), maybe one or two Lashes, depending on how you want to handle that, personally I'd go with two because she inflicts all kinds of Tilts on her foes, more than can be handled with one variation, maybe a Shadow Self variation for her &quot;clones&quot;. I'd also figure out some kind of clairvoyance variation because of her awareness via insects. Her scars would probably be along the lines of Concentration and possibly Maintenance, as she needs her bugs and if she doesn't keep on top of keeping them fed or if they are wiped out, she doesn't have access to a lot of her abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T15:17:26-07:00","id":1339250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339221#post1339221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Variation for having extra limbs or anything? I haven\u2019t seen one other than, say, Lash, but that\u2019s really only for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what you're going for, you could probably get some mileage out of a reskinned Telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:11:40-07:00","id":1339265,"title":"","content":"One issue I see with Hidden Compartments is, while producing whatever you happen to need is cool, what if I just want a secret compartment to hide a mcguffin we are stealing, or have a holster that a normal search won't find.<br /> <br /> Like a way to just store and hide stuff I already have, not produce new stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:19:28-07:00","id":1339267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339265#post1339265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue I see with Hidden Compartments is, while producing whatever you happen to need is cool, what if I just want a secret compartment to hide a mcguffin we are stealing, or have a holster that a normal search won't find.<br /> <br /> Like a way to just store and hide stuff I already have, not produce new stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you could use it for that, the game description toward it calls for things like pouches. I dont really see the need to have a separate variation so you can just modify it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T17:31:24-07:00","id":1339271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339267#post1339267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure you could use it for that, the game description toward it calls for things like pouches. I dont really see the need to have a separate variation so you can just modify it</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it might work better for what I want to instead take Integrate Technology 2 and integrate a box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-03-2019, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T20:28:15-07:00","id":1339300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339271#post1339271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it might work better for what I want to instead take Integrate Technology 2 and integrate a box.</div> </div> </div> </div>true, whatever floats your boat, both make sense anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T21:29:58-07:00","id":1339304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339271#post1339271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it might work better for what I want to instead take Integrate Technology 2 and integrate a box.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's no need for a box in this equation: Integrate Technology 2 is very specifically the thing you use for secret compartments that aren't narratively convenient sources of gear; it expressly allows you to hide an object irrespective of its function and it has clearly delineated Size restrictions like Hunter 1e's Safehouse Cache Merit.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Integrate Technology, slightly complex question: is it necessary to have the Battery Deviation from that Variation in order to use the Conductivity effect of Electrokinesis offensively without an outside source of electricity, or is there a missing detail in the Power effect for how much electrical damage it can produce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-04-2019, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T21:33:31-07:00","id":1339305,"title":"","content":"Question: so like weird thing, but can you have your own Alternate Persona and/or Symbiote (as in the Variations with a mind) as a Loyalty Touchstone? This is a weird one because I can think of media examples but I can also see why it wouldn\u2019t be allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T22:02:15-07:00","id":1339308,"title":"","content":"Hm, I don't know about mechanically, but there's a lot of fun story stuff you can do with that. Just imagine a brother and sister sharing a body or a needing to be careful in combat because it's not just you at risk of getting hurt. What about the poor symbiote!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T22:06:23-07:00","id":1339309,"title":"","content":"A handful of error-spottings for the collection, in a theme:<br /> <br /> The Chimeric example of Electrokinesis is mechanically illegal in the previewed text, having been entangled with a Scar that explicitly cannot entangle any Directed Variations.<br /> <br /> Creeping Dread and Shadows of the Past say they're Directed in the Variation writeups but not in the Quick Reference chart.<br /> <br /> Odd one out spotted while checking Directed Variations: Pheromones is missing a Perpetual or Toggled keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T23:49:50-07:00","id":1339313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339304#post1339304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's no need for a box in this equation: Integrate Technology 2 is very specifically the thing you use for secret compartments that aren't narratively convenient sources of gear; it expressly allows you to hide an object irrespective of its function and it has clearly delineated Size restrictions like Hunter 1e's Safehouse Cache Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can fit a lot more than 3 size 1 objects in a size 3 box. Also, many objects may not be integratable/safe to integrate.<br /> <br /> A powerful magic item may not be able to be integrated. There could be a small creature you wish to hide/transport for a short time. An amulet might serve as a prison for a trapped malevolent spirit and integrating it may be a very bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T06:26:21-07:00","id":1339348,"title":"","content":"Hey, we got Conspiracy Traits spoiled: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/posts/2642057\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2642057</a><br /> <br /> (Posted this in wrong thread first time around).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T07:12:27-07:00","id":1339366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339313#post1339313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can fit a lot more than 3 size 1 objects in a size 3 box.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's generally not how that system works and making it work that way invites gaming it in a fiction-breaking way. (Also, integrating anything of Size 3 is going to require Scar Power 5, which Superhuman Attribute explicitly doesn't help with.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, many objects may not be integratable/safe to integrate. </div> </div> </div>Nothing about the way the Variation is written suggests this to be the case for anything beyond the Size limit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A powerful magic item may not be able to be integrated. </div> </div> </div>If it's too big or been arbitrarily declared to have that quality, sure, but in general there's nothing to indicate anything like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There could be a small creature you wish to hide/transport for a short time. </div> </div> </div>In which case we're not talking about an object and the thing you want to integrate is a cage or carrier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An amulet might serve as a prison for a trapped malevolent spirit and integrating it may be a very bad idea. </div> </div> </div>There is nothing to suggest that this is, by default, a risk that is not equally present from carrying it on your person or keeping it in an integrated safe.<br /> <br /> You can fiat any number of extra restrictions into the power, but as-written it's a bundled combination of &quot;be better at using tools,&quot; &quot;hide objects/tools/weapons/devices,&quot; &quot;use objects/tools/weapons/devices hands-free,&quot; &quot;supply consumable resources to tools,&quot; and &quot;merge with large machines.&quot; That third one doesn't stipulate that you <i>have</i> to use integrated objects, and in fact that would often defeat the purpose of the second one. It's also able to be skinned as completely nonphysical means, as the Cephalist example indicates, so a Coactive with the Variation could just be putting stuff in a pocket dimension, which doesn't readily suggest many vectors of concern.<br /> <br /> You can definitely make use of packaging/containment around objects, but by default there's nothing about this Overt Variation that makes integrating any given unwrapped object dangerous because of its qualities by default beyond the usual concerns of &quot;if you eat a radioactive thing and you're not immune to radiation, you might have a bad time.&quot; Most things will not need a box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-04-2019, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T08:04:54-07:00","id":1339375,"title":"","content":"I see that Eric is channelling Masahiro Sakurai with that &quot;just kidding&quot; in the last update XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T08:18:26-07:00","id":1339381,"title":"","content":"Just as a heads-up, I might be a bit quiet for the next day or two, as I have to prepare [REDACTED] for Sunday afternoon. I'll circle back around to answer questions once that's handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:45:02-07:00","id":1339394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339308#post1339308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I don't know about mechanically, but there's a lot of fun story stuff you can do with that. Just imagine a brother and sister sharing a body or a needing to be careful in combat because it's not just you at risk of getting hurt. What about the poor symbiote!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah! Jaime Reyes &amp; Khani Da!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T11:34:05-07:00","id":1339419,"title":"","content":"Huh. The Center from the Pretender really maps well onto this system, I think.<br /> <br /> Looks like it\u2019ll be fun to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T14:35:46-07:00","id":1339445,"title":"","content":"How long does the benefit from Omnicompetence last? If it\u2019s just the rest of the scene, I\u2019m not sure how useful having \u201c3 dots in every skill\u201d is. On the other hand, if it lasts for the entire chapter, then you can just have three dots in every skill all the time, which ...I dunno that seems a bit broken maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T14:47:26-07:00","id":1339446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339445#post1339445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does the benefit from Omnicompetence last?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which benefit and how you activate the Variation. Anything that's not the once-per-chapter effects is always on if Persistent, otherwise/anything else lasts for a scene. You can use these effects more frequently by paying the relevant cost from your Clade's second Adaptation each extra time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T22:48:42-07:00","id":1339527,"title":"","content":"Minor thing that seems like a mistake so i'm going to call it out: Hyper-Competence has the Discrete Keyword, which is super weird as that seems to make it get worse as you level in certain ways and it's effects seem very much designed to be Tiered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","user":"SdeSpencer","date":". 10-05-2019, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T23:34:53-07:00","id":1339535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339527#post1339527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor thing that seems like a mistake so i'm going to call it out: Hyper-Competence has the Discrete Keyword, which is super weird as that seems to make it get worse as you level in certain ways and it's effects seem very much designed to be Tiered</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not supposed to be &quot;leveled&quot; and you are not obligated to raise a Variation's Magnitude. If you want a bigger dicepool with the chosen Skill then you raise Scar Power at Magnitude 2; the other Magnitudes' effects are separate benefits in the same way that having Immunity at three dots does not imply having Immunity at one or two dots.<br /> <br /> You want to more easily get exceptional successes with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 1.<br /> <br /> You want to be rolling more dice with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 2.<br /> <br /> You want to be failing fewer rolls with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 3.<br /> <br /> I don't know that anything breaks from allowing multiple purchases for the same Skill at different Magnitudes, or adding a Deviation that makes it Tiered, or making it a full five-dot spread where Magnitude 3-5 lets you mix and match the preceding levels' options, but it's very clearly not a Tiered effect when its effects are all different Perpetual dice bonuses and the Variation maxes out at Magnitude 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T23:49:53-07:00","id":1339536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339446#post1339446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends which benefit and how you activate the Variation. Anything that's not the once-per-chapter effects is always on if Persistent, otherwise/anything else lasts for a scene. You can use these effects more frequently by paying the relevant cost from your Clade's second Adaptation each extra time.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do I tell if something is Persistent or not? It has the Perpetual tag, but that doesn\u2019t seem to say that it\u2019s automatically Persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T23:56:13-07:00","id":1339537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339536#post1339536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I tell if something is Persistent or not? It has the Perpetual tag, but that doesn\u2019t seem to say that it\u2019s automatically Persistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it's not. The Perpetual keyword denotes how the Variation works <i>if</i> it's made a Persistent Variation. Most Variations have their activation method determined by their entangled Scar. This is explained in the Variations and Scars section at the end of the second backer preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T00:09:59-07:00","id":1339541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339537#post1339537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because it's not. The Perpetual keyword denotes how the Variation works <i>if</i> it's made a Persistent Variation. Most Variations have their activation method determined by their entangled Scar. This is explained in the Variations and Scars section at the end of the second backer preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Ah, ok. So, if I combined it with, say, Subliminal Conditioning, it would be Persistent and Perpetual. Does that mean activating the \u201conce per chapter \u201c effect would let me retain the skill until I changed it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T00:26:37-07:00","id":1339544,"title":"","content":"Also, I think the Indelible Mark Deviation is broken. Or I\u2019m not understanding how it works.<br /> <br /> If I\u2019m reading it correctly, it basically lets you combine two lower level Scars into a higher level one, which...I thought part of the point of Scars was that you couldn\u2019t do that, because they tend to get worse at an exponential rate as they increase in magnitude.<br /> <br /> So, I take three level 2 Variations. Normally, I would need to take three level 2 Scars or a level 4 Scar to balance those. However, if I take Involuntary Stimulus at 2 with the Indelible Mark (Bane 1) and the Continuous Deviation on top, that means I\u2019ve effectively got a level 2 Scar and a level 1 Scar acting like one level 4 Scar to cover all of those Variations.<br /> <br /> Is there something I\u2019m missing? Are Involuntary Scars so terrible that something like this is needed to get people to use them? Is there a major benefit to Permanent Scars that doing things this way doesn\u2019t grant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T02:25:53-07:00","id":1339554,"title":"","content":"I must say, so far I'm slightly disappointed by Deviant. Now I have no intention to withdraw my pledge, but I feel in an attempt to cover so many things the game just lacks a core setting. Every other paragraph is full if &quot;sometimes this, sometimes that, sometimes neither.&quot; Now from the look of this thread, other people seem to enjoy the toolboxy nature of the game, which is great! But I would have preferred at least a little more cohesion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T04:10:00-07:00","id":1339563,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If you have a Mag 3 scar and a Major Instability that you choose to downgrade by taking a scar... Must it be a new Mag 1 scar or can I raise my Mag 3 to 4 and follow that up by raising my variation?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">For that matter when I buy a new Variation must I have an already unentangled scar to pair it with or can you just choose to have one at any level your willing to stomach the cost for, for free when you make the variation purchase?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If I'm really focused on raising some scar in order to increase its variation can I choose to turn a success into a dramatic failure so I can get instability, so I can buy it off, so I can raise my scar and variance...?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":". 10-05-2019, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T04:54:12-07:00","id":1339570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339563#post1339563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a Mag 3 scar and a Major Instability that you choose to downgrade by taking a scar... Must it be a new Mag 1 scar or can I raise my Mag 3 to 4 and follow that up by raising my variation?</div> </div> </div> </div> You need to take a new, unentangled Scar (which you can then immediately buy a Variation for, if you want).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For that matter when I buy a new Variation must I have an already unentangled scar to pair it with or can you just choose to have one at any level your willing to stomach the cost for, for free when you make the variation purchase? </div> </div> </div> You need to have an unentangled Scar beforehand, or at least a Scar capable of entangling your new Variation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm really focused on raising some scar in order to increase its variation can I choose to turn a success into a dramatic failure so I can get instability, so I can buy it off, so I can raise my scar and variance...? </div> </div> </div> It's allowed by the rules as written, and I see no issue with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T07:41:21-07:00","id":1339591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339535#post1339535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not supposed to be &quot;leveled&quot; and you are not obligated to raise a Variation's Magnitude. If you want a bigger dicepool with the chosen Skill then you raise Scar Power at Magnitude 2; the other Magnitudes' effects are separate benefits in the same way that having Immunity at three dots does not imply having Immunity at one or two dots.<br /> <br /> You want to more easily get exceptional successes with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 1.<br /> <br /> You want to be rolling more dice with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 2.<br /> <br /> You want to be failing fewer rolls with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 3.<br /> <br /> I don't know that anything breaks from allowing multiple purchases for the same Skill at different Magnitudes, or adding a Deviation that makes it Tiered, or making it a full five-dot spread where Magnitude 3-5 lets you mix and match the preceding levels' options, but it's very clearly not a Tiered effect when its effects are all different Perpetual dice bonuses and the Variation maxes out at Magnitude 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few things<br /> <br /> 1. That\u2019s literally not an option. Hyper-Competence literally directly says \u201cThis Variation can be purchased multiple times, and each time its benefits apply to a different Skill.\u201d <br /> <br /> 2. It very much LOOKS like a Tiered variation, considering each level has a smaller, fairly distinct but connected bonus, and the 3 magnitude especially just straight up doesn\u2019t seem quite as strong as the 2 magnitude just at base, and it definitely seems balanced for being Tiered<br /> <br /> 3. This was very much a possible mistake report, not a prescription. If you think I\u2019m wrong, just ignore it and let Eric tell me that I\u2019m wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","user":"SdeSpencer","date":". 10-05-2019, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T07:53:37-07:00","id":1339593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339541#post1339541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean activating the \u201conce per chapter \u201c effect would let me retain the skill until I changed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Perpetual effects are the Magnitude 1/5 effects and that the Variation is always &quot;on&quot; for the purposes of answering whether you can use the per-chapter effects of the intermediate dots, which still last for one scene each.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339544#post1339544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there something I\u2019m missing? Are Involuntary Scars so terrible that something like this is needed to get people to use them? Is there a major benefit to Permanent Scars that doing things this way doesn\u2019t grant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Involuntary Scars are necessary for a Variation to have the Involuntary activation method, both of the core Involuntary Scars make all their attached Variations conditionally Overt if their own Magnitude goes over 1, both of the core Involuntary Scars have some form of cap on their own Magnitude before applying Deviations, and the Deviation literally cannot result in a Scar with a Magnitude of less than 3 before applying other Standard Deviations.<br /> <br /> The way Indelible Mark works, either you have a Persistent Scar with mechanical teeth that's active whenever its Variations are (or always, with Continuous, and unlike Short Circuit it's active even when you're using the power deliberately) without the benefits of a Persistent Variation, or all the entangled Variations are Overt, you have less control over the power, and (unless you make the secondary Scar Continuous) you don't get the opportunity to earn Beats from the Persistent Scar unless you're using the now-attention-grabbing powers you have less of a leash on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T08:23:33-07:00","id":1339597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339554#post1339554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, so far I'm slightly disappointed by Deviant. Now I have no intention to withdraw my pledge, but I feel in an attempt to cover so many things the game just lacks a core setting. Every other paragraph is full if &amp;quot;sometimes this, sometimes that, sometimes neither.&amp;quot; Now from the look of this thread, other people seem to enjoy the toolboxy nature of the game, which is great! But I would have preferred at least a little more cohesion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give some examples of what you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T08:39:56-07:00","id":1339604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339554#post1339554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, so far I'm slightly disappointed by Deviant. Now I have no intention to withdraw my pledge, but I feel in an attempt to cover so many things the game just lacks a core setting. Every other paragraph is full if &quot;sometimes this, sometimes that, sometimes neither.&quot; Now from the look of this thread, other people seem to enjoy the toolboxy nature of the game, which is great! But I would have preferred at least a little more cohesion.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the upcoming chapters (6, it looks like) should be the pre-made settings, with pre-made conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:58:11-07:00","id":1339636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give some examples of what you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, and if you are one the authors - please do not take this personally, the overall work is still the level of quality one can expect from Onyx Path. Just not doing it for me right now.<br /> <br /> If I take the section on the Transmissible form for example (won't post it here as I'm not sure that would be ok, so I'll paraphrase):<br /> <br /> <i>Some Divergences are transmissible. Most pass through diseases. Some pass through Variations or scars. Some pass through mystical means (which could be any of several options). Some affect one Variation, other affect more.<br /> <br /> In most cases they're as virulent as real diseases. In some cases, more. In other cases, barely at all.<br /> <br /> In some cases the Deviant is not always contagious. It can depend on any factor. It may also have any and all kind of counter.<br /> <br /> Most have an onset period. For some it's very long. For others, not at all.<br /> <br /> The symptoms vary. They can look like normal diseases. They can look very bad. Or not at all.<br /> <br /> The victim can fight back. The means vary. Usually if they survive they are immune, but no always.<br /> <br /> If the victim fails they suffer the Divergence. In a few days or weeks. Sometimes seconds. Sometimes months.</i><br /> <br /> Do you see what I mean? This section teaches me nothing. It's a repetition of &quot;sometimes in the middle, sometimes more, sometimes less.&quot; There is nothing specific to the setting. It's just an elaborate way of presenting anything and everything about options. If you take Vampire for example, the properties of the Blood are key to the setting and clearly explained, with some wiggle room for stories to be told around it. Here, if someone asked me of the Divergence was contagious, I'd have to reply &quot;Maybe. Sometimes. I don't know?&quot;<br /> <br /> I get that flexibility was the goal. But I fear here the game has got so flexible, it's lacking any unifying core.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 10-05-2019, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:11:47-07:00","id":1339642,"title":"","content":"What happens to a Deviant without a conspiracy? What happens when conviction makes them lash out, and loyalty wears away? Er, these are rhetorical questions by the way. I'm not legitimately looking for answers. The point is the new Joker movie came out recently and it's a prime example of Deviant-style used for psychological horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:18:00-07:00","id":1339645,"title":"","content":"There's always a conspiracy willing to look at a Deviant as a resource, and someone with Conviction touchstones but no loyalty is basically going to go on a rampage, moving from target to target, enacting vengeance after vengeance -but hey, so long as they have Touchstones, they ain't Feral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:20:45-07:00","id":1339648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339642#post1339642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to a Deviant without a conspiracy? What happens when conviction makes them lash out, and loyalty wears away? Er, these are rhetorical questions by the way. I'm not legitimately looking for answers. The point is the new Joker movie came out recently and it's a prime example of Deviant-style used for psychological horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>You latch Devotion on your fellow Renegades and pursue their conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:31:49-07:00","id":1339653,"title":"","content":"Mrr... I did say those were rhetorical questions. My point is that there's no actual conspiracy in Joker, or instead the closest he has to a conspiracy is society as a whole. To avoid spoilers, there's some pretty obvious examples of conviction and loyalty touchstones for him along with how they shift over the course of the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:42:42-07:00","id":1339657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339636#post1339636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that flexibility was the goal. But I fear here the game has got so flexible, it's lacking any unifying core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise, one of the things from the setting chapter I greatly appreciated was the bits where it firmly committed to certain things about the way the setting works and differs from our world: the public sphere is to a dramatically relevant degree a movie set papering over the dark underbelly of occult and/or exploitative elements, and lacking part or all of a soul messes with your place in the world (especially as that relates to the human sphere).<br /> <br /> I'm not going to be looking to the incredibly modular mechanics for insight into the game's identity except in aggregate or in specific examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:15:41-07:00","id":1339696,"title":"","content":"Possible errata:<br /> <br /> For P<span style=\"font-size:14px\">yrokinesis, the Mag 4 option of Extinguish states it can only be chosen if you selected Suppress at Mag 3. However, Mag 3 has no such choice. Mag 3 just allows you to increase or decrease a fire without choices of abilities like Mag 1 or Mag 4.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:22:40-07:00","id":1339701,"title":"","content":"The character creation part is done, and I need a break before I create the scenario, do I'm going to try tackling a few questions here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339196#post1339196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revisiting Telekinesis since that's what my upcoming character in a post-Kickstarter pre-release game is going to primarily use:<br /> <br /> If 'grappling' multiple people at once with Telekinesis, is the Deviant allowed to use a maneuver (damage, disarm, etc) on both of them on successful rolls? The answer seems to be clearly yes based on extrapolation from the earlier Cephalist Joe example, but I want to make sure I truly understand.<br /> <br /> Also, to resurface an earlier question - does Persistent Drawback have to inherit the Attribute Category of the linked Scar? It doesn't say that it does, but 90% of the examples do. Maybe that's just because, in 90% of those cases, it made sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question for which I don't have an immediate answer. Force fields blocking Directed Variations is a double-edged sword. It protects you from being targeted by others, but it also prevents you from targeting them back. I kinda want it to be an either/or the player determines when buying the Variation. Physical attacks like bullets and fists (and Lash, which deals damage and so could still get through) would still be blocked either way.<br /> <br /> As-written, Persistent Drawback allows you to choose the Attribute category. I'd considered changing it, but a couple comments after yours indicate that maybe it doesn't need changing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339309#post1339309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A handful of error-spottings for the collection, in a theme:<br /> <br /> The Chimeric example of Electrokinesis is mechanically illegal in the previewed text, having been entangled with a Scar that explicitly cannot entangle any Directed Variations.<br /> <br /> Creeping Dread and Shadows of the Past say they're Directed in the Variation writeups but not in the Quick Reference chart.<br /> <br /> Odd one out spotted while checking Directed Variations: Pheromones is missing a Perpetual or Toggled keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixing in the working draft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339535#post1339535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not supposed to be &quot;leveled&quot; and you are not obligated to raise a Variation's Magnitude. If you want a bigger dicepool with the chosen Skill then you raise Scar Power at Magnitude 2; the other Magnitudes' effects are separate benefits in the same way that having Immunity at three dots does not imply having Immunity at one or two dots.<br /> <br /> You want to more easily get exceptional successes with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 1.<br /> <br /> You want to be rolling more dice with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 2.<br /> <br /> You want to be failing fewer rolls with the Skill? Take Hyper-Competence 3.<br /> <br /> I don't know that anything breaks from allowing multiple purchases for the same Skill at different Magnitudes, or adding a Deviation that makes it Tiered, or making it a full five-dot spread where Magnitude 3-5 lets you mix and match the preceding levels' options, but it's very clearly not a Tiered effect when its effects are all different Perpetual dice bonuses and the Variation maxes out at Magnitude 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339593#post1339593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bInvoluntary Scars are necessary for a Variation to have the Involuntary activation method, both of the core Involuntary Scars make all their attached Variations conditionally Overt if their own Magnitude goes over 1, both of the core Involuntary Scars have some form of cap on their own Magnitude before applying Deviations, and the Deviation literally cannot result in a Scar with a Magnitude of less than 3 before applying other Standard Deviations.<br /> <br /> The way Indelible Mark works, either you have a Persistent Scar with mechanical teeth that's active whenever its Variations are (or always, with Continuous, and unlike Short Circuit it's active even when you're using the power deliberately) without the benefits of a Persistent Variation, or all the entangled Variations are Overt, you have less control over the power, and (unless you make the secondary Scar Continuous) you don't get the opportunity to earn Beats from the Persistent Scar unless you're using the now-attention-grabbing powers you have less of a leash on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed the intention of Indelible Mark and Short Circuit. More than anything, they're meant to reflect a trope wherein not only does the character's power manifest when they don't want it to, but it carries an additional downside for the hero personally. Bruce Banner doesn't just have Alternate Persona. He has Involuntary Stimulus + Indelible Mark (Alternate Persona).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339563#post1339563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm really focused on raising some scar in order to increase its variation can I choose to turn a success into a dramatic failure so I can get instability, so I can buy it off, so I can raise my scar and variance...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instability is an intentional Scylla and Charybdis. To increase Acclimation, you need to clear all the medium and major Instability, first, which makes it impossible (albeit temporarily) to get new Variations (unless you already have some Scars that are either unentangled or have extra &quot;capacity&quot;). To gain new Variations, you need new Scars (same caveats), which means you need some medium and/or major Instability to &quot;feed&quot; for those Scars, making it impossible (albeit temporarily) to increase your Acclimation.<br /> <br /> I will warn that buying a bunch more Variations can become a bit of a trap, since it means more Scars, and more Scars mean more situations that f*** with you (or allow others to do so), which can lead to your demise without the End Stage Condition ever coming into play.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Relentless Variation:</b> Still pondering this one. It will likely get split into two things - a Scar for what Invariable does now, and a Persistent-Only Deviation that emulates Suppressible. But I've been working on a scenario to run as a short demo the last couple days, so I haven't had much time to think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339696#post1339696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible errata:<br /> <br /> For Pyrokinesis, the Mag 4 option of Extinguish states it can only be chosen if you selected Suppress at Mag 3. However, Mag 3 has no such choice. Mag 3 just allows you to increase or decrease a fire without choices of abilities like Mag 1 or Mag 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>ETA: Woah. That's a throwback to an earlier draft. Fixing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-05-2019, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:36:41-07:00","id":1339703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character creation part is done, and I need a break before I create the scenario, do I'm going to try tackling a few questions here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I sense a mid-Kickstarter Actual Play?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda want it to be an either/or the player determines when buying the Variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Still curious about the multi-target grapple. I think it'd be totally fine personally; similar (but superior) effects are already available via auto-fire Lashes with Immobilize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As-written, Persistent Drawback allows you to choose the Attribute category. I'd considered changing it, but a couple comments after yours indicate that maybe it doesn't need changing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does - it makes sense that inserting an extra layer of Scar might change the way that Scar and its linked Variation works in that manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels really, really weird for it not to be tiered, to be honest. It's very powerful being tiered, yes, but I think encouraging people that focus on mundane-enhancers like this to be very powerful when the choice to do so exists in the same arena as powers like Lash is a good thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:16:46-07:00","id":1339708,"title":"","content":"From what I can see now, everything related to the Scar Attribute category will key off the secondary Scar, but I would still have Persistent Variation use the same category as the secondary Scar if just to avoid unintended interactions with future material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:23:31-07:00","id":1339710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339703#post1339703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I sense a mid-Kickstarter Actual Play?<br /> <br /> Makes sense. Still curious about the multi-target grapple. I think it'd be totally fine personally; similar (but superior) effects are already available via auto-fire Lashes with Immobilize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maaaaaaybe...<br /> <br /> Somehow missed responding to that one. I gave grapple rules a glance, and there's some room for interpretation with regards to its interaction with Telekinesis. I'm inclined to allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:54:15-07:00","id":1339718,"title":"","content":"Just general impressions here; it took a little while for me to wrap my head around entangling Variations and Scars and it definitely strikes me as something that's a bit of a barrier of entry to prospective players but well worth the initial learning curve for the incredible versatility it offers once you get the hang of it.<br /> <br /> I really, really appreciate the degree to which a savvy player can choose how much trouble they want to invite. Everything from choosing Scars that can be largely mitigated by the right merits and/or entangled Variations to setting up a train wreck into a fireworks factory just to watch the spectacle of everything going wrong all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","user":"HelmsDerp","date":". 10-05-2019, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:04:29-07:00","id":1339719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... casting my vote on tiered, yeah. Or a way to get repurchased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:07:36-07:00","id":1339721,"title":"","content":"I guess my question is more about how, with Indelible Mark, you can get a level 1 scar and a level 2 scar and have them entangling a level 4 Variation or three level 2 Variations, and I don\u2019t really quite get how that is equally as bad as a level 4 scar?<br /> <br /> Hmmm....<br /> <br /> Ok, so. I have three level 2 variations. Normally I would need three level 2 scars. I could get Involuntary Stimulus on one, so it can trigger if, say, I sense silver nearby. And I could have Bane 2 so I get hurt if I get touched by silver all the time. And another Persistent scar for the third one.<br /> <br /> Given those circumstances, that means I have two powers that are effectively always on/available, and one where I have to work a bit to activate it, unless I\u2019m in the presence of my trigger.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I can use Indelible Mark. Which means I just have Involuntary Stimulus 2 and Bane 1(Continuous). So, while I\u2019m down one Scar and Bane is now \u201csilver causes a nasty rash\u201d instead of hurting me, it also means that all three of my powers require a roll to trigger. Alternately, if I\u2019m in the presence of silver, all three of my Variations go off<br /> <br /> So...I guess, I can see it working. But it\u2019s not obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:29:35-07:00","id":1339724,"title":"","content":"Making sure of a thing: do secondary Variations and other Scar-free Variations have their activation methods and attached Scar Attributes determined the same way a Scar-free Magnitude 1 Variation from your Origin dot would?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:31:11-07:00","id":1339725,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I personally think it should be Tiered yeah, it feels very much designed for it and i think fits best under it</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>RE: Relentless Variation:</b> Still pondering this one. It will likely get split into two things - a Scar for what Invariable does now, and a Persistent-Only Deviation that emulates Suppressible. But I've been working on a scenario to run as a short demo the last couple days, so I haven't had much time to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I think that\u2019s a neat idea! I\u2019d be really interested in seeing it in action.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Note 1:</b> Earlier before the kickstarter started, you mentioned that you felt that Involuntary Scars felt kinda off-balance compared to Persistent and Controlled, and I kinda agree. It\u2019s sorta hard to really suggest a fix however, because there are a lot of variables. They vary from literally not a problem being Involuntary before you add in deviations, to enormous problems as soon as they come up, and everywhere in between. I really do not envy you in this case</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Note 2:</b> Minor thing: Why is Flying Overt anyway? Most Overt variations seem to specifically have some kind of direct obvious reason they are obvious. Does Flying only mean you are CURRENTLY Flying? Does that mean if you have Relentless on it or Activate it Involuntarily, that you can\u2019t leave the sky?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Note 3:</b> Really Really minor thing: I feel like if Creeping Dread or Pheromones have Aura, they shouldn\u2019t be considered Directed anymore, as they aren\u2019t really \u201cDirected\u201d at anyone then (also making them always on sounds like something neat)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Note 4:</b> Similarly Really Really minor thing: Why is the \u201cDirected Entanglement Rules\u201d only for Ranged Lashes? It doesn\u2019t feel like Melee Lashes have anything that really make them different in that fashion, and they feel weird being allowed for things that don\u2019t allow Directed or being banned from things that don\u2019t</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","user":"SdeSpencer","date":". 10-05-2019, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T17:42:00-07:00","id":1339731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd lean toward either keeping it Discrete and allowing multiple purchases to enable different bonuses for the same Skill, or making it Tiered, changing the rote effect to a per-scene ability and letting the various Clade Adaptations balance that out, and maybe extend the ladder so that there's an 8-Again and/or 9-Again in the mix somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339721#post1339721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my question is more about how, with Indelible Mark, you can get a level 1 scar and a level 2 scar and have them entangling a level 4 Variation or three level 2 Variations, and I don\u2019t really quite get how that is equally as bad as a level 4 scar?<br /> <br /> Hmmm....<br /> <br /> Ok, so. I have three level 2 variations. Normally I would need three level 2 scars. I could get Involuntary Stimulus on one, so it can trigger if, say, I sense silver nearby. And I could have Bane 2 so I get hurt if I get touched by silver all the time. And another Persistent scar for the third one.<br /> <br /> Given those circumstances, that means I have two powers that are effectively always on/available, and one where I have to work a bit to activate it, unless I\u2019m in the presence of my trigger.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I can use Indelible Mark. Which means I just have Involuntary Stimulus 2 and Bane 1(Continuous). So, while I\u2019m down one Scar and Bane is now \u201csilver causes a nasty rash\u201d instead of hurting me, it also means that all three of my powers require a roll to trigger. Alternately, if I\u2019m in the presence of silver, all three of my Variations go off<br /> <br /> So...I guess, I can see it working. But it\u2019s not obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of big things:<br /> <br /> 1) Involuntary Scars above Magnitude 1 mean that your Variations run on the highest level of Multiple Attribute Dependency, since they engage with at least Scar Finesse and Scar Resistance even if they don't calculate anything based on Scar Power. This further means that you have more to worry about from any degree of Instability over your Acclimation score, unless you have the Stabilizer Merit, in which case you're depending on keeping up with treatments or keeping hold of a particular item or what have you \u2014 in other words, you either deal with more from Instability or you have a separate weak point to manage on top of your Loyalty Touchstones.<br /> <br /> 2) The main problems with bundling multiple Variations into one Scar are that a) you have a more severe drawback that applies to fewer powers with no extra strength to compensate for them, and b) medium and major Instabilities have fewer channels to put additional dots of Scar Magnitude into, which means \u2014 surprise \u2014 you have to keep up with Instability more if you have fewer Scars and more Variations.<br /> <br /> Despite this, Involuntary Variations and their attached Deviations are comparatively cheap for the cost! That's the trade you make for having powers not entirely within your control, which I feel is to be expected for a class of power-at-a-price with the word &quot;Involuntary&quot; in the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T22:49:56-07:00","id":1339770,"title":"","content":"When is Deviant getting it's own CofD sub-forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T00:00:03-07:00","id":1339775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote for Discret and Repetable. Tiered is too much power imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T04:11:10-07:00","id":1339795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Relentless Variation:</b> Still pondering this one. It will likely get split into two things - a Scar for what Invariable does now, and a Persistent-Only Deviation that emulates Suppressible. But I've been working on a scenario to run as a short demo the last couple days, so I haven't had much time to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would the new Suppressible still allow you to convert toggled Variations into persistent ones? The ability to, say, have Tabula Rasa when you rouse yourself from your unending Astral Journey has been one of the most satisfying discoveries I've made whhile playing around with chargen. I'd be disappointed to see it go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T04:20:47-07:00","id":1339798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339770#post1339770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When is Deviant getting it's own CofD sub-forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Past experience says sometime after the Kickstarter ends. After all, until that point it's still not technically guaranteed that Deviant will actually be funded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T05:20:22-07:00","id":1339807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339795#post1339795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would the new Suppressible still allow you to convert toggled Variations into persistent ones? The ability to, say, have Tabula Rasa when you rouse yourself from your unending Astral Journey has been one of the most satisfying discoveries I've made whhile playing around with chargen. I'd be disappointed to see it go.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, the point of the Relentless Variation Scar is to change a Toggled Variation into a Perpetual Variation: that is, there would be no point in taking the Relentless Variation Scar if the only entangled Variations are Perpetual. Likewise, there would be no point in applying the Suppressible Deviation if the only entangled Variations are Toggled. So you'd take Astral Travel with Relentless Variation (to change it from Toggled to Perpetual), then apply the Suppressible Deviation by way of Tabula Rasa to give you a way to temporarily shut it off. <br /> <br /> I'm still not getting the reasoning why it was changed from a Deviation to a Scar in the first place; it seems to me that a \u201cRelentless\u201d Deviation for a Persistent Scar that changes all entangled Toggled Variations into Perpetual Variations would be simpler than a \u201cRelentless Variation\u201d Scar that requires you to supplement it with another Persistent Scar. <br /> <br /> That would be my suggestion: two independent Deviations for Persistent Scars; one that changes the entangled Toggled Variations to Perpetual Variations (\u201cRelentless\u201d), and another that lets you suppress any entangled Perpetual Variations (\u201cSuppressible\u201d). I could see the first being a +1 Deviation, and the second a -1 Deviation. They would not be mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-06-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T05:49:37-07:00","id":1339813,"title":"","content":"Here's a Google Docs template for a Deviant character sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can copy and paste dots and dot spacers as the easiest way to edit dot ratings; I visualize them this way to easily distinguish, for instance, Skills you have unranked and Skills you don't. Unskilled penalties matter! Add rows to tables as needed, or copy an Entanglement table and paste to add another. There are blank columns between Skills and their dot ratings in which to write Specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T08:54:41-07:00","id":1339855,"title":"","content":"The inability to teleport targets into 'immediate danger' with Translocation is really hampering my Nightcrawler build.<br /> <br /> Any chance for a higher Magnitude Deviation that removes that restriction, maybe at the cost of needing to teleport alongside the target (ref. teleporting into the air with someone and then trying to teleport away before hitting the ground)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T12:00:01-07:00","id":1339879,"title":"","content":"Can you pair Lash with Variations that have a directed Deviation where the Variation itself isn't Directed?<br /> <br /> Unrelated, but not trying to triple post: When determining whether or not a character has the correct number of Variations of the correct Clade, do you count Variations nested under eg: Hybrid Form? I'm leaning towards yes because of the examples (and because having 9 Magnitude of Invasive Variations under a Magnitude 5 Hybrid Form probably shouldn't force the concept to be Chimeric instead of Invasive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-06-2019, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T14:31:14-07:00","id":1339918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339701#post1339701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the audience regarding Hyper-Competence: Originally, this one was tiered, but some playtesters looking at it said &quot;holy yikes, bonus dice with a rote action is too powerful!&quot; so I toned it down. Given what other Magnitude 3 Variations can do, maybe this one <i>does</i> work better as Tiered. It's terrifying with Firearms or Investigation, but Deviant-type characters in media who have special powers that make them extremely dangerous with a gun or beyond-Sherlock gifted at figuring things out. What do folks think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think tiered is better, in part because investing in mundane abilities isn't as flashy or obviously cool as things like Telekinesis, Lash, or Gigantic. It takes a big boost to mundane abilities to go from &quot;oh this person is really good at that&quot; to &quot;holy crap, that's inhuman; no one is that good&quot;. For it to be narratively on par with the other powers it might need to be more powerful mechanically. It needs to feel like an actual power, not just like some Merit a baseline could have taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T14:46:19-07:00","id":1339923,"title":"","content":"Bonus dice with rote is pretty strong, but I don't think it would be out of line with other powers since the bonus dice are limited to Scar Power. Deviants can't increase this past 5, since Super Human doesn't count. Rote's effect is tricky to compute precisely but an easy rule of thumb is that it's equivalent to ~70% more dice. A player who goes all in and raises the associated attribute to 5 is getting 8 or 9 dice worth of effect. That's potent but it requires enough investment to get to that point that I don't think it's unreasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T15:52:50-07:00","id":1339948,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that if Hyper-Competence is tiered, you are also getting exceptional successes on three dice instead of five. So you get a maximum of six extra dice, and rote, plus a significant lowering of the exceptional success threshold.<br /> <br /> All three in combination mean you're much more likely to be rolling exceptional successes on a very frequent basis. At minimum that means taking this gives you a beat generating engine from the near constant beneficial conditions you'll be getting.<br /> <br /> I like Satchel's idea of making it tiered but turning the rote quality to a once per scene effect the most. The repeatable but discrete just inflates the number of scars or scar magnitude but doesn't break up the combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T16:30:08-07:00","id":1339954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339879#post1339879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated, but not trying to triple post: When determining whether or not a character has the correct number of Variations of the correct Clade, do you count Variations nested under eg: Hybrid Form? I'm leaning towards yes because of the examples (and because having 9 Magnitude of Invasive Variations under a Magnitude 5 Hybrid Form probably shouldn't force the concept to be Chimeric instead of Invasive).</div> </div> </div> </div>Got this one a few days back:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338920#post1338920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Are Variations that involve secondary Variations like Hybrid Form or Sacred Flesh subject to the rules for proportional Variation dots by Clade, or do only the dots in the primary Variation count toward the total? (e.g. Can my non-Invasive character have a Hybrid Form whose effects are just Computer-Aided Processing and Sensor Array?)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338931#post1338931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Great question. The secondary Variations don't count toward proportions of Clade/Universal Variations. I'll clarify that in my working draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T17:47:21-07:00","id":1339966,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping the last 3 days of this kickstarter are like the Contagion kickstarter, really want to have the Mutant chapter for the companion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T18:14:01-07:00","id":1339970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339966#post1339966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping the last 3 days of this kickstarter are like the Contagion kickstarter, really want to have the Mutant chapter for the companion</div> </div> </div> </div>Most KSs start strong as the early adopters get in on the ground floor, and they end strong as people get the 24 hours left reminder, change up their add-ons, or otherwise do last minute stuff.<br /> <br /> So, it\u2019s likely that it will be made to rain at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T19:04:08-07:00","id":1339977,"title":"","content":"We should should achieve a lot more rewards. New pledges and people increasing their pledges are common in the final days, particularly after the release of the full preview manuscript.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/026/387/509/18cc8c00e720d186501c0b1fdf376608_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-2.1.0&amp;crop=faces&amp;w=160&amp;h=90&amp;fit=crop&amp;v=1567796734&amp;auto=format&amp;frame=1&amp;q=92&amp;s=3155de9cdfca43c373cd1cb2c460d997\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> Deviant: The Renegades - a tabletop roleplaying game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.kicktraq.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Contribute to help us create a traditionally printed version of Deviant: The Renegades, a new game in the Chronicles of Darkness line. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T19:21:44-07:00","id":1339978,"title":"","content":"thanks for the reassurances guys/gals. sorry if it's annoying, I'm just very anxious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T21:55:55-07:00","id":1339992,"title":"","content":"Going over Involuntary Scars again. There's a particular hole in Indelible Mark/Involuntary Stimulus that I think can be plugged by making Rare and Common into Standard Deviations and/or making Unpredictable exclusive with Rare and Common in the same way that Uncontrollable is.<br /> <br /> (The hole, essentially, is that by taking an Involuntary Stimulus that is Common and/or Unpredictable, you can take a Continuous Indelible Mark and still come out with a Magnitude 4+ Scar whose only effects are &quot;the Variation uses the Involuntary activation method,&quot; &quot;exposure to a common stimulus (and/or an unknown stimulus) may cause the Variation to activate on its own, which grants Beats when it causes trouble,&quot; and &quot;you have constant access to a source of Beats in the form of a Persistent Scar that often has no other systems attached to it.&quot; Entangled with a Subtle Variation like Aquatic or Superhuman Attribute or Predator's Cunning, this has\u2026 functionally zero teeth despite the clear intent of the Deviation's wording being &quot;one of the Scars has to do more than offer Beats for this Deviation to apply.&quot; It's tricky.)<br /> <br /> Relatedly, do secondary Scars count as separate Scars for the purposes of Beats-per-Scar-per-scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T22:05:25-07:00","id":1339993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339978#post1339978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks for the reassurances guys/gals. sorry if it's annoying, I'm just very anxious</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanna see how it goes, look up their other past projects on Kicktraq. A trend should emerge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T22:34:16-07:00","id":1339994,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know secondary scars have to match the physical/mental/social category of the primary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T23:40:14-07:00","id":1339999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339725#post1339725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Other Note 2:</b> Minor thing: Why is Flying Overt anyway? Most Overt variations seem to specifically have some kind of direct obvious reason they are obvious. Does Flying only mean you are CURRENTLY Flying? Does that mean if you have Relentless on it or Activate it Involuntarily, that you can\u2019t leave the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>Variations are skinned appropriately to your Clade; the text's go-to example of this uses three different forms of Chimeric Flight along with one for each other non-Mutant Clade, and one of &quot;package a bunch of Variations into a single Overt activation&quot; Hybrid Form's example descriptions is &quot;this Psychic character hovers above the ground while manifesting significant telepathic and telekinetic powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> tl;dr Flight means you've got wings or jump jets or psychokinetic energy displacement or other obvious means of gliding/getting airborne going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Other Note 4:</b> Similarly Really Really minor thing: Why is the \u201cDirected Entanglement Rules\u201d only for Ranged Lashes? It doesn\u2019t feel like Melee Lashes have anything that really make them different in that fashion, and they feel weird being allowed for things that don\u2019t allow Directed or being banned from things that don\u2019t </div> </div> </div>It may help to think of Lash less as &quot;a Variation that affects other targets&quot; and more as &quot;a Variation that gives you a particular method of attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the main effects of Channel is that it allows you to use Directed Variations at greater range; any conceivable melee Lash is well within the normal range of a Directed Variation, so the primary benefit it offers to a Directed effect is the ability to combine it with a normal attack, particularly one that may also exist as a delivery mechanism for other effects.<br /> <br /> The Directed-exclusive Scars and Deviations on the books are:<br /> <br /> The After-Effect and Single-Minded Deviations of the Controlled Scar Concentration.<br /> The Controlled Scar Cooldown.<br /> The Ongoing Deviation of the Controlled Scar Perilous Variation.<br /> The Draining Deviation of the Controlled Scar Tribulation.<br /> <br /> One facet of the base effect of the Involuntary Scar Involuntary Stimulus.<br /> About half of the Involuntary Scar Power Build-Up.<br /> <br /> The Rebellious Variation Standard Deviation.<br /> <br /> Most of those either give the entangled Variation an ammo concern or a targeting issue, which scans well to a ranged-weapon-equivalent attack power and much less well to melee attacks, which generally model limited uses and erratic application with a different type of effect, particularly when most melee attacks measure their solitary range band in the single digits and can be avoided by either party moving far enough apart from the other.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Most of the things ranged Lashes get from counting as Directed for drawbacks' sake make Directed Variations work with considerations ranged attacks deal with, and a lot of those are negligible for melee attacks or better modeled by things that don't give you free reflexive attacks that you can prevent from hurting your loved ones by keeping five feet apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another oddity that's probably been caught in the working draft: The example of the Consequences of Instability in Preview 2 alludes to Involuntary Scars worsening at a different threshold than the other two categories (&quot;this means that only his Scars linked to an Involuntary Variation increase by a Magnitude of 1&quot;). Old version of the mechanics poking through?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T07:56:47-07:00","id":1340029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339994#post1339994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know secondary scars have to match the physical/mental/social category of the primary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric answered this one earlier - currently, they do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T11:31:04-07:00","id":1340059,"title":"","content":"Ah what the heck, I'll up my pledge. <br /> I was cautious about it in the beginning so only pledge the 5$ to see the manuscript but I'm absolutely LOVING what I'm reading so I def want the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T11:53:48-07:00","id":1340062,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure I'm parsing the Shapeshifter Deviation of Animal Transformation correctly: A Deviant with Shapeshifter gains a nearly unlimited repertoire of animal shapes within the parameters of Variation Magnitude, and it is not the case that they must choose one appropriate form for each tier (ie, &quot;I can turn into a housecat, a pelagic thresher shark, and a swarm of Japanese hornets&quot;), correct?<br /> <br /> Also, entangling Shapeshifter Animal Transformation with Fluctuating Variation must make for some very chaotic scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T13:32:00-07:00","id":1340074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340062#post1340062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make sure I'm parsing the Shapeshifter Deviation of Animal Transformation correctly: A Deviant with Shapeshifter gains a nearly unlimited repertoire of animal shapes within the parameters of Variation Magnitude, and it is not the case that they must choose one appropriate form for each tier (ie, &quot;I can turn into a housecat, a pelagic thresher shark, and a swarm of Japanese hornets&quot;), correct?<br /> <br /> Also, entangling Shapeshifter Animal Transformation with Fluctuating Variation must make for some very chaotic scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This Variation allows the Deviant to take the shape of a single animal chosen at the time of <br /> purchase.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it's Discrete so not multiple forms from different Magnitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T13:41:37-07:00","id":1340075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340074#post1340074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;This Variation allows the Deviant to take the shape of a single animal chosen at the time of<br /> purchase.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it's Discrete so not multiple forms from different Magnitudes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I mean with the Shapeshifter Deviation:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Variation becomes Tiered, instead, allowing the Remade to take the form of any appropriate animal (or swarm). However, the Broken can only activate the Variation once per chapter.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T13:49:03-07:00","id":1340076,"title":"","content":"Oh. Right. You already brought up Fluctuating Variation so treat it like that. Note each Magnitude as if you've bought it separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:30:22-07:00","id":1340083,"title":"","content":"New stretch goals!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At $72,000 in funding \u2013 SUPPLEMENT EXPANSION: The Clades Companion PDF. No Clade embodies the strange and dehumanizing effects of Divergence quite the way the Mutant does, and so The Clades Companion PDF will be expanded with new Forms that transcend the singularity of the self and the flesh-and-blood body \u2013 a human consciousness uploaded to a mainframe, a talking mystical item, or an advanced A.I. with a drone for a chassis. Or, introduce Remade who are part of a line of clones or replicants who share memories, such that physical death is little more than an inconvenience; some even have whole wardrobes of new bodies, each one customized to match an urgent practical need (or just the Broken\u2019s current mood). </div> </div> </div>\u2026and suddenly I'm reminded of Agents of THUNDER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:39:08-07:00","id":1340085,"title":"","content":"Oh, so now we're getting into some transhumanism stuff? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:40:50-07:00","id":1340088,"title":"","content":"Kickstarter comment by Eric: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Some folks earlier were asking how to play a Deviant who is a brain in a jar. *This* expansion for The Clades Companion will help me answer that question. \ud83d\ude42</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>How can we not help Eric answer the Brain in a Jar question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:48:30-07:00","id":1340090,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think Eric got the Cephalists and the Mutants mixed up: this one feels more like the \u201crealms of the mind\u201d stuff that I'd expect from Cephalists, whereas the one we got for the Cephalists feels more like the sort of \u201cyour body is different\u201d thing that I'd expect from Mutants. <br /> <br /> But that's just a nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:59:40-07:00","id":1340094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340090#post1340090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think Eric got the Cephalists and the Mutants mixed up: this one feels more like the \u201crealms of the mind\u201d stuff that I'd expect from Cephalists, whereas the one we got for the Cephalists feels more like the sort of \u201cyour body is different\u201d thing that I'd expect from Mutants. <br /> <br /> But that's just a nitpick.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cephalist piece looks to be &quot;nonhuman in a singular human body,&quot; whereas this is definitely more about having a weirder than usual bodily situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T15:03:13-07:00","id":1340096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> an advanced A.I. with a drone for a chassis </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> physical death is little more than an inconvenience </div> </div> </div>MUST... HAVE...<br /> <br /> I NEEEEEEEED IT!!!<br /> <br /> I'm considering buying extra copies of the book I don't need (maybe I could give them to a friend or something) just to make the number go up more.<br /> <br /> Edit: Any chance we can get an option to buy a physical copy of the Clades Companion through the Kickstarter? I would immediately increase my pledge to get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-07-2019, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T15:11:15-07:00","id":1340097,"title":"","content":"And yet the Cephalists get Astral Travel and other abilities that draw a divide between body and mind, which is what I see as the common thread of this latest Stretch Goal. <br /> <br /> Compare this to the first one, which dealt with inhuman Deviants (sapient animals, androids, etc.)<br /> <br /> But as I said, nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T15:15:08-07:00","id":1340099,"title":"","content":"Neverminde, i re-read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":".  Reread the preview 10-07-2019, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T15:54:09-07:00","id":1340103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340088#post1340088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can we not help Eric answer the Brain in a Jar question</div> </div> </div> </div> My answer: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sensory Deprivation 5, and ideally a few of the other ones too. Missing Limb at Magnitude 4. Native Environment at any Magnitude, and some level of Conspicuous Appearance. Finally, Miniaturization entangled with Relentless Variation.</div></div> </div> </div> With that out of the way, I am very down for this stretch goal. It's the second-best one so far, largely because &quot;be an ifrit sealed in human flesh&quot; <i>speaks</i> to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T16:30:30-07:00","id":1340108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340085#post1340085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so now we're getting into some transhumanism stuff? lol</div> </div> </div> </div>On that subject, hey kids, there's finally a game that easily supports freedom from death by aging.<br /> <br /> Not that it'll help you much when you implode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T16:49:51-07:00","id":1340109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340108#post1340108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that subject, hey kids, there's finally a game that easily supports freedom from death by aging.<br /> <br /> Not that it'll help you much when you implode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have all your touchstones be loyalty touchstones that are voices in your head via alternate personas and/or symbiotes. Never leave your hidden bunker, and spend all day hanging out with the voices in your head, taking turns controlling the body, and engaging in their various hobbies for all of eternity.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really work as a PC since they never really do anything of any importance, but I think it's rules legal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also be a Self-Created that immediately went into hiding upon Deviating so no Conspiracy has any idea you exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-07-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T17:28:36-07:00","id":1340115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340109#post1340109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't really work as a PC since they never really do anything of any importance, but I think it's rules legal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the main reasons why I don't buy any variation on &quot;your Touchstones are physically indistinct from yourself&quot; \u2014 Living Progenitor giving you a Touchstone that it's impossible to lose by any hand but your own save by player agreement is a unique benefit, and while your own physicality may be &quot;something that can be threatened or destroyed by a single actor in a single time and place,&quot; nothing about that is distinct from physically threatening you and it's not really a relationship in a sense that benefits you along the lines of &quot;remind[ing you] that even though being Remade took away a piece of [your] humanity, it didn't take all of it.&quot; (Also, &quot;voices in your head&quot; is the complete opposite of &quot;concrete and localized&quot; and engaging in their hobbies is pretty far from &quot;acting in support of&quot; a Touchstone on its own.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T17:30:47-07:00","id":1340116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340109#post1340109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have all your touchstones be loyalty touchstones that are voices in your head via alternate personas and/or symbiotes. Never leave your hidden bunker, and spend all day hanging out with the voices in your head, taking turns controlling the body, and engaging in their various hobbies for all of eternity.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really work as a PC since they never really do anything of any importance, but I think it's rules legal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also be a Self-Created that immediately went into hiding upon Deviating so no Conspiracy has any idea you exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain your alternate personas can't be Touchstones, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T17:53:19-07:00","id":1340121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340115#post1340115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the main reasons why I don't buy any variation on &quot;your Touchstones are physically indistinct from yourself&quot; \u2014 Living Progenitor giving you a Touchstone that it's impossible to lose by any hand but your own save by player agreement is a unique benefit, and while your own physicality may be &quot;something that can be threatened or destroyed by a single actor in a single time and place,&quot; nothing about that is distinct from physically threatening you and it's not really a relationship in a sense that benefits you along the lines of &quot;remind[ing you] that even though being Remade took away a piece of [your] humanity, it didn't take all of it.&quot; (Also, &quot;voices in your head&quot; is the complete opposite of &quot;concrete and localized&quot; and engaging in their hobbies is pretty far from &quot;acting in support of&quot; a Touchstone on its own.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340116#post1340116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain your alternate personas can't be Touchstones, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint:<br /> <br /> A freak supernatural accident involving a convergence of ley lines, an alignment of the planets, an unusual combination of chemicals, and a lightning strike, killed and changed a family of merchants traveling across the old west. They were transporting various chemicals including a barrel full of mercury. When the lightning struck their wagon, the chemicals exploded, killing them all. However this event altered the mercury and charged it with strange mystic energies. As the mercury flowed over their burning bodies, it absorbed their dying spirits and began to change further. The mercury seeped deep into the ground and emerged into a cavern. It sat here for a year and a day until the alchemical processes happening inside completed.<br /> <br /> It was at this time that the family awoke. They found they now shared a body of living mercury that would shift to match the shape of body of the family member who was currently in control while still appearing as shiny and silvery as mercury. They feared what would happen if they ever returned to the outside world, and soon discovered that they had no natural needs and could alchemically produce small objects, and so little by little they turned their cave into a furnished home.<br /> <br /> To this day they remain in that cave going about their strange lives, isolated from the outside world.<br /> <br /> Until of course, the PCs wander down the wrong cave, in search of water, after their car breaks down in the middle of the desert, and they find a strange silvery being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-07-2019, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T18:14:21-07:00","id":1340123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340121#post1340121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterpoint:</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-counterpoint: This is an Amalgam.<br /> <br /> It's still a single character as far as game systems are concerned, and you've handily described a Loyalty Touchstone that is concrete and has no need to be described in terms of the things that are literally the opposite of ways you manage your Instability.<br /> <br /> They can hold themselves together by tending to their little home, and they may well keep very stable indeed in this off-the-grid isolation, but they're only barely kept from becoming Feral unless they busy themselves with multiple extra projects of that sort, and &quot;there's a multifarious being deep below the earth - don't mess with their home&quot; in no way necessitates &quot;my soul-trauma is how I manage my soul-trauma.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T20:39:56-07:00","id":1340147,"title":"","content":"The final Clade themed expansion sounds great (new Forms), but my desperate hope remains for a crossover pdf that stats up the Chiron Group as part of the Web of Pain, and discusses Progenitor/Demiurge overlap (or at least conspiracies also incorporating Alchemists and azoth-Cloning to tie in thematic Promethean crossovers). Or the tie in of Seers of the Throne fronts making Servitors like the Grigori, Hollow Ones, Myrmidons, and Hive Souls...<br /> <br /> in a perfect world I\u2019d want a \u201cMortal Remains\u201d expansion chapter like BtP got for Deviant and Conspiracy aimed Hunters - but I understand not wanting to do that while 2e is in development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-08-2019, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T21:03:58-07:00","id":1340150,"title":"","content":"Heh. Yeah; that would be great: the third-tier portion of that book could have as one of its themes \u201chunting Deviants is different from any other kind of monsters; because these monsters are ones that <i>we</i> made.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T22:27:13-07:00","id":1340159,"title":"","content":"RE: Hyper-Competence: How about making it Tiered, but making Mag 2 half Scar Power? That caps the total bonus at +4 (including Specialty, and usually +2 or +3), but still makes the Mag 3 effect feel like a superpower - which is important to me, since otherwise it is narratively boring compared to every other Mag 3 Variation in the game. Doubling the Specialty bonus at Mag 1 if you have a relevant Specialty could also give it a bit more oomph at that level, but that might be an unnecessary complication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339807#post1339807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, the point of the Relentless Variation Scar is to change a Toggled Variation into a Perpetual Variation: that is, there would be no point in taking the Relentless Variation Scar if the only entangled Variations are Perpetual. Likewise, there would be no point in applying the Suppressible Deviation if the only entangled Variations are Toggled. So you'd take Astral Travel with Relentless Variation (to change it from Toggled to Perpetual), then apply the Suppressible Deviation by way of Tabula Rasa to give you a way to temporarily shut it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, since Relentless has the Toggled keyword, you can't entangle it with Perpetual Variations - and for this exact reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339855#post1339855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inability to teleport targets into 'immediate danger' with Translocation is really hampering my Nightcrawler build.<br /> <br /> Any chance for a higher Magnitude Deviation that removes that restriction, maybe at the cost of needing to teleport alongside the target (ref. teleporting into the air with someone and then trying to teleport away before hitting the ground)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleportation can pretty easily take over a game, so I was being somewhat conservative with it. In truth, I didn't add &quot;teleport other&quot; to the mix until very late in the process, and not without a bit of trepidation. Conspiracies are less of a threat if you can teleport 100 miles away from their capture squads, and being able to teleport the Linchpin 10 stories up can be too easy a way to get rid of them. As to your solution, if you can teleport back or have a way to survive a 10-story fall (such as Flight), it can still be a fairly assuredly lethal solution to all your problem. So, I'm not likely to expand the options, although groups are always welcome to adjust the game to suit their play style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339992#post1339992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going over Involuntary Scars again. There's a particular hole in Indelible Mark/Involuntary Stimulus that I think can be plugged by making Rare and Common into Standard Deviations and/or making Unpredictable exclusive with Rare and Common in the same way that Uncontrollable is.<br /> <br /> (The hole, essentially, is that by taking an Involuntary Stimulus that is Common and/or Unpredictable, you can take a Continuous Indelible Mark and still come out with a Magnitude 4+ Scar whose only effects are &quot;the Variation uses the Involuntary activation method,&quot; &quot;exposure to a common stimulus (and/or an unknown stimulus) may cause the Variation to activate on its own, which grants Beats when it causes trouble,&quot; and &quot;you have constant access to a source of Beats in the form of a Persistent Scar that often has no other systems attached to it.&quot; Entangled with a Subtle Variation like Aquatic or Superhuman Attribute or Predator's Cunning, this has\u2026 functionally zero teeth despite the clear intent of the Deviation's wording being &quot;one of the Scars has to do more than offer Beats for this Deviation to apply.&quot; It's tricky.)<br /> <br /> Relatedly, do secondary Scars count as separate Scars for the purposes of Beats-per-Scar-per-scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Unpredicatable with Common/Rare makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> In the interest of not making it possible to accumulate several Beats in each scene, I'd say it should be limited to one Scar-based Beat per scene, regardless of how many Scars come into play. I'll spell this out in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339994#post1339994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know secondary scars have to match the physical/mental/social category of the primary?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't currently, but the more I think about the question, the more I think that, thematically, they probably should. It's the whole &quot;Scars turn your natural strengths (Attributes) into weakness&quot; thing I've talked about before. I know that won't a universally popular decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339999#post1339999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another oddity that's probably been caught in the working draft: The example of the Consequences of Instability in Preview 2 alludes to Involuntary Scars worsening at a different threshold than the other two categories (&quot;this means that only his Scars linked to an Involuntary Variation increase by a Magnitude of 1&quot;). Old version of the mechanics poking through?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. Fixing in the working draft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340062#post1340062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to make sure I'm parsing the Shapeshifter Deviation of Animal Transformation correctly: A Deviant with Shapeshifter gains a nearly unlimited repertoire of animal shapes within the parameters of Variation Magnitude, and it is not the case that they must choose one appropriate form for each tier (ie, &quot;I can turn into a housecat, a pelagic thresher shark, and a swarm of Japanese hornets&quot;), correct?<br /> <br /> Also, entangling Shapeshifter Animal Transformation with Fluctuating Variation must make for some very chaotic scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct on the first point.<br /> <br /> Regarding the second, Fluctuating Variation probably shouldn't work on Discrete Variations. It's not too much trouble when entangled with Animal Transformation (or, say, Carapace), but it's nonsensical with several of the others. Immunity? Specialized Sense? A blanket prohibition might be necessary, but I'll see if I can avoid throwing out the baby with the bath water, because there are certainly some exceptions that are awesome, but I also have to watch out that any fix doesn't make Wild Variation incredibly easy to abuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340090#post1340090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think Eric got the Cephalists and the Mutants mixed up: this one feels more like the \u201crealms of the mind\u201d stuff that I'd expect from Cephalists, whereas the one we got for the Cephalists feels more like the sort of \u201cyour body is different\u201d thing that I'd expect from Mutants.<br /> <br /> But that's just a nitpick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Dividing up the stuff I wanted to include in the Companion into Clade-themed chunks was more of a marketing device. I was originally toying with making one Form and one set of mechanical options &quot;for&quot; each Clade, but it was really artificial, so my draft outline organizes it more like you'd expect (all Forms in one chapter, for example), rather than having Clades as chapter names or some such. It made for a nice way to present the contents for the Kickstarter, though, so that's how I wrote the pitches for the five pieces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340108#post1340108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that subject, hey kids, there's finally a game that easily supports freedom from death by aging.<br /> <br /> Not that it'll help you much when you implode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Achieving immortality (sans Instability death) is easy. Getting away from the conspiracies of the Web of Pain long enough to enjoy your extra years is all but impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340116#post1340116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain your alternate personas can't be Touchstones, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be hesitant to allow it, at best. I heard someone make a pretty cogent argument that made sense for one character in a very specific situation (it boiled down to &quot;letting your Amalgam + Alternate Persona borrow your body because you love her and believe she should be free to pursue her happiness, too&quot;), but even so, I'd have to be pretty confident that you'd to play that concept to the nines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T22:36:07-07:00","id":1340161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340159#post1340159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be hesitant to allow it, at best. I heard someone make a pretty cogent argument that made sense for one character in a very specific situation (it boiled down to &quot;letting your Amalgam + Alternate Persona borrow your body because you love her and believe she should be free to pursue her happiness, too&quot;), but even so, I'd have to be pretty confident that you'd to play that concept to the nines.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less the same ball. My general problem with a lot of novel ideas for characters tend to revolve around a player's failure to execute them in any way that actually plays well for a story moving forward or with other people. Lot of trying to run before learning to walk.<br /> <br /> I've had a few people pull it off, but there's a reason a lot of my disposition is geared towards &quot;normal operations&quot; regarding characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T00:50:03-07:00","id":1340173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340159#post1340159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Unpredicatable with Common/Rare makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another method that comes to mind, which is probably less fiddly (though I don't profess to know a great way of wording it) is to change the language of Indelible Mark to specify that if the secondary Scar is Magnitude 1 then the primary Scar has to be Magnitude 2 or higher before <i>any</i> Deviations \u2014 unless there's some future-proofing that needs to be done, there are only two Involuntary Scars on the list, and Involuntary Stimulus is the only one that has any Deviations of its own that make &quot;Magnitude 2&quot; mean more than &quot;you have more opportunities to take a Beat.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Relatedly, I don't know that the specification is strictly necessary in Short Circuit, because the way that Deviation calculates its Magnitude bonus means the secondary Scar is only going to offer any bonus if it's Magnitude 2 or higher.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T02:24:04-07:00","id":1340182,"title":"","content":"If Healing Touch had the Directed tag, it could be used as &quot;Channel&quot; for a Gentle [Skill] Lash.<br /> But with this, Healing Toucn cannot entangled with a Relentless Scar... maybe i want too much !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-08-2019, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T03:56:18-07:00","id":1340188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340090#post1340090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think Eric got the Cephalists and the Mutants mixed up</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a totally subjective point but...<br /> <br /> 1. As I see it, intelligent former objects and animals KIND OF fits Cephalists, but the name of the game for Mutants is versatility.<br /> 2. Replicants are described as Genotypal Mutants.<br /> <br /> Can't wait!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T04:04:48-07:00","id":1340191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340115#post1340115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the main reasons why I don't buy any variation on &quot;your Touchstones are physically indistinct from yourself&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> There's legit nothing wrong with a deviant caring about non touchstone things, like &quot;the pursuit of justice&quot; or &quot;my imaginary friends,&quot; but I find touchstones being discretely vulnerable chunks more fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T04:13:55-07:00","id":1340194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340159#post1340159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't currently, but the more I think about the question, the more I think that, thematically, they probably should. It's the whole &quot;Scars turn your natural strengths (Attributes) into weakness&quot; thing I've talked about before. I know that won't a universally popular decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay, thanks. On the plus side, if you're like me and want lots of physical stats but like mental scars, I noticed you can have a physical character with tons of uses for mental scars due to how Superhuman Attribute (other than strength), Omnicompetence, and Carapace don't have a strong need for Scar Power and Scar Finesse. Not sure if this is ill fitting or whatever<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T07:12:39-07:00","id":1340219,"title":"","content":"Manuscript Preview 4 (Let's Get Conspiratorial), is up: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/posts/2645439\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2645439</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T08:08:49-07:00","id":1340229,"title":"","content":"Good stuff. Is there any designated way for a Conspiracy to increase its standing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T10:25:39-07:00","id":1340256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340229#post1340229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good stuff. Is there any designated way for a Conspiracy to increase its standing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Subversion, under Conspiracy Versus Conspiracy, says that completely subsuming another conspiracy of equal or greater Standing increases a conspiracy's Standing by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T10:42:11-07:00","id":1340263,"title":"","content":"Doctor Victor Von Doom as a Self-Made Devoted who is the head of his own Conspiracy, the Government of the Kingdom of Latveria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Doom\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Doctor_Doom_%28circa_2019%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Doom\" target=\"_blank\"> Doctor Doom - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Doom\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Doom </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latveria\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/Latveria2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latveria\" target=\"_blank\"> Latveria - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latveria\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latveria </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T11:22:41-07:00","id":1340266,"title":"","content":"Some good stuff here, but I'm disappointed by the relative lack of guidelines on choosing a starting Threat Level. The one-word descriptors for each Threat Level tier are extremely unhelpful: what does a Hyperplasia game play like, and how does that differ from a Dysplasia or Metastasis game? About how much overt action and threat should you expect for each tier? Which tier should you generally expect to fear for your Loyalty touchstones' lives the moment the conspirators connect them to you? Which tier do they break out the submachine guns? I didn't bring this up for Manuscript Preview 2 because I assumed the Antagonists section would expand on it, but it doesn't appear to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T11:49:13-07:00","id":1340268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340266#post1340266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About how much overt action and threat should you expect for each tier? Which tier should you generally expect to fear for your Loyalty touchstones' lives the moment the conspirators connect them to you? Which tier do they break out the submachine guns?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of these sound like they are a factor of Standing. The lowest tier gang that gets weird drugs from another source and tests them out on unwilling subjects might bust down your ex's door to get back at you, and the Standing 10 three letter agency may never &quot;break out the submachine guns&quot; if they don't have the authority to do that and they try to follow the law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T11:52:45-07:00","id":1340270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340268#post1340268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of these sound like they are a factor of Standing. The lowest tier gang that gets weird drugs from another source and tests them out on unwilling subjects might bust down your ex's door to get back at you, and the Standing 10 three letter agency may never &quot;break out the submachine guns&quot; if they don't have the authority to do that and they try to follow the law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, what is? What do I expect from a Metastasis game that's different from a Hyperplasia game besides more Variations and Scars? How do I pick an appropriate Threat Level? I feel like more guidelines are warranted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T11:59:17-07:00","id":1340271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340270#post1340270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well then, what is? What do I expect from a Metastasis game that's different from a Hyperplasia game besides more Variations and Scars? How do I pick an appropriate Threat Level? I feel like more guidelines are warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the Standing and Scale sidebar on page 54 of preview 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:00:26-07:00","id":1340273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340270#post1340270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well then, what is? What do I expect from a Metastasis game that's different from a Hyperplasia game besides more Variations and Scars? How do I pick an appropriate Threat Level? I feel like more guidelines are warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Threat Level is determined by the total Magnitude of Variations possessed by the character(s) it pursues, whether that's at character creation or upon revealing a new conspiracy unconnected to one the cohort has destroyed. I don't know how &quot;bigger conspiracies are attached to characters with more power(s)&quot; is not incredibly plain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:03:05-07:00","id":1340274,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve gotten the ST chapter yet, which is where I\u2019d expect to find info on how this stuff plays and how to choose your threat level and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:22:55-07:00","id":1340277,"title":"","content":"Christ, the rules for pushing Devoted over the edge into Nemesis status are a fun dramatic tool. Kill your hunter's boss and they <i>immediately</i> get much stronger and madder even if before it was just the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:26:25-07:00","id":1340278,"title":"","content":"These rules appear to have been written with very particular ideas of chapter structure and chronicle pacing, which aren't borne out of the way these things are discussed in the system chapter or, in my experience, how they turn out in actual play. I have experienced games where these rules would result in a conspiracy completing Complexity 10 projects in less than a week because the PCs had a few really bad nights that took multiple chapters to resolve, or in the conspiracies going quiet for months because there was an extended timeskip.<br /> <br /> I <i>want</i> to like these rules (that initial preview was neat), and I'm going to give them an honest shot, but on first impression they look like the single weakest part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T12:38:34-07:00","id":1340279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340266#post1340266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some good stuff here, but I'm disappointed by the relative lack of guidelines on choosing a starting Threat Level. The one-word descriptors for each Threat Level tier are extremely unhelpful: what does a Hyperplasia game play like, and how does that differ from a Dysplasia or Metastasis game? About how much overt action and threat should you expect for each tier? Which tier should you generally expect to fear for your Loyalty touchstones' lives the moment the conspirators connect them to you? Which tier do they break out the submachine guns? I didn't bring this up for Manuscript Preview 2 because I assumed the Antagonists section would expand on it, but it doesn't appear to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can give you one example from my experience in a Metastasis game; Eric has mentioned this as well. We had a group of 4 very potent deviants all with at least some useful combat variations. We ended up breaking into a conspiracy fortress and knocking over the node there after a series of running battles through the facility. They sent several strike teams of dudes with SMGs against us and it wasn't a huge problem until they got creative with gas and AP rounds. We all walked away with (I think) only one character seriously wounded. We didn't face any dangerous devoted, just a very well armed and fortified node that was trained in dealing with problem deviants. If they'd had a devoted or two with the power to better pin us down while they brought their full forces to bear, we'd have been in trouble. A lower threat level playtest group (Hyperplasia or Dysplasia, I don't quite remember) that was faced with just one group of similar baddies with SMGs did much worse. They were in serious danger from the start and were probably ill suited for that kind of threat. I think that the makeup of the cohort will play a big part in what solutions it has to that kind of problem. My character was bulletproof, but would have been very susceptible to mind manipulation, for example.<br /> <br /> I'd say though that the better understanding of how dangerous the Conspiracy is has more to do with how many actions it can take, how big its power stat is (the most likely one used to bring this kind of action to bear against the cohort), and the makeup of its relevant nodes. To some extent, players have some control over this. By evading surveillance, you can give yourself an opening to attack in the next chapter. You can specifically target nodes for destruction that could cause SMG problems if that's what you are worried about. If a conspiracy is robbed of influence over guys with guns, they can't send them after you.<br /> <br /> One other thing I should mention: keeping your loyalty touchstones safe might be your character's goal, but might not be the player's. These are NPCs (or fellow cohort members) that the player is putting in the line of fire to serve their character's need for that connection. If you've got characters that you as a player have a real problem with the conspiracy screwing with, don't make them a touchstone. The loyalty touchstone's job is to be threatened by the conspiracy to give you an opportunity for story. The conspiracy's job is to leverage whatever means they can find to make you do what they want, and if they can't find you, they'll find your friends. If their lives are being threatened and your character is being forced to make hard choices, it's because everything is going as it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T13:51:03-07:00","id":1340292,"title":"","content":"Belated realization, but: It's fun to note that becoming Feral is less a Game Over screen and more a switch over to Hard Mode; you get no benefit from Stubborn Resolve, you can't become a Nemesis or a Guardian, and you can't heal Instability just by moving for or against the Touchstones you no longer have, but the way Stability works means you still have purely supernatural means of recovering that put the stakes a little higher.<br /> <br /> Ferals are locked out of healing any Instability worse than the minor sort without developing new Scars, and they don't have any means of holding back the minor Instability at the end of each chapter or the probably-multiple minor Instabilities at the start of every story, but they'll never Falter or lose more Loyalty Touchstones. What this means, then, is that a Feral who hopes to last needs to pursue Acclimation as quickly as possible and entangle their new Scars to avoid mounting difficulties from their rising minimum Magnitude and make it easier to roll exceptional successes on Scar Finesse and Scar Resistance rolls, which are the only vector for Scar-free healing you now have.<br /> <br /> In other words, going Feral is less of a death sentence and more of a permanent change in priorities from personal relationships to keeping various plates spinning with regards to your occult state; until you manage to hit something like an equilibrium, you pretty much have to keep scads of Experiences on hand to buy new Variations or dots of Acclimation or Attributes \u2014 maybe figure out a Stabilizer if you're lucky.<br /> <br /> It's still definitely not something you want to aim for, but it's interesting to see as a &quot;soft&quot; failure state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T14:02:22-07:00","id":1340296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340278#post1340278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These rules appear to have been written with very particular ideas of chapter structure and chronicle pacing, which aren't borne out of the way these things are discussed in the system chapter or, in my experience, how they turn out in actual play. I have experienced games where these rules would result in a conspiracy completing Complexity 10 projects in less than a week because the PCs had a few really bad nights that took multiple chapters to resolve, or in the conspiracies going quiet for months because there was an extended timeskip.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like less a problem with the rules and more because of some odd circumstances. They're clearly not Rules As Intended.<br /> <br /> I think it just needs a &quot;be reasonable&quot; line in here or the Storytelling chapter, and it'll be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T15:58:07-07:00","id":1340315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340296#post1340296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like less a problem with the rules and more because of some odd circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>Are</i> they &quot;odd circumstances?&quot; How do your own games usually shake out?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T16:37:31-07:00","id":1340319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340315#post1340315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Are</i> they &quot;odd circumstances?&quot; How do your own games usually shake out?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Does it matter? It wouldn't change if it happened to me, since the issue is &quot;how long is this session in game time.&quot;<br /> <br /> To be frank, most of the episodes I have (read here, immediate situation that needs more than a session to resolve) have been two, three at most. At some point, the ST realizes this is taking too long and starts causing lucky breaks so we can move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T16:40:37-07:00","id":1340321,"title":"","content":"Wait, can I just select Suppressible Relentless Variation and have no drawbacks for all subtle scars, and can I put this up on perpetual scars? Or is there something I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T16:46:07-07:00","id":1340323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340292#post1340292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Belated realization, but: It's fun to note that becoming Feral is less a Game Over screen and more a switch over to Hard Mode; you get no benefit from Stubborn Resolve, you can't become a Nemesis or a Guardian, and you can't heal Instability just by moving for or against the Touchstones you no longer have, but the way Stability works means you still have purely supernatural means of recovering that put the stakes a little higher.<br /> <br /> Ferals are locked out of healing any Instability worse than the minor sort without developing new Scars, and they don't have any means of holding back the minor Instability at the end of each chapter or the probably-multiple minor Instabilities at the start of every story, but they'll never Falter or lose more Loyalty Touchstones. What this means, then, is that a Feral who hopes to last needs to pursue Acclimation as quickly as possible and entangle their new Scars to avoid mounting difficulties from their rising minimum Magnitude and make it easier to roll exceptional successes on Scar Finesse and Scar Resistance rolls, which are the only vector for Scar-free healing you now have.<br /> <br /> In other words, going Feral is less of a death sentence and more of a permanent change in priorities from personal relationships to keeping various plates spinning with regards to your occult state; until you manage to hit something like an equilibrium, you pretty much have to keep scads of Experiences on hand to buy new Variations or dots of Acclimation or Attributes \u2014 maybe figure out a Stabilizer if you're lucky.<br /> <br /> It's still definitely not something you want to aim for, but it's interesting to see as a &quot;soft&quot; failure state.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting observation. The window a Feral has in which to raise Acclimation is likely to be quite short. Remember that you can't increase Acclimation if you have any medium or major Instability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340296#post1340296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it just needs a &quot;be reasonable&quot; line in here or the Storytelling chapter, and it'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a short note in the Storytelling Rules (top of p. 15 of the 4th preview) about adjusting the definitions of per-chapter, per-scene, and per-story effects to accommodate this (I tried to warn people to at least closely skim that chapter! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). The sidebar focuses on Variations/Scars/Adaptations, but you can easily apply it to conspiracy actions, as well. If you want a &quot;countdown timer&quot; on a Project based on in-world days/weeks/months instead of narrative units like chapters, you can do that. You can set rules for how Renegade actions that sap away conspiracy actions delay the fruition of Projects - perhaps by a day or week per wasted conspiracy action (depending on context). In fact, I can probably say as much outright in the conspiracies chapter.<br /> <br /> I want to be a bit careful, though. &quot;Per-chapter means per day&quot; works, and &quot;per-chapter means per-chapter&quot; works, but trying to mix them too freely in the same game without adequately communicating this to the players is a recipe for needless arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340321#post1340321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, can I just select Suppressible Relentless Variation and have no drawbacks for all subtle scars, and can I put this up on perpetual scars? Or is there something I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had a quite spirited discussion about this exact question. Suppressible Relentless Variation has some serious problems in certain circumstances, that I'm currently working to fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-08-2019, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T17:19:36-07:00","id":1340324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340323#post1340323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting observation. The window a Feral has in which to raise Acclimation is likely to be quite short. Remember that you can't increase Acclimation if you have any medium or major Instability.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can only raise it once per chapter, as well, and in the best of circumstances a character has about a fifty-fifty chance of healing minor Instability if they're rolling an unresisted Scar Finesse roll with a full set of five-dot components, which means a lot of the initial desperate push is going to necessitate burning through Experiences so you can pick up new Scars that aren't Persistent (which you can <i>also</i> only do once per chapter).<br /> <br /> It's also dramatically harder if you have a higher-Magnitude Variation and no head start on buying Acclimation, because taking new Scars when you can't leverage Touchstones means any given chapter where you don't roll an exceptional success sees your Scar Resistance penalty make no net reduction at best. Even if it all goes perfectly, you've still changed your main priorities to Get Used To Being Extremely Weird And Magic instead of having goals that relate to other people.<br /> <br /> The upshot, at least, is that buying a dot of Acclimation itself affords you a little bit of breathing room in the form of extra Stability, provided nothing else goes wrong (#ConspiratorsDoNotInteract), so if you've saved up enough Experiences and can make it through the next chapter, you can theoretically go for another increase.<br /> <br /> It's an unlikely situation and a lot of circumstances can make it borderline impossible to manage, but that's Divergence and the Web of Pain in general, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of this approximate balancing act, though: Are the restrictions on raising Acclimation such that you can't raise Acclimation with the appropriate Experience expenditure if you've had any worse Instability in the same chapter, or is it a viable scene to purge your solitary medium Instability into a new Scar in a safe location, gasp your way through the erupting pain, and then spend the remainder of that chunk of camera-time taking stock and getting to grips with your new abilities and trauma?<br /> <br /> (Also, should the exceptional success results for Scar Finesse and Scar Resistance rolls be listed under the Healing Instability section in the same way that the dramatic failure results are listed under Causing Instability?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T18:00:53-07:00","id":1340335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340324#post1340324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can only raise it once per chapter, as well, and in the best of circumstances a character has about a fifty-fifty chance of healing minor Instability if they're rolling an unresisted Scar Finesse roll with a full set of five-dot components, which means a lot of the initial desperate push is going to necessitate burning through Experiences so you can pick up new Scars that aren't Persistent (which you can <i>also</i> only do once per chapter).<br /> <br /> It's also dramatically harder if you have a higher-Magnitude Variation and no head start on buying Acclimation, because taking new Scars when you can't leverage Touchstones means any given chapter where you don't roll an exceptional success sees your Scar Resistance penalty make no net reduction at best. Even if it all goes perfectly, you've still changed your main priorities to Get Used To Being Extremely Weird And Magic instead of having goals that relate to other people.<br /> <br /> The upshot, at least, is that buying a dot of Acclimation itself affords you a little bit of breathing room in the form of extra Stability, provided nothing else goes wrong (#ConspiratorsDoNotInteract), so if you've saved up enough Experiences and can make it through the next chapter, you can theoretically go for another increase.<br /> <br /> It's an unlikely situation and a lot of circumstances can make it borderline impossible to manage, but that's Divergence and the Web of Pain in general, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of this approximate balancing act, though: Are the restrictions on raising Acclimation such that you can't raise Acclimation with the appropriate Experience expenditure if you've had any worse Instability in the same chapter, or is it a viable scene to purge your solitary medium Instability into a new Scar in a safe location, gasp your way through the erupting pain, and then spend the remainder of that chunk of camera-time taking stock and getting to grips with your new abilities and trauma?<br /> <br /> (Also, should the exceptional success results for Scar Finesse and Scar Resistance rolls be listed under the Healing Instability section in the same way that the dramatic failure results are listed under Causing Instability?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can clear your medium Instability and then raise your Acclimation during the same chapter.<br /> <br /> It should. I've updated my working draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T18:48:11-07:00","id":1340344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340319#post1340319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it matter? It wouldn't change if it happened to me, since the issue is &quot;how long is this session in game time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, <i>yes</i>, because we clearly have different experiences that colour our respective takes on the system.<br /> <br /> As for your answer, I guess I'm more interested in how much time your sessions <i>usually </i>cover, more than the anomalies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340323#post1340323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's actually a short note in the Storytelling Rules (top of p. 15 of the 4th preview) about adjusting the definitions of per-chapter, per-scene, and per-story effects to accommodate this (I tried to warn people to at least closely skim that chapter! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)..</div> </div> </div> </div> I did read it, but I'm afraid it doesn't really resolve my problem. Playing fast and loose with per-scene/-chapter/-story limits is one thing, I feel, while the Conspiracy system...<br /> <br /> <i>As far as I can tell</i>, Conspiracy Actions have an intended pacing to them, but that pacing is assumed rather than explained. This, coupled with how heavily abstracted they are, divorces them from organic play in a way I don't quite know how to resolve.<br /> In a better example, perhaps, a lot of the potential complications of a failed Conspiracy Actions (<b>Step Six</b>, p. 67) just sound like things players are given to do on a whim. What stops the characters from trying to befriend the attacking Deviant, or shoot the diplomats, or record and disseminate the attack on them using the core gameplay system?<br /> <br /> I have less of a problem with downtime actions and projects, though they hit on the same unspoken pacing issue as regular Conspiracy Actions. They feature an even greater level of abstraction, but the abstracted events are all off-screen, or would otherwise involve instances of the ST rolling against themself.<br /> <br /> (One thing I <i>had</i> missed on my first readthrough was the <b>Best Defense</b> sidebar, which neatly resolves another issue I had with the system. It's actually pretty elegant.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T19:15:22-07:00","id":1340347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340344#post1340344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a better example, perhaps, a lot of the potential complications of a failed Conspiracy Actions (<b>Step Six</b>, p. 67) just sound like things players are given to do on a whim. What stops the characters from trying to befriend the attacking Deviant, or shoot the diplomats, or record and disseminate the attack on them using the core gameplay system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the part where all of these things are set up as stakes established before the confrontation (which may not even be with the cohort themselves) and happen without the cohort needing to roll for their benefits.<br /> <br /> All of these things come up before the scene is even introduced. It's a collaborative story-direction tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T19:20:04-07:00","id":1340348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340344#post1340344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a better example, perhaps, a lot of the potential complications of a failed Conspiracy Actions (<b>Step Six</b>, p. 67) just sound like things players are given to do on a whim. What stops the characters from trying to befriend the attacking Deviant, or shoot the diplomats, or record and disseminate the attack on them using the core gameplay system?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the problem here? ST can veto some stuff, but the conspiracy explicitly screws up in a way the players can exploit, this just gives the players a chance to decide what that is. FATE does it all the time, the story comes from trying to utilize the scene in the plot hook-injected way (in order: Hellbender is in a talkative mood, but she's just having doubts right now and needs to be persuaded that what she's doing is wrong; you managed to shoot the corrupt diplomats, but now the legitimate authorities are after you; and you found a convenient place to record an obviously illegal attack on you, but now you need to make it obvious you're the victim and get around a media blackout as soon as the conspiracy realizes what you're doing).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T21:37:16-07:00","id":1340357,"title":"","content":"If you choose to develop a new Scar in order to heal Instability, can that Scar be of any Magnitude, as long as it meets the required minimum? Is there a <i>maximum</i> you can take a new Scar on at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-09-2019, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T21:51:33-07:00","id":1340359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340321#post1340321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, can I just select Suppressible Relentless Variation and have no drawbacks for all subtle scars, and can I put this up on perpetual scars? Or is there something I'm missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some other people have noticed that exploit too and pointed it out. It should be addressed in the final text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T23:40:26-07:00","id":1340371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340357#post1340357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you choose to develop a new Scar in order to heal Instability, can that Scar be of any Magnitude, as long as it meets the required minimum? Is there a <i>maximum</i> you can take a new Scar on at?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like you can just go up to 5 right away. The minimum is that each new unentangled scar has to be worse than the one before it, iirc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-08T23:59:33-07:00","id":1340375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340371#post1340371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like you can just go up to 5 right away. The minimum is that each new unentangled scar has to be worse than the one before it, iirc</div> </div> </div> </div>Minimum is equal to the number of unentangled Scars the new one would bring the total to, to a maximum of 5 (you can have more than five unentangled Scars, but every new one after the fourth has to be Magnitude 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T09:11:45-07:00","id":1340423,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> Sorry if this has been brought up already, but I was curious if you could explain how the +1 version of Identifier works with Perpetual Variations? For example, if a character has Magnitude 4 Otherworldly Connection, do they leave behind bread crumbs everywhere they walk or only when they try to exorcise an ephemeral entity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T13:22:07-07:00","id":1340480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340423#post1340423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> Sorry if this has been brought up already, but I was curious if you could explain how the +1 version of Identifier works with Perpetual Variations? For example, if a character has Magnitude 4 Otherworldly Connection, do they leave behind bread crumbs everywhere they walk or only when they try to exorcise an ephemeral entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Eric, but my guess would be whenever the effects actually come into play \u2014 for Otherworldly Connection 4 (no Wild Variation), that'd be any time you perceive, communicate with, touch, or banish something from the world the Variation represents; in cases like Immunity, that'd be whenever something would ordinarily impose the Tilt, damage, or other effect you're immune to; for Aquatic, it'd be whenever you were immersed in enough water to be able to normally move around in it and/or risk drowning without the Variation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing for the list of corrections: Cooldown is listed as an example Scar for a number of Variations that are not themselves Directed (Bioluminescence, Healing Touch, Otherworldly Connection), which probably necessitates either changing which Scars those examples use or expanding the Directed Scar keyword to something more like Rebellious Variation's restrictions.<br /> <br /> Separately: Body Snatcher says how the character's Attributes and Scars move with the Body Swap effect, but do Variations move with their entangled Scars or is the Remade's full package of Variations available to them (some of them potentially Scar-free for a time) once a transfer is made, or some other interpretation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-09-2019, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T15:59:37-07:00","id":1340696,"title":"","content":"I know this is more Cross-over and outside the scope of the kickstarter, but I had a question regarding ghosts. <br /> <br /> Since Ghosts and Souls are completely different.<br /> And since Ghosts are primarily the emotional echo imprinted in ephemera by death.<br /> And since Deviants have emotions that are both skewed and highly amplified (especially near death).<br /> <br /> Then does that mean that, on the whole, Deviants trend towards creating Ghosts more often than not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T19:08:41-07:00","id":1340706,"title":"","content":"The rules governing ghost creation require having Integrity, so RAW, they don't create ghosts at all.<br /> <br /> However, we know that Mages can cause ghosts when they die, and they also don't have Integrity, so whether or not that's actually 'true' (insofar as anything in a toolbox setting is true), we can't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T21:03:09-07:00","id":1340716,"title":"","content":"Apologies if it's been answered already (could you direct me where?). Have we gotten a sneak peek at the Settings? I believe they're coming out next week but do we know what areas are covered? They've always been a very enticing part of the second edition cores. I believe one is in South America?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T05:42:50-07:00","id":1340764,"title":"","content":"There's a South American setting that's Deviant-focused in the Contagion Chronicle, in Chile, which myself and John Burke put together. I don't believe the Deviant core settings have been teased at all, apart from the one I spoke about in the Onyx Pathcast interview I had a while back. Can't remember how much I revealed about it there :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T05:50:37-07:00","id":1340767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340716#post1340716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if it's been answered already (could you direct me where?). Have we gotten a sneak peek at the Settings? I believe they're coming out next week but do we know what areas are covered? They've always been a very enticing part of the second edition cores. I believe one is in South America?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, literally this morning we just got a partial look at Ankara, with the writeup for one of the conspiracies active there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Preview: Ankara</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ankara is the home of two powerful conspiracies duking it out for control over the city. Darwin, Australia is a complex ecology of conspiracies, each one of them as likely to be prey for the others as predator. Connellsville, Pennsylvania is a quiet little coal-mining town with a terrible secret, overseen as it is by a pharmaceutical company that sells the Remade it produces to other conspiracies. And Newark, Delaware is a college town whose university hosts Progenitors as guest lecturers.<br /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T05:59:05-07:00","id":1340768,"title":"","content":"Hah! Well, there you go, so the setting I was talking about on the Onyx Pathcast is Ankara <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It was a hell of a lot of fun to write, especially because Ankara can be a pretty weird place before you get anywhere near adding supernatural elements. The glitches in the Ankara urban sprawl? Those are an <i>actual thing</i>, caused by the speed with which the city expanded and the creation of illegal <i>gekecondu</i> streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T07:40:32-07:00","id":1340774,"title":"","content":"Super excited to see one of the example settings in my itty bitty corner of the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T08:45:05-07:00","id":1340784,"title":"","content":"Eric also mentions the other three settings in his intro to the Ankara preview:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This time, we\u2019re showcasing one of the four settings from the core book. Ankara is the home of two powerful conspiracies duking it out for control over the city. Darwin, Australia is a complex ecology of conspiracies, each one of them as likely to be prey for the others as predator. Connellsville, Pennsylvania is a quiet little coal-mining town with a terrible secret, overseen as it is by a pharmaceutical company that sells the Remade it produces to other conspiracies. And Newark, Delaware is a college town whose university hosts Progenitors as guest lecturers. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T11:05:18-07:00","id":1340807,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, and Eric.<br /> <br /> Yes, I was conflating Chile setting in Contagion with Ankara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T14:58:58-07:00","id":1340848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ankara </div> </div> </div>Just make sure that no one opens any sarcophagi from there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-11-2019, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T07:52:58-07:00","id":1340950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340848#post1340848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just make sure that no one opens any sarcophagi from there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Annoyingly enough I forgot about the sarcophagus from Bloodlines when writing the Ankara setting for Deviant, and now wish I'd crept a reference to it in there :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T11:45:35-07:00","id":1340977,"title":"","content":"On the conspiracy rules - have I missed something, or are a conspiracy's Attributes mostly worthless? Standing is important, because it sets how often a conspiracy can act. Resistance contributes to the health track. But the one thing Power and Finesse get used for is deciding whether the conspiracy pays a price when it messes with PCs. It seems to me a conspiracy that bought Resistance heavily would be much more capable than one which invested in Power and Finesse. It would be vulnerable more often, but it would have a larger safety margin, too. The marginal gain from pushing Power or Finesse past, oh, 5 or so looks a lot less than the gain from 1 Resistance dot at <i>any</i> point.<br /> <br /> I can see the logic behind it - the ST shouldn't be rolling dice unless the players are involved somehow, so there's no point to rolling for downtime actions; and PCs should oppose characters, not organizations, in action scenes, which leaves very little scope for a conspiracy's traits in those scenes. But then it's hard to see why conspiracies need Attributes at all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T17:34:01-07:00","id":1341022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1340977#post1340977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the conspiracy rules - have I missed something, or are a conspiracy's Attributes mostly worthless? Standing is important, because it sets how often a conspiracy can act. Resistance contributes to the health track. But the one thing Power and Finesse get used for is deciding whether the conspiracy pays a price when it messes with PCs. It seems to me a conspiracy that bought Resistance heavily would be much more capable than one which invested in Power and Finesse. It would be vulnerable more often, but it would have a larger safety margin, too. The marginal gain from pushing Power or Finesse past, oh, 5 or so looks a lot less than the gain from 1 Resistance dot at <i>any</i> point.</div> </div> </div> </div>A conspiracy that buys Resistance heavily is going to be that much less effective at using Nodes that actually do anything outside the conspiracy itself, and trying to use Structural Nodes to do the work of Temporal or Exploitative Nodes is inherently less effective in a way that risks the conspiracy as a whole taking more damage (which in turn forces constant reorganization). Resistance contributes to Association, but it's the least useful for actually extending the conspiracy's reach.<br /> <br /> On the larger scale, a conspiracy that turns itself into a big brick of Resistance and Structural Nodes is pretty much begging to be subverted by other conspiracies, because it's very good at continuing to exist but doesn't accomplish a whole lot else on its own (and this goes double if it <i>is</i> infiltrated by other conspiracies).<br /> <br /> The goal of a conspiracy is not simply to continue to exist, and Resistance only helps it on that front rather than in acting to preserve its Principles or halt the progress of saboteurs and infiltrators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T18:10:06-07:00","id":1341031,"title":"","content":"As two powers can flick off if people suffer a breaking point, and deviants can be quite horrific to behold, it makes me wonder: how easily do deviants cause breaking points? Is effectively any obvious deviation of scar a breaking point in and of itself? Do conspirators take fewer breaking points from deviants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T20:48:43-07:00","id":1341045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341031#post1341031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As two powers can flick off if people suffer a breaking point, and deviants can be quite horrific to behold, it makes me wonder: how easily do deviants cause breaking points? Is effectively any obvious deviation of scar a breaking point in and of itself? Do conspirators take fewer breaking points from deviants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Core CofD has breaking points occur whenever someone encounters something (typically violence or supernatural phenomena) that outstrips her ability to handle it. Baselines who have little or no experience with the supernatural could be set off by simply seeing a Deviant use an Overt Variation (or merely meeting one with an Overt Scar). Repeated exposure to the same kinds of situations will eventually dull that shock response, so a member of a conspiracy would likely grow inured to the horrors involved in creating Remade and jaded about the powers they've seen the Broken wield. Granted, ones who haven't seen a Deviant grow violent might well still suffer a breaking point if the Remade turns that violence on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T21:13:21-07:00","id":1341047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341022#post1341022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A conspiracy that buys Resistance heavily is going to be that much less effective at using Nodes that actually do anything outside the conspiracy itself, and trying to use Structural Nodes to do the work of Temporal or Exploitative Nodes is inherently less effective in a way that risks the conspiracy as a whole taking more damage (which in turn forces constant reorganization). Resistance contributes to Association, but it's the least useful for actually extending the conspiracy's reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would <i>think</i> that the dots in an Attribute correlate with the number of Nodes ties to that Attribute. But there's no such link in the text. How many Nodes are Structural has nothing to do with how many dots are in Resistance.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Attributes are irrelevant to downtime actions, which are how a conspiracy extends its reach. They only matter for actions against Renegades - and there, it's one roll per scene, and the conspiracy needs only one success on that roll. It's quite true that most actions against Renegades will use Power or Finesse; but looking at dice pool probabilities, there isn't much point to pushing either Attribute past 5, where success comes 5 out of 6 times. Whereas Resistance directly increases a conspiracy's ability to take damage, and therefore indirectly increases its ability to take actions, which gives it more chances to increase its power, in a way that scales with the Attribute.<br /> <br /> If Attributes were needed in downtime actions you would be correct; high Power and Finesse would be crucial to a conspiracy's accomplishing anything. But the rules don't say that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T22:11:48-07:00","id":1341053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341047#post1341047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would <i>think</i> that the dots in an Attribute correlate with the number of Nodes ties to that Attribute. But there's no such link in the text. How many Nodes are Structural has nothing to do with how many dots are in Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made no assertion to the contrary. <i>Using</i> Structural Nodes, though, is what Resistance is for, and the value of putting dots into the Attribute for using logistical Nodes is comparatively low if you don't actually have at least a few high-utility Structural Nodes to lean on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly, Attributes are irrelevant to downtime actions, which are how a conspiracy extends its reach. </div> </div> </div>A conspiracy extends its reach by taking conspiracy actions and completing Projects. Conspiracy actions specifically must include things like recruiting, blackmailing, killing, or otherwise meddling with the extended social circle of a Remade and her cohort; it's a viable narrative space to draw Linchpins from, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They only matter for actions against Renegades - and there, it's one roll per scene, and the conspiracy needs only one success on that roll. </div> </div> </div>Because a single success means there's no automatic way the action gets messy \u2014 and a one in six incidence of conspiracy actions getting messy is plenty of consequences when the conspiracy is big enough to be putting multiple conspiracy actions into play per chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's quite true that most actions against Renegades will use Power or Finesse; but looking at dice pool probabilities, there isn't much point to pushing either Attribute past 5, where success comes 5 out of 6 times. </div> </div> </div>\u2026Please remember how dice pool penalties work and how the Attribute distribution breaks down, because a one- to three-dice penalty is a substantial dent at that level and a conspiracy needs Standing at least halfway up the Threat Level chart to have enough Attribute dots for a secondary 5 to be feasible without sitting on multiple Complexity 10 Projects. A dice roll is a dice roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whereas Resistance directly increases a conspiracy's ability to take damage, and therefore indirectly increases its ability to take actions, which gives it more chances to increase its power, in a way that scales with the Attribute. </div> </div> </div>Again: Pretty much every time a conspiracy takes lethal damage to its Association, it has to reorganize or suffer further setbacks and can see its Principles change. Resistance and Association have <i>no</i> impact on the number of conspiracy actions (and therefore potential downtime Effort) granted by Standing.<br /> <br /> &quot;The organization exists&quot; is not the organization's goal. A conspiracy is irrevocably gone once its Association fills with aggravated damage, and any inheritor organization is a different conspiracy; changes to policy are nontrivial alterations, so &quot;higher Resistance means a conspiracy can, if it becomes desperate enough to throw itself into complete disarray, take more actions&quot; is a negligible benefit if it means half its key personnel have changed departments, its public and private faces have blurred in a weird direction, and a purge has become necessary to get the group back on track while a cohort of deviants has figured out the next mutagen refinery to bomb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Attributes were needed in downtime actions you would be correct; high Power and Finesse would be crucial to a conspiracy's accomplishing anything. But the rules don't say that. </div> </div> </div>They also do not say &quot;the cohort and their extended social circle are completely irrelevant to the functioning of a conspiracy that is specifically being engaged with in the mechanics because it is after them.&quot; Conspiracy actions do not have to be hostile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T00:36:14-07:00","id":1341065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341045#post1341045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core CofD has breaking points occur whenever someone encounters something (typically violence or supernatural phenomena) that outstrips her ability to handle it. Baselines who have little or no experience with the supernatural could be set off by simply seeing a Deviant use an Overt Variation (or merely meeting one with an Overt Scar). Repeated exposure to the same kinds of situations will eventually dull that shock response, so a member of a conspiracy would likely grow inured to the horrors involved in creating Remade and jaded about the powers they've seen the Broken wield. Granted, ones who haven't seen a Deviant grow violent might well still suffer a breaking point if the Remade turns that violence on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tolerance for Biology and Deadpan (from Mage 2e) are great for comedy relief and almost essential for security guards, secretaries, technicians and other low-level Conspiracy employees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T07:53:09-07:00","id":1341091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341053#post1341053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A conspiracy extends its reach by taking conspiracy actions and completing Projects. Conspiracy actions specifically must include things like recruiting, blackmailing, killing, or otherwise meddling with the extended social circle of a Remade and her cohort; it's a viable narrative space to draw Linchpins from, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>A conspiracy extends its reach by completing Projects, period. Conspiracy actions <i>don't</i> add to its power, they just apply it. It's part of the point that conspiracies become more dangerous when they're not involved in play - if the cohort isn't engaging with their antagonist regularly, it'll have more resources to throw at them when it does appear, so they have to pursue it if it doesn't pursue them. Therefore, conspiracy actions aren't a good source for Linchpins, or any other resource - the most you could justify, in terms of the rules, is the personnel change that can happen due to a crisis point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341053#post1341053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Please remember how dice pool penalties work and how the Attribute distribution breaks down, because a one- to three-dice penalty is a substantial dent at that level and a conspiracy needs Standing at least halfway up the Threat Level chart to have enough Attribute dots for a secondary 5 to be feasible without sitting on multiple Complexity 10 Projects. A dice roll is a dice roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that penalties on <i>that</i> dice pool are actually uncommon. Other than &quot;inappropriate Node&quot;, in fact, all the examples are effects of enemy actions.<br /> <br /> And I admit that, if you're playing at a threat level of 1 or 2, Power and Finesse are more important than Resistance, just to reach basic competence in conspiracy actions. The point here is that the marginal gain from adding Power or Finesse tapers off sharply once the conspiracy <i>is</i> competent - which is not true for Resistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341053#post1341053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so &quot;higher Resistance means a conspiracy can, if it becomes desperate enough to throw itself into complete disarray, take more actions&quot; is a negligible benefit if it means half its key personnel have changed departments, its public and private faces have blurred in a weird direction, and a purge has become necessary to get the group back on track while a cohort of deviants has figured out the next mutagen refinery to bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the rules, a conspiracy that hits two crisis points in a chapter can shift an Attribute dot for both crises, moving it from Power to Finesse the first time, and Finesse to Power the second time, ending up unchanged, aside from the damage to its Association. If a conspiracy is deliberately stressing itself to take more actions, I can't see why it wouldn't do that.<br /> <br /> And higher Resistance means more time until damage forces a purge - I'm fairly sure purges aren't supposed to happen unless the Association track is nearly full with damage of some kind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T09:24:14-07:00","id":1341099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341091#post1341091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see why it wouldn't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe cause it's blatantly against the spirit of the rules? <br /> <br /> The obvious point here is that crisis points are supposed to effect a change in the organization, if the end result of your actions is that no change has taken place because you moved stuff back and forth to a static end result, you're missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T12:02:27-07:00","id":1341115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341091#post1341091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A conspiracy extends its reach by completing Projects, period.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Except that penalties on <i>that</i> dice pool are actually uncommon. Other than &quot;inappropriate Node&quot;, in fact, all the examples are effects of enemy actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only there were some sort of pool from which Projects needed to draw their Effort, some sort of set quantity of actions the conspiracy could take. If only that pool of actions was directly reduced by having to deal with attacks from external threats in addition to potentially not having the ability to choose how the culmination of those attacks effected the conspiracy's holdings. It would certainly be preferable if such enemies had a strong incentive to press forward regularly with such an assault on a chapter-by-chapter basis, like, say, gaining Beats and Willpower and holding off further destabilization of their place in reality, but I don't know where one would find such a group of people. It's a mystery, it really is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I admit that, if you're playing at a threat level of 1 or 2, Power and Finesse are more important than Resistance, just to reach basic competence in conspiracy actions. The point here is that the marginal gain from adding Power or Finesse tapers off sharply once the conspiracy is competent - which is not true for Resistance. </div> </div> </div>You're here describing &quot;competence in conspiracy actions&quot; purely in terms of ability to do more conspiracy actions before a purge, and also implying that competence beyond the reach of most fast-food chains is a function of brand loyalty, despite &quot;this secret organization can do more at the cost of making a complete mess of itself, and it's more invested in doing that than being able to consistently deal with its super-mutant archenemies without spilling classified documents and faulty brainwashing everywhere&quot; being the opposite of a good practice for holding together a group with global influence or regional ubiquity and a vested interest in not getting found out by the wider world.<br /> <br /> The limiting factors for conspiracy actions are that they have to affect the cohort in some way, they have to be within the scope of their available Nodes, they can only be safely undertaken a number of times per chapter based on Standing (which is further cut into by Deviants attacking their Nodes and sabotage by other conspiracies), and that using them stops a conspiracy from building (as much) Effort for its projects without suffering the same disorganization as they would from exceeding their safe limit. A conspiracy in conflict with a cohort or other conspiracies doesn't need to make a purge at all if it can go a couple of chapters without taking damage, and doing that is both easier to manage by using conspiracy actions to stymie Deviant activity against their Nodes and less costly to the conspiracy's long-term assets both organizationally and in terms of retention.<br /> <br /> Pushing its limits means a conspiracy is courting disintegration, and Resistance only helps &quot;more&quot; with that in the same sense that Stamina keeps you from dying as rapidly in an armed conflict. The system is not made to model its mechanical elements existing in a vacuum for their own sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:06:48-07:00","id":1341135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341099#post1341099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe cause it's blatantly against the spirit of the rules?<br /> <br /> The obvious point here is that crisis points are supposed to effect a change in the organization, if the end result of your actions is that no change has taken place because you moved stuff back and forth to a static end result, you're missing the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course it's against the spirit of the rules! But that means the rules are faulty. If conspiracies shouldn't do the Attribute shuffle to dodge the more serious consequences of over-stress, they shouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> Satchel: if you're not going to respond to what I actually said, you'd be better off not responding at all. I said originally that, if you look at the rules, a conspiracy's Power and Finesse actually have very little influence on its capability in play, and that Resistance may be worth taking up to the trait cap, but not the others. That's because conspiracies just <i>don't roll dice</i> very often, and unlike Resistance, Power and Finesse come into play only as dice pools. Moreover, Attributes aren't even rolled on all conspiracy actions - just the ones where the conspiracy takes the initiative. When a cohort is attacking a conspiracy, the conspiracy has to use an action to respond, but it doesn't get to roll dice to influence the outcome.<br /> <br /> You are trying to prove that Resistance isn't a god stat. I never said it was. I said Power and Finesse are dump stats. Nothing you've said gives me grounds to revise that opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:57:32-07:00","id":1341150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341135#post1341135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, of course it's against the spirit of the rules! But that means the rules are faulty. If conspiracies shouldn't do the Attribute shuffle to dodge the more serious consequences of over-stress, they shouldn't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't gotten around to reading the chapter yet, so I can't contribute to the rest of this discussion, buuuuuuuuuuuut this won't get you anywhere.<br /> <br /> A) The &quot;Spirit of the Rules&quot; is more essential for any reading or enactment of the mechanics at the table than arbirtrary &quot;But the rules don't exclude that!&quot; reading, because the games are here to provide a feel and mood and some direction for what is otherwise basically a group exercise in storytelling. If the spirit of the game goes one way and you exploit a reading of the text that goes the other way, the game isn't broken by itself for doing that, you're the one who broke the game for your table, which also means everyone else thinks you're probably a jerk.<br /> <br /> That might be faulty if this were a video game. It's not. In situations like these, the writing is often laid down in the spirit of people critically thinking and not being an asshole. Maybe consider that.<br /> <br /> B) In as far as I can pick up from the conversation, the attribute shuffle is not intended to be used in the consequences of overstress, because those attributes represent the allocation of manpower, resources, and time of an organization, and that's tough enough to shuffle around when things are moving smoothly enough-in the cases of circumstances where &quot;damage&quot; is a real and immediate thing, it takes more work to get that changed around, so often an attribute change isn't going to happen as a way of responding to overstress so much as it's going to neccesarily be the fallout from that overstress some significant period of time after the fact. Again, still reading the chapter, so I may be wrong, but it seems, based on the conversation, that you're reading this wrong in the spirit of being exploitative. I'm willing to bet further contextual reading will reveal that as correct.<br /> <br /> But mostly point A. Maybe don't double down on it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T16:08:27-07:00","id":1341165,"title":"","content":"Yeah, so taking it out of pure math land and into the context of actual gameplay, yeah, switching attributes back and forth as is &quot;possible&quot; in the rules means the conspiracy is flip-flopping on it's resource utilization, which means there are going to be more Crisis Points for the organization as possible. If there needed to be a sidebar explaining that you can only flip the attributes around so much before it's no longer viable for Crisis Point resolution, or that doing so basically imparts that and one of the other consequences, that'd be understandable, but it's pretty clear you're supposed to just understand that it doesn't work like that, and therefore doing that on your part means you are pretty deliberately playing dumb.<br /> <br /> So maybe don't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T16:42:51-07:00","id":1341172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341135#post1341135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a cohort is attacking a conspiracy, the conspiracy has to use an action to respond, but it doesn't get to roll dice to influence the outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally one of the things a conspiracy is going to conceivably be spending its rolled conspiracy actions on is interfering with the cohort <i>in response to the cohort attacking the conspiracy</i>.<br /> <br /> Even under the assumption that five or six dice is an adequate amount for a large conspiracy and that such a conspiracy is unlikely to be dealing with penalties to its rolls, exceptional success opens new vectors of assault beyond the cohort and their known allies and accomplices, and the threshold where that starts to become a likely outcome is at ten or eleven dice, where the chances of exceptional success hit the one-in-five to one-in-three range. This matters substantially when most Renegades start out with more things they hate than things they want to protect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are trying to prove that Resistance isn't a god stat. </div> </div> </div>Nope!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I said Power and Finesse are dump stats. Nothing you've said gives me grounds to revise that opinion. </div> </div> </div>And more power to you, but if you think a conspiracy with its full set of actions available to it in the narrative, which is acting against characters in such a way that the relation between it and the cohort is important enough to put that conspiracy in the primary antagonist-group slot for the story, is going to be content to run itself as though its Principles don't matter and finding new lines of attack to pursue against its targets (as exceptional success accomplishes) while using the Nodes that rely on stats other than the one governing its ability to hold itself together on a basic &quot;the organization is still intact as an organization&quot; level is a viable way to run the opposition, then you're pretty definitely not approaching the mechanics in good faith.<br /> <br /> Leaning into &quot;Resistance is the best stat because it means you can take more lethal damage to your Association from breaking your limit&quot; also produces outcomes that obviously aren't intended, because that same line of thinking results in treating your Association track as a reasonable answer to &quot;how much extra Effort can I generate each chapter by running the bureau/company/congregation/family/enterprise into the ground?&quot; despite conspiracies being reactive and secretive creatures by design who want to accomplish their goals without exposure or undue strain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T17:41:46-07:00","id":1341184,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t finished the chapter but I am of two minds on the subject.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, if there is an easily accessed exploit in the rules or some other kind of weirdness about them, it\u2019s a good idea to bring it to the author\u2019s attention. Whether it goes against the spirit of the rules or not, it\u2019s worth bringing it to the attention of the people writing the book so they can decide if it is important to fix it or whatever. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the conspiracy mechanics are generally pretty ST facing and, to my understanding, are more about helping STs develop cool storylines and to give some mechanical weight to fighting against the Man, than they are about optimizing numbers and creating a cool character sheet. Like, I get that urge. I understand that urge. However, when building an NPC organization as an ST, one should probably fight that urge, much like you should fight the urge to put inescapable death traps in your dungeons. Sure, you can just say \u201cRocks Fall, Everybody Dies,\u201d but ...why would you do that to your friends? <br /> <br /> Similarly, you might be able to exploit the rules to build an unstoppable Conspiracy and turn your game into an unfun slog where the players never manage to win... but why would you?<br /> <br /> So.... It feels like the answer to any exploits in the Conspiracy rules might be to include a couple notes or reminders about what the point of the rules is? Or something? <br /> <br /> At the end of the day, any \u201cbuild your own\u201d game is going to have some exploits and hacks in it because you can\u2019t make everything perfect and, even if you could, that doesn\u2019t mean it would have the right atmosphere. Especially since anyone looking for a serious exploit is probably gonna find one eventually. Which turns it into an Out of Game issue and those are usually better handled by encouraging people to talk and try to get on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T18:49:14-07:00","id":1341193,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, the intent of the Conspiracy mechanics is ultimately for them to be available both to the Storyteller and to the players: in Deviant, we're eventually going to get a book dedicated to the Devoted, which will presumably feature Conspiracies and cohorts working hand in hand; and outside of Deviant, rumor has it that this system is also going to be seen in Mummy 2e to represent the Cults that the Arisen tend to run. <br /> <br /> So with that in mind, if there are any blatant exploits that could be abused by players running a conspiracy, that's definitely something to look at. <br /> <br /> All that said, the reason I said \u201cblatant\u201d is because I definitely prefer Onyx Path's approach of assuming good faith in the part of its players over other game systems that seem to assume that the players will try to break the rules and so they need to be made ironclad to withstand such abuse. In this regard, my thought is that if an exploit exists that can occur even if the players are acting in good faith, then patch it. <br /> <br /> But if it only occurs when they're blatantly meta-gaming the system, then only patch it if doing so is a simple fix and/or it's so tempting of an exploit that it can't be fixed through Storyteller intervention with the players (i.e., a figurative slap on the wrist and/or an admonishment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T19:23:50-07:00","id":1341199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341172#post1341172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally one of the things a conspiracy is going to conceivably be spending its rolled conspiracy actions on is interfering with the cohort <i>in response to the cohort attacking the conspiracy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, that's the <i>only</i> thing a rolled conspiracy action can do. And that's actually my point, you know - apart from interfering with the cohort, the conspiracy Attributes don't get rolled for anything. Why are you indignantly telling me something that's the basis of my case?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341172#post1341172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even under the assumption that five or six dice is an adequate amount for a large conspiracy and that such a conspiracy is unlikely to be dealing with penalties to its rolls, exceptional success opens new vectors of assault beyond the cohort and their known allies and accomplices, and the threshold where that starts to become a likely outcome is at ten or eleven dice, where the chances of exceptional success hit the one-in-five to one-in-three range. This matters substantially when most Renegades start out with more things they hate than things they want to protect.</div> </div> </div> </div>A conspiracy needs to be at Standing 7+ to be throwing ten or more dice on the typical conspiracy action, and conspiracies at that level are supposed to be reserved to <i>really powerful</i> Renegades. As in, if the PCs start out with the maximum threat level of 6, the conspiracy they tangle with after the first antagonist goes down <i>might</i> have Standing 7.<br /> <br /> In the typical high-powered Deviant game, where the primary conspiracy is Standing 4-6, its actions against the cohort are just going to succeed (producing a normal scene) with no complications for either side, most of the time. I believe a dice pool of 7 is the point with the smallest chance of any result but normal success, and Standing 4 is just where an Attribute of 7 becomes practical.<br /> <br /> In a word, then, if the ST is regularly throwing more than 9 dice on conspiracy actions, he's being <i>very much</i> a jerk to the players. The normal way for conspiracies to develop new leads on Renegade cohorts is from the surveillance roll - which is based on Standing and the cohort's recent activities, not any Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341184#post1341184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the conspiracy mechanics are generally pretty ST facing and, to my understanding, are more about helping STs develop cool storylines and to give some mechanical weight to fighting against the Man, than they are about optimizing numbers and creating a cool character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, that's true. But here's the thing. For the same amount of Effort that goes into adding one Attribute dot, a conspiracy can add one new Node and gain both a new important NPC and a new avenue of attack; or it can develop three new Icons, and give its agents in the field a significant power boost; or it can make a drastic change in society at large. All of those are much more interesting and cool than increasing an Attribute ... and increasing Attributes doesn't help a conspiracy do any of them in the future.<br /> <br /> So, from both the conspiracy's viewpoint and the ST's, what's the point of higher Attributes? A conspiracy gets much more real power to work towards its Principles by developing Nodes and Icons - it's even, arguably, better at fighting off Renegades if it does so. And the ST gets more ways to generate interesting stories by developing conspiracies that way, too. That's almost certainly intentional, but ... it's been pushed to extremes.<br /> <br /> (All that stuff I said about Resistance isn't to show that conspiracies ought to take it - it's showing that Resistance actually <i>has</i> a use, that it can be something worth forgoing Icons and Nodes for. I can't even say that much for Power or Finesse.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T19:36:59-07:00","id":1341200,"title":"","content":"As always, I'm watching this conversation closely, even if I'm not saying much. My general feeling on mechanics is that they should provide a reasonable amount of guidance and head off obvious potential arguments. I don't aim to prevent every possible way preventing abuse of the mechanics, but if routine use of the rules as written creates results that are disruptive of the spirit of the game (whether silly or frustrating), it's the rules that need adjustment.<br /> <br /> Speaking as a ST, when I use randomizers, I do so to help me choose between a couple of likely outcomes (with the occasional &quot;nobody saw that coming&quot; wild card). If this system isn't doing that well, I'd rather fix it now than leave it as a recurring irritant that folks need to house rule or ignore. That being said, we will be exploring more ways to use conspiracy actions (as well as modifiers to these rolls) in the moments-ago-announced Devoted Companion Stretch Goal here: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deviant-the-renegades-a-tabletop-roleplaying-game/posts/2651018\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2651018</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:04:07-07:00","id":1341204,"title":"","content":"upped my pledge and shared the kickstarter to others in hopes for the companion. hope everyone has people they can inform of the kickstarter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:10:19-07:00","id":1341205,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming the Devoted Companion will be made one way or the other, and that what's at stake here is whether or not it will be one of the Kickstarter rewards. Still plenty of reason to want to reach that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:20:15-07:00","id":1341206,"title":"","content":"Eric mentioned in the Discord that there are no current non-Kickstarter Deviant supplements currently in the pipeline, although they're certainly possible if Deviant is successful.<br /> <br /> However, if a Devoted Companion is intended, we'll definitely see it a LOT sooner as a successful Kickstater reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T20:23:50-07:00","id":1341207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341205#post1341205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming the Devoted Companion will be made one way or the other, and that what's at stake here is whether or not it will be one of the Kickstarter rewards. Still plenty of reason to want to reach that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also the difference between getting it as part of your KS pledge vs. buying it later, as well as how soon I can begin work on it. Something that's already paid for is likely far less of a business risk than something that isn't.<br /> <br /> ETA: Ninja'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-13-2019, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T21:44:51-07:00","id":1341214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341135#post1341135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, of course it's against the spirit of the rules! But that means the rules are faulty. If conspiracies shouldn't do the Attribute shuffle to dodge the more serious consequences of over-stress, they shouldn't be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expecting a Storyteller to engage in good faith does not make a rule faulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T21:57:08-07:00","id":1341215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341205#post1341205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming the Devoted Companion will be made one way or the other, and that what's at stake here is whether or not it will be one of the Kickstarter rewards. Still plenty of reason to want to reach that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>very true. still, may get it earlier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T22:53:48-07:00","id":1341223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341199#post1341199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The normal way for conspiracies to develop new leads on Renegade cohorts is from the surveillance roll - which is based on Standing and the cohort's recent activities, not any Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please actually read the roll results for conspiracy actions, which I am directly referencing when I say exceptional success on those rolls is how the list of viable targets expands beyond &quot;known accomplices and allies of the Remade.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T23:02:13-07:00","id":1341224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341214#post1341214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expecting a Storyteller to engage in good faith does not make a rule faulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This, a whole damn lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T23:35:39-07:00","id":1341226,"title":"","content":"Deviant as a whole has a certain amount of trust in the players to not min/max. This is the game where uou decide how powerful you are at chargen after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T07:03:07-07:00","id":1341246,"title":"","content":"So, I know crossover rules aren\u2019t going to be in the core book, but I\u2019ve been wondering what would happen if a Mage swapped out a Deviant\u2019s broken soul with a whole and healthy one. Would that simply kill the Deviant? Would it be possible to remove the soul, fix their physical issues, and then pop in a new one, and have a cure?<br /> <br /> Or is this the sort of thing that\u2019s better left to individual STs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T07:12:32-07:00","id":1341248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341246#post1341246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know crossover rules aren\u2019t going to be in the core book, but I\u2019ve been wondering what would happen if a Mage swapped out a Deviant\u2019s broken soul with a whole and healthy one. Would that simply kill the Deviant? Would it be possible to remove the soul, fix their physical issues, and then pop in a new one, and have a cure?<br /> <br /> Or is this the sort of thing that\u2019s better left to individual STs?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I recall, (non-Imperial) Supernal magic usually doesn't work properly on souls with weird stuff going on with them.<br /> <br /> If a soul has been altered, its warranty is voided and the supernal isn't going to touch that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, Supernal magic doesn't treat souls that have been altered by another template the same way as it would treat normal or awakened souls.<br /> <br /> Plus (unless I'm forgetting a change from 2e) there seems to be the concept that the &quot;soul&quot; that mages can pull out and swap around isn't the entirety of the soul. Mages who swap souls don't swap Gnosis for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T07:25:57-07:00","id":1341252,"title":"","content":"I believe that the damage to a Remade is such that soul-affecting spells can\u2019t get a hold of it. Final answer should be in the Tremere rules in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed, as Tremere hunt monsters who damage human souls (aside from the staggering hypocrisy, it\u2019s the contamination of their food source that irks them) and we had to do the rules for which ones they can then eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T10:26:32-07:00","id":1341274,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can't just fix a Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:20:16-07:00","id":1341284,"title":"","content":"Ah, fair enough. I was pretty sure it was going to be something like that, but wasn\u2019t sure how it would look. <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:50:40-07:00","id":1341288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341226#post1341226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant as a whole has a certain amount of trust in the players to not min/max. This is the game where uou decide how powerful you are at chargen after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this and the other responses to the &quot;loopholes&quot; are really important. This is a more collaborative system that perhaps requires some more give and take than other games. You build around debilitating scars that are designed to inject drama by making your character's life difficult. As a storyteller, you co-invent conspiracies with the players, making villains with mysterious powers to threaten the characters and their allies. As a player, you volunteer those allies to be in the line of fire by rooting your Broken's hopes in their wellbeing. The book's guidance around managing the spirit of this give and take is at least as important as the mechanical rules governing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:17:44-07:00","id":1341306,"title":"","content":"How does the Explosive Deviation for Lash interact with the damage type of the Lash? Does it automatically conform to the normal Explosion rules (ie aggravated damage at ground zero, lethal out to blast area, and bashing from blast area until blast area x 2), or does the damage type of the Lash apply uniformly to the entire blast area (x 2)? And would Deadly/Devastating add to the Force of the explosion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:46:16-07:00","id":1341315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341306#post1341306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Explosive Deviation for Lash interact with the damage type of the Lash? Does it automatically conform to the normal Explosion rules (ie aggravated damage at ground zero, lethal out to blast area, and bashing from blast area until blast area x 2), or does the damage type of the Lash apply uniformly to the entire blast area (x 2)? And would Deadly/Devastating add to the Force of the explosion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eric addressed Explosive Lash back on page 15.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338211#post1338211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Originally posted by <b>Sith_Happens</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338150#post1338150\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i>Do Explosive Lashes use the normal rules for damage type as a function of distance (aggravated at close range, lethal within blast radius, bashing between 1x and 2x blast radius) or does Gentle/Bruising/Cutting/Horrendous determine the damage type at all distances?</i><br /> <br /> A good question, since it doesn't say in the text. Given that Stun has its own effect, it might be easiest to say Explosive Lashes must be Cutting and follow the same rules as normal explosives (Agg at ground zero, lethal nearby, bashing farther away).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:23:23-07:00","id":1341328,"title":"","content":"The new strech goal is pretty...<br /> <br /> *Sings under his breath*<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jhOn4oPn3Bw\" data-code=\"jhOn4oPn3Bw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jhOn4oPn3Bw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:48:29-07:00","id":1341333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341315#post1341315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eric addressed Explosive Lash back on page 15.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thanks, I must have missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T22:39:23-07:00","id":1341403,"title":"","content":"Small discrepancy between the actual writeups and the quick reference lists in Preview 3: Misfortune is listed as a Social Scar in its writeup but Any in the list.<br /> <br /> Is Hemophilia 5 supposed to result in any bashing damage taken causing both the Magnitude 2 and 3 effects to kick in, since the upgraded damage is lethal, or is it just the former?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T08:46:14-07:00","id":1341445,"title":"","content":"I feel like encouraging STs to inflict microaggressions on their PCs should maybe come with a note not to overdo it and to see the sensitivity suggestions on pg. XX. I get that you want things to feel isolating and emphasize that Deviants are now the rejected Other, but enough people have to deal with those kinds of things on a daily basis that I could imagine this easily crossing a line if you aren\u2019t careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T09:45:18-07:00","id":1341462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341445#post1341445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like encouraging STs to inflict microaggressions on their PCs should maybe come with a note not to overdo it and to see the sensitivity suggestions on pg. XX. I get that you want things to feel isolating and emphasize that Deviants are now the rejected Other, but enough people have to deal with those kinds of things on a daily basis that I could imagine this easily crossing a line if you aren\u2019t careful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's what the sidebar on the X Card and drawing the line is for, but yeah, a couple words about checking that section might be good.<br /> <br /> I must say, I did not expect the University of Delaware to be the setting of a school for aspiring mad scientists and the setting for players who want to punch Nazis.<br /> <br /> It's hardly a flaw, and I dig the satire of freeze peach types. But I wasn't expecting Irene Engel with an American accent as the setting main antagonist.<br /> <br /> Also, I had no idea her secret books existed, and I feel cheated for knowing more. I'd ask who believes this garbage, but I read the RPG Horror Stories reddit. I know GMs who believe that crap. Good on this book trying to scare them off with that discussion on how much being a Deviant sucks because of the reason being poor sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-15-2019, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T13:21:53-07:00","id":1341501,"title":"","content":"I took another look at the Conspiracy rules and... now I have more problems with them. They just seem too rigid to be useful and, in places, strangely detached from the conceits of the game.<br /> Some examples:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Divergence is unpredictable and unruly, even for the mightiest conspiracies, and some lack the secret knowledge to induce it at all, but creating or recruiting a Deviant is a Complexity 1 project. As a result, whether or not a Conspiracy can get Deviants is basically ST fiat, as if the system didn't exist, but with numbers.<br /> <br /> Projects abstract away a lot of things, some of them for the best (like influencing NPCs and other ST-against-ST scenarios). As part of this abstraction, the system removes the PCs' ability to interact with the project in any sense beyond destroying the relevant Node, without addressing, say, what happens if the PCs intercept the truck carrying an Icon from Node to Node, or bust into a facility to rescue a test subject without torching the place or killing the Linchpin.<br /> <br /> What Standing means for a conspiracy's reach is defined only vaguely. Standing 1 is supposed to be <i>&quot;locally influential or regional but diffuse,&quot;</i> but Darwin's Sixth Number wield a potential apocalypse they can manifest in ten sessions (and this is an Icon, for some reason, instead of just a Project they can pursue).<br /> <br /> The Surveillance roll is presented in such a way that it doesn'treally care what the PCs do. Sure, there are modifiers to shift the probability towards specific outcomes, but the result remains down to chance. A conspiracy can fail to target you even though you haven't moved an inch since the last session, or find you unerringly even after you burn every bridge and shed even your body (though that's really the lesser of the two issues; it at least serves the premise of the game).</div></div> </div> </div> A lot of these faultlines are pretty easily resolved by just ignoring the system, but then I'm left wondering what the system is actually for.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, I think just wanted something out of the conspiracy rules that they can't or won't provide. This is honestly fine -- the game doesn't need to cater to every single possible game, after all -- but it does leave me without much to work with.<br /> <br /> On a positive note, Chapter 7 is good so far. I quite like the additional inspirations (<i>Akira</i>, at last, where it deserves to be), and both <i>Down and Out \u2014 Life Without Privilege</i> and <i>the Axis of Inhumanity and Poverty </i>look like they'll be worth reading and rereading as I run the game. I do wonder why the (clean and efficient) heist rules are here and not in the systems chapter, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T18:21:21-07:00","id":1341537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341501#post1341501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Divergence is unpredictable and unruly, even for the mightiest conspiracies, and some lack the secret knowledge to induce it at all, but creating or recruiting a Deviant is a Complexity 1 project. As a result, whether or not a Conspiracy can get Deviants is basically ST fiat, as if the system didn't exist, but with numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need an appropriate Node to accomplish it and you need to be able to spare 1 Effort on getting a Deviant on your team instead of accomplishing something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Projects abstract away a lot of things, some of them for the best (like influencing NPCs and other ST-against-ST scenarios). As part of this abstraction, the system removes the PCs' ability to interact with the project in any sense beyond destroying the relevant Node, without addressing, say, what happens if the PCs intercept the truck carrying an Icon from Node to Node, or bust into a facility to rescue a test subject without torching the place or killing the Linchpin. </div> </div> </div>Lethal damage to a conspiracy includes carrying out major attacks on Nodes and causes crisis points that the cohort may be allowed to choose the consequences of, including removing invested Effort or forcing the conspiracy to dedicate conspiracy actions to recovering assets from them before they can resume the Project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Standing means for a conspiracy's reach is defined only vaguely. Standing 1 is supposed to be <i>&quot;locally influential or regional but diffuse,&quot;</i> but Darwin's Sixth Number wield a potential apocalypse they can manifest in ten sessions (and this is an Icon, for some reason, instead of just a Project they can pursue). </div> </div> </div>Please reread the examples of Complexity 10 Projects and also understand the difference between &quot;this group could potentially end the world by completing their doomsday weapon&quot; and &quot;this group has the reach to accomplish things on the global stage.&quot; As a Standing 1 organization, the Sixth Number relies heavily on going unnoticed to be able to work on the Zero Solution, because they have one conspiracy action to work with and any destroyed Node or other lethal damage might set them back double.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Surveillance roll is presented in such a way that it doesn'treally care what the PCs do. Sure, there are modifiers to shift the probability towards specific outcomes, but the result remains down to chance. A conspiracy can fail to target you even though you haven't moved an inch since the last session, or find you unerringly even after you burn every bridge and shed even your body (though that's really the lesser of the two issues; it at least serves the premise of the game). </div> </div> </div>The Surveillance roll cannot go below Standing - 5 due to the nature of penalties versus basic dicepool components, and the only way a conspiracy can't affect you with conspiracy actions at all in a chapter is if it rolls a dramatic failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:26:21-07:00","id":1341679,"title":"","content":"This being the Deviant Kickstarter thread and all, I just want to shamelessly remind everyone that may be lurking that this is the last day of the KS. If this is a game that interests you, please consider backing it.<br /> <br /> We are very close to an exciting stretch goal that will add a Devoted Companion supplement to the materials included with the Deviant pdf. Let's get there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T13:23:38-07:00","id":1341696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Dragos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341679#post1341679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This being the Deviant Kickstarter thread and all, I just want to shamelessly remind everyone that may be lurking that this is the last day of the KS. If this is a game that interests you, please consider backing it.<br /> <br /> We are very close to an exciting stretch goal that will add a Devoted Companion supplement to the materials included with the Deviant pdf. Let's get there!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have backed, please also consider upgrading to a physical book if you only have the PDF level and/or consider adding something onto your pledge, there is a $20 ST Screen for example.<br /> <br /> Edit: we are so close to the Devoted Companion (just $718 away), if every current backer added an extra $0.45 we would hit that stretch goal.<br /> <br /> Edit2: now just $119 away, if every current backer added an extra $0.07 we would hit that stretch goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-16-2019, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T16:13:55-07:00","id":1341731,"title":"","content":"WOOOOO! $80k! We just hit the Devoted Companion stretch goal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T16:52:30-07:00","id":1341738,"title":"","content":"Can you just make Scars &quot;generic&quot; and then have variations that match them but aren't necessarily entangled? For example, someone with the Alternate Persona Scar, linked to the Involuntary Stimulus of &quot;When they sleep&quot; and have the total be something like 5 points of magnitude, then have 5 points of magnitude in variations that aren't linked to a scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:05:01-07:00","id":1341748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geomancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341738#post1341738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you just make Scars &quot;generic&quot; and then have variations that match them but aren't necessarily entangled? For example, someone with the Alternate Persona Scar, linked to the Involuntary Stimulus of &quot;When they sleep&quot; and have the total be something like 5 points of magnitude, then have 5 points of magnitude in variations that aren't linked to a scar?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't have Variations that are not entangled with any Scars (except for the one free dot granted by your Origin). You can, however, entangle multiple Variations to a single Scar, with a number of Variations after the first equal to the difference between the Scar's rating and the Variations' rating. So you can entangle two 4-Magnitude Variations to one 5-Magnitude Scar, or three 3-Magnitude Variations, or four 2-Magnitude Variations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T18:12:06-07:00","id":1341749,"title":"","content":"You can get pretty creative with chains though. You should be able to take Alternate Persona and then have &quot;Alternate Persona takes control&quot; be the Involuntary Stimulus that triggers other variations.<br /> <br /> I think that's how you would make a character like the Hulk. I mean yeah Hybrid Form but there's a limit to how many Variations that can support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:16:59-07:00","id":1341757,"title":"","content":"So, now that the Devoted Companion is being funded, who wants to play reformers of the Onachus?<br /> <br /> They don't seem like inherently bad people, just having succumbed to that distinctly Vigilant thought of &quot;we who fight monsters must become them&quot;, and I like their transhumanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T19:39:31-07:00","id":1341765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341757#post1341757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now that the Devoted Companion is being funded, who wants to play reformers of the Onachus?<br /> <br /> They don't seem like inherently bad people, just having succumbed to that distinctly Vigilant thought of &quot;we who fight monsters must become them&quot;, and I like their transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am excited to be able to play Doctor Victor Von Doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T21:14:54-07:00","id":1341777,"title":"","content":"Doom is too much of a crossover of everything. He's got super science and super magic and special powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T04:36:31-07:00","id":1341836,"title":"","content":"Just a few hours left of the Kickstarter, now. If you were planning to back, now is the time. Thank you to everyone who has already backed Deviant. It's been a really successful Kickstarter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T08:41:10-07:00","id":1341867,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty excited. On a secondary note, what's the ETA for the DtR sub-forum?<br /> Apologies if this has been asked before.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: WOOO! Kickstarter completed and all went well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 10-17-2019, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T09:52:26-07:00","id":1341887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341867#post1341867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty excited. On a secondary note, what's the ETA for the DtR sub-forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hoping it's soon - the game might not be 'released' for a while still, but given that the manuscript is out and it's playable...<br /> The sooner the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T12:00:20-07:00","id":1341912,"title":"","content":"Also, at least as far as the Sixth Number goes, they\u2019re probably going to focus more on trying to find Number 6 (hint: check a small cove up the British Coast) than they are working on their doomsday code, since they think they need six people before they can ascend properly. They wouldn\u2019t want to accidentally trigger the apocalypse before they can survive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T12:01:12-07:00","id":1341913,"title":"","content":"Congratulations on funding btw!<br /> <br /> The book looks pretty interesting. Thank you for your work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T15:26:35-07:00","id":1341955,"title":"","content":"Time to open the Deviant Sub-Forum!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:20:29-07:00","id":1341969,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the support, everyone. I don't have good access to the forums when I'm at work, so I had to wait until I got home to post here. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:32:15-07:00","id":1341970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341501#post1341501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Divergence is unpredictable and unruly, even for the mightiest conspiracies, and some lack the secret knowledge to induce it at all, but creating or recruiting a Deviant is a Complexity 1 project. As a result, whether or not a Conspiracy can get Deviants is basically ST fiat, as if the system didn't exist, but with numbers...<br /> <br /> The Surveillance roll is presented in such a way that it doesn'treally care what the PCs do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I agree. Its weird for it to suggest that a conspiracy that is good at it to kill or fail 24 out of 25 times, and then to have a large group of progenitors at a college that make people into deviants every year or even semester. It would be challenging for the US Federal Government to disappear 24 people a year, let alone multitudes of people associated with one college.<br /> <br /> The surveillance thing also has a few issues about there being no guidelines for how private-only uses of obvious powers can defer the penalties, or how variations like face stealer and memory theft can hinder the conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 10-17-2019, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T21:44:30-07:00","id":1342012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341912#post1341912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, at least as far as the Sixth Number goes, they\u2019re probably going to focus more on trying to find Number 6 (hint: check a small cove up the British Coast) than they are working on their doomsday code, since they think they need six people before they can ascend properly. They wouldn\u2019t want to accidentally trigger the apocalypse before they can survive it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is the cohort supposed to interact with them? They don't appear to have any interest in making or capturing Deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T22:29:48-07:00","id":1342019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1341970#post1341970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I agree. Its weird for it to suggest that a conspiracy that is good at it to kill or fail 24 out of 25 times, and then to have a large group of progenitors at a college that make people into deviants every year or even semester.</div> </div> </div> </div>The DuPont Guest Lecturer Series is a conspiracy that calls upon multiple different Progenitors that have their own methods of inducing Divergence that are at least consistent enough to show results multiple times, and it gives them the resources for one of those results to plausibly be produced annually.<br /> <br /> Like, I remember reading the statistic you're alluding to early on in the book, but I can no longer find it and the nearest equivalent I'm finding is the statement that even repeatable processes for inducing Divergence come with unanticipated complications that don't necessarily mean the Divergence doesn't <i>happen</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The surveillance thing also has a few issues about there being no guidelines for how private-only uses of obvious powers can defer the penalties, or how variations like face stealer and memory theft can hinder the conspiracy. </div> </div> </div>People talk and a conspiracy is by definition composed of more than one person. Cameras and supernatural powers are on the playing field. The whole point of the Web of Pain is that the people that made you what you are are only the barest fraction of an entire ocean of secret manipulators that themselves are plugged into the vast weave of humanity that Deviants mostly have to stay connected to to keep stable.<br /> <br /> The only other component of the core surveillance roll besides the highest Overt rating is the conspiracy's Standing \u2014 the only &quot;penalty&quot; Overt Scars and Variations apply is that the conspiracy has more dice to roll while it is the spotlight organization in a position to meddle with the cohort during this story. If you don't want to risk any word at all getting back to the conspiracies about you, you don't use obvious powers and you stay off the grid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342012#post1342012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the cohort supposed to interact with them? They don't appear to have any interest in making or capturing Deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think Six could possibly be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T23:39:28-07:00","id":1342025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342019#post1342019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I remember reading the statistic you're alluding to early on in the book, but I can no longer find it and the nearest equivalent I'm finding is the statement that even repeatable processes for inducing Divergence come with unanticipated complications that don't necessarily mean the Divergence doesn't <i>happen</i>.<br /> <br /> ...If you don't want to risk any word at all getting back to the conspiracies about you, you don't use obvious powers and you stay off the grid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, yeah, I think I like that interpretation better.<br /> <br /> &quot;Even Progenitors who achieve repeat Divergence and have the means to assemble a production line process face failures, irregularities, and complications that they will struggle to predict or understand. These failures come with a body count, either during Divergence or shortly thereafter, as individuals fail to survive Divergence or cannot cope with the enormity of what has happened to them. The greatest variables are always the human beings involved \u2014 Progenitors and victims alike.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmm yeah, the tone usually strikes me as not requiring like, every conspiracy to require big fat corpse stacks to make deviants (that comes later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 10-18-2019, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:15:30-07:00","id":1342096,"title":"","content":"Not entirely sure if this should be it's own topic, but now that we have the organization creation rules for both Conspiracies and Krewes, is there going to be an official release that shows off the generic version of this? Both Conspiracies and Krewes have elements that are pretty specific to each but it's obviously built on top of a generic form so hoping that something will be released for that. It would be pretty helpful regardless of the gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T09:53:46-07:00","id":1342109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342096#post1342096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely sure if this should be it's own topic, but now that we have the organization creation rules for both Conspiracies and Krewes, is there going to be an official release that shows off the generic version of this? Both Conspiracies and Krewes have elements that are pretty specific to each but it's obviously built on top of a generic form so hoping that something will be released for that. It would be pretty helpful regardless of the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would buy a Chronicles of Darkness book that's all about organizations (cults, conspiracies, clubs, gangs, etc). With rules for creating them, running them in game as antagonists, PCs working for them, PCs controlling them, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:33:16-07:00","id":1342117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342109#post1342109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would buy a Chronicles of Darkness book that's all about organizations (cults, conspiracies, clubs, gangs, etc). With rules for creating them, running them in game as antagonists, PCs working for them, PCs controlling them, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah! Something along the same lines as the recent &quot;Companion&quot; books of different lines. That'd be pretty awesome for a blue book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:19:46-07:00","id":1342196,"title":"","content":"I'm making another go at Relentless Variation. Feedback appreciated. Thanks!<br /> <br /> Edit: Hold off on this, for now. I'm pretty sure I messed up some language (&quot;higher of&quot; and &quot;lower of&quot; are the same thing, right?), but I need to come back to this when I'm not simultaneously listening to Minecraft let's play videos and nursery rhymes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-18-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:57:04-07:00","id":1342206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342196#post1342196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>Suppressible (-1 Magnitude):</b> Choose a Controlled Scar as the secondary Scar, instead. Either the secondary Scar or at least one entangled Variation must be Overt. The Broken can temporarily suppress an entangled Variation by \u201cactivating\u201d it, which requires a successful Scar Resistance roll and carries the consequences of the secondary Scar. Tribulation costs Willpower, for example, and Perilous Variation inflicts damage, but in doing so, they suppress the Variation for the duration of its normal activation (typically a scene).</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens if they take Suppressible but never intend to ever suppress it? Its basically an Overt Persistent Perpetual Variation with no Scar at that point.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh wait I misread. The problem is bigger since it can be the Scar that is Overt. So it can even effectively be a Subtle Persistent Perpetual Variation with no Scar.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: What if someone takes Electrokinesis, with Relentless + Suppressible with the Secondary Scar as Concentration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-18-2019, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:15:10-07:00","id":1342212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342196#post1342196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>Suppressible (-1 Magnitude):</b> Choose a Controlled Scar as the secondary Scar, <u>instead.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>This has the same problem as the version in the previews copy: if you take Suppressible, and choose to never suppress the variation, you get the benefits of the variation without the drawbacks of a scar. Scrap the word \u201cinstead\u201d (so that the Relentless Variation has two secondary scars, one that is in effect unless it's Suppressed and another that's used to Suppress it), and you're in better shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:30:52-07:00","id":1342218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342212#post1342212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has the same problem as the version in the previews copy: if you take Suppressible, and choose to never suppress the variation, you get the benefits of the variation without the drawbacks of a scar. Scrap the word \u201cinstead\u201d (so that the Relentless Variation has two secondary scars, one that is in effect unless it's Suppressed and another that's used to Suppress it), and you're in better shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's great! I second that suggestion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T18:37:44-07:00","id":1342246,"title":"","content":"First of all, as an academic, I love the University of Delaware setting.<br /> <br /> Second, looking at the list of possible Projects and the amount of Effort attached to each, I have questions. Namely, &quot;create a new Node&quot; is listed as a 10-Effort Project, but some of the lower-Effort projects seem like they should result in new Nodes. &quot;Subvert operatives in a national organization&quot; - how is that not represented as an Exploitative node? Or is it 7 Effort just to successfully establish a relationship, and more Effort is needed to truly make it a Node that the conspiracy can use? (And if so, is that another 10 Effort on top of the initial 7?) Same with &quot;subsume a small organization into the Conspiracy&quot; at 5 Effort. If this subsumed org doesn't constitute a Node, how do I represent its relationship to the rest of the conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T19:05:55-07:00","id":1342249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342196#post1342196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm making another go at Relentless Variation. Feedback appreciated. Thanks!<br /> <br /> Edit: Hold off on this, for now. I'm pretty sure I messed up some language (&amp;quot;higher of&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;lower of&amp;quot; are the same thing, right?), but I need to come back to this when I'm not simultaneously listening to Minecraft let's play videos and nursery rhymes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I at least say that I appreciate your willingness to run the changes by us again? Onyx Park has a great track record for transparency with its readership; but you're hitting a new level here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T19:57:36-07:00","id":1342260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342246#post1342246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, as an academic, I love the University of Delaware setting.<br /> <br /> Second, looking at the list of possible Projects and the amount of Effort attached to each, I have questions. Namely, &amp;quot;create a new Node&amp;quot; is listed as a 10-Effort Project, but some of the lower-Effort projects seem like they should result in new Nodes. &amp;quot;Subvert operatives in a national organization&amp;quot; - how is that not represented as an Exploitative node? Or is it 7 Effort just to successfully establish a relationship, and more Effort is needed to truly make it a Node that the conspiracy can use? (And if so, is that another 10 Effort on top of the initial 7?) Same with &amp;quot;subsume a small organization into the Conspiracy&amp;quot; at 5 Effort. If this subsumed org doesn't constitute a Node, how do I represent its relationship to the rest of the conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, given the placement of those examples in their lists relative to earlier tasks, the point is that those gains are temporary. The conspiracy has access to those groups within the narrative, but they're not presently integrated into the conspiracy well enough to represent a Node that needs to be destroyed to deprive them of their assets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T20:09:45-07:00","id":1342264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342246#post1342246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, as an academic, I love the University of Delaware setting.<br /> <br /> Second, looking at the list of possible Projects and the amount of Effort attached to each, I have questions. Namely, &quot;create a new Node&quot; is listed as a 10-Effort Project, but some of the lower-Effort projects seem like they should result in new Nodes. &quot;Subvert operatives in a national organization&quot; - how is that not represented as an Exploitative node? Or is it 7 Effort just to successfully establish a relationship, and more Effort is needed to truly make it a Node that the conspiracy can use? (And if so, is that another 10 Effort on top of the initial 7?) Same with &quot;subsume a small organization into the Conspiracy&quot; at 5 Effort. If this subsumed org doesn't constitute a Node, how do I represent its relationship to the rest of the conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I think the writer was coding &quot;create a new Node&quot; in a narrative way that I overlooked, since I tend to like more mechanical/game language in examples like this. I've made a note to myself to review this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342260#post1342260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, given the placement of those examples in their lists relative to earlier tasks, the point is that those gains are temporary. The conspiracy has access to those groups within the narrative, but they're not presently integrated into the conspiracy well enough to represent a Node that needs to be destroyed to deprive them of their assets.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly another possibility, although I'd like to make it a bit more clear. I'm really glad Devoted Companion is happening, so I'll get to do more with conspiracy actions and Projects in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342249#post1342249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I at least say that I appreciate your willingness to run the changes by us again? Onyx Park has a great track record for transparency with its readership; but you're hitting a new level here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't do this with every change or edit I make, but Relentless Variation is definitely the obvious Scar concept that is the most difficult to convey mechanically without breaking it in completely awful ways, so to be perfectly honest, I appreciate having a bunch of extra sets of eyes on it as I continue to polish it. An innocuous question like &quot;how does Relentless (Suppressible) work with Concentration?&quot; forces me to notice issues that hadn't occurred to me previously, which allows me to answer that question (or prevent its needing to be asked) in the text.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what happened this afternoon. I somehow completely failed to address the exact problem you and others pointed out that was the reason I'm fixing this Scar in the first place! I think I need to get to bed early tonight or sleep in tomorrow or <i>something</i>. I'm probably still pretty sleep-deprived from the Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-18-2019, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T23:42:00-07:00","id":1342286,"title":"","content":"I have a small question about <b>Integrate Technology</b> 2 and up. For something like an integrated cellphone or a laptop (something advanced that has internal data, inputs and an interface), would the Deviant have to &quot;manifest&quot; it to interact with it or can they access it entirely internally? For example, does an Invasive Renegade on a bus who wants to check Facebook sprout a touchscreen from their arm or can they just stare off into the middle distance and start scrolling in their mind's eye?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 10-19-2019, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T05:06:36-07:00","id":1342332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342286#post1342286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a small question about <b>Integrate Technology</b> 2 and up. For something like an integrated cellphone or a laptop (something advanced that has internal data, inputs and an interface), would the Deviant have to &quot;manifest&quot; it to interact with it or can they access it entirely internally? For example, does an Invasive Renegade on a bus who wants to check Facebook sprout a touchscreen from their arm or can they just stare off into the middle distance and start scrolling in their mind's eye?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either option works, as it's largely flavor. A screen on your arm lets you show it to someone else, while one on the inside of your eye is less likely to be noticed, and having the option for both probably isn't worth making it a Deviation. Just establish how it works for your character, for the sake of consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T05:09:01-07:00","id":1342333,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I wasn't sure. It really is neat how much of the flavor is up to the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T06:47:17-07:00","id":1342340,"title":"","content":"Relentless Variation is quickly becoming the Lash of Scars, both in terms of word count and customizability (this thing is basically a Controlled, Involuntary, and Persistent Scar all rolled up into one). Remembered to fix <i>the thing I was supposed to fix the first time</i>, as well as removing some Controlled Scar effects that really didn't make sense in the context of suppression. Feedback appreciated.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Relentless Variation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Secondary; Subtle; Repeatable; Toggled-Only<br /> The Variation entangled with the Scar is always active, and the Remade can\u2019t toggle it off. At best, she must take measures to bring it under control. At worst, she <i>can\u2019t</i>.<br /> <br /> Choose another Persistent Scar (the secondary Scar). All Variations combined with this Scar also suffer the secondary Scar. The entangled Variations behave as though they and the Scar are both Persistent and Perpetual (granting a +5 bonus to Clash of Wills rolls involving them). Calculate the Magnitude of Relentless Variation as follows:<br /> <br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar and all entangled Variations are Subtle, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is one less than that of the secondary Scar.<br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar is Subtle but at least one of the entangled Variations is Overt, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is the higher of (secondary Scar Magnitude - 1) or the Magnitude of the highest-Magnitude Overt Variation.<br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar is Overt, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is equal to that of the secondary Scar.<br /> \u2022 The Magnitude of this Scar is one higher if one or more entangled Variations are likely to create story complications by being \u201calways-on,\u201d such as Camouflage 3+, Gigantic, Miniaturization, or Out of Phase (Body) 3.<br /> <br /> If an entangled Tiered Variation has a constant effect (such as Bioluminescence with the Aura Deviation, or Gigantic), the Deviant\u2019s player determines the default Magnitude of each Tiered Variation entangled with Relentless Variation at the time she develops this Scar. She may change the current Magnitude (as well as any applicable Deviations) of a Variation as an action, such as to dim or brighten the light her Bioluminescence (p. XX) ordinarily produces, for example, as long as she is normally able to do so.<br /> <br /> Directed Variations (or Directed effects of non-Directed Variations) entangled with this Scar still require an action to target. Effects limited to use once per scene/chapter/story still carry these restrictions, and those with explicit durations are still limited to them (Omnicompetence 2 doesn\u2019t grant the option to have a dot in all Skills, constantly, for example). This Scar can entangle Reflexive Variations and those with a \u201cmenu\u201d of capabilities that can\u2019t reasonably remain \u201calways on\u201d (such as Electrokinesis), but it has little-to-no effect on them without Deviations.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviations</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Suppressible (-1 Magnitude):</b> The Broken can suppress an entangled Variation until the end of the scene by one of the following means, chosen at the time the Deviant develops this Scar:<br /> <br /> Concentration: Suppressing an entangled Variation (or preventing it from reasserting itself, once suppressed) follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Concentration 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> <br /> Depletion: The Broken can only suppress an entangled Variation for a number of minutes (turns, in action scenes) equal to Scar Resistance and may only do so once per scene, although Adaptations can overcome this.<br /> <br /> Deterioration: Suppressing an entangled Variation follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Deterioration (Lingering) 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> <br /> Perilous: The Broken suffers a point of lethal damage when suppressing an entangled Variation.<br /> <br /> Power Failure: Suppressing an entangled Variation follows similar rules as activating one entangled with the Power Failure Scar (p. XX). See the sidebar for details<br /> <br /> Preparation: Suppressing an entangled Variation follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Preparation (Elaborate) 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> <br /> Tribulation: The Deviant must spend a point of Willpower to suppress an entangled Variation.<br /> <br /> Unstable: The Remade suffers a minor Instability each time he suppresses an entangled Variation.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Unruly (+1 Magnitude):</b> At least one of the entangled Variations must be Directed. Once per chapter, as long as the Variation is active (not neutralized by Suppressible, the Untamed Adaptation, or the Mimicry Variation, for example), the Storyteller may direct an entangled Variation for a single turn during which the Deviant did not do so, either choosing its target or selecting one at random. The Broken\u2019s player may resist this effect with a Scar Resistance roll. If this roll succeeds, the Storyteller may make another direction attempt in a later scene but may not attempt to direct this Variation again during the current scene. Each consecutive successful roll to resist Storyteller direction imposes a -1 penalty on future rolls to resist this effect.<br /> \u2022 <b>Rebellious (+2 Magnitude):</b> As Unruly and exclusive with it, but if the Storyteller successfully directs an entangled Variation, he may continue directing it on subsequent turns until the end of the scene or until the Deviant\u2019s player makes a successful Scar Resistance roll to regain control. Each consecutive failed Scar Resistance roll to regain control grants a +1 penalty on later rolls to wrest back control.<br /> <br /> Relentless Variation and Power Failure<br /> <br /> When using the Suppressible Deviation, Power Failure is a special case, reflecting as it does some countermeasure or suppression device the Broken uses to tamp down her unruly Variations \u2014 such as a special article of clothing, continual exposure to a radio signal, or regular injections of a stabilizing serum. While this is their main purpose within the story, an enemy <i>could</i> deploy them to disable the transformed\u2019s Variations, or the Deviant might find herself in an environment where the countermeasures are in place and she can\u2019t remove them in order to use her Variations. Thus, the Power Failure option for Relentless Variation is a double-edged sword.<br /> For that reason, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes. The player similarly decides the following at the time he purchases this Scar:<br /> <b>Off:</b> Does application of the countermeasure neutralize the Variation immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation lose Magnitude every interval of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch off on a delay?<br /> <b>On:</b> Does removal of the countermeasure cause the Variation to manifest at full strength immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation gain Magnitude every interval of time (turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch on after the delay?<br /> <b>Minimum:</b> Once the countermeasure is removed, can it be reapplied right away, or is it impossible to do so for a period of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes) or until the end of the scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":".  Clarification to Concentration effect 10-19-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T07:39:30-07:00","id":1342345,"title":"","content":"Hm. If you Suppress all the entangled Variations, does that also temporarily alleviate the Secondary Scar? Or am I missing something about why that would be a bad idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T07:47:54-07:00","id":1342346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342345#post1342345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. If you Suppress all the entangled Variations, does that also temporarily alleviate the Secondary Scar? Or am I missing something about why that would be a bad idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be how Mimicry works and is not my intention here. However, I believe there is some language elsewhere that would contradict my intent, so I'll locate and clarify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T08:29:28-07:00","id":1342351,"title":"","content":"Ahh, I temporarily forgot about Mimicry. That's what I was missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T08:50:11-07:00","id":1342352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342340#post1342340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Relentless Variation (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this version! there's no real issue i can see, though personally i would<br /> 1. add a specific note for what if the Magnitude of the Secondary Scar is set below 1 (personally i would say that it counts as a Subtle Secondary in that case)<br /> 2. clarify what you mean in in the second case (Subtle Scar, Overt Variation). My understanding is you wanted to be (Secondary Scar Magnitude - 1), same as the full Subtle Version, in the case of Secondary Scar Magnitude being more than Overt Variation Magnitude, and straight Secondary Scar Magnitude, same as as the full Overt Version, in the case of the Overt Variation Magnitude being more than or equal to the Secondary Scar Magnitude, but this isn't obvious by the way it is written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T11:25:18-07:00","id":1342381,"title":"","content":"For the Concentration method of Suppressible, does &quot;Concentration 3&quot; mean any combination of the base Magnitude and its Deviations, or just one of the two options at Magnitude 3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T12:24:47-07:00","id":1342390,"title":"","content":"Would it be appropriate to post about homebrewed Variations/Scars here or should that be saved for a separate post under the D:tR sub-forum in the future? Just super excited about this game and have so many ideas coming to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T13:52:52-07:00","id":1342401,"title":"","content":"Why not just start a separate thread for Homebrew Variations and Scars, and let the people setting up the new subforum move it when they're ready?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T16:30:34-07:00","id":1342429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342340#post1342340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calculate the Magnitude of Relentless Variation as follows:<br /> <br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar and all entangled Variations are Subtle, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is one less than that of the secondary Scar.<br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar is Subtle but at least one of the entangled Variations is Overt, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is the higher of (secondary Scar Magnitude - 1) or the Magnitude of the highest-Magnitude Overt Variation.<br /> \u2022 If the secondary Scar is Overt, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is equal to that of the secondary Scar.<br /> \u2022 The Magnitude of this Scar is one higher if one or more entangled Variations are likely to create story complications by being \u201calways-on,\u201d such as Camouflage 3+, Gigantic, Miniaturization, or Out of Phase (Body) 3.</div> </div> </div> </div> This feels unnecessarily complicated and, unlike the version of Relentless Variation in the backer preview, it doesn't really make sense as a Scar anymore. At the very least, some of the calculations might be easier to follow as Deviations.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm unsure of how this variable Magnitude is supposed to work if the Scar is unentangled, and what happens if you purchase a new Variation that changes what calculation to use (or if you apply the Disfiguring Scar Variation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the secondary Scar is Subtle but at least one of the entangled Variations is Overt, the Magnitude of Relentless Variation is [...] the Magnitude of the highest-Magnitude Overt Variation. </div> </div> </div> How do you determine the Magnitude of the secondary Scar in this case?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Deviations</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Suppressible (-1 Magnitude):</b> The Broken can suppress an entangled Variation until the end of the scene by one of the following means, chosen at the time the Deviant develops this Scar: </div> </div> </div> The structure here is sound, and a clear improvement, though I'm selfishly disappointed by the reduced options, particularly the lack of Tabula Rasa.<br /> <br /> Overall, this version looks to be more balanced, but this comes at the cost of being harder to follow and, as a direct result, harder to use. I'm concerned about it scaring off less crunch-inclined players, whereas most other Scars and Variations are fairly concise -- even Lash, to which you compared it, is wordy but fundamentally uncomplicated.<br /> <br /> Running a game, I'd probably ignore this take on Relentless Variation and use the backer preview version instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 10-19-2019, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T17:33:33-07:00","id":1342439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342429#post1342429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels unnecessarily complicated and, unlike the version of Relentless Variation in the backer preview, it doesn't really make sense as a Scar anymore. At the very least, some of the calculations might be easier to follow as Deviations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking something similar: if you always have a secondary Scar that's Persistent, why not just call the secondary Scar a regular Scar and reframe this as a +1 to -1 Deviation for Persistent Scars that are entangled with Toggled-Only Variations? The four bullet points you have for calculating the Magnitude of Relentless Variation then become an issue of how much of an adjustment to the Scar Magnitude this Deviation causes. I'd simplify this to \u201cif the Scar and all entangled Variations are Subtle, this is a -1 Deviation (but see Hardship, below); if anything is Overt, this becomes a -0 Deviation instead. Hardship: if any of the entangled Variations are particularly troublesome if you can't shut them off [insert list of such Variations here], increase this from -1 to -0 or from -0 to +1.\u201d<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Suppressible and Unruly/Rebellious Deviations become standalone Deviations that can be applied to any Persistent Scar that's entangled with a Perpetual Variation. After all, Perpetual Variations are inherently relentless: you can't shut them off. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342429#post1342429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm unsure of how this variable Magnitude is supposed to work if the Scar is unentangled, and what happens if you purchase a new Variation that changes what calculation to use (or if you apply the Disfiguring Scar Variation).<br /> <br /> How do you determine the Magnitude of the secondary Scar in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div> My take: you can't apply this to an unentangled Scar; it can only be applied if there's at least one Variation entangled with it. The only time the Scar Magnitude if going to change is if everything is subtle and you entangle a new Overt Variation, in which case the effective Magnitude of the Scar increases by one. <br /> <br /> I'll comment on Suppressible later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-23-2019, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T21:12:36-07:00","id":1342460,"title":"","content":"Another take on Relentless Variation, this one rendering it as a trio of Standard Deviations:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Relentless Variation</span><br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Toggled-Only<br /> <b>-1 to +1 Magnitude:</b> The Variation entangled with the Scar is always active, and the Remade can\u2019t toggle it off. At best, she must take measures to bring it under control. At worst, she <i>can\u2019t</i>. The Scar and all its entangled Variations are Perpetual (granting a +5 bonus to Clash of Wills rolls involving them). This is a -1 Magnitude Deviation if the Scar and all entangled Variations are Subtle, and a +0 Magnitude Deviation if the Scar and/or any of its entangled Variations is Overt. Increase the Deviation Magnitude by one if one or more entangled Variations are likely to create story complications by being \u201calways-on,\u201d such as Camouflage 3+, Gigantic, Miniaturization, or Out of Phase (Body) 3.<br /> <br /> If an entangled Tiered Variation has a constant effect (such as Bioluminescence with the Aura Deviation, or Gigantic), the Deviant\u2019s player determines the default Magnitude of each Tiered Variation entangled with Relentless Variation at the time she chooses this Deviation. She may change the current Magnitude (as well as any applicable Deviations) of a Variation as an action, such as to dim or brighten the light her Bioluminescence (p. XX) ordinarily produces, for example, as long as she is normally able to do so.<br /> <br /> Directed Variations (or Directed effects of non-Directed Variations) affected by this Deviation still require an action to target. Effects limited to use once per scene/chapter/story still carry these restrictions, and those with explicit durations are still limited to them (Omnicompetence 2 doesn\u2019t grant the option to have a dot in all Skills, constantly, for example). The Scar can entangle Reflexive Variations and those with a \u201cmenu\u201d of capabilities that can\u2019t reasonably remain \u201calways on\u201d (such as Electrokinesis), but it has little-to-no effect on them without Deviations.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Suppressible Variation</span><br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perpetual-Only<br /> <b>-1 Magnitude:</b> The Broken can suppress a Variation entangled with the Scar until the end of the scene by succeeding on a Scar Resistance roll and suffering an additional effect chosen at the time the Deviant\u2019s player selects this Deviation. This \u201ccost\u201d typically resembles a Controlled Scar of Magnitude 3 (or occasionally more), with the following being typical:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Concentration:</b> Suppressing an entangled Variation follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Concentration (Tenuous) 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> \u2022 <b>Depletion:</b> The Broken can only suppress an entangled Variation for a number of minutes (turns, in action scenes) equal to Scar Resistance and may only do so once per scene, although Adaptations can overcome this.<br /> \u2022 <b>Deterioration:</b> Suppressing an entangled Variation follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Deterioration (Lingering) 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> \u2022 <b>Perilous:</b> The Broken suffers a point of lethal damage when suppressing an entangled Variation.<br /> \u2022 <b>Power Failure:</b> Suppressing an entangled Variation follows similar rules as activating one entangled with the Power Failure Scar (p. XX). See the sidebar for details<br /> \u2022 <b>Preparation:</b> Suppressing an entangled Variation follows the same rules as activating one entangled with the Preparation (Elaborate) 3 Controlled Scar (p. XX).<br /> \u2022 <b>Tribulation:</b> The Deviant must spend a point of Willpower to suppress an entangled Variation.<br /> \u2022 <b>Unstable:</b> The Remade suffers a minor Instability each time he suppresses an entangled Variation.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suppressible Variation and Power Failure</span><br /> When using Suppressible Deviation, Power Failure is a special case, reflecting as it does some countermeasure or suppression device the Broken uses to tamp down her unruly Variations \u2014 such as a special article of clothing, continual exposure to a radio signal, or regular injections of a stabilizing serum. While this is their main purpose within the story, an enemy <i>could</i> deploy them to disable the transformed\u2019s Variations, or the Deviant might find herself in an environment where the countermeasures are in place and she can\u2019t remove them in order to use her Variations. Thus, the Power Failure option for Relentless Variation is a double-edged sword.<br /> <br /> For that reason, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes. The player similarly decides the following at the time he purchases this Scar:<br /> <br /> <b>Off:</b> Does application of the countermeasure neutralize the Variation immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation lose Magnitude every interval of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch off on a delay?<br /> <b>On:</b> Does removal of the countermeasure cause the Variation to manifest at full strength immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation gain Magnitude every interval of time (turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch on after the delay?<br /> <b>Minimum:</b> Once the countermeasure is removed, can it be reapplied right away, or is it impossible to do so for a period of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes) or until the end of the scene?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Unruly Variation</span><br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Directed-Only, Perpetual-Only<br /> <b>+1 Magnitude:</b> Once per chapter, as long as the Variation is active (not neutralized by the Untamed Adaptation or the Mimicry Variation, for example), the Storyteller may direct an entangled Variation for a single turn during which the Deviant did not do so, either choosing its target or selecting one at random. The Broken\u2019s player may resist this effect with a Scar Resistance roll. If this roll succeeds, the Storyteller may make another direction attempt in a later scene but may not attempt to direct this Variation again during the current scene. Each consecutive successful roll to resist Storyteller direction imposes a -1 penalty on future rolls to resist this effect.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Rebellious (+1 Magnitude):</b> As above, but if the Storyteller successfully directs an entangled Variation, he may continue directing it on subsequent turns until the end of the scene or until the Deviant\u2019s player makes a successful Scar Resistance roll to regain control. Each consecutive failed Scar Resistance roll to regain control grants a +1 penalty on later rolls to wrest back control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":".  Suppressible Variation, not Suppressible Scar 10-20-2019, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T22:29:07-07:00","id":1342471,"title":"","content":"(Nitpick: Suppressible Variation, not Suppressible Scar.)<br /> <br /> I would like to point out that in this structure, Relentless Variation and Suppressible Variation are almost polar opposites. Almost. Relentless Variation turns a Toggled Variation into a Perpetual Variation; Suppressible Variation turns a Perpetual Variation into something not unlike a Toggled Variation. The main difference is that you need to use the equivalent of a Controlled Scar to \u201ctoggle\u201d it.<br /> <br /> This isn't a criticism; just an observation. I rather like the resulting dynamic. That said, theoretically, it implies that there might be a place for a more \u201csevere\u201d version of Suppressible Variation that actually <i>is</i> the mirror opposite of Relentless Variation, converting a Perpetual Variation into an honest to goodness Toggled Variation, with no need to use a Controlled Scar to shut it off. Theoretically. In practice, let's not go there. I'm assuming that the decision to take certain Variations as Toggled and others as Perpetual was made with care, and that the ones that were called Perpetual were selected as such because being able to just turn them off at will and without paying any sort of price for doing so was deemed to be problematic. So with that in mind, let's not even entertain the notion of being able to make a Perpetual Variation Toggled instead; Suppressible is as close as we should get to that. <br /> <br /> Unruly Variation: I'd ditch the Perpetual-Only Keyword. The idea behind Unruly Variation is that a Directed Variation may end up targeting people that you don't want it to when it's active. Applying this to a Toggled Variation may make the Deviant less inclined to toggle it on; but that's not an abuse of the rules. Allow it. <br /> <br /> In fact, consider allowing it for Involuntary Scars as well as Persistent Scars: basically, Unruly Variation gives you a way around the \u201cDirected Variations can't be entangled with this\u201d restriction. If the player doesn't get to choose who the Variation is directed at, it seems entirely appropriate for an Involuntary Scar to activate a Directed Variation. <br /> <br /> I still haven't had time to digest the exact mechanics for Suppressible Variation; so I'll say more on that a bit later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T02:40:37-07:00","id":1342490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Relentless Variation</span> </div> </div> </div> I like it. The calculations aren't actually different from before, but they're a lot easier to read with this presentation.<br /> <br /> It's still pretty verbose \u2013 I didn't mind the preview Relentless' restriction on Directed Variations, myself \u2013 but I don't think that will get in the way of using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Suppressible Scar</span> </div> </div> </div> It was good before and it's good now. I <i>really</i> appreciate the expanded options; thank you for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Unruly Variation</span> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to echo <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> here, but go one step further: this could be merged into the extant Rebellious Variation to create a Deviation with <i>Scar Type: Any</i>, possibly with the current Unruly effect as a sub-Deviation locked to Persistent and Perpetual Variations alongside this take's Rebellious sub-Deviation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T11:29:36-07:00","id":1342558,"title":"","content":"Hm. I have a question for Eric based on this. Would it be possible to have a power EXCLUSIVELY paid for by Deviations? Because now I have a few ideas based on that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T13:40:27-07:00","id":1342569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342471#post1342471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Nitpick: Suppressible Variation, not Suppressible Scar.)<br /> <br /> I would like to point out that in this structure, Relentless Variation and Suppressible Variation are almost polar opposites. Almost. Relentless Variation turns a Toggled Variation into a Perpetual Variation; Suppressible Variation turns a Perpetual Variation into something not unlike a Toggled Variation. The main difference is that you need to use the equivalent of a Controlled Scar to \u201ctoggle\u201d it.<br /> <br /> This isn't a criticism; just an observation. I rather like the resulting dynamic. That said, theoretically, it implies that there might be a place for a more \u201csevere\u201d version of Suppressible Variation that actually <i>is</i> the mirror opposite of Relentless Variation, converting a Perpetual Variation into an honest to goodness Toggled Variation, with no need to use a Controlled Scar to shut it off. Theoretically. In practice, let's not go there. I'm assuming that the decision to take certain Variations as Toggled and others as Perpetual was made with care, and that the ones that were called Perpetual were selected as such because being able to just turn them off at will and without paying any sort of price for doing so was deemed to be problematic. So with that in mind, let's not even entertain the notion of being able to make a Perpetual Variation Toggled instead; Suppressible is as close as we should get to that.<br /> <br /> Unruly Variation: I'd ditch the Perpetual-Only Keyword. The idea behind Unruly Variation is that a Directed Variation may end up targeting people that you don't want it to when it's active. Applying this to a Toggled Variation may make the Deviant less inclined to toggle it on; but that's not an abuse of the rules. Allow it.<br /> <br /> In fact, consider allowing it for Involuntary Scars as well as Persistent Scars: basically, Unruly Variation gives you a way around the \u201cDirected Variations can't be entangled with this\u201d restriction. If the player doesn't get to choose who the Variation is directed at, it seems entirely appropriate for an Involuntary Scar to activate a Directed Variation.<br /> <br /> I still haven't had time to digest the exact mechanics for Suppressible Variation; so I'll say more on that a bit later.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Fixed.)<br /> <br /> The choice of whether to make a Variation Perpetual usually came down to whether it was Subtle and not Directed. Bear in mind I was operating under the assumption that Relentless Variation was going to increase the Magnitude of a Scar because Perpetual created more complications. The goal of the Perpetual keyword was in large part to prevent people from abusing Relentless Variation by entangling it with something that carried no downside for being on all the time, since it was Subtle. That assumption was ultimately mistaken, since Perpetual is usually a net benefit due to action economy, and people are less likely to take Relentless &quot;for the free dots&quot; than I feared. Under the Deviations model, Subtle Variations with the Perpetual keyword natively are more valuable, since they save you having to bolt Relentless Variation onto them at a net reduction in the Scar's Magnitude.<br /> <br /> I might, in fact, need to review each Perpetual Variation to determine whether it still needs to be Perpetual in order for it to make sense. Rapid Healing, for example, relies on the passage of narrative time for its effects, and several Anomalous Biology effects are similarly nonsensical as a Toggled power, so those will stay as is. Carapace and Pheromones, meanwhile, might lose the Keyword (not certainly, but it's something to consider. So, I'm unlikely to make a clean &quot;a Perpetual Variation is now Toggled&quot; Deviation for that reason.<br /> <br /> RE Unruly: I think I'll leave this one as-is. Involuntary already has Rebellious Variation, in addition to Deviations specific to individual Scars, that do something similar things, so I'm not worried about them. The issue with letting Controlled Variations get in on the fun is that when you activate a Directed Variation, you're likely to use it every turn, or you're at least in a scene where it is potentially useful even if it doesn't necessarily hit a target you'd intended to affect. Healing Touch (which is now Directed) is going to be activated when there is someone to heal (and often when no one you don't want healed is around), while &quot;ignoring&quot; your active Telekinesis to use something else when you're in a target-rich environment might mean you get lucky and it attacks someone you wouldn't mind hurting anyway. This doesn't give the Storyteller as many opportunities to show your power going out of control as a Variation that is <i>always</i> active and therefore always available to complicate a scene (unless you pay Suppressible's price to tamp it down for a little while).<br /> <br /> The current version has lost the &quot;cannot be entangled with Directed Variations&quot; language. Directed Variations don't get much of a benefit for being made Relentless, with the exception of having your Ranged Lash &quot;always unsheathed&quot; (not a truly Directed Variation, but one that behaves that way in many respects).<br /> <br /> RE Suppressible: Looking forward to your feedback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342490#post1342490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like it. The calculations aren't actually different from before, but they're a lot easier to read with this presentation.<br /> <br /> It's still pretty verbose \u2013 I didn't mind the preview Relentless' restriction on Directed Variations, myself \u2013 but I don't think that will get in the way of using it.<br /> <br /> It was good before and it's good now. I <i>really</i> appreciate the expanded options; thank you for that.<br /> <br /> I'm going to echo <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> here, but go one step further: this could be merged into the extant Rebellious Variation to create a Deviation with <i>Scar Type: Any</i>, possibly with the current Unruly effect as a sub-Deviation locked to Persistent and Perpetual Variations alongside this take's Rebellious sub-Deviation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviations are structured differently than Variations, so the &quot;pick A or B&quot; format wouldn't be great here. The effects are sufficiently different that I wouldn't want to combine them into a single Deviation, and since they're both Deviations, it's easy to grab both if that's the concept you're going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342558#post1342558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I have a question for Eric based on this. Would it be possible to have a power EXCLUSIVELY paid for by Deviations? Because now I have a few ideas based on that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not shooting it down as a concept, but I'm unlikely to do this within the core. Mostly, having to explain how this works (and how it doesn't) in writing would be complicated and eat a lot of words for something I just can't see that many people wanting to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:05:40-07:00","id":1343055,"title":"","content":"This is several weeks late to ask, I think, but concerning the Invasive add-on to the Clades Companion: Is it likely or possible that the weirder gear examples we'll be getting in that might include something along the lines of engineered or jury-rigged environment suits for characters with Scars like Native Environment or Involuntary Stimulus or Power Failure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:11:44-07:00","id":1343057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343055#post1343055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is several weeks late to ask, I think, but concerning the Invasive add-on to the Clades Companion: Is it likely or possible that the weirder gear examples we'll be getting in that might include something along the lines of engineered or jury-rigged environment suits for characters with Scars like Native Environment or Involuntary Stimulus or Power Failure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too late, actually. It's a good idea, and it's a one-sentence ask in the working outline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:18:05-07:00","id":1343061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343055#post1343055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is several weeks late to ask, I think, but concerning the Invasive add-on to the Clades Companion: Is it likely or possible that the weirder gear examples we'll be getting in that might include something along the lines of engineered or jury-rigged environment suits for characters with Scars like Native Environment or Involuntary Stimulus or Power Failure?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343057#post1343057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not too late, actually. It's a good idea, and it's a one-sentence ask in the working outline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to make Mr Freeze, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T23:43:03-07:00","id":1343102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343057#post1343057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not too late, actually. It's a good idea, and it's a one-sentence ask in the working outline.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're talking broad concepts that haven't been covered and which supplement material might one day facilitate, one concept I tried to work out mechanically was a character with an inhuman Conspicuous Appearance, who could only take on human semblance by stealing one from others a la Face Thief. My first assumption was that Mimicry would cover that and then it would take some clever choices of Controlled or Involuntary Scars with conditional factors, but it doesn't look like an intended use of Mimicry to keep reactivating it at the end of every scene.<br /> <br /> In general, Mimicry is one I struggle with conceptually, and I wonder if it's even possible to use structures like the new versions of Suppressible and so on to do its job purely through entangled Scars and Deviations. It doesn't help that its most obvious application is already covered well by Hybrid Form, and that dots of Mimicry alone eat into your Variation budget, while Hybrid Form is actually budget-efficient. It feels like a very poor cousin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 10-23-2019, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T02:39:24-07:00","id":1343108,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Suppressible, here's my counterproposal, followed by my reasoning for the changes:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Suppressible Variation</span><br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perpetual-Only<br /> <b>-0 Magnitude:</b> The Broken can suppress a Variation entangled with the Scar until the end of the scene by succeeding on a Scar Resistance roll and replacing the Scar with a Controlled Scar (called the suppressant) for the duration. The suppressant is chosen at the time the Deviant\u2019s player selects this Deviation, and has the same Magnitude as the Scar that the Deviation is applied to. The suppressant works as normal, except that \u201cactivate\u201d and \u201cdeactivate\u201d become \u201csuppress\u201d and \u201crestore\u201d. <br /> <br /> There are a few Controlled Scars that don't work as suppressants: Cooldown is all about what happens when you redirect a Directed Variation, which doesn't make sense when it's suppressed; and Fluctuating Variation deals with a fluctuating Magnitude for an active Variation, which doesn't make sense when the Variation is suppressed. So you can't use either of these as a suppressant.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suppressible Variation and Power Failure</span><br /> When using Suppressible Variation, Power Failure is a special case, reflecting as it does some countermeasure or suppression device the Broken uses to tamp down her unruly Variations \u2014 such as a special article of clothing, continual exposure to a radio signal, or regular injections of a stabilizing serum. While this is their main purpose within the story, an enemy <i>could</i> deploy them to disable the transformed\u2019s Variations, or the Deviant might find herself in an environment where the countermeasures are in place and she can\u2019t remove them in order to use her Variations. Thus, the Power Failure option for Relentless Variation is a double-edged sword.<br /> <br /> For that reason, Power Failure is always treated as a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar when it is used as a suppressant, and the Common and Rare Deviations are not allowed. However, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes. The player decides the following at the time he purchases this Scar:<br /> <br /> <b>Off:</b> Does application of the countermeasure neutralize the Variation immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation lose Magnitude every interval of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch off on a delay?<br /> <b>On:</b> Does removal of the countermeasure cause the Variation to manifest at full strength immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation gain Magnitude every interval of time (turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch on after the delay?<br /> <b>Minimum:</b> Once the countermeasure is removed, can it be reapplied right away, or is it impossible to do so for a period of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes) or until the end of the scene?<br /> </div>---<br /> <br /> The original text where you take a secondary Perpetual Scar when the Relentless Variation is Inescapable and a secondary Controlled Scar when it's Suppressible was broken; but you can achieve a similar effect that <i>isn't</i> broken by saying that a Suppressible Variation always has one Scar in play: the Persistent Scar (when it's not suppressed) or an alternate Controlled Scar with the same Magnitude (when it is). This can apply to nearly any Controlled Scar, including Persistent Drawback (which lets you replace the usual Scar with a different Persistent Scar while the Variation is suppressed) and Tabula Rasa (which results in memory loss pertaining to the time that the Variation was suppressed). <br /> <br /> But if you make this change, Suppressible Variation becomes a mixed blessing, as you can use it to swap out one Scar for another. This is why I lowered the value of Suppressible Variation from -1 to -0 in my proposal.<br /> <br /> Instead of saying that the suppressant works like a Magnitude 3 Controlled Scar (which is rigid, and allows for Magnitude 4+ Variations to be suppressed with a Magnitude 3 Scar), I'm instead going back to the original idea that the suppressant has the same Magnitude as the Scar that it substitutes for. This is cleaner and more flexible. With this return to variable-Magnitude suppressants, the text for Relentless Variation and Power Failure also reverts to its original form. <br /> <br /> The other big change I made was to focus on those Controlled Scars that <i>don't</i> make sense as suppressants instead of spending a lot of redundant word count spelling out all of the Controlled Scars that <i>do</i>: the \u201cburden of proof\u201d, as it were, should be on \u201cwhy <i>can't</i> I use X?\u201d If you don't list a given Controlled Scar as inappropriate for use as a suppressant (and explain why it's inappropriate), then the players should assume that it's possible to use it and apply their creative juices to figuring out how. <br /> <br /> I would recommend that this be considered in future supplements when new Controlled Scars are introduced: if they don't make sense as suppressants (like Cooldown or Fluctuating Variation) or need to be tweaked (like Power Failure), then the write-up of the new Scar should mention that. You might even consider setting precedent for that by moving the \u201cSuppressible Variation and Power Failure\u201d box from the Suppressible Variation write-up to the Power Failure write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-23-2019, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T03:15:53-07:00","id":1343111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342569#post1342569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE Unruly: I think I'll leave this one as-is. Involuntary already has Rebellious Variation, in addition to Deviations specific to individual Scars, that do something similar things, so I'm not worried about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. However, you might want to tag Rebellious Variation with the Directed Only Keyword.<br /> <br /> Also, it might be confusing to use \u201cRebellious\u201d in two different contexts (one as the \u201cRebellious Variation\u201d Deviation, and another as a part of the \u201cUnruly Variation\u201d Deviation). Consider reformatting Unruly Variation in a manner similar to how the \u201cIdentifier\u201d Deviation is formatted: a <b>+1 Magnitude</b> paragraph and a <b>+2 Magnitude</b> paragraph, with no mention of Rebellious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-23-2019, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:19:55-07:00","id":1343147,"title":"","content":"Question, has anybody whipped up any sort of fillable character sheet or template yet? I know Mr. Gone at least can't really make one until the official character sheet comes out with the book, but it'd be handy to have some kinda sheet for myself and the other players of the game I'm in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11208-thehailstormer","name":"TheHailStormer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11208_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:23:34-07:00","id":1343165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheHailStormer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343147#post1343147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, has anybody whipped up any sort of fillable character sheet or template yet? I know Mr. Gone at least can't really make one until the official character sheet comes out with the book, but it'd be handy to have some kinda sheet for myself and the other players of the game I'm in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr Gone does have a generic fillable sheet that works well enough - you can label all of the fields to the appropriate Deviant terminology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T09:30:50-07:00","id":1343195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1342401#post1342401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just start a separate thread for Homebrew Variations and Scars, and let the people setting up the new subforum move it when they're ready?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for pointing this out.<br /> <br /> I started the thread with a few ideas I have been able to work on. People can find the thread here if they haven't seen it already: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342524-homebrew-variations-and-scars\">Homebrew Variations and Scars</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T13:56:32-07:00","id":1343268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheHailStormer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343147#post1343147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, has anybody whipped up any sort of fillable character sheet or template yet? I know Mr. Gone at least can't really make one until the official character sheet comes out with the book, but it'd be handy to have some kinda sheet for myself and the other players of the game I'm in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's designed a little more for online games than for printing out and bringing to physical tables, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1339813#post1339813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a Google Docs template for a Deviant character sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/131LAn_M_a9VUU3AzIHv74WgrHO7q8kBPyY4NegAMA40/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can copy and paste dots and dot spacers as the easiest way to edit dot ratings; I visualize them this way to easily distinguish, for instance, Skills you have unranked and Skills you don't. Unskilled penalties matter! Add rows to tables as needed, or copy an Entanglement table and paste to add another. There are blank columns between Skills and their dot ratings in which to write Specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T15:41:36-07:00","id":1343291,"title":"","content":"Can Variations that change the capabilities of your body take effect while using Integrate Technology 4 to merge with a machine? For example, if I merge with a car, could I take advantage of Enhanced Speed to make my car-body incredibly fast? Or if I merge with a submersible could I use Gigantic to make it accommodate more crew members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T16:45:46-07:00","id":1343298,"title":"","content":"Not <i>quite</i> what you're talking about; but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j18e_ID-DpA\" data-code=\"j18e_ID-DpA\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/j18e_ID-DpA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2