e probably gotten only 5 or 6 hours of sleep and probably shouldn't attempt any strenuous game design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T17:47:42-07:00","id":1343688,"title":"","content":"Quick, everyone homebrew something inadvisable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T17:51:37-07:00","id":1343689,"title":"","content":"I definitely understand. My response concerning the \u201cSuppressible Variation\u201d Deviation was likewise delayed by Real Life taking up so much of my time. I'm looking forward to hearing more from you on this, but I wouldn't want you rushing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T17:56:28-07:00","id":1343690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343689#post1343689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely understand. My response concerning the \u201cSuppressible Variation\u201d Deviation was likewise delayed by Real Life taking up so much of my time. I'm looking forward to hearing more from you on this, but I wouldn't want you rushing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read through your comments and realized it was just...not getting through to my brain. I'm sure it'll make way more sense when I'm not sleep-deprived. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T23:21:55-07:00","id":1343723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1343102#post1343102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, Mimicry is one I struggle with conceptually, and I wonder if it's even possible to use structures like the new versions of Suppressible and so on to do its job purely through entangled Scars and Deviations. It doesn't help that its most obvious application is already covered well by Hybrid Form, and that dots of Mimicry alone eat into your Variation budget, while Hybrid Form is actually budget-efficient. It feels like a very poor cousin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a couple days and I'm still extremely confused about what part of Mimicry's &quot;most obvious application&quot; Hybrid Form covers, considering Mimicry's most obvious application is &quot;turn off all the Scars you have up to Mimicry's threshold besides the one entangled with Mimicry, at the cost of losing access to their entangled Variations if they have any&quot; and Hybrid Form's primary application is &quot;activate multiple Magnitude 1-4 Variations in one action as a single Overt Variation&quot; and its limitations mean you are, at best, treating the secondary Variations as an Overt Variation one Magnitude higher than they are.<br /> <br /> Mimicry exists for temporarily stifling the obvious drawbacks of being a Deviant. Hybrid Form exists to let you make an explosive manifestation of powers that \u2014 unless you've constructed a Hybrid Form redundant with your normal abilities for some reason \u2014 you don't otherwise normally have. They fill different niches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T01:43:18-07:00","id":1343734,"title":"","content":"Mimicry is a great power and I love it, especially for being Ordo Dracul of Deviant. I'm not sure how many concepts I will have that actually make use of it, but I love the potential at any rate. It and Lash are the two most iconic deviant variations in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T10:48:00-07:00","id":1343805,"title":"","content":"To be frank, if you're running a Deviant that's going to be picking up a wide variety of powerful Variations over their lifespan, Mimicry is kind of required for them to remain playable.<br /> <br /> It has its niche and that niche has nothing to do with Hybrid Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T16:28:18-07:00","id":1343883,"title":"","content":"I just thought of an excellent Future Dark Era for Deviant; the Rise and Probable Fall of the Neoreactionary Successor to The United States.<br /> <br /> More specifically, I'm inspired by a sporking Spacebattles did of <i>Victoria: A Novel of Fourth-Generation War,</i> a rather puerile revenge fantasy against everyone the author blames for various failures in his career, which seems to include everyone whose political ideas were formulated after 1965, with horrific protagonist-centered morality (this is the same novel where the protagonists being compared to the Nazi party is objected by saying they lack some of the aesthetic, and the narrative treats this as a rhetorical slam-dunk). I'm not going into it because of the hot-button politics (look it up on Spacebattles, I'm not linking it either), but the vast fanfiction community of Spacebattles, in conjunction with the history wonks, came up with an idea for a more plausible history that is actually a really interesting bit of near-future military sci-fi.<br /> <br /> Military sci-fi is a genre Deviant was made for, especially if you're playing Devoted to a more benign group. So, idea; an alliance of the fascistic parts of the Web of Pain engineered a scandal that revealed the true depth of the supernatural to the world, collapsing the United States, and then they backed the formation of a new government that <i>claims </i>to be a call-back to a pure, safer time without all that terrible social change from WWI on (seriously, there are people advocating for a return to pre-WWI monarchies presented as allies of the good guys), but is in reality supported on the backs of dozens of Remade and other supernatural beings they've blackmailed and brainwashed into keeping their Orwellian nightmare of a state together with a rune-engraved iron fist and feared monstrous shock troops.<br /> <br /> You happen to be escapees from the program who found their way to saner successor states who both fear you as a sign of everything wrong with the regime and yet deeply need and desire you as a way to turn the enemy's spears upon them. Are you a bad enough dude to overthrow an empire?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I am aware of Mother Russia Bleeds, that's part of the thematic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-26-2019, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T12:14:28-07:00","id":1344043,"title":"","content":"Here's a challenge for you all. Try to build Grace Sciuridae, from the webcomic El Goonish Shive, as a Deviant.<br /> <br /> This is a challenge because, well, her backstory is very much in the Deviant mold, but her powers are leaving me at a loss. Origin and Clade are easy - she's a Genotypal Chimeric. Her powers, though ... she's got two major ones, shapeshifting (very flexible) and telekinesis. But the strength of her TK varies with her current form; as a human she's never used it, in her birth form (a human/squirrel hybrid) she's moved small objects and held off a homicidal blob, and in &quot;monster&quot; forms she uses it to fly. I don't see quite how to represent that limitation.<br /> <br /> She's got some other abilities that are easy - Animal Transformation 2 (turning into an actual squirrel) and Pheromones 2. It's her two main powers that puzzle me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T12:44:51-07:00","id":1344049,"title":"","content":"Multiple hybrid forms with different levels of TK","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T19:41:42-07:00","id":1344807,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>: Your suggestion makes way more sense when I've had a decent night's sleep. How does this work for everyone:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Suppressible Variation</span><br /> <b>Scar Type:</b> Persistent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perpetual-Only<br /> <b>+0 Magnitude:</b> The Broken can temporarily suppress the effects of a Perpetual Persistent Variation. Choose a Controlled Scar (the secondary Scar) with the same Magnitude as the Scar modified by this Deviation when the Deviant develops Suppressible Variation.<br /> The Remade can suppress the Scar and its entangled Variation until the end of the scene by succeeding on a Scar Resistance roll and paying the price of the secondary Scar (Willpower for Tribulation, for example). In any case where the secondary Scar would normally activate the entangled Variation, it suppresses it, instead, and in any case where it would cause the Variation to deactivate, it activates it, instead.<br /> <br /> Cooldown and Fluctuating Variation are not permitted as secondary Scars, and Power Failure is a special case (see sidebar).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suppressible Variation and Power Failure</span><br /> <br /> When Power Failure is the secondary Scar of this Deviation it reflects some countermeasure or suppression device the Broken uses to tamp down her unruly Variations \u2014 such as a special article of clothing, continual exposure to a radio signal, or regular injections of a stabilizing serum. While this is their main purpose within the story, an enemy <i>could</i> deploy them to disable the transformed\u2019s Variations, or the Deviant might find herself in an environment where the countermeasures are in place and she can\u2019t remove them in order to use her Variations. Thus, the Power Failure option for Suppressible Variation is a double-edged sword.<br /> For that reason, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes. The player similarly decides the following at the time he purchases this Scar:<br /> <br /> <b>Off:</b> Does application of the countermeasure neutralize the Variation immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation lose Magnitude every interval of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch off on a delay?<br /> <b>On:</b> Does removal of the countermeasure cause the Variation to manifest at full strength immediately, or does it take time to do so? If gradual, does the Variation gain Magnitude every interval of time (turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes), or does it switch on after the delay?<br /> <b>Minimum:</b> Once the countermeasure is removed, can it be reapplied right away, or is it impossible to do so for a period of time (measured in turns in action scenes, minutes in other scenes) or until the end of the scene?<br /> <br /> <br /> By the by, pairing this Deviation with Persistent Drawback is actually a pretty brilliant idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T21:33:58-07:00","id":1344830,"title":"","content":"Thanks; I made a point of running every Controlled Scar through the lens of \u201ccan this make sense if it's being used to suppress a Variation instead of activate it?\u201d, and Persistent Drawback surprisingly passed the test. The only ones that failed were Cooldown and Fluctuating Variation (the former because it's actually about what happens when you redirect a Variation and a suppressed Variation can't be redirected, and the latter because a suppressed Variation doesn't fluctuate); and if anyone can see a way that either of these can make sense as suppressants rather than activators, please speak up! <br /> <br /> I have a correction and a nitpick:<br /> <br /> First, the correction. In the Suppressible Variation and Power Failure sidebar, instead of:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For that reason, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes.</div>It should be:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For that reason, Power Failure is always treated as a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar when it is Suppressible Variation's secondary Scar, and the Common and Rare Deviations are not allowed. However, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes.</div>With the return of customizable secondary Scars (with variable Magnitude and potentially subject to Deviations), the restrictions on Power Failure that are in the draft also need to be reinstated. <br /> <br /> The only thing I'd change about Suppressible Variation itself would be to add an explanation why Cooldown and Fluctuating Variation are not permitted: while it doesn't matter in the context of the core book, it should help when new Controlled Scars get added to the game further on down the line, or when people homebrew their own Scars. Basically, you'd be stating a general principle that others can use as a guide when deciding whether to allow or reject a new Controlled Scar as secondary to this Deviation. And it can be accomplished in less than a sentence. Instead of: <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Cooldown and Fluctuating Variation are not permitted as secondary Scars, and Power Failure is a special case (see sidebar).</div>Say:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Cooldown and Fluctuating Variation have costs that don't make sense if the Variation is being suppressed, and are not permitted as secondary Scars.</div>That, and I wouldn't bother with the \u201c\u2026and Power Failure is a special case (see sidebar)\u201d: the fact that \u201cSuppressible Variation and Power Failure\u201d is a sidebar means that it's going to stand out, so there's no danger of it being overlooked and no need to mention it in the text of Suppressible Variation. <br /> <br /> But again, that's just a nitpick. <br /> <br /> Finally, one more observation: this version of Suppressible Variation overlaps somewhat with Mimicry: both suppress Scars and the Variations associated with them, in exchange for whatever Scars are associated with <i>themselves</i>. The difference is that Mimicry can suppress any number and kind of Scars and their Variations (Suppressible Variation only suppresses a single Scar, and it must be Perpetual). <br /> <br /> Oh: and one caveat about Persistent Drawback as a suppressant: technically, the Persistent Scar that it imposes while the Variation is suppressed could very well be the exact same Scar that Suppressible Variation is being applied to. That would be functionally equivalent to turning a Perpetual Variation into a Toggled Variation. While I recommended against allowing such a thing before, I'm no longer sure it's a bad idea \u2014 at least, not bad enough of an idea to warrant further word count explicitly forbidding it. If you think it's worth the word count to forbid it, add something to the effect of \u201cand Persistent Drawback must select a different Scar than the primary Scar when used as the secondary Scar\u201d to the end of the section about forbidden Controlled Scars. <br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't bother: while it's technically possible to do this, it's arguably a violation of the spirit of the rules; and as was hashed out pretty thoroughly earlier in this topic, Deviant assumes that everyone's going to try to hew to the spirit of the rules. So it's technically possible, but only something that a rules lawyer would attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-13-2020, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T22:05:19-07:00","id":1344836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1344830#post1344830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the correction. In the Suppressible Variation and Power Failure sidebar, instead of:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For that reason, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes.</div><br /> It should be:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For that reason, Power Failure is always treated as a Magnitude \u2022\u2022\u2022 Scar when it is Suppressible Variation's secondary Scar, and the Common and Rare Deviations are not allowed. However, the countermeasure can be as easy to bring into play (or as rare and difficult to apply) as the player wishes.</div></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and fixed. Reviewed the rest, as well. I'm grateful for your input on this one. The whole Relentless cluster was certainly the most complicated of all the Scar concepts to convey mechanically, so I've been all too happy to get feedback from the fan community to make sure it works as intended when the game is in its final form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:31:49-08:00","id":1363807,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a> Will the hyper-tech prototypes mentioned for the Clade Companion include mechanics for crafting items that incorporate Variations (with or without Scars)? Will this also allow for occult or other weird equipment specific to Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T08:34:16-08:00","id":1368752,"title":"","content":"We've finally started our Deviant game so I've looked over the rules for advancing the character. How you increase and gain new Scars and Variations. It's described in two different places (each with an XX page reference to somewhere else) in the second preview.<br /> On page 25 it says you can gain a new permanent Scar by downgrading a Major Instability or healing a Minor or Medium Instability. No mention of the Magnitude of the new Scar, nor how to permanently increase an old Scar.<br /> On page 56 it says you can choose to keep a temporary Scar or a Magnitude increase of a Scar so that they don't disappear when the associated Instability is healed.<br /> <br /> Presumably those two texts refer to the same thing, but they work differently. On page 25 you can heal Instability not associated with temporary Scars (or Magnitude increases) in order to gain permanent Scars, but doesn't mention permanent Magnitude increases, while on page 56 you can only keep the temporary Scars or Magnitude increases imposed by Instability, but it kinda implies you still need to heal the Instability in some other way.<br /> <br /> How does it actually work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T12:17:00-08:00","id":1368783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368752#post1368752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 25 it says you can gain a new permanent Scar by downgrading a Major Instability or healing a Minor or Medium Instability. No mention of the Magnitude of the new Scar, nor how to permanently increase an old Scar.<br /> On page 56 it says you can choose to keep a temporary Scar or a Magnitude increase of a Scar so that they don't disappear when the associated Instability is healed.<br /> <br /> Presumably those two texts refer to the same thing, but they work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, they're different things. The first option is a way of healing Instability (which also gives you room to entangle new Variations), while the second is <i>only</i> to make room for new or upgraded Variations.<br /> <br /> As for unentangled Scars, the rules for those come at page 128 of the &quot;Complete Preview,&quot; or page 58 of the second preview. In summary, the <i>minimum</i> Magnitude (the player can choose to take a worse Scar) of a new unentangled Scar is equal to the number of unentangled Scars you already have, plus one: \u25cf of you have no unentangled Scars, \u25cf\u25cf if you already have one, and so on.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T12:42:08-08:00","id":1368786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368783#post1368783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, they're different things. The first option is a way of healing Instability (which also gives you room to entangle new Variations), while the second is <i>only</i> to make room for new or upgraded Variations.<br /> <br /> As for unentangled Scars, the rules for those come at page 128 of the &quot;Complete Preview,&quot; or page 58 of the second preview. In summary, the <i>minimum</i> Magnitude (the player can choose to take a worse Scar) of a new unentangled Scar is equal to the number of unentangled Scars you already have, plus one: \u25cf of you have no unentangled Scars, \u25cf\u25cf if you already have one, and so on.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in order to gain a new permanent Scar I can either downgrade/heal any one Instability, or keep a Scar after having downgraded/healed a Major Instability in the last five boxes through other means. The former allows me to choose the Scar as long as the Magnitude isn't equal to or lower than the number of Unentangled Scars I already have. The latter forces me to use the Scar associated with a particular Major Instability.<br /> (And in either case the Scar is Persistent unless a Variation is bought and entangled to the Scar when it was formed.)<br /> It seems to me that the latter option's only advantage is that you can choose a lower Magnitude Scar if you have multiple, but with planning you could've downgraded the Major Instability and got the Scar you wanted before additional unentangled Scars started building up.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to permanently increasing the Magnitude of a preexisting Scar, it can only be done by choosing to keep a Magnitude increase provided by a Medium or Major Instability in the last five boxes.<br /> <br /> Am I getting that right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T16:22:22-08:00","id":1368816,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T20:46:43-08:00","id":1368849,"title":"","content":"@Tessie: You seem to understand the mechanic, now, but to give you some idea of how it's intended to feel in play, Instability is meant to convey one of two things:<br /> <br /> 1) A temporary spiritual injury that makes the Divergence a greater burden until that harm can be healed by means of Touchstones. Taking on Instability makes Scars more difficult to resist (minor), worsens existing Scars (medium), and can even cause new Scars to manifest (major). These problems ought to send most Broken into a scramble to pursue Touchstones so that the damage doesn't worsen and the injuries can actually heal, bringing back some degree of equilibrium to the Deviant's existence. Its mechanics resemble those of Health, measuring proximity to death, so it isn't surprising that in this aspect it feels closest to ticking off boxes on one's Health track.<br /> <br /> 2) A spiritual infection that, if left to fester, causes further, permanent loss of the Remade's humanity. In this aspect, taking on a new Scar, mechanically, heals a medium Instability or downgrades a major Instability, but in a narrative sense, it doesn't really feel like healing. It is more akin to cutting off an arm to rid the body of gangrene that would otherwise become deadly. It turns back the countdown to death due to Instability, but at the expense of taking a real, tangible, and <i>permanent</i> step deeper into Divergence. Most of the time, downgrading a major Instability to medium isn't a net benefit in itself (you're exchanging one extra Scar for another extra Scar and +1 Magnitude to a Scar). Similarly, medium Instability worsens an existing Scar in a way that could become irreversible (but without the benefit of healing Instability). Choosing to accept a permanent increase in the Magnitude of a Scar or the number of Scars you have is the voluntary dramatic failure of the Instability system. It is a narrative complication that drives the Broken's character development.<br /> <br /> #1 is Instability as a limited resource that the Deviant must carefully manage. #2 is Instability as historical record of the Remade's gradual slide further and further from their former humanity.<br /> <br /> To borrow an example of this from media, take the character of Rogue from the X-Men. Whenever she touches someone for more than a couple seconds, she experiences their memories, which kind of causes her to freak out for the rest of the scene (or that's how it was portrayed in the 90s cartoon), but she eventually recovers (#1 above). But we learn from her history that if she touches someone until she kills them, it leaves permanent psychic scars and layers of guilt she can never live down (#2 above).<br /> <br /> Of course, we can't forget that Instability is also crucial to the game's character progression. Unless you suffer Instability, you can't buy more Variations or improve your existing Variations. Variations must entangle Scars, and Scars worsen or multiply as a direct function of suffering significant Instability. This is not the typical model for RPGs, which usually assume that Experiences only make a character more powerful and effective - that which does not kill a character makes them stronger. But this is Deviant, so that which does not kill you simultaneously makes you stronger and weaker, more powerful and effective but also more vulnerable and generally f***ed up.<br /> <br /> If you want to spend XP on Variations, as a player, you're going to have to find ways to suffer Instability - to let that per-story minor Instability roll over into medium so that a worsened Scar can entangle an additional Variation or support higher-Magnitude versions of the Variations already entangled with it. Or to embrace bad things happening to your character often enough to earn the medium/major Instability you can convert into a new Scar of whatever Magnitude you need it to be to support whatever Variation you have your eye on. Instability is <i>almost</i> another kind of Experiences without which you cannot purchase or improve Variations. Instability is such a key part of the Deviant experience, but it's always a little bit of a drag to let bad things happen to your character and his pet NPCs, so the option to convert those &quot;Bad Points&quot; into cool new powers is the carrot the game offers to those willing to take those narrative complications in stride.<br /> <br /> That said, exactly when you might take on a major Instability in one of those last five Stability boxes isn't always easy to predict, so if you're expecting to go for a #2 path instead of a #1 path (and so probably want to be able to choose exactly which Scar you get), you should keep enough XP on-hand to buy a Variation the instant you develop a new Scar. Otherwise, you will only ever get new Persistent Scars, since you can't have an unentangled Controlled or Involuntary Scar.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope you have a great Deviant game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T02:21:48-08:00","id":1368875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368849#post1368849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the time, downgrading a major Instability to medium isn't a net benefit in itself (you're exchanging one extra Scar for another extra Scar and +1 Magnitude to a Scar).</div> </div> </div> </div>The preview states that both Medium and Major Instability in the last five boxes increases a preexisting Scar. Taking a new Scar in order to downgrade a Major Instability should only result in replacing the temporary Scar with a new, permanent Scar (which may have to be at a higher Magnitude if you've received additional unentangled Scars since). Maybe you could also move your temporary Scar increase? My gut feeling is no since it's still the same Instability, just downgraded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368849#post1368849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, exactly when you might take on a major Instability in one of those last five Stability boxes isn't always easy to predict, so if you're expecting to go for a #2 path instead of a #1 path (and so probably want to be able to choose exactly which Scar you get), you should keep enough XP on-hand to buy a Variation the instant you develop a new Scar. Otherwise, you will only ever get new Persistent Scars, since you can't have an unentangled Controlled or Involuntary Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I think the first method is superior almost always. Since downgrading a Major Instability to gain a Scar is disconnected from the Scar granted by Major Instability (if any; you could have it before the last five boxes, or instead heal a Minor or Medium Instability) you get to choose freely what Scar to get and can time it with when you have enough XP laying around (and might not even have to if the ST allows XP debt) in order to gain a Controlled or Involuntary Scar. It puts more agency in the hands of the player in terms of how and when to develope the wanted Scar while also lessening Instability in the process.<br /> The one time it's not advantageous is if you decide to get a new permanent Scar at a specific Magnitude after you've gotten too many temporary Scars that you're no longer able to get it at the desired Magnitude. But if so you wouldn't have planned it when getting those temporary Scars and is unlikely to have the right temporary Scar on hand anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368849#post1368849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I hope you have a great Deviant game!</div> </div> </div> </div>It took a few months to create the characters as well as clear up the schedule from our almost biweekly Vampire game, but the first session was a blast. The only problem is how much of a pain it can be to learn the new system for Variations and Scars, and manage to puzzle together your character the way that you want it within the given restrictions, but that's the price for a so modular systems where you're trying to balance powers and drawbacks so that both are fun and neither overpowered. We're currently reworking the characters one more time, and one of the things that gets in the way right now is that Scars can't exceed a total of five dots, meaning I can't choose a 4 dot Persistent Scar to go with Indelible Mark on my 3 dot Involuntary Stimulus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:42:31-08:00","id":1368913,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, while you're here: what is the intended benefit of the Fight option of the <i>Fight, Flight or Freeze</i> Merit? The Insane tilt seems like it mostly fucks you up, given how it tanks your Initiative and keeps you from spending Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:44:00-08:00","id":1369077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1368913#post1368913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1094\" data-vbnamecard=\"1094\">Eric Zawadzki</a>, while you're here: what is the intended benefit of the Fight option of the <i>Fight, Flight or Freeze</i> Merit? The Insane tilt seems like it mostly fucks you up, given how it tanks your Initiative and keeps you from spending Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>It got a bit of a modification post-Kickstarter. It also increases the damage inflicted by your Brawl and Weaponry attacks by one, now (in addition to Insane's +1 to attacks). All three benefits for the Merit come with significant drawbacks, but you're right to observe that Insane, by itself, doesn't balance out its bad with just the +1 attack bonus it grants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T16:04:38-08:00","id":1372197,"title":"","content":"Checking to see if I can recommend to others: do people who missed the Kickstarter but preorder on Backerkit gain access to the preview manuscript? Previous Backerkits seem to have had an option for this, but I don't see one on the Deviant Backerkit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T18:24:51-07:00","id":1378893,"title":"","content":"Welp, with current events as it is, at least I have time to get through my backlog. Including getting through the KS draft...<br /> <br /> *pages and pages later*<br /> <br /> <i>Holy hell why is there so many Variations??? </i>I haven't felt this overwhelmed by #AllThePowers since first going through V20's Disciplines!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T18:48:14-07:00","id":1378899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1378893#post1378893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, with current events as it is, at least I have time to get through my backlog. Including getting through the KS draft...<br /> <br /> *pages and pages later*<br /> <br /> <i>Holy hell why is there so many Variations??? </i>I haven't felt this overwhelmed by #AllThePowers since first going through V20's Disciplines!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are twenty-seven Universal Variations, not counting things like Superhuman or Immunity more than once, and there's five lists of five core Clade Variations. I know this because at one point I memorized them.*<br /> <br /> The core Deviant template is incredibly sparse to the point of lacking or merging basic elements of a Baseline character, needing as it does to represent a wide variety of fucked-up occult mutants through the modular systems of Scars and Variations, which themselves double as sources for Conspiracy Icons, Manticores, and other secondary use-cases. The incredible powers you develop that the conspiracies are after you for are substantially more than a cool bonus aspect of monsterhood compared to e.g. Disciplines for vampirism or Gifts for lycanthropy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Ironically, the one I most consistently forgot was Memory Thief. Evidently there are things the Electric Fish doesn't want me to know.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:45:00-07:00","id":1379062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1378899#post1378899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core Deviant template is incredibly sparse to the point of lacking or merging basic elements of a Baseline character, needing as it does to represent a wide variety of fucked-up occult mutants through the modular systems of Scars and Variations, which themselves double as sources for Conspiracy Icons, Manticores, and other secondary use-cases. The incredible powers you develop that the conspiracies are after you for are substantially more than a cool bonus aspect of monsterhood compared to e.g. Disciplines for vampirism or Gifts for lycanthropy.[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. The Remade are, in a very real way, not a type of monster, but ten thousand independent types of monster tied together by their reaction to transformation. Their Variations and Scars define their unique transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:37:01-07:00","id":1379077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1378899#post1378899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core Deviant template is incredibly sparse to the point of lacking or merging basic elements of a Baseline character, needing as it does to represent a wide variety of fucked-up occult mutants through the modular systems of Scars and Variations, which themselves double as sources for Conspiracy Icons, Manticores, and other secondary use-cases. The incredible powers you develop that the conspiracies are after you for are substantially more than a cool bonus aspect of monsterhood compared to e.g. Disciplines for vampirism or Gifts for lycanthropy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1379062#post1379062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true. The Remade are, in a very real way, not a type of monster, but ten thousand independent types of monster tied together by their reaction to transformation. Their Variations and Scars define their unique transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Hell, the complexity offered in a single Variation, it occurred to me it's very possible to build a Deviant character concept around just one Variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T23:26:47-07:00","id":1380037,"title":"","content":"I have Literally done this, made a giant based deviant, with ties to spirits with a storm and sky theme and powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:57:14-07:00","id":1380308,"title":"","content":"So if you just wanted a one dot overt relentless gigantic variation would you not take a secondary scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:05:03-07:00","id":1383484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1338786#post1338786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, I just found a flaw:<br /> <br /> For Magnitude 3 and up Deviants, there is no question of &quot;what genre of boss music do your enemies hear when you are nearby?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Invasive - Industrial metal with steam calliope and steel drums.<br /> Cephalist - New Age synth music.<br /> Chimerics - Baroque music on glass harmonica accompanied by two musical saws and a dulcimer.<br /> Mutant - Drums, lots and lots of drums.<br /> Coactives - Throat singing accompanied by rattles.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:54:59-07:00","id":1383618,"title":"","content":"A thought occurred to me recently: Is it possible for a Deviant's Origin to change if the character's understanding of their Divergence evolves over the course of play?<br /> <br /> For example, say a hiker comes across a spring in the middle of the woods and decides to take a dip to cool off, except for whatever reason the water turns them into a monster. This is completely unexpected, and so the character starts as a Pathological. Later on, the Deviant discovers that several key events in their life had been subtly manipulated by a Conspiracy aiming to drive the character down the path that they ended up taking; could the player then switch their Origin to Epimorph?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:27:11-07:00","id":1383622,"title":"","content":"It really doesn't matter outside of character creation, unless you mean to start switching around Scar/Variation dots based on the character's knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:46:00-07:00","id":1383626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1383618#post1383618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought occurred to me recently: Is it possible for a Deviant's Origin to change if the character's understanding of their Divergence evolves over the course of play?<br /> <br /> For example, say a hiker comes across a spring in the middle of the woods and decides to take a dip to cool off, except for whatever reason the water turns them into a monster. This is completely unexpected, and so the character starts as a Pathological. Later on, the Deviant discovers that several key events in their life had been subtly manipulated by a Conspiracy aiming to drive the character down the path that they ended up taking; could the player then switch their Origin to Epimorph?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think it works that way. It's how your character felt concerning the divergence that matters, not how a conspiracy tried to initiate it , and Origins really only affect your starting stuff <br /> <br /> Think of it like this. A conspiracy kidnaps a victim to use for a Rite (that will turn them into a Deviant). What they don't know is that victim has been wanting to ascend beyond the constraints of humanity and is secretly excited for what will happen. He would therefore be autotourgic, no Exomorphic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T01:45:24-07:00","id":1387208,"title":"","content":"I've confused myself a WHOLE lot reading it, but what's the idea about Scar deviations and the plus/minus one magnitude? Like say for the Dependacy Scar, why would I take the Rare deviation when I can take the common deviation, which increases my magnitude? It seems entirely counterintuitive to choose + Scar deviations as all they do is increase your effective magnitude AND hinder your character further","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:21:27-07:00","id":1387219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1387208#post1387208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've confused myself a WHOLE lot reading it, but what's the idea about Scar deviations and the plus/minus one magnitude? Like say for the Dependacy Scar, why would I take the Rare deviation when I can take the common deviation, which increases my magnitude? It seems entirely counterintuitive to choose + Scar deviations as all they do is increase your effective magnitude AND hinder your character further</div> </div> </div> </div> Negative Deviations decrease your total Magnitude, but the effects of the Scar remain at the higher level. In return, the Scar becomes less punishing in some other way.<br /> <br /> Positive Deviations instead allow you to increase the Magnitude of a Scar, so that you can potentially entangle more/stronger Variations, without worsening the effect of the Scar. Instead, you take some other, lesser drawback.<br /> <br /> For example: Dependency 3 with the Common (-1) Deviation leaves you with a two-dot Scar with the effects of a three-dot, but the substance you require is common enough that you're unlikely to run out; you can just buy it at the local grocery store, or even find it lying about. Conversely, Dependency 3 with Rare (+1) becomes a four-dot Scar that is only as severe as a 3-dot one, but you are much more likely to run out due to your dependency's rarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T05:35:25-07:00","id":1387254,"title":"","content":"MG is right. Deviations are a means of further customizing the Scar, providing alternate ways in which it can be eased or worsened. Power Failure's Rare and Common Deviations allow you to represent either a rare hazardous mineral which can wholly block out your powers (Power Failure 4 with Rare -1) or the temporary ebbing away of your powers while distracted by anger (Power Failure 2 with Common +1) at the same net Magnitude 3 rating.<br /> <br /> As for why you'd want higher Magnitude, more crippling Scars? Check out what Variations do at Magnitude 4-5. Rapid Healing 5 makes you <i>completely impossible to directly kill by any means</i> \u2013 and is impossible to develop without a Magnitude 5 Scar (or at least Magnitude 4 plus your one unscarred Variation dot from chargen). Deviants are empowered and supercharged in direct proportion to how messed up and ruined they are.<br /> <br /> Plus, sometimes awful Scars are cool. Sometimes you want to be a hideous monster man who has to hide his face from the world. A deviant's Scars are as much a part of developing how cool their concept and story are as their Variations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T17:59:58-07:00","id":1387374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1387219#post1387219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Positive Deviations instead allow you to increase the Magnitude of a Scar, so that you can potentially entangle more/stronger Variations, without worsening the effect of the Scar. Instead, you take some other, lesser drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1387254#post1387254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why you'd want higher Magnitude, more crippling Scars? Check out what Variations do at Magnitude 4-5. Rapid Healing 5 makes you <i>completely impossible to directly kill by any means</i> \u2013 and is impossible to develop without a Magnitude 5 Scar (or at least Magnitude 4 plus your one unscarred Variation dot from chargen). Deviants are empowered and supercharged in direct proportion to how messed up and ruined they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point: from the data we have available, the design space that Involuntary Scars live in relies heavily on Deviations for long-term viability; the price you pay for not having to pay a price to activate your powers or constantly suffer a drawback from their availability is that neither of the core Involuntary Scars has a core Magnitude that goes above 3 on its own, and both of them make their entire Variation package Overt as soon as it goes over Magnitude 1. Deviations let you lighten that load a bit.<br /> <br /> This is one of the ways that being a Coactive looks great on paper: your Adaptations are nearly a same as Cephalists get without double-dipping into the same resource, and your Scars thematically trend toward the least inherently troublesome baseline effects, but damage is damage and Instability will find a way to escalate your problems very quickly if you don't stay on top of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T18:20:36-07:00","id":1387383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1387219#post1387219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Negative Deviations decrease your total Magnitude, but the effects of the Scar remain at the higher level. In return, the Scar becomes less punishing in some other way.<br /> <br /> Positive Deviations instead allow you to increase the Magnitude of a Scar, so that you can potentially entangle more/stronger Variations, without worsening the effect of the Scar. Instead, you take some other, lesser drawback.<br /> <br /> For example: Dependency 3 with the Common (-1) Deviation leaves you with a two-dot Scar with the effects of a three-dot, but the substance you require is common enough that you're unlikely to run out; you can just buy it at the local grocery store, or even find it lying about. Conversely, Dependency 3 with Rare (+1) becomes a four-dot Scar that is only as severe as a 3-dot one, but you are much more likely to run out due to your dependency's rarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I understand now. Thank you and everyone else that elaborated, I'm sorry I had such a late response.<br /> <br /> Anyway, cant wait for the game, looking forward to it more than I did Hunter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T19:32:44-07:00","id":1413317,"title":"","content":"A thing for when errata-gathering time rolls around:<br /> <br /> Maintenance is, thematically and descriptively, a pretty dope Scar, but as a Persistent Scar it should probably either have the Toggled keyword or include some guidance for how the effects of failed or jury-rigged maintenance kick in on Perpetual Variations like Rapid Healing or Sensor Array or Superhuman, particularly given that it shows up in the examples for multiple Perpetual Variations in the KS draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T19:54:26-07:00","id":1413318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1413317#post1413317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing for when errata-gathering time rolls around:<br /> <br /> Maintenance is, thematically and descriptively, a pretty dope Scar, but as a Persistent Scar it should probably either have the Toggled keyword or include some guidance for how the effects of failed or jury-rigged maintenance kick in on Perpetual Variations like Rapid Healing or Sensor Array or Superhuman, particularly given that it shows up in the examples for multiple Perpetual Variations in the KS draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current draft shows it with the Toggled-Only keyword, so at some point it must have come to my attention how wonky that would get. However, I see it's still being used as an example for Sensor Array, which is Perpetual, so I'll add it to my list of things to fix during a late pass. Thanks for bringing it to my attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T18:50:07-08:00","id":1425828,"title":"","content":"*sees latest MMN*<br /> <br /> Oh hullo...Deviant's out of Layout and off to Proofing!...but whose text is still in post-editing development? Huh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T20:24:55-08:00","id":1425842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1425828#post1425828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sees latest MMN*<br /> <br /> Oh hullo...Deviant's out of Layout and off to Proofing!...but whose text is still in post-editing development? Huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in proofing. It just didn't get deleted from the post-editing development list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T20:44:14-08:00","id":1425848,"title":"","content":"Can't\u2026 wait\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T08:59:16-08:00","id":1431004,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand it's out (to backers)!<br /> <br /> As someone who was critical of the previews, I'm curious to see the final (or well, almost final) product!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 01-04-2021, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T09:46:06-08:00","id":1431013,"title":"","content":"Got it! Now I just need to find some time to read it. Darn work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T13:59:24-08:00","id":1431067,"title":"","content":"And Nevermind it was with my old email account that I have switched over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 01-04-2021, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T02:07:11-08:00","id":1431546,"title":"","content":"An approximate and non-exhaustive summary of some of the changes from the KS draft:<br /> <br /> Adaptations, Stability, Merits, Basics<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Most of the Adaptations have been tweaked to some degree, notably Untamed and Redundancy (which have changed the tenor of their effects to more all-or-nothing fare); Focus and Consume now specifically allow you to space out adding extra Magnitude at cost across the scene.<br /> <br /> If you're the direct cause of a Loyalty Touchstone's death or destruction, the accompanying Instability is major rather than medium.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acting in support of a Loyalty Touchstone&quot; is now more broadly defined and can include spending a scene deepening your relationship with it for the purposes of healing Instability.<br /> <br /> There are rules for drowning/suffocation/holding your breath, and a new one-dot Physical Merit to make it easier to manage, which adds some stuff for Aquatic and certain varieties of Native Environment to play with.<br /> <br /> Armed &amp; Extremely Dangerous and Prized Experiment have shed most of their prerequisites and picked up more mechanical utility, as promised.<br /> <br /> Stabilizer now only goes to three dots, which is probably the way to go for not completely trivializing low Stability.<br /> <br /> Fight, Flight, Freeze has been renamed &quot;Human Prey&quot;; the &quot;Fight&quot; response now also increases your Strength.<br /> <br /> All Tilts now have their effects delineated as moderate or severe, which affects some mechanical tagging.<br /> <br /> Discrete Variations now cannot have their Magnitude temporarily adjusted, barring specific exceptions (such as Carapace and Lash), which predetermine higher- Magnitude effects at the time of purchase; effects that would decrease a Discrete Variation's Magnitude instead shut it down after a number of failed Scar Resistance rolls.<br /> <br /> Nested secondary Scars are now explicitly forbidden.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Universal Variations<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The number of Variations with scaling other than 1-5 has decreased; there are now a lot more Variations with an &quot;Aura&quot; Deviation (the basics of the mechanic are now covered in the section on Directed Variations), and many Variations with formerly limited Magnitude now have a &quot;Defensive&quot; Deviation like Out of Phase and Translocation did.<br /> <br /> Enhanced Speed has split the old Fleetness option into a Speed-based effect and a Defense-based effect, giving it three possible Magnitude 3 effects to parcel out over the top half of its Magnitude.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Recollection&quot; Deviation of Face Thief now specifically limits the features you can duplicate to those you can reference from the record, but also allows you to make a disguise of a non-specific person with your choice of features.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Velocity&quot; effect of high-Magnitude Flight has gotten dramatically faster.<br /> <br /> Healing Touch has been renamed Healer, is a Directed Variation, and can specifically be used on yourself unless it has the Aura Deviation now available to it. <br /> <br /> Holographic Projection has lost the Deviation that expands the size of your holograms, but solid holograms can now be used as a moderately effective Retainer with no expertise under your direction.<br /> <br /> Hyper-Competence is now Tiered; the Magnitude 2 bonus has been halved; it has a mutually-exclusive +1 and +2 Deviation that increase the number of Skills a single instance of the Variation applies to.<br /> <br /> Immunity now has a Deviation that makes it Toggled in exchange for extending its effects to a 10-yard radius around the character.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Channel&quot; option for Lash is now subject to the same rules of dealing damage as applying Tilts with a Cutting/Bruising/Gentle Lash, and Channeled Variations entangled with a Controlled Scar explicitly still exact their cost. A &quot;Conjured&quot; Lash now adds the Variation's Magnitude to its dicepool. There is now a &quot;Quick&quot; option that makes activating/&quot;drawing&quot; Lash a reflexive action. The &quot;Circle Strike&quot; Deviation now uses the Long-Burst Autofire mechanics, limited to a one-yard range. &quot;Gunshot&quot; Cutting Lashes are now subject to the effects of ballistic armor.<br /> <br /> Miniaturization is now Tiered; its new &quot;Defensive&quot; Deviation allows the character to functionally Dodge an attack with successes equal to Scar Power.<br /> <br /> Out of Phase (and Astral Projection) now includes a note specifying that being intangible to something prevents the character from targeting it with Directed Variations, Lash, or Variations that require physical contact.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Pyrotechnics&quot; and &quot;Extinguish&quot; effect of Pyrokinesis now describe more concrete mechanical effects; Magnitude 2 now also grants minor firestarting capability, and both Magnitude 4 effects are now options at Magnitude 3 (though &quot;Ignite&quot; no longer gives fires it starts an automatic heat bonus); the Variation has an Aura Deviation that also grants functional immunity to direct harm from fire below a heat threshold determined by Scar Power.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Shared Vision&quot; of Shadows of the Past is now a free element of Magnitude 3; reaching Magnitude 5 now allows you or one of the people who projected with you to bring back an &quot;echo&quot; of something from the past (of a Size limited by Scar Power) once per story without consequence.<br /> <br /> Storm-Caller now has the type of environmental phenomena set upon acquisition unless the &quot;Universal&quot; Deviation is taken, which makes the Variation once-per-chapter and still requires all simultaneously active effects to fall under the same class type of phenomena. The Variation's range is now larger outdoors, but the &quot;Control&quot; effect is no longer available; the &quot;negate opposing environments&quot; trick is now a default aspect of the Variation at Magnitude 1; &quot;Intensity&quot; is now the sole Magnitude 4 effect. Environmental Tilts and Extreme Environment levels no longer come out of the same &quot;budget&quot;; Environmental Tilts &quot;cost&quot; more to impose if they are severe rather than moderate, and until Magnitude 3 they must be imposed over multiple turns rather than all at once.<br /> <br /> Superhuman Strength now allows a character to throw objects without respect to their Size; Superhuman Dexterity no longer specially benefits autofire attacks.<br /> <br /> Telekinesis now specifies that the character's rolls to maintain the grapple or execute available grapple moves on a character grappled with the Variation become reflexive, making a single Scar Finesse roll for all victims each turn; the &quot;Force Field&quot; effect now requires the player to determine upon its acquisition whether the shield counts as non-transparent cover to Directed Variations and other targeted supernatural powers (all-or-nothing, not selectively applied), which is a two-way barrier as it is for physical objects and attacks.<br /> <br /> Translocation's &quot;Conjuration&quot; Deviation now specifies that teleporting an item out of another character's possession may be contested.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Clade Variations<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Body Snatcher now specifies that each of its effects involves a separate Scar Finesse roll and includes notes for how Variations and Scars interact with its use; neither of the original Magnitude 5 effects is available (Magnitude 5 now provides access to both Magnitude 4 effects), and &quot;Puppet Possession&quot; now upgrades the minor Instability incurred by riding a character's senses when they die to a medium Instability.<br /> <br /> Creeping Dread 1 now triggers an immediate penalized breaking point roll, or inflicts the Shaken Condition on supernatural targets.<br /> <br /> Telepathy 2 now allows characters to spend Willpower to maintain a telepathic connection with a willing target from chapter to chapter (as Face Thief or the &quot;Body Swap&quot; effect of Body Snatcher); the &quot;Recontact&quot; Magnitude 3 effect does not require a roll for a willing target, and the penalty for rolling to contact an unwilling target is -4; the &quot;Hivemind&quot; Magnitude 4 effect can now have its limit overcome by Adaptations; the &quot;Forceful&quot; Magnitude 4 effect now allows the character to force their memories on the target, causing them to regain Willpower, suffer one of the standard Integrity breaking point Conditions, grant a relevant version of the Informed Condition, or (depending on the target's supernatural quality) damage the target's [Integrity/Stability/Willpower].<br /> <br /> Hybrid Form has been renamed Monstrous Transformation; the secondary Variations it grants specifically do not count against out-of-Clade restrictions and all use the same Mental/Physical/Social category as Monstrous Transformation; Monstrous Transformation is a specific exception to Sacred Flesh's new restriction of &quot;no secondary Variation with secondary Variations.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pheromones now has a keyword for what Persistent forms of it are (it's Perpetual).<br /> <br /> Predator's Cunning now has two Magnitude 1 options, the first of which is the original (now named &quot;Elusive&quot;) and the second of which is effectively a scaled version of most of the original Magnitude 2 effect (now named &quot;Vigilant&quot;). The &quot;Uncanny&quot; Magnitude 3 effect now also causes the character to no longer suffer reduced Defense from multiple attackers. The Variation also now has a Magnitude 5 ability best summed up as &quot;unless you are successfully ambushed, you effectively ambush everyone else in the first turn of combat who does not use a pre-empting power and beat you in a Clash of Wills.&quot;<br /> <br /> Blessing is now a Directed Variation; all of its original effects have been reduced in Magnitude and it has an Aura Deviation that allows the character to use its effects on themself.<br /> <br /> Fate's Agent now works on the same model as Immunity 3 or Otherworldly Connection, with each instance corresponding to a different type of supernatural being; the Magnitude 5 effect is no longer available, but there is a &quot;Universal&quot; Deviation that lets it apply to the abilities of all supernatural creatures in exchange for making each effect a once-per-scene ability. The &quot;Dispel&quot; effect only neutralizes large area effects in a 10-yard radius.<br /> <br /> Onomantic Influence has been renamed Psychic-Onomastics; the ability to permanently erase a true name has been removed in place of the ability to erase or change a true name and greater mechanical consequence for namelessness.<br /> <br /> Precognition 1 now has the effect formerly assigned to Blessing 1. The Magnitude 2 effect is now Directed rather than touch-based.<br /> <br /> Hidden Compartments has changed its &quot;Extra Capacity&quot; Deviation to increase the Size cap to 1 + [half Scar Power (rounded up)] and removed the &quot;High Capacity&quot; Deviation; its new &quot;Varied Inventory&quot; Deviation increases the frequency with which each Magnitude's effects can be used by one step.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Battery&quot; Deviation of Integrate Technology now generates electrical current capable of dealing damage proportionate to Scar Power and does not have a limited number of sockets.<br /> <br /> Omnicompetence has replaced its original Magnitude 5 effect with constant access to the &quot;Jack of All&quot; Magnitude 2 ability and access to the &quot;Journeyman&quot; Magnitude 2 ability as a once-per-scene power, in addition to its duplication of the Magnitude 4 effects.<br /> <br /> Deadly Ichor now includes a note that each attacker can only trigger one counterattack per turn. The &quot;Aura&quot; Deviation has been renamed &quot;Proximal,&quot; presumably to avoid confusion.<br /> <br /> Rapid Healing 1 now carries over to all subsequent Magnitudes.<br /> <br /> Sacred Flesh cannot be used to grant any version of Sacred Flesh or any other Variation that grants a secondary Variation (Monstrous Transformation is an explicit exception). Variations granted by Sacred Flesh are the same Mental/Physical/Social type as Sacred Flesh and specifically do not count against out-of-Clade restrictions; secondary Variations that must be Persistent and Perpetual (e.g. Rapid Healing and some forms of Anomalous Biology) last until the end of the chapter instead of the end of the scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Controlled and Involuntary Scars<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As with Variations, a lot fewer Scars have weird aberrant scaling.<br /> <br /> Persistent Drawback now directly addresses the notion of taking secondary Scars that would otherwise be long-term issues \u2014 lingering effects stick around until they're used up normally, and Scars that apply their effects once per chapter apply them each time the entangled Variation's activated.<br /> <br /> Preparation now splits between &quot;this is an extended action&quot; and &quot;this takes time&quot; before converging at Magnitude 5; one of the Magnitude 4 effects outright prevents the Variation from being activated in the context of an action scene.<br /> <br /> Unstable Variation is now fully scaled and applies its cost with every activation; at Magnitude 2+, Scar Resistance rolls are penalized for the rest of the scene and another Scar (Storyteller's choice) temporarily worsens in Magnitude.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Uncontrollable&quot; Deviation of Involuntary Stimulus is now a +1 Deviation.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Persistent Scars A-H<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Alternate Persona 2 now lasts for minutes (rather than until the end of the scene) and penalizes subsequent Scar Resistance rolls for each successful resistance within the chapter; Magnitude 3 makes transformations more common and longer-lasting and applies the same rolls for resisting takeover to rolls to temporarily reassert control while the alternate persona is active once per scene. There are more Deviations available; &quot;Bestial&quot; is now a single +1 Deviation, and &quot;Forgetful Persona&quot; and &quot;Blackouts&quot; now have counterpart Deviations mutually exclusive with them called &quot;Aware Persona&quot; and &quot;Perfect Recall&quot; that give the relevant personality clear awareness of their counterpart's actions; &quot;Cross-Purposes&quot; now simply gives the persona different Touchstones rather than reshuffling the character's normal ones, and its mutually exclusive counterpart &quot;Partner&quot; instead prevents the persona from having a different Aspiration from the character; &quot;Superior Persona&quot; and &quot;Inferior Persona&quot; are mutually exclusive counterparts that lock the character off from using the entangled Variation or lock the persona off from using Variations it's not entangled with; &quot;Invoked&quot; allows you to voluntarily yield control to the persona.<br /> <br /> There is a new Persistent Mental Scar called Bestial Mind, which inflicts various Conditions and Tilts on the character and hampers their ability to Build Equipment, use Mental Skills, or use sophisticated tools.<br /> <br /> Fragility and Hemophilia no longer have Deviations that reduce the character's number of Health boxes.<br /> <br /> Genetic Disorder 5 now prompts a Scar Resistance roll once per chapter (rather than once per day) and inflicts lethal damage or a minor Instability (player's choice each time, rather than always lethal damage), but supernatural powers cannot outright heal the damage.<br /> <br /> Glitch no longer references hallucinatory effects or incorporating mental or emotional Conditions; the Magnitude 2 effect exempts Willpower expenditures that are Willpower costs for supernatural powers from the triggers for the Scar; the Magnitude 3 effect maintains this specified application and consistently inflicts the Distracted Condition (rather than the Insane Tilt in action scenes); the Magnitude 4 effect adds Willpower costs back into consideration for the Magnitude 2 effect; Magnitude 5 makes the Distracted Condition last until the character regains all their Willpower.<br /> <br /> There is a new Persistent Mental/Social Scar called Hallucinations, which starts from imposing the Distracted Condition, proceeds to introducing false persons or objects into a scene that the character needs external observation to dismiss, and goes on to elaborate imaginary scenes and/or narrowing the list of people who can bring them back to reality to just their Loyalty Touchstones.<br /> <br /> Hemophilia now explicitly exempts itself from the sources of damage that cause a character with it to start bleeding out at Magnitude 3+.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Persistent Scars M-P<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Maintenance has, appropriately enough, been overhauled; it's now Repeatable and Toggled-Only, no longer calls the Build Equipment rules, and starts its mechanical effects at the end of any scene in which an entangled Variation was used rather than at the end of the story; maintenance takes time based on Scar Resistance (minutes at first), and using an entangled Variation without maintenance prompts a Scar Resistance roll (penalized for each entangled Variation activated since the last maintenance) to see if it shuts down until it's repaired. Further Magnitude adds limitations like needing someone else to be the primary actor in the maintenance roll, upgrading the maintenance time from minutes to hours, or adding a [damage/Willpower/Instability] cost to those Scar Resistance rolls (price determined when the character develops the Scar).<br /> <br /> Misfortune is no longer a purely Social Scar and no longer tracks a pool of Misfortune; instead, minor misfortune can strike once per chapter (modifying dicepools against the character's favor mitigated by Scar Resistance), with higher Magnitude increasing that to once per scene and/or introducing serious strokes of bad luck once per chapter (downgrading success to failure or failure to dramatic failure).<br /> <br /> Missing Limb now has full 1-5 scaling; the new Magnitude 2 effect gives one of two sub-Tilt-level effects that are replaced by the Magnitude 3-5 effects, which are the original Magnitude 2-4 effects.<br /> <br /> Murderous Urge 2 now specifies that Loyalty Touchstones and cohort members don't usually prompt the roll to avoid escalation.<br /> <br /> Native Environment now has a -1 Deviation that allows the character to tolerate Extreme Environments and Environmental Tilts that are a product of their native environment commensurate with the hazards being out of it apply; the original Magnitude 1 and 2 effects have effectively been merged into the Magnitude 2 effect.<br /> <br /> Paranoia 4 now includes members of the character's cohort along with their Loyalty Touchstones on the list of people they don't find it harder to trust, and having the Spooked Condition from a secret roll allows the Storyteller to reduce one of the affected rolls to a chance dice and prevents the character from forging new Loyalty Touchstones or affirming Wavering ones. Paranoia 5 now prevents the character from switching a Conviction Touchstone to a Loyalty Touchstone without Wavering first (though not the other way around).<br /> <br /> Phobia now has full 1-5 scaling; the new Magnitude 3 effect removes the ability to spend Willpower to suppress the fear and changes the Scar Resistance roll dynamic from &quot;each failed roll gives a bonus&quot; to &quot;each successful roll gives a penalty.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Persistent Scars S-T<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sensory Deprivation is now a single contiguous Scar instead of a loosely-linked Repeatable ladder of single-rating Scars with the same name; options are more or less sorted in the order that they were in the original list, with partial and complete deafness and blindness further spacing out; there is no &quot;lose your sense of touch&quot; option, and at Magnitude 5 the character either can't see and can't hear, can't see, smell, or taste, or can't hear, smell, or taste and has bad eyes.<br /> <br /> Silence now has a Magnitude 4 effect that removes writing and sign language as work-arounds for the lack of speech and further penalizes attempts to use body language to communicate.<br /> <br /> Sluggish Metabolism now has full 1-5 scaling; Magnitude 3 now provides a set of options that lock out supernatural healing, upgrade damage for the purposes of healing, and prevent more severe damage from healing without long-term care; higher Magnitudes add more choices from the list.<br /> <br /> Suppression is now fully scaled and no longer applies a ceiling to the affected Attribute; Magnitude 2+ prevents the character from spending Willpower on rolls or resistances with the Attribute and removes 10-Again from relevant rolls.<br /> <br /> Thin Skin is now fully scaled and has turned its original effect into a pair of mutually exclusive Deviations; the Scar now serves the same role as the missing Deviations for Fragile and Hemophilia, with each Magnitude above 1 subtracting two Health boxes from the character's total.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Standard Deviations<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Disfiguring Scar is now limited to one Scar, though its effect may be applied to any other Subtle Scars or Variations and there is a further +1 available if the character makes all of their Subtle Scars and Deviations Overt, much as Identifier works.<br /> <br /> Relentless Variation is a Deviation, largely as previewed in this thread before; Suppressible Variation, likewise; Unruly Variation, ditto.<br /> <br /> There is a new Standard Deviation called Target Restriction, which adds one or two Magnitude to the attached Scar based on how narrowly its entangled Variations can be used.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T03:48:49-08:00","id":1431553,"title":"","content":"Thanks Satchel! As I didn't read the previews in detail, would you mind sharing how you feel about the changes? Have they significantly altered the game in some areas? Are you happy with the new versions overall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T07:56:53-08:00","id":1431569,"title":"","content":"The Anomalous Biology Variation for Mutants has changed slightly in how Bloodless works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why do Deviants still have the once-per-turn WP expenditure limit? That rule was changed to once-per-action ages ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T08:13:20-08:00","id":1431574,"title":"","content":"Good hustle, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. Two things you missed, though: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Willpower extension effect of Body Snatcher has been moved down to Magnitude 2, affecting both lines instead of just Body Swap, and</li> <li>Suppression 3+ explicitly doesn't affect Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance.</li> </ol><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431569#post1431569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Deviants still have the once-per-turn WP expenditure limit? That rule was changed to once-per-action ages ago.</div> </div> </div> </div> I checked my books, and it seems like the ones that list out the Willpower rules like Deviant does use the &quot;per turn&quot; language, while books describing Willpower in natural language say &quot;per action.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-09-2021, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T08:32:23-08:00","id":1431575,"title":"","content":"Well, Satchel <i>did</i> say that the list was not exhaustive. But thanks for adding to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T11:25:36-08:00","id":1431593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431575#post1431575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Satchel <i>did</i> say that the list was not exhaustive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, five hours in the middle of the night does not completeness foster.<br /> <br /> Some others:<br /> <br /> General<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Dauntless Merit no longer exists; the Beaten Down Tilt now specifically applies to Baselines.<br /> <br /> There is now a sidebar for &quot;Goon Combat,&quot; for the sake of modeling large numbers of generic foes and smaller numbers of key opponents without condensing the entire thing to Down and Dirty Combat. They act on the same Initiative, subtract effective headcount on the same rationale as Beaten Down, and add dice to their collective actions based on how many of them act and how well the action fits their role.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Antagonists (Conspiracies and Devoted)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The &quot;Harmonious Community Interaction&quot; example Icon now grants 8-Again to conspiracy members using specific Skills, rather than to the conspiracy making relevant Finesse rolls.<br /> <br /> Completed Projects now execute at the <i>end</i> of the next chapter and are subject to disruption by the cohort in the intervening period.<br /> <br /> Crisis points can no longer remove a point of Effort from an active Project.<br /> <br /> The bonus to conspiracy actions for being led by a Linchpin has decreased from +2 to +1, increasing to +2 if the Linchpin is Devoted.<br /> <br /> Identifying Scars and Variations no longer namedrops Unseen Sense and Specialized Sense in the bonus for &quot;exotic sensory equipment or [occult] senses,&quot; which now lists a range from +2 to +3 rather than +1 to +3. The &quot;Identify Subtle Variation or Scar&quot; action can now explicitly be used to gather more information on an identified Overt Scar or Variation.<br /> <br /> Madeline &quot;The Wall&quot; Hager now has Demolisher 1 (replacing Dauntless). Tristan &quot;Echo&quot; Howe now has Defensive Combat [Brawl] (replacing Dauntless) and Marksmanship 3 (replacing Demolisher 3).</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T11:50:40-08:00","id":1431597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431593#post1431593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, five hours in the middle of the night does not completeness foster.</div> </div> </div> </div> You got all the ones I noticed/could remember and more, which is pretty damn comprehensive.<br /> <br /> Here's another I remembered: the text of the Stunned Tilt finally matches the Stun weapon property<i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T13:09:29-08:00","id":1431616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431553#post1431553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Satchel! As I didn't read the previews in detail, would you mind sharing how you feel about the changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I greatly appreciate not having to remember nearly as many scaling aberrations or consign a bunch of Scars to the domain of &quot;bad thing that you can use as fodder for major Instability,&quot; and a lot of the Variation and Adaptation adjustments have made awkward bits less so, added necessary clarity, and better smoothed the power curve for elements that were overpowered, underwhelming, or inflexible. Tremendous improvement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have they significantly altered the game in some areas? </div> </div> </div>The inability to completely negate Scar Resistance penalties with a maxed-out Stabilizer is a lot, the broadened criteria for healing Instability through Loyalty Touchstones opens up Guardian play that doesn't involve putting them in harm's way to heal, the reduced amount of Scars directly fucking with your Touchstone allocation makes certain high-Magnitude Scars less nightmarish to manage.<br /> <br /> The two Overt Merits that directly affect how the conspiracy treats you have a pretty concrete impact now, environmentally-limited Deviants now have more options available to them, and the two Clades with damage-based repeater Adaptations largely improved their special tricks.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy actions are now slightly more incentivized to be helmed by Devoted, and there's now a little more incentive to go after an active Project even if it's just completed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you happy with the new versions overall? </div> </div> </div>I'd say so, yeah, though I'm pretty easy to please on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T19:32:04-08:00","id":1431646,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity, how would a storyteller separate between the Terrible and Monstrous effects of the Conspicuous appearance Scar? I struggle to imagine how one would present them exclusively from each other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T20:24:10-08:00","id":1431647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431646#post1431646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, how would a storyteller separate between the Terrible and Monstrous effects of the Conspicuous appearance Scar? I struggle to imagine how one would present them exclusively from each other</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest line to draw would be the one implied in the first line of the Magnitude 4 description: <i>either</i> &quot;fantastical enough to make headlines&quot; (Monstrous, which builds on the &quot;weird enough to get people talking&quot; aspect of the Scar) <i>or</i> &quot;clearly part human, part something terrible&quot; (Terrible, which builds on the &quot;this may frighten or revolt others&quot; aspect of the Scar).<br /> <br /> A Monstrous Conspicuous Appearance is striking, prominent, and distinctive. A Terrible Conspicuous Appearance is <i>scary.</i> The two can overlap, obviously, being part of the same Scar, but it's relatively easy to divide &quot;obviously supernatural and therefore spooky&quot; from &quot;threatening to look at.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T20:35:55-08:00","id":1431648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431647#post1431647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest line to draw would be the one implied in the first line of the Magnitude 4 description: <i>either</i> &amp;quot;fantastical enough to make headlines&amp;quot; (Monstrous, which builds on the &amp;quot;weird enough to get people talking&amp;quot; aspect of the Scar) <i>or</i> &amp;quot;clearly part human, part something terrible&amp;quot; (Terrible, which builds on the &amp;quot;this may frighten or revolt others&amp;quot; aspect of the Scar).<br /> <br /> A Monstrous Conspicuous Appearance is striking, prominent, and distinctive. A Terrible Conspicuous Appearance is <i>scary.</i> The two can overlap, obviously, being part of the same Scar, but it's relatively easy to divide &amp;quot;obviously supernatural and therefore spooky&amp;quot; from &amp;quot;threatening to look at.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok, as an example, would you say a deviant that appeared almost wolfish, like a werewolf in Dalu form would be Monstrous while one like a draugr would be Terrible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T22:00:58-08:00","id":1431651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431648#post1431648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh ok, as an example, would you say a deviant that appeared almost wolfish, like a werewolf in Dalu form would be Monstrous while one like a draugr would be Terrible?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the draugr look is particularly scary (deathly pallor, visible fangs, bloodshot/animalistic eyes, etc) and the wolfman isn't angling toward Dalu form's &quot;this has a power specifically about frightening a group of people into giving up your prey&quot; threatening vibe, sure.<br /> <br /> Any Conspicuous Appearance at Magnitude 3+ is going to be at least a little off-putting and make it easier to sic hunters of some stripe after you, but a Terrible form is more personally frightening while a Monstrous one better accelerates the rumor mill by being a hard-to-ignore talking point. A Terrible Appearance actively hinders the character's ability to socially engage with normal people even if they've resolved the Notoriety Condition imposed by the Scar; a Monstrous Appearance instead draws outside attention even if your community doesn't think ill of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T22:19:06-08:00","id":1431652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431651#post1431651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the draugr look is particularly scary (deathly pallor, visible fangs, bloodshot/animalistic eyes, etc) and the wolfman isn't angling toward Dalu form's &amp;quot;this has a power specifically about frightening a group of people into giving up your prey&amp;quot; threatening vibe, sure.<br /> <br /> Any Conspicuous Appearance at Magnitude 3+ is going to be at least a little off-putting and make it easier to sic hunters of some stripe after you, but a Terrible form is more personally frightening while a Monstrous one better accelerates the rumor mill by being a hard-to-ignore talking point. A Terrible Appearance actively hinders the character's ability to socially engage with normal people even if they've resolved the Notoriety Condition imposed by the Scar; a Monstrous Appearance instead draws outside attention even if your community doesn't think ill of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I know it's a niche question so I really appreciate you answering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-09T22:46:20-08:00","id":1431653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431574#post1431574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppression 3+ explicitly doesn't affect Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thing we both apparently missed: Suppression now specifically has to share its Mental/Physical/Social category with the suppressed Attribute.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind, it's just been moved from the first described Magnitude to the general description of the Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-14-2021, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T05:35:38-08:00","id":1431676,"title":"","content":"So can I use Relentless on the Persistent Scar of an Indelible Mark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T10:23:41-08:00","id":1431701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1431676#post1431676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can I use Relentless on the Persistent Scar of an Indelible Mark?</div> </div> </div> </div>The effect of Relentless Variation, which is a Deviation for Persistent Scars, has the Toggled-Only Keyword, and makes the entangled Variation Perpetual (i.e. always active), can probably not be used on a secondary Scar attached through Indelible Mark, which is a Deviation for Involuntary Scars (i.e. their primary drawback is that the power activates on its own under certain circumstances) that can only apply if the total Magnitude of the primary and secondary Scars (before applying Standard Deviations like Relentless Variation) is 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> Did you have something in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:13:33-08:00","id":1431715,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, this is the version of the rules I wish I had while running my Deviant game! : P<br /> Everything is far clearer and comprehensive [the added clarification that Deviations increase Magnitude for calculations based on Magnitude in particular], and the Tilts section is just... chef's kiss. An improvement on the ks manuscript all around, imo, and probably the mechanically tightest CofD 2e book I've yet seen.<br /> <br /> But mostly, the changes to the Variations and Scars would have made my players' concepts <i>so much</i> easier to achieve. The changes to Alternate Persona would have benefited one character in particular. She had this whole deal with her identity slowly dissolving as she absorbed the identities of everyone around her, occasionally manifesting a gestalt personality with its own unique abilities. The addition of Superior Persona would have made modeling that so much easier! Instead we had to nest Alternate Persona into Power Build-Up, so that the gestalt would automatically be in control whenever the Variations were used. Entangle <i>that</i> with a 5 Magnitude Monstrous Transformation and you get a mess!<br /> Also, the changes/clarifications to the Attune effect of Telepathy would have made the core power of that same character, uh, come up a lot more. There would have been a lot less cost-benefit analysis every time she wanted to get a benefit for other minds intruding on her own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T21:23:16-08:00","id":1432162,"title":"","content":"Collating some further observations:<br /> <br /> Other Posters' Notes<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As SomethingFishy observes above, the basic effect of Telepathy 1 (Attune) no longer requires Adaptations to use multiple times in a chapter.<br /> <br /> As Tessie observed previously, Anomalous Biology (Bloodless) now works on vampire/mummy/ephemeral harm rules for weapons rather than applying a ballistic Armor rating.<br /> <br /> As MCN observed previously, the chapter-by-chapter Willpower cost of extending Body Snatcher can now be paid Magnitude 2 onward, rather than from the Magnitude 5 version of the &quot;Body Swap&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> As MCN observed previously, Suppression 3 and above now specifically do not affect Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance, as the sole exception to the Scar's effects carrying over to derived traits.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Variations<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Bioluminescence's &quot;Aura&quot; Deviation now applies the Blazing Light Tilt within long range, not short range.<br /> <br /> Environmental Adaptation engages with the new moderate/severe tagging system for Environmental Tilts, and its &quot;Generalist&quot; Deviation now makes the Variation Toggled with a once-per-chapter limit.<br /> <br /> Gigantic's bonus to derived traits and static effects based on Strength and Stamina is now calculated based on the increase in Size, rather than the Variation's Magnitude; also, as with Superhuman Strength, an object's Size is not included in the calculations used to determine how far the Deviant can throw it.<br /> <br /> Shadow Selves no longer vanish after moving a certain range from the Deviant.<br /> <br /> Superhuman Dexterity now applies the animal rules for Defense calculation.<br /> <br /> Astral Projection 3's &quot;merging&quot; is now a Directed effect, and it provides the Informed Condition regarding the victim rather than granting a bonus to research or social maneuvering against them.<br /> <br /> Aside from the previously listed changes, Body Snatcher's &quot;Puppet Possession&quot; works like the Magnitude 5 version of the effect. Also, it is specified from Magnitude 1 onward that the effects of the Variation do not end if the target moves out of range.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T22:47:46-08:00","id":1433362,"title":"","content":"Quick question about Mutants. The rejection a mutants body does, and more importantly, the change it wroughts upon the body, can still appear entirely supernatural rather than simply a biological twisting right? Like say a mutant was victim to a Warlock using the space Arcanum, would it be a Mtant divergence if instead of absorbing that energy, the body twisted to the point of becoming a contradiction of Space itself (the body overlapping itself, twisting at impossible angles, shrinking yet expanding)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T23:22:10-08:00","id":1433366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433362#post1433362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question about Mutants. The rejection a mutants body does, and more importantly, the change it wroughts upon the body, can still appear entirely supernatural rather than simply a biological twisting right? Like say a mutant was victim to a Warlock using the space Arcanum, would it be a Mtant divergence if instead of absorbing that energy, the body twisted to the point of becoming a contradiction of Space itself (the body overlapping itself, twisting at impossible angles, shrinking yet expanding)?</div> </div> </div> </div>To borrow language from another game, your character's Clade is their <i>idiom</i> \u2014 where their powers come from and how they manifest.<br /> <br /> Not all Deviants with psychic powers are Psychics, but every Cephalist's Variations come from the mental trauma that led to their Divergence, whereas a Chimeric might develop &quot;psychic&quot; Variations through hybridization with a telepathic or manifested Astral creature; a Coactive just needs to have been infused with the right sort of intangible creature/energy (and that's not hard, given that Mage and Beast's models tend to place the Astral higher up the supernatural tree of life for good reason), and a mind-reading Cyborg is a simple matter of being installed with the right sort of relic.<br /> <br /> Mutants can have psychic powers from having weird brain tumors.<br /> <br /> The world is such that the body can interact with parts of reality we would not expect it to just by having unusual configurations of meat, bone, blood, and nerve. &quot;Biology&quot; is a broad umbrella in a setting where long-term possession can make you grow metal armor and stutter-step from Point A to Point B.<br /> <br /> So, to speak to your example, a Grotesque Pathological Deviant resulting from exposure to a spatial warp is likely going to result in the character's genes scrambling to adapt a way out of whatever untoward applications of Space prompted the Divergence, which could theoretically look like anything but will ultimately be rooted in something resembling biology, albeit maybe very weird and/or finely-grained biology.<br /> <br /> Maybe her bones are now radioactive in a way that reinforces mundane spatial configurations. Maybe she's got eyes where eyes don't belong from trying to adjust to a psychedelic Escherscape. Maybe whatever part of the human body lets her soul tell her body where it is is working overtime so there's three of her.<br /> <br /> A Progenitor might be able to figure out the combination of factors that trigger her specific reaction, but the point of the Mutant Divergence is mostly that your Variations come from your body instead of your mind or whatever foreign entity you were blended with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T23:52:53-08:00","id":1433370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433366#post1433366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To borrow language from another game, your character's Clade is their <i>idiom</i> \u2014 where their powers come from and how they manifest.<br /> <br /> Not all Deviants with psychic powers are Psychics, but every Cephalist's Variations come from the mental trauma that led to their Divergence, whereas a Chimeric might develop &amp;quot;psychic&amp;quot; Variations through hybridization with a telepathic or manifested Astral creature; a Coactive just needs to have been infused with the right sort of intangible creature/energy (and that's not hard, given that Mage and Beast's models tend to place the Astral higher up the supernatural tree of life for good reason), and a mind-reading Cyborg is a simple matter of being installed with the right sort of relic.<br /> <br /> Mutants can have psychic powers from having weird brain tumors.<br /> <br /> The world is such that the body can interact with parts of reality we would not expect it to just by having unusual configurations of meat, bone, blood, and nerve. &amp;quot;Biology&amp;quot; is a broad umbrella in a setting where long-term possession can make you grow metal armor and stutter-step from Point A to Point B.<br /> <br /> So, to speak to your example, a Grotesque Pathological Deviant resulting from exposure to a spatial warp is likely going to result in the character's genes scrambling to adapt a way out of whatever untoward applications of Space prompted the Divergence, which could theoretically look like anything but will ultimately be rooted in something resembling biology, albeit maybe very weird and/or finely-grained biology.<br /> <br /> Maybe her bones are now radioactive in a way that reinforces mundane spatial configurations. Maybe she's got eyes where eyes don't belong from trying to adjust to a psychedelic Escherscape. Maybe whatever part of the human body lets her soul tell her body where it is is working overtime so there's three of her.<br /> <br /> A Progenitor might be able to figure out the combination of factors that trigger her specific reaction, but the point of the Mutant Divergence is mostly that your Variations come from your body instead of your mind or whatever foreign entity you were blended with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh i understand now. So the mutant clade simply means that somehow, the body itself is rejecting change (or simply twisting in a way that is trying to adapt to change). I guess I have one more question. With the Cephalists, I understand the cause of their divergence is trauma, but how does one get variety with it? Like I can see a hundred unique Mutants/Invasives/Chimerics/coactives, but I struggle to visualize Psychics in any other way than simply as people who force their will on the world through their minds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T03:34:39-08:00","id":1433378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433370#post1433370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Cephalists, I understand the cause of their divergence is trauma, but how does one get variety with it? Like I can see a hundred unique Mutants/Invasives/Chimerics/coactives, but I struggle to visualize Psychics in any other way than simply as people who force their will on the world through their minds</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare the physically broken (Missing Limbs 5, Silence 4) Cephalist who can only communicate through Telepathy and move through Telekinesis, with the Self-Made Cephalist who challenged themselves physically and mentally until something in their mind snapped and become able to transform their body by force of will alone (Face Thief, Superhuman Attribute, Rapid Healing, Concentration, Preparation, Tribulation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T07:48:00-08:00","id":1433391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433370#post1433370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I have one more question. With the Cephalists, I understand the cause of their divergence is trauma, but how does one get variety with it? Like I can see a hundred unique Mutants/Invasives/Chimerics/coactives, but I struggle to visualize Psychics in any other way than simply as people who force their will on the world through their minds</div> </div> </div> </div>Invasives, Chimerics, and Coactices derive their powers from what was combined with them. Mutants derive their powers from what their bodies attempted to adapt to.<br /> <br /> Cephalists derive their powers from the way their minds broke/adjusted/reacted under the strain of Divergence \u2014 note/recall that their Clade Variations tend to involve breaking down the barriers/connections/limits of the mind (including a literal &quot;cause breaking points&quot; power) and observe all the different ways trauma and coping can manifest in a setting where the supernatural (and especially the violent/intrusive supernatural) is inherently traumatic to encounter for most people.<br /> <br /> To be flip, where a Mutant Divergence can be described as &quot;his body just <i>did</i> that,&quot; a Psychic Divergence can be described as &quot;Have you every been so [scared/angry/ecstatic/etc] that you [impossible thing]?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, to borrow discussion from another different game, while other splats get their powers from robot implants, shapeshifting animal totems, or entropic murder-ghosts, Cephalists can develop new powers by <i>training really hard</i>; it's the &quot;Mutants run on biology but biology is weird&quot; caveat applied to knowledge and perception instead.<br /> <br /> As far as visualization goes, understand that the special effects of your Variations can look like just about anything as long as your Overt Variations are still noticeable; you have all of history and ideology to play with for imagery, as long as you're consistent with how the same powers manifest.<br /> <br /> Maybe Translocation is a combination of tricking the world into not recognizing you for long enough that you can cheat distances, and so a bit of subvocalization and unconscious theatrics accompany the relevant mental gymnastics (Manipulation, Preparation). Maybe your training regiment to develop a functional Carapace requires you to deaden your emotions to deaden incoming blows (Wits, Persistent Drawback: Frozen Heart). Maybe whatever ideal form you're trying to invoke long-term for a bunch of your Variations looks really inhuman and tweaks its surroundings to match it whenever you leverage it (Conspicuous Appearance, Identifier).<br /> <br /> The key is information \u2014 the stuff that informs a Psychic Divergence is in many ways more intangible than the Coactives truck with, but the imagery can draw on any aspect of the incident or conspiracy that made them, whether it's religious iconography, corporate slogans, or things you saw in a single earth-shattering nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:29:03-08:00","id":1433421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433370#post1433370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh i understand now. So the mutant clade simply means that somehow, the body itself is rejecting change (or simply twisting in a way that is trying to adapt to change). I guess I have one more question. With the Cephalists, I understand the cause of their divergence is trauma, but how does one get variety with it? Like I can see a hundred unique Mutants/Invasives/Chimerics/coactives, but I struggle to visualize Psychics in any other way than simply as people who force their will on the world through their minds</div> </div> </div> </div> Have you ever been exposed to <i>Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</i>? Stands -- which usually look like strange buff anime men -- are essentially psychic powers depicted in a way that makes them visually interesting in sequential art. The first three Stands in the series are basically just iconic psychic powers with bodies: telekinesis (Star Platinum), pyrokinesis (Magician's Red), and thoughtography (Hermit Purple). On the opposite end of the scale, a Cephalist's Variations might manifest as something indistinguishable from the wire-fu martial arts of a wuxia flick, being more about body control and superlative awareness than consciously forcing your will on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T15:58:03-08:00","id":1433429,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> thank you. I'm sorry for the odd question, I just have trouble visualizing the Cephalist Clade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T10:42:28-08:00","id":1433723,"title":"","content":"I've been reading my backer's copy of <i>Deviant: The Renegades</i>, and I have a question about the &quot;Monstrous Transformation&quot; Variation.<br /> <br /> The text mentions that when you purchase &quot;Monstrous Transformation,&quot; the form possesses a number of Scar-free Variations. When selecting these Variations, do they count as part of the Magnitudes given to you during character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T10:50:59-08:00","id":1433725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433723#post1433723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading my backer's copy of <i>Deviant: The Renegades</i>, and I have a question about the &quot;Monstrous Transformation&quot; Variation.<br /> <br /> The text mentions that when you purchase &quot;Monstrous Transformation,&quot; the form possesses a number of Scar-free Variations. When selecting these Variations, do they count as part of the Magnitudes given to you during character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, much as they don't count toward your proportion of Clade Variations. Monstrous Transformation functionally allows you to activate multiple Variations entangled with the same Scar as a single Overt action and does nothing else; a Magnitude 5 Monstrous Transformation is not actually eight or nine Magnitude of Variations for the purposes of Threat Level if you don't fill it with Magnitude 1 Variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T10:53:58-08:00","id":1433726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1433725#post1433725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, much as they don't count toward your proportion of Clade Variations. Monstrous Transformation functionally allows you to activate multiple Variations entangled with the same Scar as a single Overt action and does nothing else; a Magnitude 5 Monstrous Transformation is not actually eight or nine Magnitude of Variations for the purposes of Threat Level if you don't fill it with Magnitude 1 Variations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T03:06:38-08:00","id":1434244,"title":"","content":"Can anybody tell me, if I &quot;pre order&quot; the pdf, do I get acces to the pdf now or have i wait until the final release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"M