iner b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1434247#post1434247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should get access to thenPDF now through BackerKit.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah I did <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T05:17:21-08:00","id":1434370,"title":"","content":"So when is Deviant going to get its own subforum like the rest of the games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T11:09:35-08:00","id":1434405,"title":"","content":"You know how one of the things that the stretch goals unlocked were devices for deviants? Stuff that isn't just useful, but also flawed, kind of like the deviants themselves? Well, that's kind of like what the Onyx path forums are like. Something broke a while back, and they haven't been able to fix it. And that brokenness prevents them from adding new forums. <br /> <br /> So we won't be getting a Deviant forum in the foreseeable future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T22:44:17-08:00","id":1434815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1434370#post1434370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when is Deviant going to get its own subforum like the rest of the games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly more detailed answer was given here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1418012-no-https\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1418012-no-https\"> no https - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1418012-no-https\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1418012-no-https </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Why is this forum insecure? All user names and passwords can theoretically be eavesdropped? Why this choice to host an insecure website/forum? edit: I realized </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T14:21:35-08:00","id":1435249,"title":"","content":"Has the errata phase ended already for Deviant? I've been continuing to pick up bits of errata here and there but when I tried to open the submission form recently it said it was closed.<br /> <br /> (I may have just answered my own question.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T19:46:42-08:00","id":1435267,"title":"","content":"Just had the thought at how Deviant would be a great fit, mechanically if not entirely thematically, with Strikeforce: Morituri. Strikeforce: Morituri was a cult superteam book from the mid-eighties about super powered heroes in a future Earth that had been invaded by an alien race called the Horde. However the strange process that gave the superheroes their powers could eventually kill them, often in spectacular fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strikeforce:_Morituri\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/Strikeforcemori.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strikeforce:_Morituri\" target=\"_blank\"> Strikeforce: Morituri - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strikeforce:_Morituri\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strikeforce:_Morituri </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10304-rester","user":"Rester","date":". 02-11-2021, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10304-rester","name":"Rester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T11:14:51-08:00","id":1435568,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/T.H.U.N.D.E.R._Agents\" target=\"_blank\">THUNDER Agents</a> had a similar notion of powered heroes who were slowly being destroyed by their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T13:17:04-08:00","id":1436575,"title":"","content":"I know and love the unspoken agreement around the game to not min-max, but... Idk, I wonder if minmaxing would be that bad in Deviant. It feels like Deviants really put the min in min-max. To get the maximum power from Variations for one set of activities means often taking Scars that make everything else a nightmare. Want to be an unkillable killing machine? Sure thing. Good luck interacting with Touchstones outside of murder. and so on. I mean, you could cheese it somehow, like a set of Scars that requires rare materials or procedures but you took Resources 5 and bully your ST into letting that trivialize getting expensive and rare goods and services. Or some other way I don't know. But it generally feels like an internally balanced game<br /> <br /> EDIT: another &quot;exploit&quot; that no sane ST would allow. Hidden Compartments Variation that allows you to pull out the stuff necessary to deal with your Five-Dot Maintenance Scar on command","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-22-2021, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T13:58:43-08:00","id":1436578,"title":"","content":"It is far too easy to set up Scars that are drawbacks in name only. Especially Relentless Variation and Involuntary Stimulus can be cheesed to be basically meaningless. The former on Monstrous Transformation (aka Hybrid Form) and Conspicuous Appearance means you're getting the drawbacks of looking like a monster while using a Variation that makes you look like a monster, and the latter can way too easily be set to trigger in situations where you want it to be triggered. Consider putting a Lash on Involuntary Stimulus where the stimulus is fear, and suddenly the Scar works in your favour because it reflexively activates your Lash for you whenever you enter combat.<br /> Both examples are not entirely without drawbacks, but they're by far much less potent than intended. When designing a Deviant it's really up to you how punishing you want the Scars to be. Five dot Scars are absolutely devastating, to the point where I can't see why anyone would want take some of them, but you could just as easily use Standard Deviations to bring it down to two lenient Scars at two and three dots for your massive five dot Variation.<br /> Hell, there's even a side bar in the Scars section (or used to, in the KS manuscript) that basically says &quot;yeah, you can totally make broken combinations but please don't&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-22-2021, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T16:21:50-08:00","id":1436592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1436578#post1436578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, there's even a side bar in the Scars section (or used to, in the KS manuscript) that basically says &quot;yeah, you can totally make broken combinations but please don't&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still there. Page 173.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidebar: Choosing Scars</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Variations, Scars are highly flexible and modular, allowing for a massive array of combinations and character concepts. Certain combinations of Variations, Scars, and Deviations might render the Scars\u2019 intended drawbacks ineffective or make the game less fun for other players \u2014 the book can\u2019t take every possible permutation into account. In cases like this, always err on the side of staying true to the spirit and themes of the game, and choose another combination or bend the rules as-written to make the pairing viable as a fun and dramatic Scar that complicates the Deviant\u2019s life and, at higher Magnitudes, can be deadly or otherwise ruinous. The Storyteller is the final arbiter of these decisions and may disallow disruptive or nonsensical combinations of Variations, Scars, and Deviations where needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T17:17:55-08:00","id":1436597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1436578#post1436578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is far too easy to set up Scars that are drawbacks in name only. Especially Relentless Variation and Involuntary Stimulus can be cheesed to be basically meaningless. The former on Monstrous Transformation (aka Hybrid Form) and Conspicuous Appearance means you're getting the drawbacks of looking like a monster while using a Variation that makes you look like a monster, and the latter can way too easily be set to trigger in situations where you want it to be triggered. Consider putting a Lash on Involuntary Stimulus where the stimulus is fear, and suddenly the Scar works in your favour because it reflexively activates your Lash for you whenever you enter combat.<br /> Both examples are not entirely without drawbacks, but they're by far much less potent than intended. When designing a Deviant it's really up to you how punishing you want the Scars to be. Five dot Scars are absolutely devastating, to the point where I can't see why anyone would want take some of them, but you could just as easily use Standard Deviations to bring it down to two lenient Scars at two and three dots for your massive five dot Variation.<br /> Hell, there's even a side bar in the Scars section (or used to, in the KS manuscript) that basically says &amp;quot;yeah, you can totally make broken combinations but please don't&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wondering since you set that example. Would it be balanced to give Conspicuous appearance to Hybrid form, but with the caveat the form is either Persistent OR last to the next scene (but without the benefits. Think shutting down slowly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T11:24:50-08:00","id":1437990,"title":"","content":"I just realized something about how Supernatural Tolerance works for Deviants:<br /> <br /> Page 94: ST is calculated at Acclimation + highest-Magnitude Variation. Even though Acclimation goes from 0-5, this combination gives Deviants the usual 1-10 range of ST, since they're always going to have at least one one-dot Variation..<br /> <br /> Page 111: For a Clash of Wills, Deviants use Acclimation + the Magnitude of the Variation in question. Every other splat uses ST + rating of the power(/activation trait/Ability/idk just make stuff up if it's Beast).<br /> <br /> So when any other roll adds Supernatural Tolerance, Deviants are operating on a 1-10 scale, but specifically for Clash of Wills, they're operating on a 0-5 scale? Am I reading this correctly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T12:05:11-08:00","id":1437994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1437990#post1437990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something about how Supernatural Tolerance works for Deviants:<br /> <br /> Page 94: ST is calculated at Acclimation + highest-Magnitude Variation. Even though Acclimation goes from 0-5, this combination gives Deviants the usual 1-10 range of ST, since they're always going to have at least one one-dot Variation..<br /> <br /> Page 111: For a Clash of Wills, Deviants use Acclimation + the Magnitude of the Variation in question. Every other splat uses ST + rating of the power(/activation trait/Ability/idk just make stuff up if it's Beast).<br /> <br /> So when any other roll adds Supernatural Tolerance, Deviants are operating on a 1-10 scale, but specifically for Clash of Wills, they're operating on a 0-5 scale? Am I reading this correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Clash of Wills dice pools uses Supernatural <i>Potency</i> plus a relevant trait (at least if we consider what's written in Changeling). Unfortunately Deviant doesn't even mention Supernatural Potency so it's probably intended to be the same as Supernatural Tolerance as in most games (only game where it isn't is Demon, and that's only according to a side bar in Changeling), but if you'd like you could consider Acclimation alone to be their Supernatural Potency, in which case Deviant follows the general rule.<br /> Besides, Clash of Wills have always been &quot;unfairly&quot; distributed for the different splats. For those who use Supernatural Potency plus a supernatural trait (Discipline/Arcanum/Renown etc) they gain a variable dice pool that goes from 2 to 15. For those who use Supernatural Potency plus an Attribute because their powers aren't dot rated, gets to use a dice pool that goes from 2 to 20. Deviants are just extra unfairly treated (just like they tend to be in-setting) since their dice pool goes from 1 to 10.<br /> Small side note: Perpetual Variations gain a +5 duration bonus to CoW rolls. This is in fact one higher than the +4 that all other splats gain from using powers with a duration of a year or higher. But a difference of one is far from enough to balance it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T12:44:48-08:00","id":1438001,"title":"","content":"So to recap Supernatural Tolerence is 1-10 (Acclimation + highest Magnitude),but Potency is just Acclimation?<br /> That works.<br /> How many Gnosis/Blood Potency/Primal Urge 10 PCs show up at your table? Cover 10 Unchained at least have all their rules in print and don't need to spend most of their time in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> Iirc, Deviant is supposed to be lower power level than most of the other gamelines (explicitly called out as bigger than Hunter though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:18:42-08:00","id":1438006,"title":"","content":"Deviants being relatively bad at Clash of Wills rolls *except* for always-on powers is entirely intentional, and was even part of the initial pitch to White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:26:46-08:00","id":1438009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1438001#post1438001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Gnosis/<b>Blood Potency</b>/Primal Urge 10 PCs show up at your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three. Used to be four but one player got too busy for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T13:50:31-08:00","id":1438016,"title":"","content":"Clash of Wills is Variation Magnitude + Acclimation (so a range of 1-10 in most cases), with a +5 bonus if the Variation is Perpetual. (see p. 94 &amp; 110-112)<br /> <br /> Supernatural Tolerance is Acclimation + highest Variation Magnitude (also a range of 1-10). (see p. 94)<br /> <br /> Perpetual Variations aside, other splats will eventually outshine them at CoW, but their dice pools at character creation aren't usually that much different than those of other splats - 1-7 for Deviants vs. 2-6 for, say, a mage.<br /> <br /> They often have quite high Supernatural Tolerance at the start compared to other splats - 1-7 for Remade vs. 1-3 for the others (for the most part).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:39:08-08:00","id":1438022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1438009#post1438009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three. Used to be four but one player got too busy for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that is impressive","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T14:39:42-08:00","id":1438023,"title":"","content":"Perpetual Variations do get a +5 bonus t